window.INNKEEPER_CHAPTERS=(window.INNKEEPER_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":2301,"title":"Chapter 2301: Sudden request I","paragraphs":["Daekol was in no rush as he worked on the barrier around the human’s body. If anything, he preferred to take things slowly so that he would not make mistakes. Laws replicating the effect of the Dao were something he had actually never encountered before, and he wanted to study them thoroughly.","The fact that these laws could even disregard his commands meant that they were of a higher authority than his own, which at this point could only belong to Dao Lords. Yet the human was far from reaching the Dao Lord realm. In fact, he wasn’t even a Celestial Immortal yet.","It was quite intriguing, to say the least. He wanted to thoroughly study the application of these laws. Moreover, he dared not be too aggressive in breaking it. He had no idea if the human had contingencies in place, but based solely on the calmness depicted in his eyes before he fell asleep, the human clearly felt like the situation was redeemable.","Thus, to avoid any lingering traps, and more importantly, to avoid accidentally harming the human’s body, soul, or system, he could only take things one step at a time.","Besides, he had found himself an incredibly convenient location to lay low within the dome covering him. Like this, it would be impossible for anyone to determine his location, and it wouldn’t be easy to get to him either. He could work on retrieving the human’s system all the while focusing on strengthening himself simultaneously. This was a win-win situation for him.","No sooner had he had that thought that something changed. The human’s body started to grow stronger for some random reason, and with it, the barrier around him grew as well.","Daekol paused, and his expression fell. Although it was difficult to ascertain the actual cause of the issue, this was not a good sign. He looked around the dome, and decided to add his own measures into the mix, completely isolating them from the outside.","There was no reason for the human to grow stronger randomly on his own, which could only mean he was getting some kind of feedback from the outside. He would need to improve the isolation to prevent any such instances from happening again, just to be safe.","Upper Battlefield","Years had passed since River and Pearl entered the Upper Battlefield, and they had grown immensely, and experienced much. In fact, they had experienced far more than they could have imagined.","Their identities seemed to have been leaked even before they arrived, and they were imprisoned by the elves on their very first day in the Upper Battlefield. They were stripped of all their belongings, including the ring that contained some kind of immortal inheritance, with the necklace being the sole exception.","It was almost as if the elves weren’t able to see the necklace at all. In comparison, though they took the ring, they found nothing unusual about it. That was because Pearl had already learned how to disguise it from Cliff long ago.","They were naturally being held to lure out Karev Sunborne. It was only then that they learned that the immortal inheritance tokens Karev got his hands on seemed to be more valuable than any of them had previously guessed, so much so that there were rumors that even other immortals had exerted their influence within the Upper Battlefield to get it.","Since then, they had conducted a daring escape, retrieving the ring in the meantime. They built their own reputation, fought for treasures, built connections, and completed many quests.","The duo barely got any time to rest, but as a result, Pearl was now nearing the peak of the Golden Core realm.","Cliff made fewer and fewer appearances of late, but the duo only assumed that he was hiding since they were interacting with stronger cultivators. Previously, they used to think that he was a Golden Core cultivator.","Now that they had entered the realm themselves, they knew that he was much stronger. They even silently suspected that he may be a Nascent Soul cultivator who got his hands on some immortal inheritance. Or maybe even... an Earth Immortal who had encountered a terrible enemy!","The very thought of such a thing filled them with trepidation, as well as awe. The trepidation was caused by the thought that even an immortal could be brought down to this state. The awe was because they might have been receiving the guidance and tutelage of an immortal.","Currently, River and Peal were hiding on a ship, wearing disguises to keep their identity hidden as they traveled across a great sea. The captain of the ship was a Nascent Soul cultivator, so getting this close for this long was quite dangerous.","If it hadn’t been for Cliff’s marvelous technique that no one else could see through, they would have been exposed. They were on their way to pursue rumors of an item that could fulfil one of their quests when, suddenly, Cliff appeared as usual - on the head of the strongest person around.","Instead of wearing his usual casual attitude, Cliff’s expressions this time varied between confused and solemn, then back to confused and so on.","That was not an expression they had seen before from him, so they weren’t sure how to interpret it, though it was clear neither of the couple could guess what was on his mind.","\"I need you to do something for me,\" Cliff said, not turning to look back at the two. \"Naturally, since this request is so abrupt, I’ll reward it like the highest level quest. I need you to go in that direction and investigate something for me.\"","Cliff pointed out into the sea, towards nothing specifically. There were no visible landmarks anywhere in sight, and they were far from any kind of landmass. If they ventured off the ship now, even if they ignore the countless monsters that inhabited the sea, they might not be able to find their way back so easily. To suddenly go off would be akin to a deathwish.","Then again, it was not everyday that Cliff made such an abrupt request, so they were also curious about what it was about. Moreover, they were no longer the inexperienced amateurs that they once were.","It didn’t even take long for them to decide. Asking the captain to stop was impossible, so they quietly slipped off from the ship, stealing a rowing boat by hiding it in their spatial ring as they did.","No matter what, swimming in this sea was too dangerous, so a boat or ship of some sort was absolutely mandatory."]},{"number":2302,"title":"Chapter 2302: Sudden request II","paragraphs":["It was suicide, really. Anyone with the most basic level of common sense would agree. To leave the protection of the traveling ship while on these perilous waters was akin to self mutilation at best, and immediate and unquestionable death in any other circumstance.","But the two young lovers had, to a large extent, become numb to the sensation of danger. It wasn’t because they expected Cliff to help them - he stayed true to his word and never interfered. At most, he would offer them an early warning should they be about to encounter an enemy far beyond their cultivation level.","The reason they had become numb was because they had, time and time again, overcome unbelievable odds through their advanced techniques and incredible teamwork. While sometimes they became a little conceited, it only lasted until the next time they encountered danger to remember that even their techniques and the tips on their teamwork came from Cliff, so they were never ungrateful to him.","This was already far more than what most could hope to get, which was why they didn’t even hesitate once when Cliff asked them to endure lethal danger to investigate something.","Naturally, since this was something Cliff had asked them to do, he made sure to help them avoid detection of most underwater monsters, however there was nothing he could do against the tumultuous tides and rising waves. Those were obstacles they had to overcome on their own.","The journey was unexpectedly long, causing them to travel by boat for nearly two weeks. Though they were traveling by rowing boat, their speed was not slow, which only alarmed them to the extreme range of Cliff’s awareness. How had he detected something so far away?","That was a question they wouldn’t get an answer to, however, soon enough they found the thing that attracted Cliff’s attention.","Black cracks appeared in the air above the sea, almost like cracks formed in glass. The spirit energy around the cracks was chaotic, and space itself became extremely tough to move through, suppressing the two so much that they couldn’t even approach the cracks if they wished.","Cliff, however, seemed unbothered by the pressure. Instead, he appeared and stared at the cracks in a daze.","The reason for that was quite simple. One of the earliest quests Lex had ever gotten was to establish a permanent guest district inside the Midnight Inn where guests could reside forever. However, to establish that district was far from simple.","There were a number of prerequisites to fulfil, some of which were easy and some of which were hard. Two of the most difficult requirements were to grow a Winding Road Vine, and own at least one Karmic Lily.","Growing that vine wasn’t simple or easy, which is why he hadn’t distracted the turtle by asking him to grow it - he already had too many projects on hand.","Similarly, finding a Karmic Lily was easier said than done. Even now, Lex had no real leads on the lily, yet right in front of him Lex could see cracks in space. Much more important was the fact that within those cracks, Lex could see Winding Road Vine!","Now that he was laying his eyes on the vine himself, he could finally understand why it was so valuable. The vine was not an actual plant, but was a mutation in space laws. Its applications in space were numerous, and even Lex could think of many uses for it - especially in his necklace!","In fact, a new idea started to form in Lex’s mind, and he altered his plans for the necklace somewhat. An absurd thought flashed through his mind. What if... Lex created his own space wherein he was akin to a Sovereign?","But he pushed that thought away. What even was a Sovereign? Why did they have such incredible powers? Why did the universe love them so much? These were things he did not quite understand, but he had a few guesses. Maybe if he...","Lex flicked his finger, and sent a certain technique into Pearl’s mind. The technique, once used, would allow her to remove the Winding Road Vine from the cracks and submit it to the necklace. It would not be easy for her to do before becoming a Nascent Soul cultivator though, which is why he also taught her how to create a space anchor which she could then later use to teleport back here through a formation targeting that anchor.","Moreover, he even taught her ways to hide the existence of these cracks so that no one else would discover them.","While the couple got to work, not wasting a single second, Lex continued to stare at the cracks, and a soft smile began to form on his lips. The fires of ambition once again began to burn in his heart, and all the suffocation and suppression he felt from his defeat at the hands of Stalker disappeared.","Suffering a defeat was no big deal, even if his losses were substantial. He would take back everything he had lost, and he would come back stronger than ever.","Within the Midnight Inn, Jack changed his plans abruptly. He set off to find Dr. Charles. He needed to consult the good doctor on certain matters regarding Taro’s Journal. It was unfortunate that his plans about keeping his second identity unconnected to the Midnight Inn were ruined, but what that connection was could still be defined by him.","No one needed to know the specifics of the connection between him and Lex. As for his connection to the Innkeeper, he intended on leaving it ambiguous.","Plans, once made, could still be changed. What was important was being flexible enough to reap the most benefits from any given situation.","Lex didn’t mind using up the Winding Road Vine for himself rather than saving it for the Inns quest. Honestly, he wasn’t fond of the thought of permanent guests inside the Inn anyway. Though, technically, it was a system quest so he was certain that there was some reason behind it, and some distinction from other guests who could just pay to stay as long as possible."]},{"number":2303,"title":"Chapter 2303: I swear","paragraphs":["Dr. Charles Best stared at the fairy with an incredibly odd expression, and then looked at the letter in his hands. It contained a list of topics about which Jack required detailed information. He then looked back at the fairy.","\"What is the meaning of this?\" the doctor asked, looking at Jack oddly.","Jack rubbed his temples, as if he was an exhausted worker, on the end of his rope from being overworked.","\"What do you mean, what is this? These are things I need detailed information on. You can get it from Taro’s Journal. Naturally, the one who told me to go to you to collect all this information was the Innkeeper. You can go ask him if you want confirmation, just hurry up. I have other things I need to do,\" he said, his tone filled with complaint.","Charles would, naturally, confirm with the Innkeeper if he was available. Unfortunately, for months already, he had disappeared. Such an occurrence was actually quite common inside the Inn so they weren’t too bothered by it. This, however, was very sensitive information and he couldn’t just hand over this information without confirming the situation.","Since he couldn’t contact the Innkeeper, he reached out to Mary, who appeared the very next moment. Unlike Charles and the rest, she was aware of the fact that Lex was missing and that something had happened to him. To now encounter a random Fairy who not only affected the progress of the whole realm, but claimed to have instructions from the Innkeeper was... well suspicious was not the right word, but she found it hard to believe nonetheless.","After studying the fairy, she realized that she had no strong impression of him, nor had Lex ever mentioned anything regarding the fairy to her.","\"When did the Innkeeper give you these instructions? What did he say?\" she asked, skipping the preamble and getting right into the thick of things.","Jack shrugged.","\"Why are you asking me? Ask the Innkeeper. I didn’t even know I was working for the Innkeeper until I came to the Inn. He must have erased my memories or something. Even now, I don’t really know what I’m doing, I’m merely following orders. Just so you know, I’m certainly not from the Inn or whatever.","\"I’m a respectable pirate- I mean, I’m a respectable trader with a respectable crew, conducting proper, legal business. This mission is just something I’m doing on the side - I don’t work for anyone.\"","The more Jack tried to insist that he was independent, the more Mary became sure that he was actually someone who secretly worked for Lex. As for respectable and proper...","She glanced sideways and saw the hamster trying to fit an entire almond tree inside its cheek to carry it away. In another section, the gnome was getting his beard treated and trimmed, but every time someone combed through it, some stolen gold would fall out of it.","In another section of the Inn, a golden duck was awkwardly stuck inside a solid gold pool. To be clear, it was normal water when it entered - the pool had just turned to gold afterwards, causing it to get stuck in its place.","An elemental with a physical body was exceptionally rare across the whole universe, but he had two of them in his crew, with the crystal alligator being the second.","To say that he was doing nothing dubious would be one of the most absurd lies, but she didn’t press him on that. She was concerned about the timing for when the instructions came. Was this something Lex had arranged before he disappeared, or was it something he had done after?","Or was this possibly a probe from some enemy who had targeted Lex?","She did not let her thoughts show in her expressions, but Lex knew Mary well enough to be able to determine her thought process.","\"Listen, I don’t enjoy this either. How about I swear a big oath or something and get this show on the road?\" asked Jack as he placed one hand on his heart and raised another in the air.","\"I swear on the Heavens, and on my very wings, the instructions given to me were by the Innkeeper, and I only want to fulfil them before getting onto my own other tasks.\"","Mary raised an eyebrow. Various oaths had various levels of binding power. While there were occasional loopholes, they weren’t so easy to make use of. In this instance, for example, he only proved that Jack thought he was working for the Innkeeper, that’s it. If he was fooled, this oath would still work.","After deliberating for a while, Mary could only internally sigh. She couldn’t take actions on behalf of Lex, and she could at most manage some things. Since the journal was a closely kept secret, this should be a part of Lex’s plan. Maybe it was a contingency he set in case something went awry.","Mary nodded towards Charles to let him pass on the information, and disappeared. She had to focus on building her body as quickly as possible. The situation was so precarious that she did not even know exactly what dangers they were facing. She only hoped that Lex would return soon.","She wasn’t the only one with that thought. Ever since Almira had returned, and Lex had disappeared, the staff of the Midnight Inn had become oddly... silent. Prominent members of the staff seemed to have disappeared, and their jovial attitude was hard to find. Now, they were strictly professionals, acting to fulfil their orders.","Meanwhile, in the Temple of Fasting, the training of the Inn’s staff continued, but this time the main focus was not on new cultivators at lower levels. No, the main focus was on stronger, higher leveled cultivators, who were learning about the laws of the universe in the most orthodox and standard ways designed for humanity.","Each of them had enough unique experiences - now it was time for them to raise their foundation as high as possible.","Of course, they didn’t spend all their time inside the temple. Some of them occasionally had to go back when their holidays were used up. In that case, they would continue their training while they worked."]},{"number":2304,"title":"Chapter 2304: Join the crew","paragraphs":["Jack stood atop the arched bridge, staring at the flowing river underneath, appreciating the swimming ducks and floating flowers. Blossom petals danced in the wind, not only creating a serene and beautiful environment, but carrying with them a fragrance of spirit plants.","It was... like a scene out of a painting that could be auctioned for a ridiculous amount of money. That thought put a smile on Jack’s face, even if he no longer valued money. With a duck that could make gold with every step, and an alligator could turn even the wind to crystal, money in itself no longer had any value. Now, what he valued were rare and hard to find resources. Oh, and unique and talented individuals.","\"Have you thought about my proposal?\" Jack asked, even though no one seemed to be around him save the ducks in the river underneath.","Only the blowing wind answered him. That is, until, the dancing blossom petals all came together to make the outline of a young woman.","\"Have you no fear?\" she asked softly, looking at Jack with curiosity. \"I already told you last time about the predicament that plagues the Trelops. Would you still dare to take me along?\"","Jack smirked, looking at the outline of a young woman with amusement.","\"The day we met, I already told you about my crew. I dare negotiate with Dao Lords, and look Sages in the eyes. What makes you think I’ll hesitate to take on a Trelop into my crew?\" he asked.","The Trelop formed only an outline of a body, which is why it was difficult to ascertain her thoughts and feelings. There were no expressions to read. Even so, Jack could tell that she still felt hesitant.","He had noticed her while waiting to complete his negotiations to travel to the Folklore realm, and had struck up a conversation. Almost immediately, he had decided to invite her into his crew!","\"The Trelops are a new race, born in the Crystal realm,\" the Trelop said, her speech somewhat mechanical, as if she was repeating something she had said a thousand times. \"Despite the relatively short duration of our race’s existence, due to the unique nature of our ability to merge with landscapes, we hold the potential for immense power. Previously, before the Crystal realm matured, the Holy Birds kept our race suppressed.","\"After the ascension of our realm, the Trelops adapted quickly to the Primordial Garden, and somewhat overtook even the birds in strength. That is when a Lord of the garden came to us and informed our elders that our race had immense potential, even by the standards of the Primordial Garden. For the sake of the development of our race without interference, we were told to stay within the Garden until we produce at least four or five Dao Lords.","\"Despite such grand ambitions and plans, the elders still decided that it was best for me to leave the Primordial Garden, and spend my days inside the Midnight Inn. Neither the elders of my race, who harbor great ambitions, nor the lords of the garden, who have grand plans, felt it was a loss for me to leave the Primordial Garden. Why, then, do you want someone like me to join your crew?\"","Could Jack honestly admit that his purpose in inviting her was to, once and for all, eliminate the smell of sweat stained wood from his ship? Never!","\"Your elders have their own plans, and the lords their own as well. Why should either of them interfere with ours? The only thing that you need to concern yourself with is how you feel. Do you want to set sail, and explore the universe? Nod for yes, and recite the entire Cosmic Ascendance Spectrum list for no.\"","The Trelop chuckled as she used her hand to cover a non-existent smile.","\"Please think again. I am not like the rest of my race. I am not too powerful, nor can I properly fuse with landscapes. That’s why I was allowed to leave,\" she said one more time, just to make sure that Jack knew what he was getting into by inviting her. It would be quite unfortunate if he expected her to have the strength of her peers.","\"We are a peace loving crew, and hardly ever fight anyone,\" said Jack shamelessly without even blushing. \"Of course, if other people offend us, then the rest of us are more than capable of defending ourselves. We won’t ask you to fight under ordinary circumstances. I don’t want to lie to you, though. We may face unexpected challenges and unanticipated foes. It’s just a part of traveling the universe I’m afraid. In that case, you should focus on defending yourself and not worry about the rest.\"","The Trelop felt touched at the invitation, and found it hard to resist. After all, staying inside the Inn all the time was too boring.","\"Alright, in that case, I’d love to join you! You can call me Rose!\" she said, clasping her hands together in joy.","Jack raised an eyebrow.","\"Rose? Shouldn’t it be ’blossom’, considering you’re using blossom petals?\" he asked, looking at the pink and purple petals that formed the outline.","Rose, however, shook her head vehemently.","\"My mom’s name is Blossom, and my grandma is Daisy, so I can only be Rose,\" she explained, as if that answered all her questions.","Jack nodded, as if her logic made complete sense.","\"By the way, can I ask you a question? Have you heard of a Trelop called Jeena? Why is everyone so afraid of her?\" Jack asked.","That was something he’d long wondered. It would have made sense if she was abnormally strong, but there were countless other Trelop Immortals, yet none had a reputation as fearsome as hers. Despite that, he could never figure out what exactly made her so dangerous.","The question made Rose freeze, and she looked at Jack with a... well, she was only an outline, so he couldn’t tell what her expression most likely was, but based on her silence it was either extreme fear, shock, or excitement.","\"I don’t know what you’re talking about,\" she answered, revealing herself to be the worst liar Jack had ever encountered. \"Aunty Jeena is the nicest, warmest Trelop around. Why would anyone be afraid of her? It’s absolutely preposterous. Let’s not talk about that any more - it’s just the most insane thought anyone could ever even come up with.\"","Jack nodded, but his curiosity couldn’t help but grow even greater. But oh well, finding out would have to wait for later."]},{"number":2305,"title":"Chapter 2305: Emotions","paragraphs":["Getting Rose to join the crew was a random idea that occurred to him, and he didn’t mind doing it since it didn’t interfere with his personal plans whatsoever. The Henali had arrived, and Jack had told them that he needed to be securely and discreetly transported to the Folklore realm alongside his crew.","Remunerations and such could be discussed between the Henali and the Innkeeper the next time they had a meeting. Seeing as how their own meeting was occurring inside the Midnight Inn, and the Innkeeper had not reacted to being mentioned so directly, the Henali concluded that Jack truly was working for the Innkeeper.","As such, they told him that they would assist him, but preparation would take some time. After all, traveling through the Void was tough enough. Doing it discreetly, and to a spot such as the Folklore realm was far from easy.","Waiting inside the Midnight Inn, while the realms laws upgraded, under the eyes of so many forces, was far from ideal. However, since there was nothing he could do about it, Jack just pretended as if everything was normal.","His interaction with the paladins, too, continued as if routine. They weren’t surprised by the existence of a fairy paladin, which could only tell Jack that they were used to paladins of other races.","However, that was the extent to which their interaction went. They asked Jack which battalion and regiment he was from, but he could not give an answer. He was not a part of their empire.","Thus, while they did not shun him for being an external paladin, they did not reveal any of their secrets to him either, or even explain what was happening. Previously, when he had approached them using an identity from the Inn, not only had they welcomed him with open arms, they even explained their history to him.","The difference in treatment was clearly a result of the difference in their background. Lex was first introduced to the universe with a prestigious background. It was only now, due to certain difficulties, that he was able to see the other colors of the universe that he hadn’t seen before.","He didn’t mind though. Even if he couldn’t learn their secrets, he basically understood that the paladin path was his most promising path to progress past his current realm. The laws of the universe, for some reason, restricted fairies from growing stronger beyond a certain realm.","The paladin path, however, seemed exempt from those restrictions. Perhaps it was because, in essence, most cultivation techniques and power systems relied on the resources of the universe itself to grow stronger. The path of paladins, however, relied on the self, the recognition of the universe, and continuously overcoming challenges.","In a sense, it relied more on feedback from certain laws rather than resources. It was just that, even now, Jack could not accurately gauge what those laws were.","Thus, Jack waited inside the Inn, doing his best to avoid attracting attention and causing any kind of scene. Besides, just staying inside the Inn was tremendously rewarding these days.","It wasn’t just the Primordial Sunlight which strengthened their body and improved their souls. No, the very upgrade to the realm also provided all of them with some feedback.","For example, Pebble’s fur became extremely luscious, its color deepening to golden-brown. Even the elasticity of his cheeks improved, allowing him to attempt even bolder acts than fitting an entire tree in his cheeks. It wasn’t just his body - even his ever changing prosthetics were of improved quality. For example, on days he had eyepatches, the patches no longer had worn stitching and faded leather. Instead, there was neat needlework, and an appearance of quality about them. Or on days when he had a wooden peg for a leg, the color of the wood was richer, and the work on the prosthetic more refined.","Longbeard’s beard improved, avoiding the many natural tangles he had to brush out regularly. Tiny-Sparkle’s sparkles became shiner.","Everyone got something, and they also understood that the Midnight Inn was not a place they could mess about, which is why they all remained at their best behavior. Thus, the days passed in relative peace. At the same time, Jack paid special attention to the news and rumors spreading around these days - especially concerning Eden and the sudden invasion by the Sage races.","Comparatively, the years that passed in the Upper Battlefield were much busier, but nothing truly concerning happened. At least, nothing that aroused Lex’s attention. For the young couple, the two years were extremely exciting, and for various reasons.","First off, Pearl entered the Nascent Soul realm. She used the formation to go back to sea and retrieve the vine and submit it to Cliff.","In response, Cliff rewarded her heavily, guiding her in any field and aspect she wanted. As such, she not only became a notable master of formations, recognised across the Upper Battlefield, she also became a master of arrays!","Her fighting strength improved drastically, which allowed her to follow up leads regarding her ancestor, Karev. Cliff, naturally, helped her by giving her a technique that allowed her to track anyone with her bloodline - and also warned her that things might get troublesome if she actually found him.","Even so, she insisted. As her strength grew, so too did her desire for vengeance. Although her personality had been quite docile back when she began cultivating, the hate that had been suppressed in her heart came roaring out when she became a Nascent Soul cultivator.","It was only natural - her own parents had been killed by these people. Why wouldn’t she harbor resentment?","River, throughout this period, did his best to support her. Yet the more and more her anger started to emerge, the more and more River started to become quieter. His charisma slowly became suppressed, and on most days he simply focused on helping and supporting Pearl.","These past two years, where they had become stronger than ever before, had seen less laughter and joy among the two of them than any period since Lex had joined them. Yet such was the nature of humanity.","Emotions, often enough, were the source of the greatest beauty humans could create, as well as the source of much of their ugliness.","For the most part, Lex focused on developing the necklace, and only observed the young couple. He did not interfere with their actions at all. How they would handle this obstacle would determine how they spent the rest of their lives. At the same time, Lex wanted to see their true nature.","Thus, he only responded to their requests, never telling them right from wrong.","This continued until, one day, a major event occurred within the Upper Battlefield!"]},{"number":2306,"title":"Chapter 2306: Unexpected decision","paragraphs":["The news spread faster than the wind. Over one hundred Nascent Soul cultivators, all of different races, including orcs, beasts, monsters, elves, dwarves and more, joined together to ambush the Oolin who had the immortal heritage token.","The Oolin was killed after putting up a furious fight, and the token fell into the hands of an orc, which then attracted the joint attack of the remaining cultivators. Eventually, a massive brawl broke out, with a majority of the hundred cultivators dying. Only around twenty of them survived, all of them gravely wounded.","Who gained the token in the end was entirely unknown because the situation had become too chaotic to keep track of such things.","The fight in itself was major news, as well as the fact that no one knew who had the token anymore. Even greater, however, was the issue of the death of the Oolin.","Compared to everyone else, the Oolin was a relatively lowkey race. They offended no one, had no massive enmities, and often kept to themselves and focused on their own development.","The reason they could do all that, though, was because they were strong enough not to be offended. They were a Noble race, after all. They could not be compared to the vassal races.","The response was almost immediate.","The Oolin responded, and they didn’t care about who was ’technically’ responsible or not. What they carried out was an absolute massacre. A single Oolin can unleash an attack far above their cultivation realm, so when many of them attack together... it was the cultivation world’s equivalent of a nuclear bomb.","The entire alliance was mobilised, not to seek revenge, but to attempt to calm the Oolin down. There were even rumors that Immortals from the actual Greater World had been summoned. Yes, the very same Greater World from where the Upper Battlefield fell down.","What most did not know, though Lex could see plain as day, was that Immortals had already intervened, and had been beaten up thoroughly by the Oolin.","After all, the Oolin too had immortal seniors. If the others could send up word, why couldn’t the Oolin? For too long, everyone was used to bullying vassal races to the point where they forgot that there were repercussions for messing with someone with a genuine background.","Lex couldn’t help but feel somewhat curious, though. What was the big deal even if they found the heritage? Was an Immortal heritage really enough to entice other immortals? That should only be the case if it was related to a Celestial Immortal, right? But shouldn’t there be Celestial Immortals in the Greater World? Wouldn’t it be easier to just approach them?","There was a hint of a conspiracy in the air, and now it was becoming somewhat complex for Lex to discern the truth at a glance. He also didn’t want to exert his energy on these things, so he could only wait to see how everything was resolved.","Using the help of Lex’s technique, Pearl eventually found Karvev Sunborne, hidden in an extremely remote island, pretending to live as a homeless man and beggar. His concealment of his cultivation was perfect, to the point where Pearl doubted she had even found him.","In the end, she decided to trust Cliff. He had never led her wrong.","When Pearl approached Karev, the man assumed he had been found by his enemies. When she revealed her identity as his descendant, he didn’t believe her and tried to fight it out.","Unable to suppress the guilt, the tension, the anger, and the confusion in her heart, she decided to give this ancestor of hers a thorough beating.","Combined with River’s help, the two of them fought Karev, and discovered that it was actually a struggle to win. Unexpectedly, Karev was cultivating the True Path. Unlike the two of them, who had Lex’s help, Karev was a true prodigy, who had discovered things on his own.","It was only after they fought for a long time, and Karev found himself hurt but not seriously wounded, that he finally believed that these two meant him no harm. After all, they had the opportunity to harm him many times.","Then came the reunion - after relocating of course.","Then came the emotional reunion, where Pearl revealed all that she had suffered, the death of their relatives, and everything she had been through. Of course, she kept Cliff’s existence hidden because he had expressly forbidden her from revealing it.","That’s when Karev, tired, exhausted, revealed everything. The token he had received was not for one inheritance. Rather, for each cultivation realm, the token would take him to an inheritance spot and allow him to undertake a test to receive a certain inheritance. He had no idea what the upper limit of the inheritance was, but it had shown no indication of ending any time soon.","Moreover, the token was not restricted to one person. He could use it as many times as he wanted, and that’s what caused the issues. There were certain entities which wanted to monopolize such an immense opportunity, and so had been doing everything in their power to hunt him down.","Karev had been on the run for countless years, and was reaching the limit of what he could bear mentally. He was on the verge of burning out. Just as Pearl had lost family, Karev too had lost many loyal friends and supporters.","However, unlike Pearl, Karev did not harbor a deep resentment in his chest. Although he would not give up on retribution, Lex could see that his personality was still rooted in kindness, which is why he was progressing towards exhaustion and burn out instead of being consumed by anger and hatred.","Then, after the reunion, the three of them came to a conclusion that Lex, honestly, had not been expecting at all. Although Karev offered to take the two of them into the heritage sites as well to receive inheritances, the young couple did not value that too much. After all, they had Cliff.","They agreed, but decided to do it later. Instead, they decided to reopen the Guest House!"]},{"number":2307,"title":"Chapter 2307: More time","paragraphs":["Lex really hadn’t expected that at all. The last time they opened the Guest House, it was merely to take advantage of a hidden Spirit node. It wasn’t like he was addicted to opening and running an Inn.","This time, however, the reasoning was more complex. First, it was because even Pearl could see that Karev was at the end of his mental rope, and he needed to rest and recuperate. He also needed to have some normal interactions lest he develop a Heart Demon.","Second, it was because no one would expect Karev to hide in plain sight. With his existing skills, supplemented by techniques Pearl could get from Cliff, hiding Karev’s identity should not be a problem at all.","On a deeper level, however, they knew that whether Karev was exposed or not did not matter. Those pursuing them would not be careful about who they harmed, or the Oolin would not have been targeted. So, the existence of the Guest House was also a trap!","That was the hidden purpose of the Guest House! Karev had not been the only one hunted down. Pearl and River had long been targeted, and they had noticed it. Someone had been putting pressure on them from the dark, using them as bait to bring out Karev.","Although they seemed to have escaped the influence of the invisible figure for now, it was only a matter of time before they were found again. Eventually, once the tactic failed, they would try something more drastic.","That is when the Guest House would reveal its true purpose! As a genius and well trained formation expert, the extent of what Pearl could do could no longer be judged so straightforwardly. A noble race or a vassal, they would all be the same when they step into her domain.","Thus, what followed were simple, peaceful days. Considering the bubbling hate in Pearl’s heart, that was the opposite of what he had expected.","The built the Guest House within the territory of a Beast that had excellent relations with the alliance. They pretended to be at the Golden Core, with only Pearl at the early stage of the Nascent Soul realm, and welcomed guests from all races.","Much more experienced than they used to be, the size of their Guest House was much greater since they were better able to handle a bigger business. They hired other workers and helpers, better enabling Karev to hide among them.","At the same time, River resumed his habit of cataloging rumors, and even started a secret business of selling information from the Guest House, making it somewhat famous. They used their income to help themselves buy materials to either help Pearl improve the formations in and around the Guest House, or to fulfil quests.","They didn’t make any other suspicious moves. In fact, they tried to remain hidden. That was the only way to make their disguise more believable. Anyone who discovered them would only assume that Pearl and River were biding their time, using the Guest House to acquire money to cultivate. After all, cultivation was not easy - especially for vassal races - and could not be done without sufficient resources.","Like this, another two years passed by. During this time, Karev and Pearl spent a lot of time together, and slowly their relationship became more and more like a grandfather and granddaughter.","It was not a matter of age, or their respective powers, or even their actual relationship. It was simply a natural result of two, deeply wounded people who understood one another, taking care of each other.","As their relationship developed, Karev began to offer Pearl certain insights into his own way of thinking. She was an adult now, so he did not directly offer her any advice, or try to change her perspectives. He simply exposed her to his own thought process.","He had enemies, and a desire for vengeance and retribution. Yet he never let those motivations affect his heart, or warp his personality. After all, doing so would not harm his enemies in any way, but it would basically kill the person that he was originally.","While saying as much was a little dramatic, Karev was unwilling to compromise on who he was or the things that he valued for something as meager as power.","Pearl did not understand his words, and even thought they were absurd. The absence of power was one of the greatest sources of trouble in life - she had experienced as much herself.","Lex, on the contrary, looked at Karev seriously for the first time. A man who valued his principals greater than anything else was rare. It was even rarer for them to survive in the cultivation world, because sooner or later their principals would force them into a situation where they faced death.","However, such people were also worthy of befriending. If they could survive long enough, these were the kinds of people who left behind legends.","Whether his words had any effect on her or not, Lex could not say for certain. However, the change of pace certainly helped calm her down.","It was during this time that one of the conspiracies Lex had spotted in the early days of the Land of a Hundred Rivers started to show some effect.","It was a random day, with guests coming and going as usual, when River spotted an oddly familiar carriage. At first, he could not figure out why this one felt familiar as compared to so many others that went by. It was only when it came closer, and he spotted the words under the logo on the side, that he was startled.","\"Reddings Logistics?\" he muttered, surprised to find it here.","As it happened, the day was coming to a close, and the driver of the carriage stopped at their Inn. A familiar face emerged from within the carriage, and looked at the title of the Inn with confusion. It seemed that the name was one he recognised, but hadn’t expected to see here.","\"Albert?\" River called out as he stepped out of the Guest House and looked at the man. \"Albert Reddings? Is that really you?\"","River and Albert had met only once, when they struck their deal and made connections back in the early days of the Guest House. Years had since passed, and both of them had been through a lot since then.","\"River? Is that... really you?\" Albert asked, shocked to see the once frail, weak man now radiating a powerful aura.","Neither of the two expected to see a familiar face here in the middle of nowhere. Yet now that they had met, of course they had to catch up on old times. Old friends were hard to find, so old acquaintances would have to do.","Pearl, naturally, automatically began to suspect that Albert was up to no good. This was too much of a coincidence. Yet he came, he reminisced, even formed a deal with them regarding supplies, and then he went. He did nothing unusual, nor did they encounter any misfortune after his departure.","For all intents and purposes, it seemed like that really was just a chance encounter.","More years passed, and only two years were left until Lex’s deadline. This time, they did not seem like they were going to reach it, especially since River was still stuck in the Golden Core realm.","Thus, Pearl asked Cliff if it was possible to get an extension. Of course, if they needed to fulfil certain requirements for that extension, they were willing to do it.","Cliff spent some time thinking about his plan. Currently, he required two things. He needed time to complete the changes to the necklace, and he needed resources.","The Upper Battlefield was not a good place for resources, since they were generally low leveled, but it was a great place for time. However, getting his hands on the Winding Road Vine granted him a very valuable resource that he could still work with for a while longer. But alone, it wasn’t worth it. He needed supplementary resources.","He began calculating whether he could find anything of use in this place, and found quite a few options simply because of the number of legacies left behind.","\"Fine. I can add an option for additional time in the list of things you can redeem from your points. However, it won’t be cheap, and each instance of additional time will require certain valuable items that you’ll need to go get. I can provide you with the location of those items, but they won’t be close.\"","Seeing that Cliff was willing to accommodate their request, Pearl felt much better. However, she knew this was only a temporary solution. They needed to increase their cultivation efforts. It was just that reaching the immortal realm in only a couple of decades of becoming a Golden Core seemed impossible.","She could not help but turn her attention towards the ring on her finger. Apparently, even her grandfather knew nothing about it, and hadn’t been able to withdraw any items from it. He had left it behind because it attracted too much attention, but wasn’t worth it. Selling it would cause him even more problems since people might assume he’d kept even better treasures for himself.","Leaving it behind for his family to figure out was the only solution he could come up with.","If they could only figure out how to get it to work, everything would change for them.","\"What’s the origin of the ring to begin with?\" Pearl asked one day."]},{"number":2308,"title":"Chapter 2308: My dream","paragraphs":["As it turned out, even Karvev did not know the actual origin of the ring. He found it on the corpse of an enemy orc he killed during his time serving in the army. The ring appeared to have no limits. Its internal space extended far beyond anything they could sense, and the deeper one checked, the more valuable the resources became.","At the same time, there seemed to be no way to properly gain control of it. Whether they used blood to bind the ring, or their spiritual energy, or they communicated with it, nothing worked.","The problem was that some people could see more in the ring than others, and certain races could sense that the ring was incredibly valuable. Such a thing was nothing but a time bomb. Karev was not so driven by greed that he could not see its dangers, which is why he left it behind.","Even now, the ring offered no solution.","In truth, River and Pearl had even asked Cliff about the ring. Lex, in turn, had looked into it. The ring’s origins were cleverly hidden, and if he wanted to discover them he would need to exert more energy than he cared to. He also could not discern the true means of bonding with it, though when he investigated it he did gain some insight.","The ring once had a spirit that controlled it - a treasure spirit to be precise. For some reason, that spirit had died, which might be the reason the ring could not be accessed.","Lex himself felt some temptation for the ring too, but he could not use it yet so there was no need to think about it. He would need to improve his necklace some more before he could safely use the ring with attracting attention or alerting anyone who might know of the ring’s existence.","Instead of saying that, though, he only said that to learn the secrets of the ring, they’d need to pay 500,000 quest points. That effectively put an end to their efforts to learn its secrets since, basically, that number of points was more than enough to turn them both into immortals!","Once their routine at the Guest House was set, River once again started to venture out to explore for new treasures and bring back valuable items. It was more dangerous than it used to be, so whenever he ventured out, he took the necklace with him.","The years passed, and River became a Nascent Soul cultivator, and even managed to leak his location to a few parties. The time for their trap to spring would be coming soon. At the same time, they were running out of points to use to extend their deadline, so the couple was getting desperate.","Unfortunately, one could not just become immortal just because they wanted to. It was an incredibly difficult process - one that restricted most of humanity from taking that step.","Eventually, the long awaited day came.","A passing group of travellers, seemingly entirely ordinary, stopped by the Guest House. They remained entirely unaware that Pearl’s formation had long recognized that among the group there was one Earth Immortal and twelve peak Nascent Soul cultivators.","Such a large group could basically bulldoze through the Upper Battlefield and find no opponents.","Unfortunately for them... the gates of hell were closed, but they came barging in.","*****","\"To call it a fine weapon would be to call gold dirt,\" said Bob as his gaze fell upon the golden brown baguette being presented to him, untold wisdom hiding behind those eyes. He brought the baguette close to his ear and pressed its center firm.","A fresh baguette would give off a fluffy sound, with the slightest crunch from the outer layer. However, this baguette which had been aired and aged, which had been fanned from the tails of generations of Drama-cats, gave off no sound at all. It was firm, unyielding, as if the destruction of the world itself could not cause it to bend.","Which teeth dared to dig into this magnificent rod of gold? None!","\"Through a thousand generations, through hairball epidemics and yarn shortages, we cats have endured,\" spoke the Drama-cat standing in front of Bob, a grey colored robe hiding his body and face. \"Through pain and pleasure, we have endured. Through glory and dishonor, we have endured . With hope in our hearts when hope did not exist, through strength in our resolve when we lacked it in our limbs, we have endured!\"","The Drama-cat suddenly looked upwards towards Bob, the hood on his head falling back, revealing uneven braids and locks that would leave his hair tangled for days. Gasps echoed in the room as the other Drama-cats looked at the one speaking, horrified at the condition of the speaker!","\"I am merely an insignificant captain in your army, honored with the post of Midnight Inn Daycare mascot. What future I will see, I do not know. But I pray, Lord Bob, that my descendants see the day when the Drama-cats rule the world.\"","His words echoed through the hall, washing over the congregation of Drama-cats, fueling in their hearts an ambition they had never known before.","It was true. Most common Drama-cats were pathetically weak. Besides Bob, they had no strong warriors, so it would make sense that the dream that most resonated with them was of acquiring strength.","Yet amidst the sea of widening eyes and awe filled hearts, Bob remained unmoved.","\"What feeble dreams,\" Bob uttered as he placed the baguette on his shoulder and turned around, looking up into the heavens. There, in the sky, hung a star in the shape of a crow. Of course, Bob couldn’t see it because there was a ceiling in the way, but why did that matter?","\"Is it power you seek? The strength of your arms?\" Bob asked, looking wistfully at the sky that he couldn’t really see.","\"How many can grow strong? How many can become rulers? How many can leave behind legacies? Dost thou not wish for something more original? More unique?\" his voice bellowed, shaking all the cats free from their stupor and bringing their eyes to him.","\"The dream that comes to me in my sleep, and the dream that lingers, lingers even when my eyes open and greet the light of dawn, is far greater than that.","Every land has a king. Every realm has a ruler. Every tiny speck of land in the fabric of existence has one who places his posterior upon a throne and calls himself master. Everywhere you go, you will find some stronger than others.","\"To dream of strength? Futile. Mundane. Mayhaps, it could even be called boring. What I dream of is far greater. What I dream of is rare. It is precious. It is like a taco that has survived Tuesday.","\"I dream... to follow the captain. To witness with my eyes the age his footsteps shall leave behind. To witness the chaos unfold... to see for myself his grand designs so that one day... one day I can, perchance, say, with tears in my eyes and glory in my heart, that I was there. I saw him. I followed him.\"","Tears streamed down Bob’s eyes, and as the Drama-cats watched him speak, the passion overwhelmingly packed in every word he spoke, tears started to stream down their eyes too. Bob was like looking at the sun with their bare eyes - blindingly bright, and radiating the very warmth that sustained life.","A single cat fell to his knees, and then one by one, so did the others. They now had a dream so beautiful that... they couldn’t fully understand it. Who was the captain? What was he captain of? Why was Bob following him?","These were questions they didn’t have answers to, but that hardly mattered. All that mattered was the dream.","While Bob was trembling, trying to hold himself together as he welled up. The dream was too beautiful.","Yet, as if omniscient about what was happening here, the captain sent a message to Bob that very moment.","An Inn worker approached and, after knocking, entered the hall filled with kneeling cats and handed Bob a small note.","\"We’re about to leave. Come back.\"","That was all it said, but it was enough. With his baguette in hand, and a smirk on his face, Bob teleported away - the three Boblings watching from in the corner, shaking from excitement.","The crew all gathered onto the Jolly Rancher, and used a tavern to head to the Origin realm, from where the Henali would secretly escort them to the Folklore realm.","As a result of all that was happening, almost all forces inside the Inn were watching Bob, Jack and their crew. Their departure was highly suspicious, and could grant leads on the Innkeepers next moves, or even his whereabouts.","Amidst all the silent plotting and conniving happening, no one seemed to notice that there was a small group who were exclusively watching Z, and recording all his moves."]},{"number":2309,"title":"Chapter 2309: Humanity’s destiny","paragraphs":["Remy Lavern. That was a name that Lex had paid some attention to in the early days of the Inn. But as the Inn grew, and it faced greater horizons, it was a name that was relegated to the background - not completely forgotten, but mostly unimportant.","Lex had even received a quest related to him once. Remy, upon learning about the wondrous uses of the Midnight Inn’s golden keys, wanted to use the Midnight Inn as a meeting location to discuss matters with members of his secret intelligence organisation. Communication across galaxies was too slow and difficult, but with the Midnight Inn it became a simple matter of congregating at the same time.","Back then, he was someone who seemed to know the inner workings of the Jotun Empire, which was a huge breach of security. When Lex was weak, it seemed unbelievable and monumental. Later on, he couldn’t be bothered by it because the Jotun Empire was far from the strongest empire he had been facing.","Nowadays, dealing with organisations with Dao Lords and control over several Major realms, he seemed to have become even less worthy of notice. That wasn’t to say that he would be looked down upon as a guest. Rather, even when Lex had the Host Attire, he wasn’t someone Lex paid special attention to.","After all, even if he knew a few secrets, were they worthy of his attention? Or could they even be secrets from Lex at all, based on the numerous intelligence sources he had spread out across the universe?","First was Velma in the Humanoid Alliance, who was a master of gossip. He also had Anita’s undead spread out across the Origin realm. There was also Roland’s covert intelligence ring which originally comprised the children who came to the Midnight Daycare, but had long since grown and entered into various levels of society.","Besides them, he even had the two Rhinocentaurs who shared intel on a daily basis from their own original sources. Last but not least, he had the Newsroom where people could come and sell information for MP, or trade it for information they needed.","Compared to all of that, what could Remy even have to offer? Thus, his was a name that was of little importance. Not to mention, Lex didn’t even have access to the Host Attire anymore, so even if he wanted to, he could not spy on him.","Yet, for some odd reason, it was this Remy Lavern, who was once again having a secret meeting inside the Midnight Realm, who seemed to have access to information that, for various reasons, seemed out of reach of the members of the Midnight Inn.","At the head of the conference table sat Remy, a member of the Atila race - a race that mutated off from humans. Although they originated from humans, the Atila race were actually much stronger than humans, and even had the ability to shapeshift into any humanoid race, making them perfect for espionage.","The only drawback of their race was that the stronger they became, the more violent tendencies they had, causing them to form somewhat of a bottleneck in terms of growth and utility.","\"I’m glad to see that you all have been making steady progress in your missions,\" Remy said, his tone and expression at ease, as if everything had been going well for him in life. \"I was recently contacted by Lord Kingmaker who has updated me on several matters, and given us a new set of missions.\"","Across the room, the various members of the secret intelligence agency nodded and listened eagerly.","\"First, the focus of the universe has shifted. These are things that are far beyond us, but we should know anyway to better understand the local trends. Many forces have attacked the Angels, and the Humanoid Alliance has focused strongly on their defense. The scale of the attack on the Angels basically means that a lot of pressure has been shifted away from the other races.","\"While for other Noble races, such as Devils, Elves, Dwarves and Celestials, it hardly matters since they will be forced to divert their Dao Lords to protect the Angels, this has created an opportunity for certain Vassal Races. Key among them are the humans.\"","Lex, within the Upper Battlefield, assumed that the titles of Noble Races and Vassal races were specific to that realm. What he hadn’t realized was that these terms were generic to the whole universe.","The top ten races on the Cosmic Ascendance Spectrum were the Sage races. From the eleventh to the hundredth position were the Elder races. Below the Elder races were the Noble races, which basically included all races below the hundredth spot, and had a minimum of five Dao Lords across their race.","All races below that were Vassal races, even if they had as many as four Dao Lords. While it was somewhat unfair to lump races with one to four Dao Lords in the same category as races without even a single one, in the grand scheme of things, it was all the same.","After all, their status in the universe could only allow them to be vassals of other, more powerful races. At best, they were somewhat more capable vassals than others.","\"Using this opportunity where attention is diverted away from keeping the humans suppressed, many forces are trying to revive the legacy of the humans. Of course, many other races are attempting to do the same, for example the mermaid race or the cherub race.","\"Our focus, however, will be focused on the humans. Many ancient legacies, heritages and sects will open their doors to humanity. The techniques, paths and even Daos of ancient humans will come within reach. Our goal will be to find and focus on any and all humans who seem to be carrying a hint of Humanity’s destiny.","\"With the Nexus event approaching, this could be the turning point for the human race. This is the only opportunity for them to rise from the ashes. Simultaneously, it is the only chance for us to get our hands on the ancient legacies of humanity. Even if we do not gain access to the legacies, by establishing a close relationship with these chosen few, we can benefit from the rapid growth that they will likely experience during this time.","\"Almost all forces will be looking to do the same. In fact, many suspect that even the Midnight Inn focused on nurturing so many humans because it already anticipated such a thing long ago - not that the Inn’s actions have anything to do with us.","\"The Kingmaker merely wants us to...\""]},{"number":2310,"title":"Chapter 2310: Target acquired","paragraphs":["\"Everything we do, we do for the future of the human race,\" said the man seriously as he looked at the four others in the small room with him. \"We are taking on great risk, and are offending many powerful figures. It is likely that we will be hunted down, and even killed. But if our mission is successful, the whole of humanity will benefit. There is no better cause for which we may lay down our lives.\"","The man’s words were not mere rhetoric. He genuinely believed them, and so did the others. They knew that the actions they were about to carry out weren’t exactly moral, or even fair. But for the sake of humanity’s future, the suffering of a few was a small price to pay. Not to mention, the target of their actions today should feel honored!","Every second of every day, trillions of beings died across the universe, but their deaths brought nothing of value to the universe, or even their lives. For their target to be able to affect the course of history, even if it was only by a small extent, was a great honor.","Whether the target wanted that honor or not was no longer up to him.","\"Our window will be small,\" the man continued to speak. Up until this moment, none of them knew the plan. It was safer that way. However, since their mission was mere minutes away from happening, they had been informed, so that they could prepare themselves. They only needed to act as instructed - everything else had been taken care of.","\"We have news that the Dream tavern in the Dream realm will soon close operations. While it still operates, it is under the joint protection of the Henali and the Humanoid Alliance. Our operation will take place in the exact last minute of the tavern’s operations, right before the respective Dao Lords retreat from their given posts.","\"It is said that the Innkeeper is absent from the Midnight Inn, which is what has given rise to the possibility for our operation to succeed. If he were present, it would be impossible to fool or distract him. The two Dao Lords, however, will be distracted by someone else for exactly one minute.","\"During that time, we will locate the target, capture him, and bring him out of the Dream tavern. As soon as that is done, our mission will be complete. We no longer need to concern ourselves with what will happen afterwards.\"","The four stood up, their expressions grave as they did. The future of humanity rested on their shoulders. It was a grave responsibility, and an unbearable burden. Still, they had to carry it out.","\"We stand in the shadows, unknown, unrecognised, and seek no glory,\" the five of them recited together, as if it were some kind of mantra. \"For the sacrifices of the past, for the prosperity of the future, we act to bring light to the darkness, to bring hope to the hopeless, to restore what has been lost.\"","With unquestionable belief and certainty in their hearts that what they did was correct, the five of them crushed the tokens they had been given. A protective shield wrapped around their bodies, containing the power of an unknown Dao Lord.","This shield would prevent them from being detected by the existing two Dao Lords protecting the Inn, and even keep them from being sensed by the Security team in the Midnight Inn. They had already been tested before, which is why the one orchestrating their actions from the shadows knew they would work.","The five of them entered the Dream tavern separately, and perfectly blended in with the guests of the tavern, raising no suspicions. The staff informed them that the tavern was about to shut down, and that they would not be able to return to the Dream realm once it did. If they wanted to go back, they had limited time to do so.","They were already aware of that, but thanked the staff for letting them know, and expressed that they were intending on going back.","Afterwards, they all spread out across the tavern. Naturally, they would not be able to sense the location of the Dao Lords, but that wasn’t their mission anyway. They only located other Celestial Immortals within their vicinity, and how close they were to the target.","They searched for security or other personnel who might interfere. Once all their reconnaissance was done, they quietly got into position and waited for the signal to start.","Time passed by quickly, and just as there was only a single minute left for the Dream tavern to shut down, a Mirage covered the entire tavern, transporting all the guests within.","A Mirage was a place created from the thoughts of a Dao Lord, and it could protect those below the Dao realm from being exposed to the aura of Dao while Dao Lords wreaked havoc.","Everyone was alarmed, confused, or perhaps even unaware. Yet before anyone - even the Inn staff could react - the five Celestials acted. They were at the peak of the Celestial realm, and had been stuck there for ages. The chances of them ever reaching the Dao realm was nonexistent.","However, among Immortals, they still could not be challenged easily. One of them acted to isolate Little Blue so that he would not be harmed. At the same time, Z was separated from his mount.","Three other Celestials acted in unison, chaining his entire body before he could even act, restricting his spirit energy and locking his tenet, making it go dormant. The last Celestial grabbed Z and placed him within a spatial prison that had been specially prepared to transport the target.","\"The inheritor of the Human King Zarek’s legacy has been captured,\" the Celestial said out loud before crushing another token. It did not teleport him out - rather it wrapped him in another powerful shield created from the powers of a Dao Lord.","Then, his body directly tore out of the space of the Mirage, and then the Dream tavern, entering the Dream realm. What happened after that, not even the Celestial Immortal himself knew.","The entire action, from start to finish, took only one second. What the other fifty nine seconds of their mission were reserved for, the Celestial Immortals neither knew, nor cared.","The remaining four Celestial Immortals began their own escape.","One of the requirements of the mission was to ensure that no guests or workers of the Inn were harmed, to avoid provoking the Innkeeper excessively. He had merely lost a single Immortal worker. For a Dao Lord, such a thing was not a big deal.","Sure, this immortal was a little special due to his connection to the ancient human king Zarek, but it was within manageable levels. The situation would not escalate beyond that, and the Innkeeper could be compensated in other ways.","Lex, who was focused on his ring, remained entirely unaware of all of this. After all, he himself was isolated from such news, while Jack had already left the Inn. At the same time, this could be considered a failure of two massive organisations, which is why even they would do their best to suppress the news and handle the matter quietly.","To begin with, most did not even realize what had happened beyond the sudden appearance of the Mirage. Thus, whether Lex would learn of this any time soon... was entirely uncertain."]},{"number":2311,"title":"Chapter 2311: Slow on the uptake","paragraphs":["Everything happened too quickly, attracting minimal attention. Most guests did not even realize anything had happened at all, and continued to act as normal. Their entry and exit from the Mirage was seamless, and the actions of the five Celestial Immortals was hidden by the Dao Lords. How could any of them detect anything?","Even Little Blue, who served as Z’s mount, did not realize anything happened because he was influenced by the Dao Lord who created the Mirage. Within the entire Dream tavern, only the two other Dao Lords knew what was happening, yet they weren’t able to stop the enemy.","Their inability to act was for one, sole reason: as soon as the Dao Lord acted he made his intentions plain.","\"I am only here for one human. If you try to stop me, I will destroy this whole tavern and everyone in it,\" the Dao Lord said, showing no fear in the face of two others - even though he kept his identity hidden.","A clash between Dao Lords was far from simple, and it would take years for any real progress whatsoever. In that case, if one Dao Lord unleashed his power without restraint, all those below the Dao level would die. While it was possible to stop him, it required certain circumstances which didn’t exist at the moment.","Such a situation was not present, so they needed to make a choice. Ordinarily, their very presence itself was a deterrent. After all, once this confrontation was over, it was almost certain that they would attempt to discover this person’s identity and rescue whoever they took, lest the Innkeeper hold them accountable.","Yet the fact that they acted anyway meant they weren’t afraid of being discovered.","All of that, however, was for the future. At the moment, they had to deal with the situation so that the Innkeeper wouldn’t cancel out any chance of working with them in the future.","\"While we’re here, let me make a proposition,\" the Dao Lord attacking said. \"I have heard the Innkeeper is absent from the Midnight Inn. Besides taking my target, my next goal is to find out for certain if he’s really missing. Why don’t you two cooperate with me on this? Your organisations will benefit from this information as well.\"","The mere proposition infuriated the two Dao Lords. They were naturally prideful. Forcing them to not act was bad enough, now he was asking them to purposefully derelict on their duty?","\"The moment I am free from this task, I will seek you out to find out just what benefits you’ve acquired this time around,\" said the Henali angrily.","Yet his words did not intimidate anyone.","\"Will you search for me, or the one who hired me to act, or the ones taking away the target kidnapped from this realm? Because they are all separate. I want to see for myself just who you will choose to follow.\"","The Henali grit his teeth, but the Dao Lord from the Humanoid Alliance simply remained silent, searching for any weaknesses or traps.","While their confrontation continued, across the entire Midnight Inn, only Mary realized what was happening. The System sent countless notifications to Lex, but he could not hear them at the moment, nor could he respond in any manner.","She, too, was powerless to respond in any meaningful way. In fact, if anything, she was grateful that the enemy was still wary of the Innkeeper and was only kidnapping one person. Otherwise the consequences could have been catastrophic.","But the situation wasn’t over yet. Disaster could still strike. All she could do now was pray.","Fortunately, on the sixtieth second, the Dao Lord disappeared from the Dream tavern, unwilling to risk the return of the Innkeeper. It was said that the Innkeeper could attack while keeping 100% of his aura restrained, thus achieving true stealth among Dao Lords. That was not something he wanted to risk.","As soon as he left, the two organizations immediately launched an investigation, but all immediate traces had been erased. Moreover, the Inn staff, entirely unaware of what had happened, shut down the Dream tavern and returned it to the Midnight Inn as expected, putting an end to the Inn’s connection and access to the Dream realm.","The Inn staff were celebrating, happy that they had successfully completed their orders without facing any issues. A few noticed that Z was missing, but they only assumed he was busy elsewhere.","The organisations immediately applied to meet the Innkeeper, but he was not available so they met with Mary. She could not make any decisions on behalf of the Inn, so she merely nodded along and allowed them to carry out whatever plans they came up with to get to the bottom of the issue.","None of them asked why Mary hadn’t helped with the situation. Since they were responsible for security at that time, they were ones who had to deal with all associated issues.","Their failure this time meant that the Innkeeper might not be willing to work with their organisations in the future.","To think that they had asked for access to the Dream tavern for millions of years, but they could not even complete one year without issue. The shame from their failures would haunt them for a while.","A long, long time later, Z opened his eyes. He had not even realized he was captured, nor was he aware of anything else that happened in between. One moment he was atop Little Blue, and the next he was waking up in some kind of shoddy dungeon.","\"Lookie here, the newbie is awake,\" said a hoarse voice, echoing through the dark, humid hollow. The sounds of clinking and clattering chains rang out in the distance, alerting to the fact that this dungeon was quite big.","He didn’t quite understand what was happening. How could his surroundings suddenly change? Was he involved in some kind of event? He hadn’t been informed of any upcoming events like this.","\"Looks like he’s a little slow on the uptake,\" spoke another voice, filled with schadenfreude. \"In that case, let me help you. Welcome to the Army of Slaves boy. Your only options here are to fight or die - there is no in between, and you have no luxury of any other choice.\""]},{"number":2312,"title":"Chapter 2312: Test","paragraphs":["Years. So many years had passed, and Lex had used up all the resources that the Upper Battlefield could offer him. Still, Pearl and River had only reached the peak of the Nascent Soul, and made no real progress towards the Earth Immortal realm.","Lex did not want to blame them - they were genuinely trying very hard. However, he also found it irritating. It was just the Earth Immortal realm. What was the big deal? Why were they making such a big fuss about this?","He turned his gaze towards the basement. There, in her formation, Pearl even had an Earth Immortal trapped. They had attacked the Guest House with the intention of learning River and Pearl’s secrets, and hoping to use them to find Karev. Well, they learned some of the couple’s secrets, and that was enough to kill all the Nascent Soul cultivators.","They lacked the ability to kill the Earth Immortal no matter what they did, so they simply trapped him in a formation designed by Lex to keep him from accessing laws.","They kept asking for more time, but at this point Lex had nothing left to gain from the Upper realm, so he could no longer delay his departure.","\"I’ll tell you what,\" said Cliff as he looked at the no longer young couple. \"Cultivating traditionally will not allow you to breakthrough any time soon. You need some opportunity or resource that will help you bridge the gap between your current ability, and that which is required to become Immortal. While the Upper Battlefield does not lack such opportunities, I think it’s about time you attempt the test Karev offered through his token.\"","Pearl’s ancestor, Karev, had also recovered a lot during these past few years. His mental fatigue had waned, and his weakening resolve had once again been strengthened. He was feeling much better, and was once again ready to resume his cultivation journey.","The reason he was lingering was not because he couldn’t break through, but because he was enjoying the time too much. How long had it been since he was able to live such a relaxed life?","Unlike them, he could break through to the Earth Immortal realm whenever he wanted. After all, unlike them, Lex recognized him as a true, genuine genius. What’s more, he had what it took to be identified as a Destiny’s Child, meaning he would always find opportunity amidst hardship.","The reason he wasn’t transcending to the next level was because he didn’t want to leave Pearl and River behind, which would inevitably happen when they entered the Immortal realm.","Once they asked him, he was more than willing to take them. To begin with, he didn’t understand why they had been resisting in the first place.","They left the Guest House running, since there were many capable staff who could keep it operating behind their back, and pretended to go on a trip to search through a recently discovered heritage site.","Once they were far away from the Guest House, and they were sure that there was no one nearby to observe them, Karev activated his token and led the three of them into a whole new realm!","Almost immediately, Lex was hit by a sense of deja vu, for he could swear he had been there before. A moment later, however, he realized that it wasn’t deja vu. Rather, the layout of whatever area they had entered was particularly similar to the Temple of Fasting.","Of course, it wasn’t the same for Lex to recognize the laws of the Origin realm, and even the unique energy signature of the Temple. Still, it was obvious that this place was related to the temple somehow. That explained why this token was passing out a heritage to anyone who passed its test!","There were a couple of reasons why Lex wanted the couple to come and experience this place. First, he himself was curious about it, and wanted to know what the big deal was all about.","As far as he could tell, this place was likely worth the hype if it was really connected to the Temple in some way. Although the Temple was focused solely on humans, based on what happened to the Oolin, this could give something to other races as well. Maybe, this place was even superior to the Temple somehow. If that was the case, hopefully it could help them reach the Earth Immortal level soon!","The second reason he asked them to experience it was because he was hoping to encounter more valuable resources. As things were, he’d used up basically all the mortal level resources he would need, and to further improve the necklace he would need more valuable ones. That wasn’t even counting the need for absolutely rare resources that he usually had on hand, which were obviously now lacking.","The couple went through the process of getting tested, and the tests lasted a long time. Pearl took six months to pass, whereas River took nine! During the three months of wait time, Pearl retreated to a cultivation room within this unusual yet empty place.","All she did was cultivate - though she shared the inheritance she gained with Lex as well. The inheritance she received was quite unique, and would change her cultivation to make her similar to a fire elemental. Her body would evolve, and have two states - a normal state and an inflamed state.","Clearly, this cultivation technique had been specifically customised for her!","Though that was not the thing that had stunned Lex. It also wasn’t the fact that River came out receiving an inheritance for paladins.","No, the most shocking thing for Lex was that when he went into the test with River, who was wearing the necklace, he was teleported into a separate testing region of his own!","While Pearl was proving she deserved to become half elemental, and River was learning that there were other ways to improve a person’s life than to simply give them things, Lex found himself in a white chamber with the necklace harboring his soul hanging above a vat of silver liquid.","As for the test? It was simple. He had to create a mechanism by which Relational laws operated differently within his necklace. Basically, he needed to choose any Relational law, and make sure that within the necklace that law operated differently from how it normally would.","The only external resource available to him to make that happen was the vat of silver liquid beneath the necklace.","Lex extended his spirit sense and investigated the liquid. He wasn’t sure what it was, he’d never encountered or learned of something like this before. He would just have to find out on his own."]},{"number":2313,"title":"Chapter 2313: Odd reward","paragraphs":["\"How interesting,\" said Lex as he materialised outside the necklace and looked at the silver liquid. He was more and more convinced that this place, whatever it was, was related to the Temple in some way. Otherwise, it would not have been able to so easily separate him from Pearl, or allowed him to undergo a test.","Lex dipped his finger in the silver liquid - though he was technically just a projection. Still, since when had being a projection stopped anyone from doing anything? Of course, in reality, he did far more than just dip his finger in the liquid.","He channeled his energy into it and observed how the liquid reacted, taking in all of its properties. By now, Lex had enough energy to basically use his powers normally without issue.","A big fight would be challenging, but fortunately he wasn’t in a fight. This place also had abundant energy, so it would not be a problem.","After a few hours of testing, Lex decided to call the liquid Silver Ink because it had a very unique property. Array characters were unique characters that were formed as a result of the actions of laws, and they could be used to form arrays.","Basically, array characters allowed array users to make use of laws to certain effects without directly interacting with the laws. The very important thing to keep in mind was that the relationship between them was hierarchical, since arrays depended on laws.","Well, the Silver Ink allowed array characters to be written, used and applied outside of arrays. While such things could be done without the Silver ink as well, the effect would not nearly be as impressive.","In short, the ink was valuable, but not too valuable. The issue Lex was facing was that he was supposed to use array characters to permanently alter the function of a certain law within his necklace. For a very specific instance or circumstance, it was possible since Lex could design a sufficiently complex array.","But to account for an entire law, regardless of circumstance, to work differently was not a simple or easy task. Lex would have gone and said it should be impossible, if only he knew that impossibility didn’t technically exist.","Fortunately, Lex did not have to actually limit himself to arrays. While it was the only resource given to him, he could make use of the necklace itself, not to mention all the low level resources he’d accumulated over the years.","\"What law to pick?\" Lex asked himself as he pondered over this challenge. He wasn’t too worried. It wasn’t like he’d be stuck here if he couldn’t pass. He’d just be giving up on the reward - whatever it was. Yet he was curious about what he’d get, so he started to ponder.","This first thing Lex focused on was his goal for the necklace. He had many, but the most fundamental to any of them would be the necklace’s ability to gather sufficiently large amounts of energy regardless of its location.","Lex thought about his goal, and the resources available to him. Fortunately, he even had access to the characters from the Book of Changes, which were perhaps the most special characters he’d ever come across. Moreover, arrays used energy from the universe to power themselves. So, if he... no, that wouldn’t work. What if...?","Nah, that was ridiculous.","Lex shot down idea after idea, plan after plan, for no matter what he thought of, he couldn’t identify a convenient law to affect, and how to affect it.","For nearly one month, Lex did nothing but sit and think. Such a long duration of planning was, for him, quite rare. To encounter a problem he couldn’t find a solution for was even rarer.","In the end, Lex came to the conclusion that something like this wasn’t a problem that could be resolved with only theory. He would need to attempt his ideas and practically determine the outcome before progressing step by step.","Thus began his journey. The law he was targeting was one that he was exceptionally familiar with - karma! He wanted to make it so that karma would not attach to the necklace as was standard. That meant that if the necklace did something - for example, give Pearl additional energy recovery and healing - then the karma between her and the necklace would not be formed.","Although it seemed simple enough, it was actually quite complicated. Karma was not simply something used to trace events. It was what allowed so many other laws to function normally - laws that depended on a sequence of events, or growth, decline, reward, punishment and so many more.","While the Masterless technique already hid Lex, reducing the karma of his necklace would help it hide better.","Yet as he attempted to turn that goal into a reality, he was faced with the reality that he wasn’t nearly adept enough in manipulating karma to achieve such a massive change permanently. Thus the goal changed. Instead of negating all karma, he decided to divert it.","Instead of the karma attaching to the necklace, as it ordinarily should, Lex decided to make it so that the karma would attach to anything within the necklace itself. For now, it was meant to be random, but he could change it later on if he needed to. This was merely a start.","Over the next four months, Lex focused on nothing else, and managed to achieve his goal using the Silver Ink, the characters from the Book of Changes, and the inherent quality of the divine ore to facilitate miracles.","The best part was that since this was made using an array and silver ink, the array would not disappear on its own, and its actions would be fueled by the universe and not the necklace’s own energy reserves.","In fact, over the course of completing this test, Lex got a few more ideas about how and where to source the energy from the necklace.","He managed to complete the test long before Pear and River, and had to admit that the test was very obviously designed with his skills and limitations in mind. What he didn’t understand was his reward!","Instead of receiving some kind of inheritance, he received an inert, iron coin.","He called it inert because he could channel no energy into it, nor could he make use of it in any obvious way. For once, he had no idea what he was dealing with. Yet instead of being annoyed, he was only intrigued.","After all, his instincts, which had been silent for too long, told him that the coin was very important, and it would reveal its use soon enough."]},{"number":2314,"title":"Chapter 2314: Comparison is the thief of joy","paragraphs":["\"So I’m giving you three more years,\" Cliff said to River and Pearl once everything was done and settled. \"If you can’t reach the Immortal realm in three years, then I will have to leave you behind.\"","The Guest House was doing absolutely fine when they returned, and they hadn’t been secretly attacked or plotted against by some unknown evil enemy - what a shocker. Not having a system to continuously attract trouble really changed the way people lived their lives. Lex couldn’t understand it.","\"Three years? Isn’t that absurd? How can anyone become an Immortal so fast? What if we can’t prepare enough and are defeated by the tribulation?\" River asked in genuine shock. Pearl didn’t say anything but she clearly also shared his apprehensions.","Unfortunately for them, their concerns only made Cliff scoff.","\"What do you mean? I literally had to put a seal on my body to stop myself from reaching the immortal realm because the damn tribulation just kept wanting to show up otherwise. When I finally decided to undertake my tribulation, I did it while fighting hundreds of other immortals to use the tribulation to kill them. Now you’re telling me you’re afraid of taking the tribulation... alone?\"","Cliff gave River a look that very clearly made it obvious that he thought River was a pansy. River, on the other hand, stared at Cliff with his jaw hanging. The man’s claims were so obviously ridiculously fake and impossible that River couldn’t even understand why he thought that would work as bragging.","RIver opened his mouth to argue again but Cliff held up his hands.","\"Enough,\" he said, though this time his voice carried an authority Cliff hardly ever revealed. \"You are giving excuses for your failures before even trying. If this is your attitude in life, you will never go far, and I might as well put an end to our journey right now.","\"The task may be difficult, but it is never impossible. Yet if even the thought of the task itself is enough to halt your steps, then you are ill suited to the path of the paladins. In that case you should make yourself comfortable at your current cultivation level, and live out the rest of your life accepting that this is your limit. At least that way you won’t waste your time waiting for success to fall into your lap.\"","Cliff disappeared, leaving River and Pearl both stunned. For as long as they had known him, Cliff had always been a cheerful and usually relaxed person. No matter what obstacle they faced, he always treated it lightly, and often that was enough to give them the motivation to face it despite its difficulty.","This was the first time they had sensed any dissatisfaction from him. Was it because they weren’t willing to accept his deadline? Unlikely. They’d been working with his deadline for years, but he never expressed any dissatisfaction towards it. No, it seemed like he was upset that they let the difficulty of the task discourage them.","River, especially, felt shocked by the latest interaction because the paladin path was all he had. It was different from normal cultivation, but it was not without its benefits. He once thought that the Golden Core realm was entirely out of reach, and now he had even become a Nascent Soul cultivator. So how could this path be ill suited to him?","Wasn’t it normal to try to avoid impossible or suicidal tasks? Wouldn’t everyone try to do that? It was the logical thing to do.","Then again, the very act of cultivation was to raise oneself beyond the realm of their birth, which went against logic.","River and Pearl looked at each other, doubt in their eyes. They wouldn’t go on and take a life-threatening risk just because Cliff was upset. However, they were also aware that Cliff knew a whole lot more about cultivation than they did, and losing access to him would be a huge loss. To do that they would have to...","\"Did I really... am I a coward?\" River suddenly asked, interrupting Pearl’s thoughts.","Pearl paused, and looked at the sincerity on his face. This question seemed important to him.","\"What dangers have you not faced? When have you retreated in front of an enemy? If tomorrow an army of Immortals came to attack me, I have no doubt that they’d find you standing in front of me, holding both your shields. Cowardice cannot even be mentioned in the same sentence as you,\" she answered, speaking from her heart.","Upon hearing those words, River did not feel better, oddly enough. He shook his head.","\"So why did he look so disappointed?\" River asked, thinking about Cliff. When had he started caring so much about what Cliff thought? Even he himself had no answer to that. All he knew was that instead of afraid, he felt frustrated. Why had he resisted Cliff’s three year deadline? When had he led them astray? Never. So why, then, had River doubted him?","Was he really so afraid of the tribulation? Or had he been affected by the fear all those around him felt?","As he asked himself these questions, River strengthened his resolve. Whether he succeeded or not, he at least couldn’t accept failing before even trying.","In truth, River and Pearl were good students, and anyone would be proud to be their teacher. Yet Lex never officially recognized them as his students, only considering them temporary travel companions.","While much of it was because he didn’t want to form connections because he knew that in the future, whether in three years or later, he would have to leave them behind, there was another reason. It could only be said that comparison was the thief of joy.","While he had technically spent a whole lot more time training them than he had ever spent training Z, he could not help but think back to the time they shared. No matter how absurd or crazy Lex’s requests for him were, the kid never questioned him, and always lived up to his unreasonable demands.","While back then, most of the time Lex had only been trying to tease Z because it was fun to do, that didn’t change the fact that he always met the mark. Whether it was in the Inn, on the battlefield when the battalion was captured, or in Abaddon, or anywhere else.","In truth, River’s resistance to Lex’s unreasonable timelines and quests was completely normal. Unfortunately, in life in general, but especially in terms of cultivation, one could not achieve great success by being normal.","Lex closed his eyes. Three more years, and then one way or another he would leave. That was just enough time to finish the changes he was making to the necklace. After that, the necklace would develop an internal space that would be its own, independent space. Moreover, it would be incredibly stable.","While it could not be called a realm just yet, it was a first step."]},{"number":2315,"title":"Chapter 2315: Deadend","paragraphs":["\"You jinxed it,\" River said as he looked beyond the limits of the Guest House;s formation. \"You just had to- dammit, let me at least complain in peace!\"","The sound of River’s roaring was drowned out by the sound of hundreds of attacks smashing onto the Guest Houses protective formation, shaking the building’s very core.","A little over two years ago, during a shared, tender moment between River and Pearl, she’s said that if an army of immortals ever came for her, she’d fully expect to find that River would be there to protect her.","Well, as River looked out at the hellscape around their humble guest house, he could not help but recall what Cliff said about flags. He had explicitly stated that making analogies while referencing unrealistic, challenging situations was known as raising a flag. Once a flag was raised, they’d have to deal with the situation sooner or later.","At the time, River thought that it was yet another one of the strange and weird things he would occasionally say - especially since Cliff followed up that explanation by informing River that he did not, in fact, believe in flags.","Well, if flags weren’t real, what was going on outside their humble inn? The previous attack by an Immortal and some Nascent Soul cultivators had failed. They had questioned the Nascent Soul cultivators as well as the immortal, so they knew that no one else was aware of the attack. Theoretically, they were safe where they were.","However, the news about the attack must have leaked, or someone must have found out somehow, because this time a few dozen Immortals brought with them an entire army to attack. There should be no escaping this - at least in ordinary circumstances.","River shook his head, and then went down to the basement where Pearl, Karev and all the other workers were waiting for them. At this point, it was basically impossible to determine if any of the other workers had betrayed them and they weren’t really interested in finding out, so all the other workers were also restricted by the formation.","He ignored the rumbling of the formation as it experienced countless attacks and stepped onto the teleportation formation in the basement.","\"I’m telling you, trigger a tribulation and kill all your enemies with it,\" said Cliff for the hundredth time since they had been surrounded. \"It’s a very effective way of establishing dominance.\"","Neither River nor Pearl bothered to respond to him. Even if they had agreed to attempt to reach the Earth Immortal realm within three years, they weren’t crazy enough to listen to all of Cliff’s advice regardless of how wise he was generally.","The teleportation formation activated, undetected to any of the countless immortals outside. The reason was, naturally, because Cliff had told Pearl what to do. On her own, she could never have created a formation like that.","Once the teleportation ended, the workers were sent to a safe place away from them, while the three of them were sent to a safehouse that the young couple had established long ago.","\"On a serious note, though, whatever you guys do, Karev needs to undergo his tribulation. No matter how you hide, he will continue to attract more and stronger enemies regardless of his location.\"","Lex did not bother explaining to them about how carrying a greater destiny was a double edged sword. If he didn’t grow strong enough fast enough, the burden of his own destiny would kill him.","Fortunately, all three of them had planned to undergo their tribulations soon so that they could ascend to the Greater World together.","\"I’ve activated the formation’s self-destruction sequence. That should keep them off our trails for a while, and maybe even hurt them a little,\" said Pearl as she looked around their safehouse to make sure they were all fine.","\"It won’t work,\" said Cliff lamely. \"Since they’re making such a big move, your only option is to grow stronger, ascend to the next level, and find out exactly what is happening yourself. I recall the alliance paid close attention to the rules. Maybe once you’re in their domain again, they will give you protection again.\"","In truth, even within the Upper Battlefield, there were regions where the Alliance exerted its authority. In fact, the alliance was the one that was supposed to be stopping immortals from acting here which meant that either they were aware of what was happening and were supporting it, or someone had temporarily diverted their attention, keeping them from finding out.","Either way, growing stronger was the only option left to them.","Over the next few weeks, the group prepared, and then decided to undergo their tribulations altogether. They were not next to one another, but were in their own individual spaces that Pearl had prepared.","The reason that River was able to undertake the tribulation as well was because he had gained a special paladin inheritance when he had passed the test, while Pearl had gained special resources that strengthened her foundation and helped her reach her limits.","Everything started off just fine, with all three of them triggering the tribulation at the same time. The formations Pearl had prepared to protect them and hide their tribulations were also working just fine.","Unfortunately for them, none of that mattered, for their enemies were one step ahead of them.","Cliff, watching everything, just shook his head. He had told them to just kill all their enemies with the tribulation, but they wouldn’t listen. Now their enemies had set a trap for them all. As much as he could guide them on how to avoid Immortals, how could a few formations be entirely foolproof?","As the three tribulations were triggered, an army of death warriors charged towards them, not only to attack them, but also to increase the strength of the tribulations to force them into a dead end.","If these guys were motivated enough to provoke even the Oolin, then how could three humans escape so easily?","Lex stretched his legs and watched the show. Maybe, if he was feeling up to it, he would help. But if he did that, the tribulations would become even stronger due to his interference, so he would need to act outside the radius of the tribulations.","Well, he’d see how things went."]},{"number":2316,"title":"Chapter 2316: Joro realm","paragraphs":["The tribulations were... okay. Lex looked at the three tribulations and was both impressed and bored. He was impressed because River really stepped up. As a paladin, and the one in the group with the strongest defense, he really stepped up.","When he saw the swarm of death warriors, and the countless Immortals standing in the back, watching with a smirk, he knew it was up to him. Although he did not believe Cliff’s story of fighting hundreds of Immortals during his tribulation, at this moment that was exactly what he would have to do.","If only he knew that ’Cliff’ had been humble when telling that story, and hadn’t mentioned the fact that the tribulation was inside an area with highly volatile laws.","Lex was also bored because as soon as River stood up, and towards the death warriors and immortals, the immortals were frightened out of their minds! River barely managed to involve one immortal in his tribulation before the rest all escaped as far as possible.","Suffice to say, the very first bolt of lightning killed all the death warriors, and seriously hurt River as well. Fortunately, he was wearing Cliff’s necklace which helped him heal very quickly. At the same time, his paladin powers became stronger the more hurt he was, for he had embarked on a very special path even among paladins.","With his two shields, and his divine abilities, River barely managed to keep the immortal around long enough till the immortal was seriously hurt, and then forced to escape using desperate measures.","The other two went through their tribulations with varying levels of difficulty, but they managed to survive. It was only River that was basically a light breeze away from dying when the tribulation ended.","Since he was in no condition to pay attention to anything, he did not notice that towards the end, even his necklace bore the brunt of the tribulation. Lex did not make the tribulation easier for him. Instead, he just sent a bit of healing energy into his soul which kept his body and soul from being extinguished. Still, it wasn’t like Lex’s actions were foolproof.","He had only acted discreetly and with a fraction of his powers. Even that caused the necklace to be attacked by the tribulation - not to mention the strength of the tribulation increased in proportion to the help Lex gave.","The necklace itself was unharmed by the lightning, though Lex’s soul had to tolerate a bit of pain. It consumed a lot of his energy, but that was no longer the concern.","Once River successfully passed the tribulation and survived, the universe’s feedback came. His mortal body had been baptized by the lightning, slowly turning immortal, and the feedback helped him heal and complete his status as an Immortal. Unlike regular human immortals, he did not form a tenet. Instead, his paladin powers concentrated into the shape of a single tool which personified his path so far.","In his case, it was a shield. Of course, this shield was not a physical shield that he could summon. Instead, he could rely on its power and imbue other items with its might and power. Unlike ordinary human immortals, he could not manipulate all laws at will. Instead, his manipulation of laws was more focused towards existing paladin powers.","As the three concluded their tribulations, no elation filled them. Instead, they surveyed the surrounding area and came to the realization that their enemies were far stronger than they had ever imagined. Who was the one pulling the strings behind the scenes? They did not know.","They exchanged glances, Pearl and Karev both awestruck at what River had achieved. He had literally saved both their lives by almost sacrificing his own.","Before any of them could speak, however, the sound of clapping echoed through the lands as the air rippled and a team of Immortals walked through. The one leading them was of the Celestial race, though obviously the three of them could not have known that. Only Lex realized as much.","\"I am impressed,\" said the Celestial as he observed River closely. \"According to the reports it’s your ancestor who’s remarkable, but I see you don’t fall short either.\"","For some reason, the Celestial was unable to tell that it was actually Pearl, not River, who was Karev’s descendant. His understanding of the situation was based on the stories that had spread of River across these lands.","\"I commend you for your bravery,\" he said as he turned to look at the devastation left behind by his tribulation. \"If you hadn’t acted as such, I would not have noticed the anomalous tribulation, and I would have remained ignorant of what is happening here. I promise you, the perpetrators behind these actions will get what’s coming to them - and much sooner than you think.\"","River let loose a sigh of relief as he realized that this new immortal in front of him - the one who had an aura much stronger than any River had felt before - was not his enemy.","\"You don’t need to worry about any of that anymore. Now that I have personally taken note of this issue, it will come to a swift end. Instead, you should say your farewells and handle any remaining business you may have in these lands. I will personally escort you all out of this realm.\"","Lex raised an eyebrow. Now that was a twist he didn’t see coming. River and Pearl hadn’t seemed to realize the issue, but Karev did.","\"We won’t be going to the Greater World?\" he asked, looking towards the Celestial with a cautious expression.","The Celestial shook his head.","\"If you were immortals of any other humanoid race, that’s where you would go. But humans... no, humanity itself is going through a massive change. The Humanoid Alliance has fought hard to present this opportunity to humanity, but it is only the members of your own race who can grasp this opportunity.","\"You all will be going to the Joro realm, one of the three Major realms still harboring undiscovered human legacies. Besides the Joro realm, the Humanoid Alliance has also attacked the Tyranum realm, and the Geb realm. There, you will contribute to the war, and hopefully gain the chance to inherit one of the old Daos of humanity, and change the fate of your race!\""]},{"number":2317,"title":"Chapter 2317: Respect and reverence","paragraphs":["Everything that followed was a blur. The trio left behind the Upper Battlefield, and were brought to a massive city in the Greater World where they were allowed to get accustomed to their powers, and were taught the basics and general knowledge affiliated with being an immortal.","In the few days that took, the Celestial Immortal, as promised, caught everyone involved in targeting Karev. It all happened so easily that it felt like a dream. The whole thing was, apparently, planned by a group of influential immortals.","The group consisted of elves, dwarves and even angels. Up until now, River and Pearl had never encountered any angels, because low level angels all resided in Eden. Only at the Immortal level did they start to spread out across the universe.","Not only were they all captured, they were executed publicly! It was less about getting justice for Karev and Pearl’s family, and more about how they broke the rules of the alliance, but the result was the same!","Up until the very end, Karev could not believe how easily the situation had been resolved. Was that really it?","Of course not. Lex did not need to put any effort at all to see that a few people had escaped getting caught as a result of their background and influence. The few immortals of this group, while guilty, also served as convenient scapegoats for some others.","The Humanoid Alliance was not nearly as just or clean as they had presented themselves to be to Lex, not that he cared about this either way. Now that this matter had attracted the attention of the Celestials, all the games would disappear.","Whether it was the elves, the dwarves, the vampires, the Oolin, or whoever. Once they stepped in front of a Celestial, all they showed was the utmost deference and obedience. As the de facto leaders of the Humanoid Alliance, their might could not be questioned.","The more and more that River and Pearl were exposed to such an environment, the more that they naturally began to revere the Celestials as well. It was inevitable. After all, they were a mere Vassal race, looking up to the very peak of a Noble race.","There were even rumors that the Celestials had what it took to become an Elder race, but purposefully avoided adopting that mantle.","Lex only shook his hands.","\"Respect others, but there is no need to push it to reverence or worship,\" Cliff’s voice rang in Pearl’s and River’s ears. \"Respect the strong, but do not automatically become subservient. Protect your hearts from viewing yourselves as below them, or that is what you will become.\"","For reasons they couldn’t understand, his words suddenly woke them up, and made them feel as if a certain veil had been removed.","They couldn’t understand what it was, but Lex knew. It was the natural effect being very high up on the Cosmic Ascendance Spectrum had on those far down below.","Once all those breaking the Alliance’s rules were punished, the three of them were sent to Joro, as promised. But things were very different from before.","Though they were immortals, and though they had not been conscripted into an army, they had to follow the alliance’s directions. As humans, they had no choice but to go to Joro. Over there, they would have some extent of freedom, but they had to obey the rules of the alliance, and so basically to do anything at all, they would need to first contribute to the alliance’s efforts with that ongoing war.","At this level, the conspiracies became too complex for Lex to see through at a glance. He could not differentiate whether this was genuinely meant to help humans, or if the alliance had some ulterior motives in play. It did not matter.","River and Pearl could not help but wonder just how strong Cliff really was. They were now immortals and were beginning to realize that... even now, they could not even glimpse at the extent of his power. They did not have even an ounce of his insight and knowledge.","Thus, it was in the midst of all that confusion that they arrived in the Joro realm. More specifically, they arrived in a certain portion of the Joro realm where the Humanoid Alliance had carved out a battlefield for Earth Immortals.","The flow of time here was ten times faster than a Major realm. The resources here were abundant, and more importantly, there seemed to be ancient human legacies here that could only be discovered and unlocked by humans. These legacies, apparently, were all at the Dao level!","The new rulers of the realm, the Gon race, did not take kindly to that news and were fighting furiously to find out why they hadn’t been able to discover these legacies before.","As River, Pearl, and Karev arrived at their destination, they were amazed at the scale of the city, and of the fight. There were billions of Earth Immortals in front of them - something they couldn’t properly even fathom.","The cities, the forts, the armies, they were all on a scale that the trio could not come to terms with so quickly. Yet the young couple’s shock was interrupted by a familiar stream of information. Cliff had handed out a new list of quests, and just as before, offered many rewards.","The difference was that this time, alongside techniques, he even offered insight into the various laws. River and Pearl could not understand just what was happening.","They had only recently been exposed to how grand laws were, and they could not even properly manipulate a single law!","Like most normal humans, they would most likely focus on a single law and spend the next many centuries simply learning how to manipulate that properly and effectively. Unfortunately, Lex wasn’t interested in waiting that long.","\"I’ll give you fifty years to reach the Heaven Immortal realm,\" said Cliff, but then paused for a minute as he did the math. Fifty years would be equal to five years in a normal Major realm. He could afford to wait a little more.","\"Okay, never mind. I’ll give you sixty years to reach the Heaven Immortal realm, otherwise... well, by now I’m sure you know how this works.\"","One of the reasons he gave them so much time was because he could tell just how many valuable resources were available here. The journey to getting his revenge could finally begin properly in this place."]},{"number":2318,"title":"Chapter 2318: Dead man walking","paragraphs":["\"Are you sure you’re an Earth Immortal?\" asked the slave standing behind Z, watching in horror at the destruction he had wrought.","Before them was a scene of utter destruction and devastation. Before this, whenever they fought other immortals, they would only get victory or defeat. Never had they experienced the feeling of overwhelming domination. Now, having tasted such a victory for themselves, they felt no elation. Instead, they felt only fear.","Whoever this new slave was, he was not of an ordinary background - he could not be. For someone like him to join their slave army, it could mean only a few things, but all of those things ended with the rest of the slaves dead. Whether to hide the secret of Z’s participation, or because they were about to face greater foes, or because...","The watching slaves could not finish the thought. The only watched as Z turned around silently, yanking at the purple collar around his neck as if he was loosening a tie. Since they were slaves, and they were fighting a war, they were naturally chained.","Yet these chains and collars were far from normal. They gave the... they gave the Grand Conqueror full control over the slaves, allowing him to freeze or even cripple any one of the slaves with a single thought. But was that all? Far from it.","He could hear every thought that any of the slaves had, he could tell every intention that they harbored, and he could program the collar to react to certain conditions. For example, feeling even the slightest hint of anger or hate towards the Grand Conqueror would cause the collar to send paralysing, debilitating pain coursing through the slaves body regardless of the situation they were in.","If that happened in the middle of a fight, it was a death sentence.","The reasoning was pretty simple. The collars would either condition the slaves into being obedient, or it would dispose of them! Yet even death was not an escape, for once someone died wearing the collar, the collar would absorb the soul, waiting for the Grand Conqueror to collect.","Rumor had it that he tortured the souls to extract some kind of unique energy from them. But it was just a rumor - the slaves dared not verify it, because they’d probably have to do that with their souls!","\"Of course I’m just an Earth Immortal,\" Z answered with a comforting smile, as if he wasn’t bothered by his situation at all. He had adapted surprisingly quickly, but it was clear that he hadn’t been subdued by the collar. Rather, he had extreme self control, and had managed to learn the rules of the place and gone along.","Yes, he had an initial bout of resistance, but that hadn’t lasted long.","The slave speaking to Z was about to speak again when he felt it - that familiar command from the collar telling him to kneel for the Grand Conqueror was coming!","Without any hesitation he kneeled, just in time for the Grand Conqueror to arrive, alongside his ever present entourage. Naturally they ignored everyone and went to Z. Before speaking a single word, one of the Grand Conqueror’s followers raised a large mace and slammed it across Z’s face, throwing him to the ground, his face bleeding.","\"From now on, you will fight exclusively using weapons,\" spoke the Grand Conqueror, looking down at Z with indifference in his eyes. \"You will use a different weapon in each battle, as well as the exclusive fighting techniques of King Zarek. Every time you return from battle without establishing a resonance with King Zarek’s lost legacy, you will be whipped, so better get at it quick.\"","The Grand Conqueror stared at Z a little longer, and could not help but remember his time in the Midnight Inn. Back then he hated it so much - hated all the lost potential that the Inn was wasting catering to guests instead of conquering lands and growing stronger.","Now, he stood above one of the most famous members of the Inn, and he could not help but feel like it was pathetic. He still dared not confront the Inn himself - he could not fight a Dao Lord. But he also no longer cared to do so.","Back then, he had hated the Inn because he himself was weak, and he took out his self hatred on the Inn. Ever since he received the Grand Conquest System, and subsequently conquered the starting realm, he no longer thought about others. Instead, he only focused on his own goals.","An unexpected benefit was that the starting realm, which he now ruled, had a flow of time considerably faster than most Mature realms. The drawback was that it peaked at the Heaven Immortal realm.","After leaving, he had already begun his conquest by attacking many other, smaller realms, and had also successfully broken through to the Celestial Immortal realm. He was slowly planting the seed of the empire that he would one day build, and hating the Midnight Inn served no purpose in pursuit of that goal.","Of course, when someone from the Humanoid Alliance came to him to work together against the Midnight Inn, he did not reject it either. On one hand, it was an opportunity to build an alliance with a stronger entity. On the other hand, it was the Humanoid Alliance itself who was responsible for keeping the Innkeeper from locating them, so he was playing a small part.","Besides, his role in this whole thing was quite small. He only needed to set the vessel on the right path.","As for the vessel...","He looked down at Z, whose name was no longer important.","\"Oh, and you have ten years to become a Heaven Immortal. You don’t want to find out what will happen if you fail,\" he said, and then walked away, stepping on Z’s head as he did.","Throughout this entire exchange, Z felt not the slightest bit of anger towards the Grand Conqueror. He only felt the same exhaustion he felt when Lex used to give him extra work back at the Inn, as if he was reluctant to do any extra work.","After all, why should he feel any anger towards a dead man walking? His fate was sealed, he just didn’t know it yet."]},{"number":2319,"title":"Chapter 2319: Unleashing the Daddy","paragraphs":["Within Arch-Heaven, millions of beings had their sights fixed on the massive, crystal dome which had trapped countless Dao Lords. They watched, and often enough, reported what they saw. Updates on the trapped Dao Lords were very important to most forces in the universe.","In comparison, the Dao Lords within the dome had established very clear rules for each other. They had established their own territories within the dome, and remained there. None of the Dao Lords interacted with each other, and instead worked independently to either find a way out, or to secure themselves within their territory.","Trust was in a great deficit at the moment, and the uncertainty of the situation was forcing everyone to act extremely cautiously.","It was at this time that the countless forces observing the dome noticed a change. To be specific, nothing inside the dome had changed, but something outside.","Someone was approaching the dome, as if to investigate. This was not the first time something like this had happened, yet it still attracted sufficient attention and wariness.","The figure was wearing a hooded cloak, making their identity hard to determine at first. Yet soon enough, someone realized that the hood was a normal piece of clothing, and it did not hide or inhibit the appearance from being seen.","Underneath the hood was a pale crone, her straight, long black hair hiding her face from view, but not her skin. If she were to be a human, the extent of her paleness would make her appear like a corpse.","Yet this was not an undead, nor was this a humanoid. Instead, this was one of the rare races that had an unusually similar appearance to humanoids without actually having any relation. For some reason, no one mistook her for a humanoid race either. Maybe just how unusual she appeared... or maybe it was the aura of a Sage race around her that gave her identity away.","\"A Weaver,\" someone whispered, realizing who this was.","Like most Sage races, very little was publicly known about Weavers besides their appearance. The only thing most rumors seemed to have in common was that Wevers were the best diviners and oracles in the universe. Although, some people often claimed that this was a misinterpretation of their powers, for their actual strength lay in reading the flow of destiny rather than divining the future.","The Weaver ignored the whispering crowd, and instead approached the dome cautiously, avoiding triggering any of Arch-Heaven’s traps. When she placed her hand on the dome, finally, she began reading the flow of destiny, only to realize almost immediately something was amiss.","\"No!\" she shrieked as she tried to retreat, but it was too late. Her body exploded into a cloud of white, harmless mist, blanketing the entire region, including the observing crowd.","\"Is this... Dao Mist?\" someone asked in shock, unable to process what such a thing meant.","After all, the only plausible explanation was that the Weaver they had seen was actually a Dao Lord. She had discovered something unexpected and terrible about the dome, but before she could reveal it, she died. It did not even take one second, and she died. A Sage Dao Lord died in an instant, without being able to put up any resistance at all whatsoever.","What could such a thing mean? No one had any idea, but this was the first public death of a Dao Lord since the universal war had started.","Since the first domino had fallen, more would inevitably follow. The universe was now, officially, no longer safe even for Dao Lords.","The news spread like an unstoppable tsunami as the many forces of the universe prepared themselves. Many of them especially focused on the Weavers to see what kind of reaction they would have.","That was, awkwardly, when most forces realized that they had no idea where the Weavers resided. No one even knew the name of whichever realm they may reside in. Perhaps only a select few across the universe were privy to that knowledge.","*****","It took three years for Jack to reach the edge of the Folklore realm. Those were three years according to the flow of time in a Major realm. Surprisingly, those three years were quite uneventful, mainly because they were escorted personally by Dao Lords.","After the Henali screwed up business inside the Midnight Inn, their guilty conscience forced them to take any task related to the Innkeeper very seriously, which is why Jack and the rest received the very best treatment. Of course, no one officially told them the reason for why they were getting such a treatment, nor was the situation with Z revealed to any from the pirate crew.","The Henali had tried to search for Z, but someone was actively interfering in search attempts regarding him, and they could not determine who it was. They also couldn’t make any progress finding him.","It was as if the enemy was intimately familiar with the Henali, and knew exactly how to block their search.","Jack and the crew knew nothing about that, and with a Dao Lord keeping watch, even Bob wasn’t able to cause any problems. Thus, the crew spent these three years relaxing and upgrading their cultivation.","Jack, especially, made tremendous progress. Although placing his identity as a fairy in his back allowed Jack to cultivate beyond the Earth Immortal realm, he still needed an appropriate cultivation path to progress through levels. He decided to use the Paladin path for that, and was making great progress.","He did not even need to do any special tasks to fulfil his existing oaths. He’d already done so much that as long as he properly digested the gains, and converted them using paladin cultivation practices, he’d be pushed to the edge of the Earth Immortal realm.","Today was special, though. Today he would not cultivate, for today was the day he and his crew returned to the Folklore realm.","The Henali did not enter the realm, but escorted the crew to the very edge of the realm, and allowed them to enter through a proper, legal channel in the system’s boundary. Since their history with the realm was rich, they faced no problems and entered easily.","Instantly, the Jolly Rancher arrived at the side of a serene mountain, on a seemingly very peaceful day, with nothing going amiss.","The crew actually had quite a lot they wanted to do inside the Folklore realm, but Jack first had to start on his master plan to cause major havoc across the universe and speed up the Nexus event.","Jack brought out the black piece of cloth that was wrapped around his secret weapon, and very carefully opened it. After a few moments, the contents were revealed to not only the eyes of the crew, but to the laws of the Folklore itself.","One could say that in front of Jack lay a book, much in the way someone could own a mountain of gold and say they were above the poverty line.","Slowly, gently, carefully, he brushed his fingers over the cover as he read the title of the book.","The book was simply called Ultimate King Emperor: All the Gods call me Daddy!","\"Find the nearest city,\" Jack whispered his command. \"We need to get this copied, and spread it as far and wide as possible.\"","Once the contents of the story were spread in the realm, the laws of the realm would do the rest of the work. Jack actually felt slightly frightened at what he was unleashing onto the universe, but desperate times called for desperate measures.","Rose, the newest member of the crew, and the Trelop with the unusual mutation, watched the captain act a little strangely, but did not put much thought into it. She had heard that many of the crew members were from the Folklore realm, so it made sense that they were emotional upon their return.","Bob, with his newest baguette weapon resting upon his shoulders, looked at the captain with wonder in his eyes.","\"So much chaos emanates from the captain’s every move. If only others were as fortunate as I to see the truth behind his actions, they would weep with jubilation. Oh what joy to follow the footsteps of one as bold as he.\"","The boblings in the back trembled with excitement to hear Bob speak as such, but the rest quickly distanced themselves from the Drama-cat. Without a divine wine cork to keep him quiet, staying with Bob was like sleeping next to a nuclear bomb. Technically, it would not kill you, until everything went wrong and then nothing could save you.","The Jolly Rancher opened its sails and took to the skies, once again gracing the Folklore realm with the sight of its majestic flight. As for the consequences of this flight, only time itself could reveal.","\"Longbeard, I want you to finish reading this book before we reach the town. After that, you’ll be responsible for retelling the story in all nearby inns and taverns.\""]},{"number":2320,"title":"Chapter 2320: King Khalid","paragraphs":["\"I finally did it,\" said Pearl as she looked at the crystal burning in front of her, a deeply exhausted expression on her face.","How many years had it been since they arrived in Joro? She wasn’t quite sure, but it had been a few decades. She had entirely given up hope of achieving Cliff’s most recent demand because she had not even reached the second level of the Earth Immortal realm, let alone the Heaven Immortal realm.","In fact, after all these decades, she had finally achieved sufficient mastery over magma flames to be able to manipulate the associated laws to work inflammable objects. Now, she could use anything she wished as fuel for her fire.","Although this seemed pathetically simple, it had taken her all these years of effort to learn how to manipulate laws enough to be able to do that. This was in the context of the fact that she had only focused on that one, single law all this time, and had not bothered with other laws at all. Only then could she achieve as much.","Cliff seemed genuinely confused at her slow progress, at least as far as she could tell. However, when she talked to other immortals, her speed seemed terrific. Many of them took a century or two before gaining control of a single law, and went thousands of years before they could effectively use the law for combat. To use only a couple of decades for that seemed like she was going incredibly fast.","She would have almost believed that Cliff’s expectations were unreal, if only it weren’t for her ancestor, Karev. During this time, not only had he mastered five laws, he had even learned to use a simple Lawcraft.","Of course, that Lawcraft was something Pearl redeemed from Cliff for her ancestor. Cliff had then come up with an ingenious way to send the information to Karev without arousing suspicion, making Karev think that he had an epiphany on his own.","Compared to him, her progress was nonexistent. Still, even he was slow by Cliff’s standards, and no amount of redeemed help could change the fundamental flaw of how slow she learned.","In comparison, River was doing very well these days. In fact, River and Karev had become the main fighting force of their group. Karev had amazing talent, and River didn’t need to learn law manipulation in the way that they did. In fact, he had a limited number of abilities he could learn, and all he could do was improve them.","There were other, secret paladin arts which could increase the number of abilities River could display, but even Cliff himself did not know them. The few that he had learned were through the inheritance that Karev had.","Since they had reached a new realm, they could naturally take the inheritance again. Since they were going again, Lex tested his theory that the inheritence might be related to the Temple of Fasting by employing the Masterless technique.","It worked. The place seemed to respond to the presence of the technique, and he was granted entry, though the reward for the test seemed less significant somehow. He simply got ahold of some valuable resources in the form of other inks similar to Silver Ink. It wasn’t like he was complaining - that was exactly what he needed.","The past few decades, Lex had not only improved his necklace by a large amount, he had begun to use the ink he’d gotten to begin to inscribe some basic functions into the necklace itself. Since the most important thing for the necklace, at the moment, was having an infinite energy source, he approached the issue from a few angles.","The first was by manufacturing the trait into the necklace, allowing it to absorb energy from the Void. However, using the ink, he wanted to add more features into the necklace, such as absorbing energy from any law that touched the necklace. He also wanted to strengthen the space within the necklace to an absurd extent.","Fortunately, he was adept in the laws of space, not to mention in treasure forging, so that was a very easily accomplished task for him.","While he did all of these things, he paid close attention to River, Pearl, Karev, and even the rest of the universe. The situation in the Joro realm was chaotic, but everyday the human race was making some progress.","The Alliance was a mixed bag, mainly because of how many different races were a part of it. When they focused on their task, though, then they could really deliver. Almost on a weekly basis, they could hear stories of discovered legacies and gained opportunities.","Once, even someone they personally knew gained a tremendous opportunity left behind by a longdead human immortal, and reached the Heaven Immortal realm in less than ten years!","The war to suppress the humans was being fought, but because most of the pressure was on the Angels, the humans had found themselves a short time span within which they could try to gain whatever advantage they could.","As a result, the human race’s position on the Cosmic Ascendance Spectrum rose nearly every few weeks.","This was something that genuinely impressed Lex to the point where he even considered trying to search for these legacies himself. But these things could not be sought out, they could only be discovered coincidentally, or if someone resonated with them. If it was easy to find them, then these legacies would have been discovered long ago.","No one actually knew how to find them, they were just doing their best and hoping for a reaction. These three realms were apparently realms that the human race used to control once upon a time, which is why the chances of legacies existing here was the highest. For all anyone knew, the greatest legacies were hidden elsewhere.","From time to time, stories would emerge of someone or the other who managed to gain a tremendous opportunity, and then gained the Humanoid Alliance’s protection.","One such story was of some guy who called himself Grand Conqueror who was operating in the Geb realm. Apparently, he had discovered a legacy belonging to one of the original human kings. More specifically, he had discovered the legacy of King Khalid, who was known as the greatest human general to have ever lived.","It was said that the Humanoid Alliance had taken him into the alliance, protecting him and nurturing him as one of the potential key figures for the revival of humanity itself.","There were many other prominent examples, and it was even said that many other races were getting involved in this. For example, the Henali were also apparently playing a big role in this.","They had brought many humans over, and were focused mainly on the Tyranum realm. It was said that instead of focusing on the legacy of the original kings, the Henali were searching for the legacy of the Sephore family.","If that was the case, Lex was sure that Jotun, and his other ancestors had come to that realm, not to mention Alexander and the rest. He wondered if the Henali had tried to recruit some of the Inn workers into participating.","Maybe if Z showed up, he would be able to find the legacy of Zarek.","But, as far as Lex was concerned, there was no need for them to stand out like that. What they lacked were not legacies, but time. As long as they laid low and kept cultivating within the Inn, they’d all reach the peak anyway.","He was also using this time to get the young couple to find him more resources, while he himself was planning for what to do. His time with them would come to an end, and at that point he’d need to move on his own. He couldn’t keep staying with them because the Earth Immortal area had very limited resources that he needed. He would have to go to higher levels to find what he needed.","It was during this time that he was planning for the future that the coin he’d received from Karev’s legacy began to tremble. It was pointing towards something, as if it had been activated by something.","Lex paused, and then considered this coin. He had been unable to discern anything of value from it at all, but his instincts had told him that it was important to him. Now that it had gone from an inert to active state, he could even sense a strange aura from it.","For reasons he couldn’t quite understand, the aura felt oddly similar to the Axis Eternum of the Origin realm - or at least the ticket given to him by the Governor of the Origin realm. The ticket had read Glaticus Necropolis, and apparently had the aura of the Origin realms Axis Eternum.","Since the aura from this coin was oddly similar to that, did that mean it was related to the Axis Eternum of the Joro realm? How interesting.","If that was the case...","Cliff appeared in front of Pearl after a long, long time and gave her an all too familiar look.","\"Are you interested in a special quest? Who knows, this one might even solve all your recent problems.\""]},{"number":2321,"title":"Chapter 2321: A humble perspective","paragraphs":["Pearl almost laughed at Cliff’s claim. Lately, other than feeling helpless at the slow pace of her progress, she’d also been feeling somewhat empty. Previously, she’d felt numb. Once that numbness had gone, she felt rage. She wanted revenge on those that killed her family and tried to hunt her down.","Then, apparently, all those responsible were killed in public executions. Pearl saw them herself. Even so, she felt empty and unfulfilled. The enemy was gone, but her family had not returned. River and her were together, but it seemed like she had nothing to look forward to anymore.","What was she working hard for? Why did she want to get stronger? These were questions she had no answer to.","In truth, Lex could easily see through her mental barriers, and even understand why they existed. He could have given her a pep talk of some kind, but he’d avoided it. Even now, he wanted to witness how they worked through this problem themselves.","Although it might have seemed pointless to many, Lex’s journey with River and Pearl had given him a different perspective on the struggles of common humans. Even if he claimed that he could rise to his current level because of his own hard work, he had to at least admit that without the help and resources of his system, he would not have gotten so far so fast.","Even with his help, giving River and Pearl the best cultivation techniques and shortcuts, their progress speed was only mediocre by his standards. Any random worker inside the Midnight Inn cultivated faster than these two.","Was it because these two were lazy or lacking in talent? No, it was because the resources available inside the Midnight Inn were just too unique, even across the whole universe. Even the Temple of Fasting, which was the foremost training grounds for humanity in the universe, could only train and teach his workers. The resources it gave were in no way comparable to even the very air of the Midnight Inn!","Thus, through witnessing their struggles, Lex got a better understanding of the standard human experience. He’d always interacted with the very best the universe had to offer. He always met kings and leaders, or the heads of powerful organisations. The humans he encountered were the best of the best.","Was Jotun ordinary? Was King Cornelius someone who could be compared to others? Even weaker people he usually met were extraordinary geniuses, such as Alexander, Rafael and Marlo. Although he ran an Inn that catered to everyone, his understanding of the typical struggles and experiences were lacking.","River and Pearl, despite having so many benefits, were standard examples of that. Without his help or guidance, they would have died long ago. Even if they barely survived, they were too deeply embroiled in too many conspiracies.","Even when they achieved their goals and gained power, they were still not free to make their own decisions. The reason the two had not realized it was because from the moment of their birth, they had been indoctrinated to be vassals. They felt it was completely normal that the Humanoid Alliance dictate which realm they’d be stationed in, what tasks they were allowed to do, and how they could behave.","In fact, many times already River and Karev had supported the alliance during their missions and operations. They felt it was completely normal to cooperate with the alliance - especially when they were getting paid or compensated for their work. To them, it seemed like they were the ones benefiting since they could get the resources, or the treasures that they required.","Despite Lex’s efforts to guide them, they lacked that innate resistance to being controlled, and lacked the arrogance to face off against those stronger or superior to themselves. He tried many times to teach them respect but not reverence towards Celestials, yet it was impossible. The more they saw how powerful the Celestials were, and how afraid the other Noble races were towards them, the more they themselves began to become subservient towards them.","This was something Lex lacked - even when he had been trying to avoid those stronger than himself to save the Inn from destruction, he had never been completely cowed by them. This was not the effect of the system’s resources or his cultivation techniques - it was something innate in him. The system and its resources merely fast tracked his progress.","In short, through the actions and experiences of River and Pearl, he could see an alternate life and path that he may have needed to go through if he hadn’t found the system.","Compared to them, Karev was more like those Lex usually met with. Even if he didn’t have anyone holding his hand and helping him across every obstacle, he was resourceful enough to make it through. He obeyed the Celestials, but was never subservient.","In fact, he was the only one who suspected that the enemies who had targeted him previously may still be alive. It only made sense. As a proper cultivator of the True Path, his instincts about these things were strong, which is why he could detect certain flaws and inconsistencies in the stories they were told.","These thoughts flashed through Lex’s mind in an instant as he watched the struggle on Pearl’s face. If he were in her shoes, he would try to get stronger so that he could break free of the cycle of others informing him or telling him that the situation had been handled. The constant control that the alliance exerted on their life would be suffocating to him.","But since Pearl had been experiencing it from birth, she found it to be completely normal that they did such things. In fact, she could not even come up with the thought of one day being so powerful that she would no longer be under the umbrella of the alliance. Instead, to her, the alliance was a behemoth existence that would always remain a part of her life.","There wasn’t anything specifically wrong with that. Everyone had their own goals and pursuits. It was just that since Lex had witnessed the various levels of the alliance, he had seen the result of its haphazard structure.","With multiple races working together at various levels, there were varying levels of corruption and effectiveness, simply because each of them had their own goals. While the Celestial race appeared to be the controlling and guiding hand, trying to keep the alliance pure, there was only so much oversight that they could exert.","As he thought about that, Lex had a new idea. He wouldn’t try to enforce it, but... he could at least present it as a possibility to Pearl.","\"Okay, forget about the quest for a moment,\" Cliff said, seeing how conflicted Pearl was at the moment. \"Instead, tell me this: have you ever thought about your future? About what you want to do moving forward? Have you ever considered your past experiences, and what you can learn from them?\"","Pearl looked stunned and confused. This was... very unlike Cliff, who usually left them to their own devices. Still, she wouldn’t reject his insight if he was offering it."]},{"number":2322,"title":"Chapter 2322: Mom’s spaghetti","paragraphs":["\"My future... looks very empty to me,\" Pearl said after a long silence. She did not usually show a defeated or exhausted expression in front of others. Only River, who was the one she relied on the most, and Cliff, who had been a teacher and guiding hand throughout her life could see this side of her.","Although she could see that Cliff still kept a distance from the both of them, that did not change that he had been silently helping them for most of their lives!","\"What about your past?\" Cliff asked, seeing that she was feeling dejected. Something like this was actually quite dangerous. Immortals did not easily develop mental issues, but once they did they were harder to relieve than issues for mortals. Yet if these issues were not addressed, they would sooner or later develop into a Heart Demon.","Truly the cultivation path for ordinary humans was quite difficult, and filled with unexpected pitfalls. Not everyone had the temperament and capacity to walk through it.","\"My past? I seem to have had a wonderful past,\" she said, though she had a sad smile on her face. \"I’ve adventured and explored the lands with River. I’ve had unique experiences others can’t even imagine. I’ve overcome countless obstacles. And yet... I can’t bear to think about the past because it fills me with so much sadness.","\"I keep thinking about... what my parents would think and feel if they could have seen me today. From looking up to Golden Core cultivators as unreachable existences, all the way to becoming an immortal, I have come far. Yet even immortals cannot bring the dead back to life. Even an infinite lifespan cannot replicate the simple pleasure of being woken up by my mother early in the morning with a hot breakfast ready. Even...\"","She stopped speaking, and then shook her head while she sighed. There was no point in dwelling on it.","Cliff nodded, as if he understood. Then he offered her a different perspective.","\"You came from the Land of a Hundred Rivers. It’s been at war for as long as you can remember. Countless mortals die every hour of every day. Tell me, if you went there now, with the power you have, could you not change that? Could you not end that war with a single wave of your hand?\"","Pearl was stunned. She’d never thought about that. But then she realized that there was a flaw in that thought.","\"I might be able to, but the orcs probably have immortals as well. You remember the Watcher in the Land of a Hundred Rivers? I didn’t realize it then, but he was no doubt an Earth Immortal, which means that even an Earth Immortal cannot change the situation there\" she said, and Cliff only nodded.","\"You’re right,\" he said, but then continued to talk. \"Actually, what even is the worth of a single Earth Immortal when you’re looking at the big picture? There were hundreds, if not thousands of territories like the Land of a Hundred Rivers.","\"That means billions if not trillions of people all under the alliance’s oversight. Even if each territory has one immortal watching over them, how can they protect everyone? That would explain why certain people were able to break the alliance’s laws without getting caught.\"","Listening to his words, Pearl felt even more pathetic. She had felt proud about her achievement of becoming an Earth Immortal, but what was the worth of an Earth Immortal really? Just that much. They were just another cog in the machine.","\"Most of these immortals watching over these territories are from Noble races, right?\" Cliff continued to ask. \"What would they even know about the experiences of someone from a Vassal race such as yourself? They probably don’t even register what you consider an injustice as something out of the ordinary. Their perspective is limited by their own experiences. What would they even know about the struggles of vassals?\"","He looked at her, and saw that his words seemed to irritate and provoke her. She felt despondent, and at the same time, she felt unresigned.","Yes, there was so much corruption, but what could a mere Earth Immortal do about it? The Nobles lacked perspective, so even if they weren’t corrupt, could they even understand the needs and predicament of the vassals?","Was the alliance doing a poor job? Not really. They had created a system that allowed so many to survive and grow, but could they be blamed if there were minor flaws or gaps in their management? That was simply the result of having such a large setup.","There were so many people struggling, just like she had. But she was lucky enough to have River for support, and for Cliff to guide her. What did the others have? Nothing.","As her thoughts reached that point, she looked up at Cliff with questions in her eyes. She did not necessarily need an answer - even some direction would be good enough.","\"A mere Earth Immortal really isn’t enough to change or affect anything,\" Cliff said as he looked at her. \"But what if you were stronger? What if your voice in the alliance held sway? From the start of your journey until now, you have relied on my help to overcome obstacles. Yet have you never considered helping others as well, just as I helped you? What if you can save even one person, even just one family from the same experiences as you? What if you can improve the alliance so that... it no longer has the flaws you had to suffer through?\"","This was the idea Lex came up with. Since Pearl and River could not conceive a reality where they were not apart from the alliance, why couldn’t they be made to join it, and affect it from within?","Why couldn’t they take control, or at the very least affect the alliance themselves as a goal? It was an impossible goal, honestly. But for as long as Cliff had been with them, he had taught Pearl and River one simple thing: impossibility did not actually exist. Everything was possible - it was just that the right method of achieving something may not yet have been discovered.","Pearl really couldn’t imagine a reality where she became strong enough to affect the alliance. It was just so... big, and its leaders held power she could not even fathom. Yet once upon a time, she could not have even fathomed reaching the immortal realm - something she had already accomplished.","Cliff’s words were right. Maybe she could not get her revenge, but couldn’t she stop similar events from ever occurring again?","Gloom and sorrow had begun to fill her life lately, but a small fire was suddenly lit in her heart, pushing back the descending darkness. Now whether she could nurture that small flame into a flaming inferno was entirely up to her.","\"I’m going to ask you one more time,\" said Cliff, his signature smile now taking on a whole new meaning in her eyes. \"Are you interested in a special quest? One that might change your future forever!\"","The words rang like thunder in Pearl’s ears, alerting her to the fact that this might be her one shot, her one opportunity. She could either seize it, or let it slip."]},{"number":2323,"title":"Chapter 2323: The clues were right there","paragraphs":["Pearl asked Cliff if they should leave behind Karev for this mission, but he let the old man come. It wasn’t just because he was the strongest of the three, but because that bit of destiny he carried on him could be a great asset.","Regardless, if Lex’s suspicions about the key were correct, then he would definitely have to make a move this time around. Thus, the actual strength of the three became somewhat irrelevant. At most, they would need to focus on keeping themselves safe if things escalated too much.","Lex summoned the coin and looked at it once more, studying it carefully as he did.","This was a random coin he got from within Karev’s heritage, but it was suddenly giving off an aura similar to the only Axis Eternum he’d ever known.","Before heading straight towards where the coin was pointing, however, Lex needed to take many precautions. Even if this portion of the realm had been carved into a separate battlefield by the Humanoid Alliance, it was a fact that this was a Major realm controlled by the Gon race.","Not only could there be enemies at the location, there was even a possibility of Dao Lords being present. He had to act carefully.","Lex tested how much power he could use. The theory was that he could use his full strength even in this form, but in practice that was far from the case. The structure of the necklace did not exactly facilitate multitasking, not to mention it could not replicate the durability and strength of his body.","Even without his full strength, Lex did not doubt that he could best any Heaven Immortal he met. It was nowhere near safe enough, but when had that ever stopped him? He was already in a desperate situation, and he was in the search for something to help him fulfil his plan.","When they set out, the young couple found an excuse to bring along Karev, telling him that they had gotten a lead on a valuable treasure. It wasn’t exactly false since Lex gave them a replica coin that would point them in the same direction as his coin.","The group set out, and Lex even removed the hidden trackers the alliance had placed on the three of them, letting them move unhindered and unmonitored. However, when they departed, they had not anticipated how long the journey would be.","The group, despite being immortals and moving at fairly quick speeds, took them nearly four years to complete. When they finally reached their destination... there was nothing.","They reached the base of a tall cliff where the coin was pointing towards, yet no matter how Lex scanned the area he could find nothing. He even tried to use the coin, but except for pointing towards the very base of the cliff, Lex scratched his head, unsure of how to proceed. He began to study the coin and the location once more, trying to determine if the treasure would only reveal itself at a certain time.","Meanwhile, River, Pearl and Karev were also studying the location.","\"What’s going on?\" Karev asked, displaying a surprising amount of calmness for someone who had traveled four years for what seemed like nothing.","\"I’m not sure,\" said River as he looked towards the cliff, where he could see Cliff trying to understand what had gone wrong. If even Cliff didn’t know, how could River? \"This is where the coin is pointing towards, I’m sure of it. I’m not sure why there’s nothing here. Maybe we need to wait for something or...\"","His voice was suddenly interrupted by Cliff, who was, for the first time since River had known him, startled by something.","He looked towards River, and then back towards Karev, and then at Pearl as if he was trying to figure something out.","The realization he suddenly had was so startling that Lex actually started to laugh out in disbelief. Instead of staying hidden, he revealed himself in front of Karev.","Karev, on the other hand, did not seem too surprised to see Cliff.","\"I take it you’re the one who has been looking after these kids,\" Karev said calmly, as if he had expected everything. \"If that’s the case then I must thank you as their elder.\"","Lex only shook his head.","\"No need to thank me, these two worked for every benefit they got. As a firm believer in the ways of capitalism, I wouldn’t even give them a fever for free,\" answered Lex as he waved his hand. \"Jokes aside, they’re good kids. If anyone deserved it, they did.\"","Compared to Karev, River and Pearl were stunned. In all the time... in all the decades that they had known Cliff, he had never revealed himself in front of anyone, let alone casually joke with them. His sudden actions gave them a premonition that... something was about to change.","\"Then I take it that you’re the one who brought us here?\" Karev asked, looking at the coin in Cliff’s hand and noticing how it looked identical to the one River had. \"What is it for?\"","Cliff only shook his head with a wide smile, filled with disbelief.","\"You know, I’m actually so stupid. The clues were in front of me the whole time - I can’t believe I didn’t connect the dots before,\" Cliff said as he squatted next to the cliffside and called River over.","\"Some time ago I learned of a place filled with countless treasures that can only be enjoyed inside that place, and nothing can be taken out. That magical place - the one that’s as big as a Major realm and holds unbelievable treasures that can entice even Dao Lords - is called the Gilded Hollow. Does that ring any bells?\"","For a moment River and Pearl felt confused, but Karev immediately realized what the man was referring to.","\"You don’t think... the ring?\" he asked, but Lex did not respond.","Instead, he asked Karev for the ring and placed it headfirst in a small groove in the cliffside. The coin suddenly started to glow before it shot out of Lex’s hands and into the cliffside, turning into a bright, shining outline of a door.","The cliff trembled, and then that trembled spread across the entire realm, and then the universe itself. The legendary Gilded Hollow, which had been sealed for countless eons, had suddenly reopened.","Doors of light, just like the one in front of Lex and the others, opened all across the universe, sometimes in front of people and sometimes in empty places.","Those who stepped through could be called lucky, or maybe unlucky. Only time could tell.","\"Proceed at your own risk, because I won’t be able to help you inside,\" said Lex as he looked towards the three of them. \"In fact, as abrupt as it may be, this might be farewell. If you guys become famous enough, maybe one day I’ll find you again.\"","Lex waved at them, and then stepped through the light, taking the necklace with him. He didn’t tell them that within their bodies he had sealed some of his power which could protect them if their lives were in danger. He also didn’t opt for a long, emotional goodbye - he didn’t have the time for it.","The door to the Gilded Hollow would only be open for a very short time."]},{"number":2324,"title":"Chapter 2324: Bait","paragraphs":["Everything happened so fast. Lex had always thought that his separation from the two would be something he’d see a long way coming, for example the end of their deadline. Although Lex had done his best to remain detached, and had not actively helped them out during their struggles, he had to admit that he was still somewhat attached.","The two of them were idiots, basically. Despite living such long lives, overcoming such impossible odds, and achieving such great things, considering where they started out from, they were still just kids who had a bit of strength now.","Sure, life had forced some wisdom down their throats due to all their experiences, but for the most part they were just two kids who were hopelessly in love with each other. If Lex hadn’t grown immune to the cringe one liners, and their mad displays of affection for one another, he might have gone crazy.","Lex shook his head as the grin on his face slowly faded. He would miss them, but it was for the best that they live their own life now and find their own direction. For too long had they been influenced by him and his deadlines. Now they could finally slow down and enjoy life.","He was certain that if the pressure from his deadlines hadn’t always kept them on their toes, they would have been married with kids by now. Without him urging them on to gain more strength, maybe they could consider such things.","As he moved his thoughts away from the young couple, Lex could not help but think about the Gilded Hollow itself.","The first time he heard about it was through Ventura himself. Everyone had been revealing some secrets, and not wanting to be left out, Ventura revealed that the Gilded Hollow would be opening soon.","What Lex wondered now was whether Ventura knew that it would open through Lex’s hands, or if it was some kind of inevitability. Since the ring belonged to Karev’s descendants, maybe destiny would have forced Karev, or maybe Pearl, to bring the ring to Joro realm.","Certain events might have forced them to bring the ring to this location. All that would have happened was that it would have taken a bit longer than it did now. So was this all a part of Ventura’s plan, or was it something he had foreseen? Or was Lex just an unwitting victim of destiny’s design?","These were questions he could not answer for now, which is why he thought about other things. For example, had he been carrying the Gilded Hollow all this time, or was the ring simply a representation of what the realm actually was? After all, an entire realm shouldn’t have been able to fit inside a single ring, right?","He recalled that Ballom himself had claimed that no one actually knew what the Gilded Hollow really was. All anyone knew about it was that the entrances to the Gilded Hollow would randomly appear all across the universe, inside every single realm, whether they were Major or minor.","The Gilded Hollow was supposedly filled with countless treasures, wealth and resources. The only catch was that all the treasures and resources needed to be utilized within the Hollow, for if they were brought out, they would disappear - just like the resources from the ring.","Furthermore, the resources encountered inside correspond to the cultivation level of whoever entered, including Dao Lords!","Oh, and as far as records went, no one inside the realm had ever met anyone else from the outside. Many took that to assume that the size of the realm was unbelievably vast. Lex just felt like the realm might be purposefully segregating people.","More important, however, was that the Gilded Hollow also had dangers. Yet saying such a statement might cause others to underestimate the dangers of the Hollow. The last time the Hollow was open, nearly 40% of all Dao Lords who entered had died.","At the time, Ballom had also mentioned that he too found the timing of the Hollow’s appearance to be suspicious. It had been gone for so long, but to reappear now during so much instability was just asking for trouble. Yet it was an open conspiracy. Even Dao Lords would fall for it, because they too needed resources.","Although Lex couldn’t imagine what Dao Lords needed or did with those resources, they still clearly needed them, which is why they would opt to enter the Gilded Hollow. As for what would happen to the universe while they were gone... no one knew.","Speaking of things no one knew, the duration for which the Hollow would be open was a total mystery. Lex had, however, done some research and learned of the most common theory. The duration of the Hollow’s presence had nothing to do with time. Instead, it would last as long as it needed to until a certain number of resources from it had been harvested.","Strange, but he wasn’t complaining. Instead, Lex just happily looked forward to the teleportation ending so he could begin harvesting. The only thing that still bothered him was why the coin had the aura similar to the Origin realms Axis Eternum and what that had to do with the Hollow.","While Lex was still undergoing teleportation and wondering about such things, the doors to the Hollow all across the universe finally closed. The doors had been open for a total of eight minutes in each realm, respective to their own flow of time.","It was neither long nor short, and depended entirely on one’s perspective.","Deep within the Dream realm, there was a large castle that looked like it had come right out of... well, someone’s dreams. The castle could not be reached through ordinary means, and was swarming with Sandmen who were going about their business. The castle had not seen so much activity in Ages.","Within the depths of the castle, a particular figure was watching a live screening of the fight between Wu Kong and Erlang, which was still ongoing. Both of them had sustained serious injuries, and for the first time, Erlang was actually regretting picking a fight with Wu Kong for the monkey had gone completely crazy!","\"Dream Master, there has been a report,\" a Sandman said as he entered the room and glanced towards the fight.","\"Yes?\" responded a feminine voice - one that would have surprised Lex if he heard it.","\"The Gilded Hollow appeared ahead of schedule, but that has actually worked in our favor. Our projections indicate that nearly 12,000 Dao Lords, or an approximate 31% of all Dao Lords in existence, have entered the Hollow.","\"That is far more than the 12% we had originally expected. That’s because the doors opened in the middle of a number of battlefields, prompting many Dao Lords to prioritise the Hollow over the wars. As a result, there has already been a massive shift in the defense of countless realms.\"","The Dream Master paused, and then smiled.","\"The bait is in place. Prepare the armies. Once everything is over, history will remember this as the Age of Dreams.\"","The Sandman merely nodded and headed out. The Dream Master looked towards Wu Kong once more, and continued to watch the show unfold."]},{"number":2325,"title":"Chapter 2325: My boss","paragraphs":["Z stepped out in front of the swarm of Godrix Worms, his expression entirely plain, as if he was going about another day’s work. Godrix Worms, born from the rotting bodies of living Deities, who were imprisoned and deprived of their power, were a real, damn menace.","They were not easy to kill, not easy to defeat, but they bred faster than rabbits and could suck the spiritual energy from the air till a region was left completely barren. These worms were especially useful in war, and were often used by members of the Path of Chaos during realm wars.","Z had no idea why they were in the Geb realm, nor did he know who even brought them here. After all, from what he had seen, neither side in this ongoing war seemed too pleasant to him. Then again, his exposure was highly limited - being constrained to the Slave army and all.","\"What weapon shall I use today?\" Z asked out loud, as if talking to himself. The army of slaves that stood behind him knew that he was talking to them though.","\"Why don’t you use a sword?\" asked Nadia, one of the strongest members of the army and, coincidentally, a sword user. \"It’s one of the most common weapons, is especially useful in war, and you have been avoiding it.\"","Z smirked, and looked back at her. Nadia was human, and not even a one of the human subraces, which is what most would have expected when they saw her height. Standing at 7 feet 2 inches (2.18 meters), she was taller than most humans Z had ever known.","Matched with her flawless ebony skin, dark braided hair, leather armor and longsword that was 5 feet (1.5 meters) long, she made for an impressive and intimidating sight.","\"You just want a turn with the violin,\" Z said, seeing through her the true meaning behind her words. He did not reject her, though, as he handed her his violin, and grabbed her sword instead.","\"Well, I didn’t lie. You really have been avoiding using a sword all these years. I wonder why,\" she said as she appreciated the violin in her hands. Though it was made of wood, it was tougher than most hammers, and could completely be used as a weapon to bash faces in. Of course, that was not what Z actually used it for.","\"My boss uses swords,\" Z said as he spun the sword around in his hand, getting used to the weight. \"I guess I just wanted to avoid embarrassing myself. I’m sure if he ever found out I fought with a sword, he’d add swordsmanship to my training regime lest I continue to embarrass him, and that just sounds like so much extra work.\"","Z sounded both like he was reminiscing, and complaining, which Nadia and the other slaves found interesting. Even now, even after all these years of fighting and torture, the Grand Conqueror had not been able to affect Z’s personality in the slightest, which was both amazing and unbelievable.","\"Why does it almost sound like you’re more afraid of your boss than the Grand Conqueror?\" she asked, though the question was meant as a joke. How could that even be possible? Yet it hit closer to the truth than she realized.","\"Do you know who my boss is?\" Z asked as he grabbed the sword with both hands. Its weight meant that using it singlehanded slowed his mobility. \"Never mind. I couldn’t tell you even if I wanted to. What I can tell you is that if my boss ever found out what had happened to me...\"","Z didn’t complete the sentence, and instead shook his head as if he didn’t want to think about it.","Nadia froze, and exchanged expressions with the other.","\"You can’t possibly think that your boss could try to come save you?\" she asked hesitantly.","The question caused Z to snort.","\"Heck no. He’d tell me to think of this as training and figure out my own way to escape and get revenge,\" Z said. His boss was always finding new ways to give him work.","As if put off by the thought, Z no longer talked with Nadia and began to walk towards the Godrix Worms still practicing with the sword as he walked.","Normally, the entire army would follow him. After all, this was the mission of the whole army. Yet they did not move.","\"Escape? On your own?\" Nadia repeated in disbelief. \"How can that even be possible? The Grand Conqueror’s collars can trap even Celestial Immortals, not to mention he’s received the legacy of one of the founding human kings. He’s been recruited by the Humanoid Alliance as one of the future leaders of humanity. How can someone even hope to seek revenge against someone like that?\"","She knew Z could hear her words, but he did not answer and just kept walking. Humanoid Alliance? Human King? Future leader? Z didn’t care about any of that. It just sounded like so much unnecessary work to him.","Then his thoughts went to Lex, and the news of his disappearance. He was only half convinced. After thinking about it, he didn’t believe there existed anyone who could get one up on him. As far as he was concerned, this was just an elaborate ruse by Lex to get his enemy to lower his guard while Lex himself set up an elaborate plan to stage his comeback.","He knew... the moment Lex came back, he’d just give Z a whole lot more training if he ended up having to rescue Z. That thought... finally lit a certain fire in Z’s heart. He could not even imagine how many new anime he’d missed over the years. Someone would pay for that.","As he raised his sword, the sound of a lone violin began to resound across the battlefield. The tune was a slow, mournful one, as if the person playing had lost all hope... or as if there was no hope left for Z’s enemies.","The army of slaves stood atop the battlefield and watched in silence as Z alone fought the battle that should have required them all. They were used to it.","In the name of training, Z always fought alone. Though he had an odd habit. Whenever he fought, he required background music.","One of the slaves began to hum, and soon another joined him. One by one the army of slaves joined in a wordless chant, acting like Z’s personal choir as if to serenade his enemies with one final song before their demise.","In Z’s own mind, he was still the same, lazy old teenager who wanted nothing but to sit in the Gamer’s lounge, watch anime and play games. He was simply forced to do things he didn’t want to do. In everyone else’s, however, he was a walking calamity like no other."]},{"number":2326,"title":"Chapter 2326: Insignificant","paragraphs":["\"What the hell did you do?\" Ballom questioned, his entire being radiating with anger as he barged into the meeting room, Dao radiation leaking from every pore of his body.","The fact that there were so many secrets being kept these days might have made people forget, but it was almost impossible to keep secrets from Dao Lords. Or, well, at least incredibly difficult and costly.","Thus, it was only a matter of time before the whole affair was revealed to everyone. While the Innkeeper had allowed the Humanoid Alliance to use his Inn to access the Dream realm, he had asked them to protect the tavern during the time that they did.","While certain factions of the alliance did just that, other factions of the alliance used their access to the Inn to learn everything they could about it and kidnapped one of the Inns’ workers from within the very tavern they were meant to be protecting!","Since they were privy to the security details of the tavern, it only became easier for them to plot out the perfect plan to ensure that their mission was a success!","Yes, for a time, they had managed to keep this a secret. But it was inevitable that this secret would be revealed. To begin with, something like this wasn’t worth the effort and investment it would take to hide it from other Dao Lords.","Now, it was an open secret among the Dao Lords that the Humanoid Alliance had abused their agreement with the Innkeeper. The funniest thing was, most of the Dao Lords who learned about it felt like this was a terrible exchange. If they were going to strain their relationship with the Innkeeper, it should at least be over something valuable?","A single, immortal human? Going for him was basically the same as annoying the Innkeeper for no reason. The Humanoid Alliance had, to a small extent, attracted disdain from others. Of course, it was only a small amount, for most weren’t qualified to pass judgment on a behemoth like that.","The meeting room held only two others. One was the Runeking Dao Lord, and one was a Celestial Dao Lord.","The Dwarf looked a bit amused, even smug, as he looked at the furious Ballom, while the Celestial looked annoyed.","\"Ballom, intruding on a disciplinary meeting is against protocol,\" the Celestial said as he looked towards the Devil.","\"Oh, I forgot, we don’t allow intruding on meetings but betraying allies, provoking friends into enemies and ruining the reputation of the alliance are fine,\" Ballom retorted furiously.","The Celestial seemed to have anticipated such a response, and so wasn’t fazed by his anger. The Dwarf, however, actually seemed to enjoy Ballom’s fury.","\"Oh come now, don’t overreact,\" the Runeking said as he waved his hand. \"It’s a mere immortal human, and he’s not even related to the Innkeeper. Besides, the Innkeeper has indicated many times that he’s interested in allying with the alliance. If that’s the case, shouldn’t he contribute to our cause?","\"A single human with the chance to inherit the legacy of Zarek is not too precious yet not so useless. He has a decent chance of reaching the peak of the Celestial realm, but that’s all. If he can’t even contribute that much to the cause of reviving humanity, then what right does he have of trying to join the alliance?\"","The Celestial suddenly waved his hand, locking Ballom in place and preventing him from transforming into his Devil form. On one hand, the radiation from that would pollute this meeting room for centuries, and on the other hand, he didn’t want to deal with a fight with all he had going on.","\"Runeking is not wrong - joining the alliance would mean that the Innkeeper would have to contribute. No one can simply take benefits from the alliance. Having said that, there are ways of going about this. Your aggressive manner was highly inappropriate, and regardless of the value of the human, the disrespect to the Innkeeper will become a hurdle in trying to recruit him. At the same time, this has affected the credibility of the alliance.","\"This has also reduced the chances of cooperating with the Innkeeper in the future, thus I cannot look the other way. Runeking, you will be sentenced to a hundred years in the forge, crafting for the alliance. You are forbidden from leaving until your time is up.\"","The Runeking didn’t seem bothered at all by his punishment, and merely winked towards Ballom as he hopped on his feet and slowly sauntered off.","Ballom’s anger hadn’t subsided in the least. In fact, he seemed even angrier than he was when he came in.","\"When the fallout from this comes, and it will come, do not expect the Devils to participate in the clean up,\" Ballom said angrily towards the Celestial.","\"You cannot speak on behalf of the Devil race, Ballom. Besides, you know I agree with you on this matter. Runeking shouldn’t have acted against the human. Losing access to the Midnight Inn’s teleportation capabilities could be a huge blow to the alliance.\"","Ballom snorted.","\"If you agree with me then return the human to the Inn before the situation gets worse! At least that way there’s a chance to redeem the situation,\" Ballom exclaimed.","The Celestial, unfortunately, shook his head.","\"I wish I could, but the Runeking has a large lobby behind him, and they’re all dissatisfied with the attention that the Innkeeper has been getting. They feel like if he joins the alliance, it will severely affect the distribution of resources among Dao Lords, so they want to use this event to pressure him and remind him that even if he joins, he would be a newcomer.","\"While there are many who feel like this is pointlessly offending the Innkeeper, however since they’ve lost the initiative it’s not so easy to overturn the situation at this moment. The best we can do right now is damage control. If you want to return the human, you can gather up a lobby of your own, but with the situation at Eden getting a vote through is nigh impossible.\"","Ballom was clearly furious, but instead of arguing with the Celestial anymore, he only smiled, and then let out a low laugh.","\"You all keep saying that you ’ just took an immortal’ . Buddy, when you sit in front of the Innkeeper and he looks at you, immortals and mortals with the exact same gaze, you’ll come to understand that you’re just as insignificant to him as that immortal is to you.\"","Ballom turned around to leave, no longer interested in continuing the conversation. He now had to do his best to make sure that when the fallout came, he wouldn’t get caught up in it. Ideally, he could even discover where Z was being kept. Yet that was easier said than done, for he was sure that the Runeking was specifically blocking him.","He’d see how things went."]},{"number":2327,"title":"Chapter 2327: Destruction & creation","paragraphs":["The teleportation ended, and Lex found himself inside a forest... except all the plants were made entirely out of stone. He spread out his spirit sense to get an understanding of his surroundings, and assess for any dangers. It was clear that he was far from the only living being in the region.","Yet before he could concentrate on the oddity of his surroundings, or the buzzing of countless insects, or the deep footprints in the ground left behind by massive animals, Lex realized that there was something very wrong with this place on a fundamental level!","To be clear, the laws of this place were foreign and alien to Lex in ways he’d never encountered before, yet that was far from all. Lex’s very presence in this place started to immediately affect the laws all around him, as if he was assimilating this realm around him.","Yet clearly he wasn’t doing that. Instead... it was as if he was being used as some kind of transmitter for the laws of his universe to amalgamate everything within the Gilded Hollow.","Suddenly, Lex froze. Yes, his universe. That’s why the laws felt so different. They were clearly different from the laws of his universe, but were being converted right in front of him in real time. Did that mean that the Gilded Hollow was actually a remnant from another universe?","There was a very specific reason why Lex reached such a conclusion. Once, he’d used a Life level token to receive a reward, and one of the rewards available for him to get were the scraps of the Mantle of Pentagal.","According to the description, Pentagal was another universe. It was not explicitly stated or mentioned anywhere, but Lex strongly suspected that Pentagal was a universe that had been absorbed by his own universe somehow. Or at least parts of it had. Now, standing inside the Gilded Hollow, watching its law be changed before his very eyes, Lex’s mind began to race as countless thoughts came up in his mind.","Was he witnessing the devouring of a universe before his very eyes? Was that why no resource could exit the Hollow? Because its very existence depended on the alien laws of this place?","No, that didn’t make sense. In front of his very eyes, the laws that constituted these resources were being rewritten, and they still continued to exist. So why?","Clearly, the answer was beyond the limits of his imagination. That didn’t matter though. As Lex stood inside the forest of stone, he entered a trance. The process by which the alien laws were being changed was a type of destruction and creation Lex had never even thought possible.","Watching it, Lex’s first thought was to memorise it and learn as much as possible from it as he could. When he did that, insight into the eight ruling laws began to flood his mind faster than he could actually absorb and comprehend, leaving him just standing there.","In fact, his comprehension of these laws was evolving at such a rapid pace that if he had been outside the Hollow, he would have immediately triggered a tribulation, even in his necklace state.","Within the Hollow, however, the laws of the Heavenly tribulations sensed his changes, but did not act for some reason. It was as if they were suppressed by laws of a higher order.","Lex sensed even that , allowing his understanding of the universe’s laws to enter a whole new level.","For a few hours, nothing happened. He just stood there, observing, recording, learning, as the laws of the world all around him continued to change. This was not a quick process, or one that would end in a day or two.","Then, as if spurred on by the very creation and destruction that caused the laws around him to change, the necklace which actually acted as his vessel began to exert a pulling force on everything around it.","At first it was slight, barely causing the stone leaves of the surrounding trees to flap as if by the wind. But with each passing moment, that attractive force became greater and greater until the first spec of dirt from the ground flew up and into the necklace.","Even that speck of dirt, as it turned out, was an invaluable treasure. It contained an abundance of energy, not to mention vitality. It could even be called soil with fertility high enough to plant herbs able to affect even Heaven Immortals.","Then another speck of dirt was absorbed by the necklace as it was pulled up and into the necklace. As Lex witnessed the final struggle of a universe long dead, and the unstoppable, victorious spread of another one, he saw two futures for himself: one where he met his end despite his best efforts, despite all that he had achieved and all that he was, and other where his victory was unquestionable, unstoppable, and overwhelming.","Another speck was absorbed into the necklace, destroyed the moment it was absorbed, and then recreated as a part of the necklace itself. The force of attraction from the necklace... the force of gravity exuding from it grew as Lex mimicked the actions of his universe itself, and used the final vestiges of Pentagal’s corpse to recreate himself into something far greater.","In the forest, there were countless living beings, and all of them were ready to undergo the baptism of the new universe, and be welcomed into their new home. Yet they no longer thought of that as they all ran, causing a stampede. They ran in any direction at all, as long as it was far away from the terrifying aura growing in the very heart of a forest that had stood for an unknown number of years... a forest that would soon cease to exist.","Within the Dream realm, inside the dome created by Lex’s aura, Daekol was still working on breaking the barrier around Lex’s body when he heard the faint sound of tribulation thunder, and frowned.","He looked around, but found no tribulation in sight, nor did he sense any tribulation laws being triggered. He looked down at Lex, and the expression in his eyes became even more solemn."]},{"number":2328,"title":"Chapter 2328: All new Domination","paragraphs":["When Lex came to, there was no forest around him. There was nothing, not even the ground. Instead, there was a deep, circular pit in the shape of a dome, for everything within a mile (1.6 km) of the necklace had been sucked into it.","Lex was not surprised, though. He’d been in a trance, not asleep. He was aware of everything that had happened. Everything within the Gilded Hollow was an extremely valuable resource - everything ! He didn’t know the exact reason, but he had a few theories.","If the Gilded Hollow truly was the last vestige of the universe known as Pentagal, then there was a chance that it existed in a state of profound compression, with every remaining speck of its being forged into material of astonishing purity and quality.","For years already, Lex had been using low level, rare resources to build a faint foundation for his necklace to alter it in the way that he wanted. In matters like that, it wasn’t just about getting rare resources, but they needed to be the right ones that appropriately complimented the existing structure of the necklace while moving it towards the direction Lex wanted it to go in.","Over here, however, Lex had done something odd and unique - something he would not be able to replicate without the help of the universe itself. He had destroyed the resources, and remade them into exactly what he needed. In a sense, it didn’t even matter what it was he was absorbing - just the level of the resource itself.","In a way, it was an ability similar to what Lotus used, except this was less energy intensive since he wasn’t creating something from scratch. Yet whether it was Lotus’ ability to create items using only energy, or the current ability demonstrated by the laws of the universe to destroy and recreate, neither of them were things Lex could perform at a whim.","Even now, the only reason he had been able to do it was because he had been resonating with and replicating the actions of the universe itself. The fact that he was even able to do it was likely some kind of reward from the universe for using him as a beacon to affect the laws in the Gilded Hollow.","Moving forward, unless he encountered a similar situation, he wouldn’t be able to do the same.","Lex turned his focus towards the necklace, and observed the changes it had undergone. Its shape had been somewhat altered, looking now like it was a crystal key pendant of some sort. Was he so used to keys that he subconsciously changed the shape of the necklace?","It didn’t matter. The shape of the item wasn’t something he paid great attention to. Instead, he focused on the quality of the necklace itself.","Its stability was off the charts, and its strength had grown tremendously. Lex wasn’t sure he could scratch the necklace even if he used Naraka to attack it!","He smiled faintly. While increasing the necklace’s stability hadn’t been his primary goal, it was something to celebrate nonetheless.","With all other issues addressed to varying degrees, there was just one more mystery. Why had he detected the same aura as the Axis Eternum from the coin, and in fact, what was the coin to begin with? He got it from that temple, so he could conclude that this whole thing was not some great mystery to Nuwa, but it was to him.","The aura had disappeared since entering the Gilded Hollow, but that only increased his curiosity. Could it be that the Origin realm’s Axis Eternum also contained a piece of Pentagal? Or was there some other connection between these two?","He wasn’t sure.","Lex thought about it some more, but couldn’t come up with a plausible explanation. To be specific, he could come up with many explanations, but there was no way to verify any of them at all, so it was best not to assume lest it affect his judgment in the future.","With that put behind him, there was just one thing left for him to do. He had to find and absorb the most valuable resources that he could, and take this opportunity to develop the necklace to the best of his ability.","It would not be easy to find so many high quality resources again in the short term. Thus, it would be best if he formed a nascent form of his own system within the necklace, or at least upgraded the necklace until it was in a state where he could use it to combat Stalker, his enemy.","A thick, overwhelmingly strong spirit sense surged out from the necklace like an unstoppable tsunami, covering thousands and thousands of miles all around it, surveying everything as if a lord was observing his domain.","Spirit sense was usually illusory, able to sweep past any without being detected at all. Yet when Lex unleashed his own spirit sense, it carried a very real weight with it, as if trapping all beings in a pool of quicksand. They could move, but doing so would be incredibly difficult, and they had to resist the spirit sense for every bit of movement.","That palpable, oppressive pressure was followed by an extremely domineering and overwhelming aura of royalty and supremacy. Every insect, every animal, every plant, and even those that did not fall within those categories, all felt a feeling of submission emerging from the very core of their being. It was no longer a matter of bravery and cowardice - they could not even conceive resistance.","After so many years, Lex’s cultivation had not increased at all, but that did not mean he hadn’t gotten stronger. With years and years of free time, Lex had pondered the laws, observed how they affected mortals and immortals alike, and deepened his own understanding about the universe.","All that was before he studied the overwhelming way in which the universe overwrote the laws of reality within the Gilded Hollow!","Lex’s Domination, once a technique used to copy Dragons Might, had now reached a whole new level. Dragons could use their Dragon’s Might to control and somewhat affect the universe itself. Well Lex had veered from that path, and instead used his Domination to exert Supremacy over the area within his spirit sense, and take control of it. Within the scope of his Domination, Lex was like a Sovereign and a monarch. This was his territory, and there could be no doubt about that.","Lex’s eyes flickered. His progress was great, but it wasn’t enough. He didn’t know how it would hold up against a real Sovereign, and he didn’t care to find out, because as far as he was concerned, this technique was still incomplete. It was still far from reaching the ideal state he had visualised in his mind. Soon, he would correct that."]},{"number":2329,"title":"Chapter 2329: For the first time, but not the last I","paragraphs":["As with so many other things, for example the Dream realm, entering the Gilded Hollow brought Lex to an area that coincided with his cultivation level. The problem - not for him, but everything else - was that Lex was as strong as the average Celestial Apex while still being in the Heaven Immortal realm.","Fortunately, Lex wasn’t the least bit interested in carrying out a mass slaughter. He was only interested in resources.","He did not stroll, or saunter across the Hollow. No, for once, Lex was not interested in stopping to smell the roses. The necklace shot out like a rocket, speeding through the Hollow at a speed no other living being could follow. Any resource that was even remotely useful to him that came within 5000 miles (8000 km) of the necklace was pulled from the ground and teleported to him, only for him to absorb it in the very next second.","Since he had no idea how long the Gilded Hollow would remain open, he would make the best use of it. While a portion of his mind focused on reaping resources from the Hollow, a small part of his mind was focused on detecting the dangers of the Hollow. He hadn’t forgotten that even Dao Lords died here.","The remainder of all his attention was focused on developing the necklace. At the moment, he was working on three aspects of it. The first was making sure the necklace could absorb an abundant amount of energy regardless of its location. The second was in developing an independent space within the necklace, created using solely Lex’s application of space laws and the nourishment of the resources he provided.","He didn’t want to risk tearing out a piece of space from the Hollow, only for it to disappear once he left.","Surprisingly, creating space was not impossibly difficult for him. In fact, due to his fusion with Lotus, and his deep understanding of space laws, this was actually a task he could complete with little strain.","The third task was to begin construction of a very basic system. For now, it would not have any complex tasks or requirements. Instead, the system would artificially regulate the laws within the space within his necklace, forming a fake realm.","The laws of this fake realm, which he was in the process of creating even now, would operate according to his whims. For now, he just needed to be a stable space that could support simple, mortal life.","Once that was achieved, he would begin to grow and expand not only the fake realm within the necklace, but the scope of the system’s actions and capabilities.","Was he trying to create a portable realm similar to the Midnight Realm wherein he could control every aspect of it, like he did inside the Midnight Inn when he put on the Host Attire? Yes. Absolutely yes. In fact, he was aiming for something far greater than that.","His newest, most powerful weapon to date would be a realm he carried with himself wherein he was the only Sovereign, and only master. Weapons such as swords, at his current power level, were becoming somewhat limited in what they could accomplish. He needed more complex weapons at his disposal.","To create his fake realm, Lex needed resources which contained hints of laws trapped within them, just like the Cosmic Erosion Elixir Lex had used to gain a spatial affinity back in the day. Fortunately, this place was filled with such items.","Thus, piece by piece, Lex acquired the required resources and forged the space within the necklace to grow larger and stronger. Moreover, he kept using the Ink he’d received from his previous clearance of Karev’s inheritance to write down arrays and formations within the necklace itself.","The tool was, naturally, affected by the laws outside of itself, but once these formations were activated, the system Lex would design would take control of the laws and determine how they behaved.","This was too grand a task, and for now Lex could only broadly outline how the laws would be affected rather than go into details.","Once Lex actually began the work, he realized that he had even more advantages than he’d originally realized. He had witnessed the birth and development of the Midnight realm with his own eyes.","Even if, back then, he could not understand the ways in which the laws operated, merely witnessing the event provided him with a tremendous amount of insight. Previously, all of that knowledge had remained dormant. Only now that he was trying to create his own realm from scratch did it start to become useful once again.","At that point, his comprehension of laws underwent another growth spurt. Lex was now certain that the moment he left the Hollow, or perhaps the moment he reimagined control of his body, he would undergo another Major tribulation. It wasn’t that he wanted to become a Celestial Immortal - it was more like the universe itself found his cultivation level unacceptable for the extent and depth of his understanding of laws.","If Pearl, who spent decades barely beginning to understand the laws of fire, were to ever learn how quickly ’Cliff’ was expanding his understanding of laws, she might faint - or straight up just give up cultivation forever. It was a good thing she wasn’t around.","Busy as he was, three years passed by within the Gilded Hollow without any changes. It wasn’t that Lex didn’t encounter any dangers. Instead, the dangers he faced were so weak compared to his strength that they barely qualified to attract his attention.","He’d made great progress during this time, and there were no signs of him slowing down at all. For him, this was practically a vacation.","The rest of the universe, however, was not having nearly as great a time as he was. In three short years, according to the flow of time of Major realms, over a dozen Dao Lords had been killed in the war, and two had been killed within the Dream realm.","Such earth-shattering news rocked the whole universe, for so many Dao Lords had not faced death in countless years, and now they had died in quick succession.","But that... was far from the worst thing that happened. On that particular day, a certain piece of news spread like wildfire across the universe, shocking all . The Pokore Major realm had been conquered, and had new owners now. Before anyone could process that news at all, it was quickly followed by the news that... the Major realm had been destroyed!","For the first time in this Age, a Major realm had been destroyed! Not just that, the destruction was clearly not accidental. Someone had done it on purpose. It was just that... no one could understand what that purpose was!"]},{"number":2330,"title":"Chapter 2330: Dread","paragraphs":["Whether they were big shots or insignificant lone cultivators, everyone felt the impact of the destruction of a Major realm, and felt some form of apprehension. A Major realm was deeply connected to the laws of the universe, and was the most stable, energy dense entity in the universe itself.","Not even Eclipse, and not even Dao Lords had access to as much energy as a Major realm, nor could they influence the laws of the universe on the same scale. Maybe if those eight beings above the Dao Lord realm weren’t constrained by the fact that the universe didn’t allow them to use their full power, they might have come close. Heck, they may even be equal to it, or even surpass it.","But they did not live in a ’what if’ situation, they lived in reality, and in reality, even those eight beings could not control such power.","A Major realm was hung in the Void, and due to its very nature, the Void was devoid of almost everything. It was an infinite void of darkness where time and space meant nothing, making it nearly impossible to traverse under ordinary circumstances, and even harder for any kind of physical force to travel from one point to another.","As soon as any kind of energy was introduced into the Void, it would be devoured and transformed into the most potent Chaos energy, which was only suitable for destruction.","Yet there was something else present in the Void as well - the universal laws. Not the laws of realms which ordinary immortals could easily control and manipulate. No, the Void mostly contained universal laws, which were the highest authority and most powerful laws in the universe.","It was like the eight ruling laws, but because of the sheer magnitude of them, even Celestials could not easily control them at their whim.","In this instance, though, that did not matter. While the physical blast from the destruction of a Major realm got lost in the Void, the tremor it caused in the laws of the universe traveled far and wide. An incomprehensible dread and sorrow filled all living beings across the universe, regardless of the level of their life or cultivation level.","A Dao Lord was just as insignificant in front of the death of a Major realm as a mortal, so they all felt it to the exact same extent. Fortunately, they only felt dread, and not something more serious, or all mortal life across the universe might have ceased to exist at that moment.","Most beings in the universe did not understand where such existential dread came from, and retreated to any safeholds they had. Economic activity ceased. Animals went into hibernation prematurely. Storms eased up, and even calamities dared not strike. Empires stopped their expansion, thieves stopped stealing, corruption stopped, but so did policing, patrolling and anything at all that was less than absolutely necessary.","Yet even that was merely the very first, instantaneous response from the universe. What followed it was entirely unexpected - at least for most. Some extremely learned scholars had been able to predict it, and even fewer who had lived from ancient times knew first hand what was to come.","With the laws of the universe as a conduit, the immense energy caused by the destruction of a Major realm traveled all across the universe, enriching it! The energy levels rose across the universe, even if only by a small amount in most places.","Moreover, the laws, instead of being strained by the burden, actually became stronger, firmer and more stable as the strain on the universe suddenly decreased! The strain on the universe was the very thing that allowed the universe to continue existing, but it was also what was limiting its operations.","The universe had existed for too long without ascending to the next phase, and so had created too many Major realms, and birthed too many Dao Lords, causing it to bear an immense strain the likes of which could not be fathomed by most.","In seconds following the destruction of a Major realm, the fallout from it had only just begun, but every major organisation in the universe was holding emergency meetings trying to figure out what it meant.","While all other things had ceased or slowed due to the destruction, the actions of Dao Lords became even more frantic after the initial shock. The war became more destructive, more chaotic, and the search for treasures within the Dream realm became even more frantic.","Whether it was due to the war, the Dream realm or the Gilded Hollow, nearly 99% of all Dao Lords in the universe had become active once more in some capacity, an event that hadn’t happened since the early days of the Enlightenment Age.","Within the conference rooms and meeting halls of the various organisations, they tried to dissect the purpose behind the destruction of a Major realm. It ranged from anywhere between harvesting rare treasures, accumulating countless souls for some heinous ritual, enhancing some forbidden Dao, and more.","One specific conclusion many of them reached, independent of each other, was that someone might be making an attempt at forcing the universe to evolve. Finding Eclipse and forcing her out of her realm was, ironically, more difficult than destroying a Major realm.","Thus, many began to theorise that if enough Major realms were destroyed in a short amount of time, the sudden reduction in Universal Strain could trigger a profound change in the universe. Combined with the strengthening feedback the laws received by the energy released from the destruction of a Mature realm, the universe might begin to transition into the next state even without Eclipse.","This was just a theory, as this was the kind of thing that could not actually be tested. Dao Lords understood laws better than anyone, but even they could not boast complete understanding of all the laws of the universe, and the complex ways in which they might respond to such a series of events. There were too many variables to account for.","This was the kind of nonsense not even a fiction writer would entertain as a real thought. Yet now they were all forced to consider that, among all their other theories, this too might be the goal of whoever plotted the destruction of that realm.","While these meetings were going on, and minutes passed, more and more information started to trickle in. Alongside the Mature realm, over two hundred Dao Lords had been caught in the unexpected blast, and all of them were believed to be dead.","This was confirmed by the massive shift in the rankings in the Cosmic Ascendance Spectrum!"]},{"number":2331,"title":"Chapter 2331: Sacrilege","paragraphs":["Fear. For the first time in a long time, a deep feeling of fear spread out among the Dao Lords of the universe. Killing a Dao Lord was so incredibly difficult that even sworn enemies who might dedicate their lives to killing each other might not succeed.","Instead, among Dao Lords, it was a much more common practice to simply seal, restrict or trap another Dao Lord for an extended period of time. Although, the ease in difficulty was only relative, for it was not easy to fool any Dao Lords.","Among cultivators there were many who could gain their cultivation levels through luck. Even among mortals, there were those who gained level simply using external assistance, and had any measure of luck and opportunity. However, among Dao Lords not a single one could be called lucky.","If they reached that level, then luck had little to do with it. There were no weaklings among Dao Lords, none who used connections or family influence or anything of the sort. Only the absolutely very best even touched upon such a level, let alone pass the tribulation and achieve it.","None of them were fools, or inexperienced. Thus, to affect them, or fight them, or trap or harm them in any way required such meticulous planning that non-Dao minds could not even adequately comprehend it.","In short, it was for good reason that Dao Lords hardly ever died,so for so many of them to suddenly die shook the very foundation of their understanding of reality. It became abundantly clear the extent and power of the silent mastermind behind the scenes. If so many of them could die so easily, then they weren’t safe either.","Unfortunately, the complex state of the universe also meant that most of them could not retreat into safety if they wished. After all, if the very realm their safe haven was in could be threatened, then what safety and security could they have?","The silent, unknown threat and the uncertainty of the situation pushed the conflict into a whole new realm of warfare. The first to feel the brunt of that change were the Angels in Eden, who faced greater pressure than ever before.","Even with all their allies, contingency, and plans, the situation was devolving so rapidly that considering a full retreat from Eden became a genuine reality they began to consider.","It was during this time that the Artica race first made their presence felt universe-wide.","Although they had many tentative agreements, they mattered for naught considering the current universal situation. As soon as a Mature realm was destroyed, the Artica race declared martial law across their realm and ’politely’ requested all foreigners to the realm to leave.","Within a single day, they evacuated all of them out of the realm - or evicted them based on who was asked.","They were absolutely not afraid of being challenged, which became abundantly obvious when some unknown entities probed them some time later, and were thoroughly thwarted.","Another entity which made their presence known was the Nine Swords Sect. Although they were not considered the peak of the universe, they were briefly involved in a conflict among Dao Lords, and gravely injured the opponent in a short period of time.","All of this happened on the first day following the blast. By the second day, another Dao Lord’s death had been confirmed, this one as a result of a sudden shift in the war. Similarly, many new forces were beginning to make a name for themselves.","During this time, entities such as banks, which were considered to be incredibly wealthy, but had little power to back it up, became targets. At first, it was the minor banks and organisations who were targeted, but on the third day, someone tried their luck and attempted to challenge the Versalis bank.","It appeared that... some people had forgotten that certain organisations and entities were the tools and instruments of certain Sage races. The Versalis bank’s director was a Primal, so it was easy to guess who backed the bank.","The response was both swift and overwhelming! Not only were the assailants attacked, their backers were thoroughly investigated. Within two hours of the attack on Versalis bank, the Primal race personally launched a retaliatory attack and decimated the entire organisation, resulting in the injury of 32 enemy Dao Lords, the trapping or sealing of 104 Dao Lords, and the death of three more.","The peacekeepers of the universe had shown exactly what their qualification was to overview the universe.","By the time one week had passed since the explosion, the situation was barely managing to regain some semblance of peace and order. But then something unexpected happened. Rumors began to spread of a prophecy, not from any old oracle or diviner. No, this so-called prophecy apparently came from a prominent Weaver - an esteemed member of the Sage race - not that anyone could confirm it.","According to the prophecy, when there were only 3000 Mature realms left in the universe, a new Age would dawn!","3000 Mature realms might sound like a lot... but considering it was less than half the number of existing Mature realms, it was absolutely unacceptable!","Panic spread at an unprecedented rate, and the war devolved into an unrecognisable state. It was no longer the Path of Order against the Path of Chaos. Now it had turned into a clash of madness against a different kind of madness. The future was becoming increasingly uncertain.","During all this time, Jack found himself unaware of the changing tides of the universal war. Within the Folklore realm, he had also felt the descent of the uncontrollable, irresistible dread, yet he did not know the actual cause for it.","Every person he met had a different story, and told a different version of events, all of them equally untrue. Since he had no deeper contacts within the Folklore realm, he could not get in contact with anyone who might know the trends of the universe, so he just continued to act as usual.","The Jollyrancher traveled from town to town, city to city, spreading the story from the book he carried. At the same time, Jack placed his fairy identity in his back and began focusing on developing his cultivation.","Although he was no longer constrained by the limitations of being a fairy, he needed a path to grow stronger, and the paladin path suited him just fine. At this level, it was not just about fulfilling his oath, but about developing his existing paladin powers as well.","It was a process he was learning slowly but steadily. Everything was going about as well as could be expected, and he only had acquired an arrest warrant in 79% of the towns he visited which was a shockingly low number considering he always traveled with Bob.","On this particular day, however, Jack encountered a situation he had not expected at all. Instead of Tiny-Sparkles coming over to give him a report about how Bob had brought down disaster on the town and their crew, Bob himself approached Jack’s captain quarters.","\"Forgive me, captain, for interrupting your cultivation,\" Bob loudly requested as he knocked on the captains quarters. \"I commit this folly not lightly, for there is a grave development that requires your attention and subsequent efforts!\"","The door opened, revealing a tiny Jack sitting atop a tiny bean bag, meditating.","\"What’s the matter?\" Jack asked, focusing on the Drama-cat. It wasn’t everyday that Bob came to him for help, so he could not even imagine what had caused such a situation to occur.","\"I ventured forth into the collection of poorly and inefficiently designed buildings, surely specifically designed to give any decent architect lasting nightmares, called a town, and encountered something unusual. Pastors, priests, missionaries and apostles were abound, the divine energy on their bodies carrying a distinct flavor.","\"Upon investigation, I discovered not a local Deity with a unique flair, nay! From others they may be able to keep their secrets, but my eyes see through their deception. These missionaries are followers of the Deity Oracle!\"","Jack raised an eyebrow, and looked towards Bob. He was unfamiliar with Oracle, but even more than that, he found it odd that Bob kept tabs on other Deities. That was surprisingly... sensible of him.","\"What these unfortunates remain unaware of is that Oracle is actually O.R.A.C.L.E. and is a Deity native to the realm ruled by A.I. This is of the utmost importance, captain!\"","Jack’s expression changed as he realized what Bob meant.","\"A Deity from a different realm is proselytizing in the Folklore realm?\" Jack asked, understanding the gravity of the situation. \"Does that mean that the Deity has traveled between realms?\"","He had already anticipated something like this might happen once he learned of the Divine ore, the very kind from which his necklace was made!","\"Yes, but that’s not important!\" Bob exclaimed seriously, dismissing Jack’s greatest concern! \"Oracle preaches a standardization across the board, which includes an even and unchained calendar where the first day of every week is Monday! Captain, grant me permission! We must launch a holy war against the sacreligious Oracle at once!\""]},{"number":2332,"title":"Chapter 2332: Holy War","paragraphs":["Lex’s relationship with Deities was complex. To say that every Deity he had encountered was his enemy would be false - some of them even worked for him. Orin the Deity of Hammers from the Midnight Realm, Vinei the Deity of Darkness from the Crystal realm, and Bob were all Deities that he had good relationships with.","However, to date, the strongest and most vile characters Lex had ever faced were also Deities. Ra and his daughter Sekhmet were responsible for so many of the problems he faced. Ironically, Bastet, Ra’s other daughter, was Lex’s first guest and the one responsible for him getting Regal Embrace.","Then again, there was also the HOA, an organisation of what Lex assumed to be evil, exiled Deities who were dedicated to doing evil stuff.","In short, while not all Deities were bad, they all warranted caution when dealing with them for they weren’t exactly simple characters.","Jack looked at Bob and considered his concerns. While he could not claim to understand Bob’s issue with Mondays, he certainly wanted to investigate the issue revolving around the cross realm proselytizing. Surely the higher ups of the realm were already aware of it, and had allowed it to happen or he wouldn’t have encountered such a situation.","\"Take me to them,\" Jack said, standing up and patting down his clothes. \"Let me see for myself what these missionaries are up to.\"","Bob seemed pleased by Jack’s response, clearly taking this to mean that the captain was giving this issue of Monday’s his utmost attention.","\"Beware, captain, for those that preach the ideology of Monday are the most insidious of all. The slightest carelessness will allow them to creep up on you like a 6 am alarm you forgot to disable, ruining the glory of the weekend and trapping you in a bog of despair.\"","Jack shivered, as if experiencing some long forgotten trauma that had been refreshed by Bob’s words. He had to give Bob some credit - there was nothing worse than a Monday morning alarm.","Jack, Bob and Ollie left the Jolly Rancher, with Ollie hiding in Jack’s shadow as he followed them out into the town. The strange appearances of the buildings in this place did not really bother Ollie, who was used to living in a tree before the Jolly Rancher, but Jack could not help but speculate on the odd choices. For example, some buildings were made in the shape of a boot, or a jewelry box.","While the buildings themselves were a little odd, the residents of the town were ordinary enough. In fact, a majority of them were in the mortal realms, going about their daily lives with a hint of wariness.","The unexplainable dread that had affected them some time ago was still fresh in everyones memories. Perhaps that was exactly why Jack found a large crowd gathered in the town square, listening to the preaching of a missionary.","\"Unlike other Deities, Lord Oracle’s gospel is fixed, and with a measurable response. Instead of offering vague and ambiguous promises, Lord Oracle is quite straight forward in what he promises,\" preached the missionary, a Beast man of the canine family.","\"Miracles are less mysterious and more standardised, but they’re also easier to anticipate and ask for. Lord Oracle does not require constant worship. Every time you desire something, there is a fixed exchange rate for worship that can get you what you desire. What’s more, your worship can be credited in times where you lack desire, and saved for a critical moment!","\"Do you want to be healed for a mortal ailment? Seven days or one hundred and sixty eight hours or worship can cure any mortal target. Do you want to avoid disaster? Depending on the size of the disaster and number of people you want to save, you exchange a few hours to a few weeks of worship.","\"Or, if you lead a town or city, you can organise faithful rituals for expanded feedback. If you attain the status of a recognized preacher with a certain number of followers for Lord Oracle, you can even ask for miracles in advance and pay it back in monthly installments!","\"There is no reason to doubt, for Lord Oracle is always transparent in his exchanges and his rewards for his followers. Instead of praying hopelessly and endlessly for a response that might never come, it’s much better to follow Lord Oracle for a guaranteed response!\"","Jack crossed his arms and stared at the missionary, not only taking in Oracle’s message and learning about the Deity, but also learning about the missionaries and observing the divine energy that filled their bodies.","He could immediately feel the difference. Unlike ordinary missionaries, who were filled with the divine energy of their respective Deity within their bodies, these ones carried the divinity in an external container - one made of the very same divine ore that made up Lex’s necklace.","What’s more, Jack could also tell that these containers were connected to some distant entity, perhaps not even in this realm, constantly being refilled with divine energy so that they don’t actually ever run out.","\"Bob, do you think Oracle is in the Folklore realm, or is he somewhere else?\" Jack asked as an idea came to him - one that he could not ignore.","\"How could a coward step out of the shadows and into the light? He is surely not within this realm,\" Bob exclaimed passionately as he stared at the missionary with a burning hatred.","Jack nodded, for he too felt like that was the case.","\"Alright, I’ve seen enough. Let’s go back,\" said Jack as he turned around.","Bob gave the missionary one last, hateful look before quickly following Jack. Within the chambers of the Jolly Rancher, a meeting of the highest order was called, and certain matters of the utmost secrecy and importance were discussed.","A few hours later, the crew left the ship and toured the city as if everything was new and exciting. Rose, who was mostly oblivious about what was happening, especially enjoyed the outing as it served to expand her horizons.","That night, after gathering all the information that they wanted, the crew took advantage of the moonless sky, and spread out across the town in secret. Then, just as the clock tower in the shape of a shawarma roller struck midnight, the struck.","With each ringing of the tower, one of the crew members struck. They were not assassinating any targets, nay. They were simply... appropriating the divine items in the possession of the missionaries to better help them make use of such valuable resources!","The loud noise of the ringing bell drowned out the sounds of the crew’s actions, yet not everything could always go smoothly. The target that Jack was assisting in safeguarding his possessions was the strongest of the group, and he managed to sense Jack’s actions and managed to resist being... assisted .","\"I sensed your malicious gaze from a mile away,\" the missionary claimed, glaring at Jack with unfathomable disgust in his eyes. \"Do you really think it is so easy...\"","Before he could finish his sentence, Jack attacked again, this time holding nothing back.","\"Yes, I really think it’s this easy,\" Jack said as he caught the missionary mid-speech.","The missionary crossed his arms, blocking the attack successfully.","\"Heh, feeble pirates. You cannot fathom the... hey, where did you go?\" the missionary asked as he lowered his arms and found that Jack was missing. For a moment he felt smug, as if he had guessed that the robber had run away. The next moment he realized that the item providing him with divine energy seemed to have disappeared.","In the middle of the night, the Jolly Rancher rushed into the sky amidst the sounds of Bob’s laughter, settling amidst the sea of clouds, hidden from view from the town underneath.","Jack sat back in his room, observing all the items he’d gotten. They were mostly weak, which is what anyone should expect from items stolen from mortal missionaries. Yet he didn’t care about that.","What Jack found interesting was that his paladin powers... could absorb the remaining divine energy with those items, purify them, and then absorb them to strengthen Jack. This was a form of cultivation for paladins neither Jack nor Lex had ever encountered before, but it was highly interesting.","Besides that, if he could purify the divine ore and then somehow send it to Lex... the thought filled him with excitement.","\"Bob, I have witnessed first hand the vile nature of Oracle,\" Jack said as he approached the Drama-cat. \"The plague of Mondays cannot be allowed to spread unchecked. Spread the word, we will initiate the Holy War to save the common people from the unjust, unspeakable terrors that Oracle preaches.\"","Bob fell to his knees and he cried. He cried, for where else would he find someone so enlightened!","\"But Oracle cannot be our only target,\" Jack suddenly said, freezing Bob where he kneeled. \"We must keep an eye out for all sacrilegious Deities like this. Though the burden of righteousness may be great, we will carry it with unwavering hearts and unbending backs.\"","As he spoke, Jack absorbed the divine energy from all the items, and felt the bottleneck keeping him from the Heaven Immortal realm loosen."]},{"number":2333,"title":"Chapter 2333: The Pocket Calamity","paragraphs":["His recent actions were quite different from the way Lex normally operated. While hunting for treasure and valuables wasn’t something new to him, he hardly ever provoked anyone on his own. However, things were different now.","Previously, he had the massive behemoth known as the Midnight Inn, not only offering him perpetual safety but also an endless stream of resources and connections. Although it wasn’t always possible to get the best or most valuable resources, with the backing of the system he always had an abundance of opportunities to encounter high value resources.","Now, however, his main body was captured and wounded, he was cut off from his system and Inn, and he existed in the form of a fairy and a necklace.","To say his existence was in threat would be going too far, since even if he lost his original body he would still be alive. However, that was a loss he was unwilling to accept. A part of him had considered employing his most dire survival plan.","As long as he was alive, all other things could be reclaimed. Thus, his most critical plan in case his life was in danger would be to either send the necklace or Jack into a highly safe and secure location, and slowly rebuild strength.","He then dismissed that plan entirely. Logic and reason dictated that he have further contingencies in place while he attempted to retake control of his main body. However, Lex was not an emotionless A.I. operating solely on logic. His emotions and drive were not weaknesses, they were one of the foundations of his strength.","Instead of wasting time, resources and opportunities on alternatives, he’d rather focus 100% of all his resources on the plan for his return. His tenet was of supremacy, and although Lex was hardly ever ruthless or merciless in his actions, he didn’t necessarily view supremacy as being the same as a ruthless dictatorship.","Now that he was provoked, however, not through his friends and workers being in danger, but himself, Lex had been exposed to a side of himself he had never experienced before. When the Midnight Battalion was trapped, Lex had been consumed by fury. Heck, he’d even threaten the damn Henali alliance itself inside the Origin realm with Earth Immortal level missiles, putting his own life at risk along the way.","When Almira was trapped, Lex had once again been infuriated and acted with extreme prejudice.","Now that he himself was trapped, oddly enough, he was not overcome with a blinding fury. Instead, the spark of his ambition had been lit into a roaring inferno. He hated not Stalker, his enemy, but reflected on his own shortcomings. Ever since reaching the Heaven Immortal realm, his cautiousness had decreased and he had been bolder in his actions.","That in itself was not a mistake. The mistake was that he felt himself strong enough, and his efforts to strengthen himself had remained steady. What he should have done, instead, was increase his efforts manifold. After all, the amount and extent of training he could endure as a Heaven Immortal was far greater than before.","His strength had increased, his vision and perspective had evolved, but his drive to reach new levels of power had stayed the same because he felt that he was good enough. Well, reality had reminded him of just how mistaken he was.","Thus, while he did not usually provoke others for no reason, things had changed. Lex had a new plan for how to grow stronger, and he would follow it through! If getting his hands on even more divine ore could help that plan, then he would do so.","Not to mention, absorbing divine energy trapped within that ore was somehow strengthening his paladin powers, which was in contradiction to Lex’s understanding of the paladin path. Only by experimenting further on it could he fully understand why that was so. For both of those reasons, Jack did not hesitate. Yes, provoking countless Deities was not the smartest play. However, this was the Folklore realm - one of the strongest and strangest realms in the universe. Even Deities had to tuck their tails and behave here - especially if they were foreigners.","Jack conveniently ignored the fact that he, too, was technically a foreigner. With a crew filled with locals, and his connection to the seven Dragon Dao Lords, he was basically the equivalent of an ’immigrant’ who had acquired the ’passport’ of this realm and become a citizen through back channels.","\"Do you realize what you are doing?\" roared an angry missionary as he stared at the Jolly rancher with eyes filled with anger and hate. He was not alone. In recent months, the Jolly rancher had been stealing from all followers of all foreign Deities, offending many. Fortunately, they only stuck to stealing and not killing.","As a result, however, of offending so many, the Jolly Rancher was now surrounded by over a hundred missionaries from different Deities, all of them at varying power levels. One of them was even a Celestial Immortal! As it happened, the Celestial Immortal was the head of this proselytization mission, and was also the one who had screamed.","Jack, who stood at the bow of the ship, however, only smirked as he looked at the missionary, not a hint of fear on his expression.","\"Why are you getting so angry?\" Jack asked casually. \"I thought that as a follower of Oracle, you were meant to be calm and logical at all times. Such an absurd display of emotions... isn’t it blasphemous to Oracle himself?\"","The missionary was suddenly embarrassed, and filled with conflicting emotions as he realized his mistake. Yet before he could respond, he felt a connection from Oracle, and quickly gave over control of his body to his lord.","\"Pirate Jack the Pocket Calamity, for what reason have you chosen to make enemies of us?\" Oracle asked through the body of his missionary, maintaining a cold and emotionless voice.","Jack’s lip twitched. The Pocket Calamity? What the hell was that? He didn’t remember getting such a ridiculous nickname. The utterance of such a nickname elicited a far greater reaction from him than the actual encirclement of his ship.","\"Enemies? I don’t see my actions as making enemies of you all. If that were the case, I would not have spared your missionaries to inflict maximum damage to your operations,\" Jack responded calmly, despite the agitation he was feeling.","Within the ship, Bob watched his captain and engrained his every action in his heart. Bob had merely wanted to destroy his enemies, but the captain had taken the slower, more ruthless method of slowly draining them dry by allowing their missionaries to live, turning them from assets into liabilities that needed to be protected.","Such tactical genius was truly magenta!","\"You have disrupted standard proselytizing operations, stolen high value, irreplaceable treasures and affected the spread of all faiths. If such actions do not qualify as treating us as enemies, what exact category do you place them under?\" Oracle asked, not feeling the slightest bit of astonishment at the blatant audacity of the Pocket Calamity.","\"Naturally, I consider it free and fair competition for limited resources in a free market,\" Jack responded with a hint of disdain in his voice, as if he was speaking to an amateur. \"The resources you covet are followers and their unwavering faith. The resources I need are the treasures made from the divine ore and their contained divine energy. While it seems that puts us at fundamental odds, in reality I am giving you a platform upon which to acquire more followers.","\"Promises without demonstration or tangible feedback won’t get you much in the way of followers - at least not in the Folklore realm. But with a formidable opponent to overcome, you can expand the limits of your associated fables within this realm.","\"In simple words... right now, you’re nothing more than talk. If you want to succeed in the Folklore realm, you need your own legends that were crafted within this realm. If you can’t even overcome me, then you’ll never be able to establish a foundation in this place.","\"So, the way I’m looking at it, I’m providing you with an invaluable service! Without my help, you’d never be able to properly embed yourself into the fabric of this realm. No need to thank me for my services, your treasures will be enough.\"","Within the ship, Bob wiped his tears with his baguette as he memorized the effortless way in which the captain infuriated those blasphemers. It was too beautiful.","Outside, Oracle observed Jack for a few silent moments, emotionlessly judging the content of his words, not minding his shamelessness.","\"Very well, then,\" he finally said as his consciousness slowly began to fade, allowing his priest to retake control. \"Let us carry out this so-called ’free and fair competition for resources’.\"","That was the signal for all the missionaries who began their assault on the Jolly Rancher. If this was free and fair, then it was time to put it to an end. Jack, however, merely smiled. How could he be worried about this attack when he had put so much effort into making sure it happened?","Going around stealing treasures was all well and good, but making all the loot come to him was the hallmark of a true pirate- eh, no, he meant, he would continue to assist these Deities by serving as a formidable presence in the fables of their associated faiths for years to come.","\"If the flap of a butterfly’s wings can cause a tornado, do you want to see what my wings can do?\" he asked softly, not that he was expecting a reply."]},{"number":2334,"title":"Chapter 2334: Charity","paragraphs":["Countless missionaries and agents from various Deities attacked the Jolly Rancher, but Jack did not even move. He just stood atop the mantle of the ship, smiling at them confidently.","\"Good job, Rose. You don’t need to worry about the fight or anything else. Just keep protecting yourself,\" Jack said after a moment, looking down at the ship.","The silhouette of a woman made from the same bark as the ship appeared next to Jack with her arms crossed.","\"Why do I get the feeling that you’re using me?\" she asked doubtfully.","Jack, in response, shook his head.","\"Ridiculous. Just watch as I take care of these guys. You just focus on defending yourself. I’ll make sure to eliminate the threat without your help, even if it means laying down my life,\" Jack said, his words filled with overflowing passion. Rose looked at him sceptically, but could not determine if he was being honest.","To date, neither Lex nor Jack had actually seen the true body of a Trelop. All of them fused themselves with various geographical features, some taking over forests, mountains, lakes and so on. They would then use materials from those geographical locations to build a substitute body through which they talked and conversed.","Rose, on the other hand, was a little different, which had caused her to become an outcast among her people. She could not fuse with geographical features or locations. Instead, she could fuse with objects!","Jack wasn’t sure why the distinction existed. Both were dead, right? And if looked at from a macro perspective, both could be simply referred to as objects. However, the distinction existed nonetheless.","But what was an embarrassment and humiliating for Rose was extremely useful for Jack. The Jolly Rancher was not just an object, nor was just a ship. It was a vessel that had been enhanced by his own fairy dust, enchanted by the Humanoid Alliance, and it had accompanied the crew on various adventures. Within the Foklore realm, the ship alone had legends of its own!","However, since Jack himself was merely an Earth Immortal, he could not make full use of all that the ship offered. With Rose fusing with the ship, however, she could both protect herself and, if she really wanted to, help them out in a fight.","She had a vague suspicion that she was being used, but the crew appeared quite genuine so she couldn’t determine if she was just being overly cautious. For example, instead of staying back and waiting for her to help, Jack really did fly into the fray.","The others did not hold back either. Whether it was the Drama-cat, the gnome, the hamster, the bear cub, the owl, the unicorn or the crystal alligator, they all fought. Surprisingly, the three mysterious beings who only referred to themselves as Boblings also fought, and they were quite powerful.","The extent of their power was a mystery, but it was clear that this fight did not put any pressure on them. In such a situation, if she truly did nothing but protect herself and let them fight to protect her, she’d feel incredibly guilty.","With that thought, she flew the ship straight into the Celestial Immortal. While her own realm was nowhere near that level, the vessel she had bonded with was made of materials that were more than sturdy enough to deal with him.","Oracle’s missionary glared at Jack with red, hate-filled eyes, yet before he could attack him, the damned ship slammed into his body, knocking him back.","For a Celestial Immortal, such a hit did no harm... ordinarily. In this case, as soon as the ship slammed into him, one of the wooden boards of the ship pried loose, wrapped itself around the necklace made from divine ore he was wearing, and snatched it before his body could fly away.","In a single exchange, his personal body shield made of Celestial Immortal energy had been torn through, and his personal equipment had been stolen. Something like that had never happened before in his life, stunning him in place!","It couldn’t be helped. It wasn’t that Rose had a secret weapon - it was that the Jolly Rancher itself was an ultimate weapon!","The other missionaries did not have it any easier. Pebbles ignored every attack shot his way and kept biting through protective shields to swallow up the divine ore equipment, storing them all in his cheeks.","Longbeard used his expanding beard to whip and stall enemies while Ollie snuck through the shadow plane to them grabbing their equipment and running away.","Tiny-Sparkles shot out rainbows from his horn like bazookas, aiming to cause maximum carnage while Goldilocks and the Crystal alligator turned their enemies into their associated elements and snatched their equipment.","For the missionaries, this was meant to be a fight to the death, but the pirates couldn’t care less about that. They only focused on stealing treasures, as per their captains orders.","Speaking of their captain, Jack still stood on the bow of the ship, watching with his arms crossed even as he flapped his wings rapidly.","He was a paladin and had paladin powers. But, as with all races, the method of using them was unique to his specific race. To be more specific, he could use his powers identically to how Lex used them, but if he used his wings as a conduit for his powers, the effect was greatly amplified.","In this battle, Jack did not bother fighting. Instead, he had gone back to the roots of his cultivation. Once upon a time, Lex’s defense was the best and most unquestionable aspect of his cultivation. That was hardly the case anymore, as was evident from his recent defeat.","He had been coasting through his cultivation, relying on the lingering effects of Regal Embrace.","Well, he had decided to change that now. He would once again put conscious effort into his defence. He found it absolutely unbearable that his defeat had come at the hands of a Celestial Apex - even if he was a Sovereign . Losing to a Dao Lord or Demi-Dao Lord would have been acceptable. But a mere Celestial Apex? Absolutely humiliating.","Thus, Jack stood there, and focused solely on defenses. To be specific, he built barriers using his paladin powers, protecting his crew, and restricting the enemies, causing them endless waves of frustration.","Even their miracles seemed fake and ineffective in front of Jack, for both of them were relying on divine energy. After all, paladins could also control divine energy.","Thus, Jack used his powers to enact one of Geeves’ dreams, albeit in a slightly different fashion. Geeves dreamed of frustrating enemies till they coughed up blood by having his suits have such a formidable defense.","In this case, while he lacked those suits, Lex still frustrated his enemies with his unwavering, ever present defenses that kept his crew completely protected. The fight which should have been an epic struggle, eventually concluding in the victory of the Deities, ridding them of the pest of pirates, was going in a very different direction.","In secret, there were countless observers there, watching the play to see how it panned out. Nothing was more valuable in the Folklore realm than a good story - nothing - and so how this confrontation was resolved would have drastic consequences.","As it was, the legend of the Pocket Calamity had already begun to spread. The nickname, first uttered by Oracle, had been heard by countless, and would no doubt spread across the land.","For bravely facing countless missionaries all the while protecting a certain member of their group, and coming out as the victor would ensure that soon, the magic of the Folklore realm would begin to affect them. Even the Deities did not know the extent of the consequences this fight would have.","As the fight continued, the moment that the crew had acquired every single present piece of divine ore treasure, they retreated onto the ship. When the missionaries tried to follow them, they found that a massive barrier was blocking their entry!","Moreover, because the treasure containing all their divine energy had been stolen, they were all weakened. Missionaries and zealots who relied on the grace of their associated Deity were extremely powerful when empowered by their Deity, and significantly weakened without that connection.","In a different realm, those treasures were the only source of connection to their Deities. Without them, they were much weaker than even ordinary cultivators - it was the price they paid for easy growth.","\"Thank you all for your generous donations to our welfare fund. Your charitable intentions have been noted down, and will surely be rewarded in the afterlife. As much as I would like to continue accepting your generous hospitality, we have other donors who are anxiously waiting for our arrival. Thus, I bid you farewell.\"","The two gravity eels chained to the ship suddenly gained a flood of energy - to be specific, Jack channeled the harvested divine energy into them, causing them to suddenly fly out into the air as if they had boosters tied to their rears.","The missionaries hopped out of the way for they could not tolerate getting slammed by the Jolly Rancher, proving that they could have left whenever they wanted. Their encirclement became a huge joke - a joke witnessed by countless people, soon to be spread across the realm."]},{"number":2335,"title":"Chapter 2335: I swear","paragraphs":["Months went by, and eventually the notorious pirate crew that had recently come to be known as the Pocket Pirates - much to Jack’s utter dismay - suddenly disappeared. The observers had no idea, but the various Deities and missionaries knew the full extent of the harm he had done to them.","In total, he had stolen almost 400 kgs of the purified, divine metal that made up the various treasures they’d made after getting their hands on divine ore. In truth, that was an absurd amount! Jack literally had more divine metal than quite a few Dao Lords and most Deities!","The meager number should not fool anyone - this was an extremely rare resource that was difficult to come by - especially since the Artica realm closed its borders due to the war - and due to the immense competition, most did not get their hands on much to begin with.","Some Deities literally tried to ally with the Dao Lords of the realm to exact their sweet vengeance on that pirate, but that is when they discovered that in the Folklore realm, people did not respect power. No, they didn’t respect money or status either. The only thing they respected was a good story, and Jack the Pocket Calamity had good stories.","From his trip into the River Styx, or how he struck a deal with the Dragon Dao Lords, to how he had played with Deities like they were puppets, Jack had a lot of good stories, and the potential for a whole lot more of them.","So none of them received help, no matter how they asked or tried to persuade. Of course, it could also just be that no one wanted to provoke seven Dragon Dao Lords just in case they thought fondly of him. Who could say?","Jack himself had no idea, for after accumulating enough divine metal, he went into hiding. He needed to absorb that divine energy, strengthen his cultivation, and try to send the metal all the way to Lex. Since he’d done it once before, he figured he might be able to do it again.","Thus, he took the smallest, most invaluable treasure of the lot he had stolen and began his experiments. He drained the divine energy till the treasure was basically empty, and then began to bond with it.","The process was slow, but surprisingly smooth. He thought that breaking a Deity’s connection to the tool would be incredibly hard, but he forgot that miracles did not need to make sense, and that he was practically swimming in the energy that granted miracles.","The issue, however, was that miracles could not be granted on demand. Once he bonded with the treasure, he focused on what he wanted. He focused on sending the divine metal to the piece of his soul fused with the necklace - to send it within the Gilded Hollow. Yet it was easier said than done.","The last time he achieved such a thing, it had been by accident. This time, trying to do it on purpose, especially when his target was potentially within an extremely difficult to find, closed off place, was not something he could do so easily.","Jack was not one to quit so easily, though, so he continued to try, and slowly a few more months passed. His focus had not wavered this entire time, yet something happened that suddenly diverted his attention.","A contingency that he had put into place had been triggered. Z was undergoing the Heaven Immortal tribulation! That was... faster than Lex had expected.","Although neither Jack nor Lex could sense Z’s location, he could sense the activation of his contingency, which likely meant that the kid was doing alright. Heck, if he was breaking through to the Heaven Immortal realm, he was probably better than alright.","Across realms, maybe even across universe’s, Lex and Jack smiled at the same time. If that lazy child was working so hard, then Lex had no excuse not to work harder. He closed his eyes, closed his mind, and focused on nothing else. It was not a matter of whether it could be done or not - impossibility did not exist. He would send the divine metal over to the necklace, make the necklace far stronger than it currently was, and reclaim everything he had lost.","Jack’s wings began to flap, and the divine energy from the various treasures around him began to flow out and pour into his body. Overhead, the dark clouds of a Major tribulation began to gather as Jack teetered on the boundary of ascension.","*****","It had not been an easy journey, not only because of his predicament, but because Z always refused to take his help. He marched on the battlefield with an army, but all they ever did was play music for him while he honed himself on the battlefield.","They called him the Mad Slave. They called him one who had lost all reason, and even the will to live. They called him many things, but what they did not know was that Z was none of those things. From the start, he had only focused on one thing - matching up to the standard of Lex.","Maybe, one day, he hoped he could be stronger than him, but if not then at least being his equal would suffice. Yet if that was the case, how could he accept help? How could he walk the easy path, the path that everyone else walked?","So then today, or rather, these past few months, when he faced an enemy he could not defeat directly, what did he choose to do? Naturally, he spent the month carefully positioning everyone, orchestrating the battle directly and indirectly, to bring himself face to face with the strongest opponent. Then? Well naturally, he learned from Lex, and used a Major tribulation to defeat his enemy.","On a distant mountain, the Slave Army stood, playing a number of instruments as if Z’s personal orchestra as lightning rained down from the sky, the thunder almost synchronising with the music.","Standing in the center of a scorched wasteland, Z heard an unexpected voice inside his mind.","\"If you’re hearing this, then that means I’m not around for your Heaven Immortal tribulation,\" spoke Lex in a very casual tone. \"I doubt the lightning and fire tribulations should be an issue for you, but let me give you a piece of advice for the Spirit tribulation. Do not trust the voices on the obelisk.\"","The voice sounded like something that had been recorded as an afterthought, and it caused Z to click his tongue. Why the hell was he so casual about the lightning and fire tribulation? Those things could literally kill immortals!","Z didn’t have time to waste on Lex’s nonchalance. Instead, he activated one of his new forms that he had created after years of study and practice.","\"I swear to the Innkeeper, if he’s chilling somewhere sipping a pina colada...\" Z muttered. He did not finish the thought, mainly because he could not afford to distract himself. The lightning was coming for him.","*****","Lex smiled as he felt his contingency for Z activate, but he didn’t think about it for long. While Jack was trying to send him divine metal to improve the necklace further, Lex had been devouring the resources of the Gilded Hollow like a black hole.","Not only was he strengthening and restructuring the necklace, he was also adding things to the space inside. He had ground up resources until they were fine sand and poured them inside the space in the necklace, forming a bed of grey and black sand.","He added countless organic and inorganic material inside, and then unleashed concentrated spirit essence, forming a sea of spirit essence within the necklace. The weight of the essence would, over time, turn the sand into stone and provide him with the perfect foundation upon which to continue developing the space inside the necklace, and enhance his fake realm.","At the same time, he gathered items which contained trapped fragments of law, and used them to create pillars within his fake realm. For now, he let them stay as they were, but he would eventually use them to establish an artificially designed set of laws for his realm.","After years of devouring, the necklace had undergone a significant evolution, the likes of which he could not have even imagined. He had already surpassed his original plan - the one he had formed before he knew he could enter the Gilded Hollow.","What did that mean? That meant that, theoretically, the necklace could already produce the amount of strength Lex thought he might need to exact his revenge. Now, he was developing it even more .","Lex suddenly paused, and interrupted his thoughts, when he sensed something on the very boundary of his spirit sense. He’d already gotten used to the Gilded Hollow so far, and had not encountered a single danger that could actually threaten him at all - not that he took things lightly because of that.","He would not make such a basic mistake. How could a realm that could kill Dao Lords ever be simple? That’s why, the moment he sensed something unusual, he paused immediately. Yet upon investigation, he found that what he sensed was not a threat.","Instead, it was a message in a bottle."]},{"number":2336,"title":"Chapter 2336: How boring","paragraphs":["The cultivation world was far more complex and developed than Lex had imagined back when he was a mortal, which is why the sheer simplicity of finding a message in a bottle stunned Lex. It seemed that certain classics just never got old.","He approached the deep green bottle, and swept it with his spirit sense to investigate it thoroughly to make sure that it wasn’t some kind of trap. As far as he could tell, the bottle was a treasure with only two functions. The first was to preserve the message inside, so that the dauntless flow of time did not render it unrecognisable and illegible. The second function appeared to be one that completely suppressed the bottle’s aura, karma or anything of the sort. It seemed that whoever had put the message inside was trying to hide it from someone or something, but that also seemed unlikely. After all, the bottle was still easily identifiable and detectable, not to mention the contents could be easily seen.","Just to be safe, Lex created a basic golem using some nearby materials and had it open the bottle cork. Yet nothing happened - there was no attack, no sinister plot or curse. The golem took out the letter written on a very high quality parchment, and read it on behalf of Lex.","Surprisingly, the words on the paper were from the Soul script - a certain language that anyone with a soul could read without issue, regardless of cultivation level!","’ To all survivors,","If you are reading this, then you fit into one of two categories. Either, like me, you have become stuck inside the Gilded Hollow, unable to exit for one reason or another. Or enough time has passed, and the Gilded Hollow has opened once more, allowing you to enter anew.","Actually, I just realized that you could also be a descendant of two or more of either of those groups who was born inside the Gilded Hollow. Damn, I can’t erase this. Just forget everything I said before. In essence, as long as you are alive, and inside the Gilded Hollow, this letter is for you.","My name is Romulus Valecar, and I have taken it upon myself to establish a bastion for all. You may already know this, but the Gilded Hollow is not as straightforward or simple as it appears. The more resources you take and absorb, the more positive karma you will accumulate within our universe. Unfortunately, not only is that positive karma useless within the Gilded Hollow, it will actually make you a target of the Hollow itself!*","I have tentatively taken to calling my self created bastion Fortune city, wishing good luck and fortune upon its residents. Why this matters to you is because I have established ways in which you may survive in Fortune city, even if you are being targeted by the Gilded Hollow.","All are welcome to Fortune city, and whether you wish to merely survive, or contribute to the city is entirely up to you and won’t be forced on anyone.**","The question, you must now be wondering, is how you may find Fortune city. I have prepared two means of achieving as such, though which one works for you is based on your own luck. The first is a teleportation character at the base of this letter. You only need to channel your energy into it, and the character will teleport you to its destination, which is Fortune city.","If, for any reason at all, the character fails to work, then you will have to rely on the second, slower and more dangerous method of locating the city. Basically, the message bottle this message came in can be used as a compass. Any time you spin it on the ground, it will point directly towards Fortune city.","That’s about all I can offer you so good luck on your journey. Since you have had the opportunity to encounter this bottle, may you also have the fortune of meeting me.","Best Regards,","Romulus Valecar.","*In case you have not realized yet, the Gilded Hollow, whatever it is, seems to have a will of its own. That will is locked in a fierce competition with the laws of the Vaelûn, and we all have become unwitting pawns in that competition. The more you take from the Hollow, the more Vaelûn will reward you, and the more the Hollow will hate you. That hate is the primary source of danger with this realm, so beware!","**Naturally, the city will have some basic laws to maintain civility and stable operations. Those who break those laws are not welcome, and may be punished with any number of punishments including, but not limited to, docking of pay, loss of food rights, lack of worker protection, the cone of shame etc. ’","Lex blinked, and then used the golem to hand himself the letter as he read it again just to be sure. This letter seemed to provide him with great insight into the Gilded Hollow, answering some of his questions while raising even more.","It was his understanding that the Gilded Hollow was a remnant of the Pentagal universe. If that was the case, it made sense that their universe was trying to absorb it, while this remnant was trying to resist.","By bringing people from the universe into the Hollow, they allowed Vaelûn to gain the advantage at the risk of provoking the will of Pentagal - if that’s what this truly was. Actually, this explained why things got so dangerous here, for the dangers he’d encountered so far were quite manageable.","Just how many resources must one devour to be targeted by this place or realm? If that was the case, the higher the cultivation level, the more likely one would be targeted by the Hollow, for they’d be more effective at taking resources.","Also, it seemed that it was possible to meet others in this place - if that weren’t the case, then the letter would not make sense. How could Romulus build a city and populate it if he was alone?","The question now was, did Fortune city still exist? He could not estimate just how old this letter was, for he had no accurate idea for how long it had been since the Hollow last opened. If that was the case, the chances that Freedom city had ceased to exist were pretty slim.","Lex rubbed his chin for a moment, and then tried to activate the teleportation character. As he expected, the character failed to work.However, when he spun the bottle, it consistently pointed in a certain direction.","Since he was just traveling randomly while harvesting resources, it didn’t matter to him if he started to follow the compass’ directions. In fact, if Freedom city still existed, or even just the ruins of it, then the chances of encountering resources above his current cultivation were pretty high.","Also, he was quite curious about why certain people had been unable to exit the Hollow. He did not want a repeat of that happening to him. Thus, he began flying while following the direction the bottle pointed.","While traveling, he did not reduce his flying or resource harvesting speed, though he wondered if the remnant will of Pentagal was still active. He’d taken quite a lot, but he didn’t feel like he was being targeted at all.","Still, he did not lower his guard.","The repetitive monotony of his harvesting situation made it so entire months went by without anything notable happening, causing him to feel like time was passing him by too quickly. It was like water, slipping through his fingers, escaping no matter how he tightened his grip.","Yet that monotony was accompanied by the feeling of progress and growth.","The necklace continued to grow stronger and sturdier every day, right up until one day, Jack succeeded. He managed to send a piece of divine metal through his soul - using up a fair bit of divine energy!","But Jack had a tremendous amount of divine energy stored up in various treasures, so he didn’t mind utilizing it like this either!","Lex smiled, and fused the divine metal into the necklace, causing it to gain just the slightest bit of weight. Yet that seemingly insignificant amount of weight strengthened the necklace immeasurably, increasing the necklaces’ threshold to accommodate miracles within itself!","At that moment, Lex could not help but lament that he didn’t have the system to help him at that moment. He didn’t require the system for the Midnight Inn. Rather, he was beginning to miss its ability to bring him a tremendous amount of trouble - or more specifically, he missed its ability to bring him face to face with the greatest opportunity in his vicinity.","The Gilded Hollow hid a lot more secrets than just Fortune city and the clash between two wills. If only he had the system to get him into trouble like that randomly, then his gains from this place would be so much greater. As it was, he was stuck swallowing up resources without any significant interruptions or unlikely challenges. How boring."]},{"number":2337,"title":"Chapter 2337: Immature thoughts","paragraphs":["While flying, improving his necklace, and harvesting more resources, Lex also began to address one of his most important concerns. He had no idea how long the barrier around his actual body would hold. Heck, for all he knew, it might have already been broken!","If, previously, he had some faint connection or understanding of what was happening around his body, now he could not sense it at all! He had a feeling that his stalker had put up some isolation barriers to make them harder to find - an understandable series of actions considering that Lex was supposed to be under the Innkeeper’s protection.","What he did not know was that the reason for more isolation formations was not the Innkeeper, but the fact that his body kept getting feedback from Jack’s and his own actions.","Previously, there was nothing he could do about it. Even if the barrier was broken, Lex could not do anything about it simply because he had no confidence in facing him.","Now, Lex had addressed the few fundamental issues that limited the necklace’s ability to allow him to use his full strength. He’d also added a preliminary framework for his new Domination and altered the necklace enough where it could allow him to fight his stalker without getting suppressed the way he was previously.","That did not mean Lex was in a rush to go fight him - far from it. He had been so heavily suppressed in the previous fight that Lex doubted he’d seen the full extent of his stalker’s powers. Thus, what was originally his full plan to get revenge had now become his bare minimum.","Jack’s transference of the divine metal from his body to the necklace proved that the divine metal could move from one soul to another. Thus, his first task right now was to establish a connection between the necklace and his main body. He wanted to make it so that as soon as the barrier broke, or at least when his body or soul were in danger, he’d be able to sense it so that he could transport himself over.","Ensuring such a thing was easier said than done, but he had to do it anyway. However, that was merely a contingency plan. His best bet would be to stay in the Gilded Hollow for as long as possible and strengthen the necklace as much as he could.","While his own strength was, technically, not growing by doing this, the means available to him became more diversified, and he’d be better capable of reacting to different situations.","He remembered that back in Abaddon he’d done something similar. He’d created a Lawcraft that could only be used in Abaddon - the Abaddon Inn! While not exactly the same, the premise was still that within the Abaddon Inn he’d have greater control.","It was not something he tried again because a similar Lawcraft was much harder to design outside Abaddon. However, he had not considered creating a treasure that could allow him to do something similar. The reason was that usually Lex preferred to strengthen himself rather than relying on treasures. Besides, he had Naraka and the Karmic Bead.","Making another treasure of similar quality would not be an easy task, so he had not done it at all. Well now, he had no choice. At least the necklace was not strictly an external tool, since it was a part of himself.","Connecting to his main body also wasn’t something that could be achieved easily, not to mention that transporting to his main body would take up an immense amount of divine energy.","Thus, Lex and Jack worked in unison. Lex tried to forge a connection between the necklace and the main body so that it could be sensed easily, while Jack began working on sending a piece of divine metal that was filled to the brim with divine energy.","Whether he returned in response to an emergency, or he gained all he could from the Hollow, his preparation now would be the foundation of his return in the future.","As for his chances of reaching Fortune city...","Lex looked at the glass bottle in his hand that kept changing directions slightly every time he crossed a certain checkpoint, and then looked at his surroundings. Not a single speck of land in the Gilded Hollow lacked valuable resources.","Whether it was rare herbs growing as commonly as grass, forests filled with trees that were rarer than rare, or barren mountains that were actually entirely made up of valuable ore, the Hollow had it all! Honestly, even though the resources were on the level of Heaven Immortal, the sheer quantity of them, not to mention their high quality, made Lex feel extremely satisfied.","In fact, he was beginning to not mind the peaceful nature of harvesting so many resources without any real trouble. Sure, some of the forests fought back, and sure some of the mountains tried to eat him. But so what?","To him, that was still peaceful. He shouldn’t be ungrateful for the rare moment of peace he was having. Actually, considering how much trouble he was in, it would be less than ideal if he got pulled into the greater dangers of the Gilded Hollow. His previous thoughts of boredom were somewhat immature.","He calmed himself down, and continued to enjoy the plentiful harvest.","Lex shot through the sky like a shooting star, pulling up all resources within a certain range of himself without reserve, creating quite the spectacle, making him hard to ignore. Considering that he hadn’t really run into any other sentient beings - or at least beings that weren’t entirely controlled by their instincts - he had no intentions of stopping.","Off in the distance, however, a snake suddenly opened its eyes, noticing the odd situation.","\"What the hell is going on? Is that imbecile not afraid of the Hollow’s retribution?\" she asked, filled with equal parts horror and shock. Her gaze locked onto the figure at the center of the phenomenon, and suddenly she was stunned. That aura... it was so different? Who was this person?","At the same time, Lex felt someone’s gaze falling upon him, and he paused, immediately locking in on the beast staring at him. A mere glance was all he needed to see through her entirely. After all, she was merely in the middle of the Heaven Immortal realm.","\"A primordial earth serpent? The race seems to be right, but she lacks all primordial aura... a descendant? But wouldn’t that cause a mutation in the race?\" Lex muttered.","Primordial beings were those that were born at the beginning of the universe. Their descendants, while carrying some of their traits, could no longer take on the same exact race as their ancestors. The closest they could come to their ancestors was to reach the level of Mythic beings - the beings that were usually born at the birth of a realm. Mythic beings had the highest possible talent and bloodline potential in modern day.","So why was this snake... an exact primordial race while still lacking all primordial aura? How interesting."]},{"number":2338,"title":"Chapter 2338: Lord Fortune","paragraphs":["The moment Lex spotted the snake, the snake felt an unprecedented sense of terror, as if its life and death had already been determined! In her entire life, even in the occasional times she suffered through the Hollow’s retribution, she had not felt this kind of danger!","The grey scales on her body gently curved, creating sharp edges along her body so that whatever touched her would be cut by her scales, yet it would hardly be useful here. Before she could even think of escape, the figure appeared right in front of her.","He looked like a human, but she had never met a human this terrifying, not to mention the aura around him was too unfamiliar.","\"Senior, I apologize!\" she immediately exclaimed, not bothering with any pretense whatsoever! \"I did not mean anything! I did not mean to criticise!\"","She closed her eyes and bowed her head, as if to show complete deferral. Out in the wilds, there was no law and order. Her life and death were entirely in the hands of this human, she knew that well. Without any tools that could help her escape, she could only hope that this senior was merciful.","Lex smiled amusedly. He could tell that the snake in front of him likely anticipated that he could read her thoughts easily, so all her thoughts were about completely giving up any desire to fight back.","\"Be at ease. I didn’t come here to harm you, I just came here for some information. You’re the first sentient being I’ve seen since I entered the Gilded Hollow,\" Lex said casually. He was not concerned about leaking his information because in front of him, this snake could not resist at all.","Upon hearing his swords, the snake was stunned, and then her eyes widened!","\"You... you’re from Vaelûn!\" she suddenly exclaimed, naming the universe itself as if it were no big deal. In fact, even Lex was stunned to hear it.","Even if he had not already known the name, as a native of Vaelûn, the moment he heard the name he would know it belonged to his universe. The issue was that hardly anyone ever took the name directly. He wasn’t sure if there were any taboos related to it.","Even if there were, it seemed they didn’t exist within the Hollow.","\"Yes, and it appears to me that you’re someone from the Gilded Hollow,\" Lex said as he observed her curiously. \"That’s quite strange. According to the information I had before coming in, no one has ever encountered another person in the Hollow before, and the chances for anyone to survive in the Hollow are slim to none.\"","The snake heard Lex’s words in a daze, and then suddenly felt a surge of excitement fill her.","\"Do you- does that mean... is it really? The Gilded Hollow has opened once more?\" she asked, the sheer excitement filling her making her somewhat incoherent.","\"Yes, it has been a few years. I’m not sure how long the Gilded Hollow will remain open. It seems you know quite a lot about it,\" said Lex, his words carrying a certain meaning of their own.","The snake suddenly recovered from her shock and realized what the senior was hinting at. He wanted her to give him information about this place! That wasn’t a problem at all! Excitement started to tingle her scale, causing her to almost shiver!","\"Yes, yes senior! Let me tell you all about it. Actually, I may not know the full history of the Gilded Hollow, but I know the gist of it,\" she said, eager to impress. \"My name is Mithon, and I was born inside the Hollow, given life by Lord Fortune, ruler of the Fortune stronghold.","\"According to the teachings of the Fortune stronghold, we are inside a place known as the Gilded Hollow, which exists inside a ’universe’ known as Vaelûn. No one knows what Vaelûn is like, except that it is not as tyrannical and difficult to survive in as the Hollow.","\"Most residents consider the teachings of Vaelûn to be a legend or fable, since most of us were born and raised in the Hollow. But since these are the teachings of Lord Fortune, none dare reject it out right. I, at least, have never met anyone from Vaelûn besides you, senior.\"","Mithon tried to give Lex a flattering, appeasing look, but a smiling snake was not exactly pleasant to look at.","\"Who is this Lord Fortune? What is the Fortune Stronghold? What are the dangers of the Hollow?\" Lex asked, cutting right to the heart of the matter.","Mithon seemed stumped, as if unsure how to answer these questions.","\"Lord Fortune is... well, he is the lord. I don’t know what other way to say it. He is the ruler of the Fortune Stronghold, the only city inside the Hollow. He is the one who has given life to almost all who live within the Hollow, with the few others being the descendants of those who also supposedly came to the Hollow from Vaelûn.","\"The Fortune stronghold is both a city and a fort, and is the only one within all of the Hollow. According to some legends, once upon a time there were many such cities and forts, but now only the Fortune stronghold has survived. I heard there were other lords as well, but I’ve never heard of them. Either they’ve died, or they all work for Lord Fortune and no longer claim any lordship.","\"I don’t know the reasons, but I can guess pretty easily. It’s probably because none other than Lord Fortune can resist... Hollow’s retribution. When it comes, Lord Fortune protects those who live within the stronghold. As for those outside, they are entirely on their own. The lucky survive, and the unlucky die. That’s all there is to it.\"","Lex frowned as he pondered her words. Was it really all just a matter of luck? What exactly was this retribution? Did no one other than Lord Fortune know how to resist it?","Before he could ask these questions, Mithon spoke on her own.","\"But now that the Gilded Hollow has opened up once more, the rules have changed!\" she exclaimed with excitement. \"The Lord Fortune taught us all. Once the Hollow opens up once more, it’ll be our one opportunity to escape this place once and for all! After all, that’s the one time where the Hollow’s retribution is suppressed to a certain extent, giving us a chance for survival!\"","Lex raised an eyebrow out of curiosity. The retribution was suppressed while the Hollow was open? Considering the fact that so many Dao Lords had died the last time it opened, believing the retribution was weakened was... a little scary."]},{"number":2339,"title":"Chapter 2339: The three retributions","paragraphs":["Lex looked at Mithon, continuously scanning her and her spirit for any signs of falsehoods, but found nothing. Everything she said was true, or at least she believed it to be true. It was quite interesting, but Lex still had more questions.","Primary among them was understanding what the Hollow’s retribution really was, since that seemed to be the primary source of danger here.","\"Calm down, you’re too excited,\" said Lex. \"Tell me about the retribution. What is it and how does it work? How can one avoid or resist it? How do you all plan on escaping the Hollow?\"","Mithon shivered, her excitement completely extinguished, as she focused on the retribution.","\"There’s only one way to avoid the retribution outside of the Fortune stronghold, and that is to go unnoticed. The reason I have survived is because I have spent the last 42 million years in dormancy, not moving, not acting, not cultivating, completely blending into the surroundings.","\"Only in that way was I able to avoid being detected by the Hollow’s retribution. But most of the time, even that isn’t enough. The best way to avoid retribution is to have no existence at all. That does not mean using some technique to hide or suppress your aura - that may work on other immortals, or even other lords, but it doesn’t work on the Gilded Hollow at all. It can always see through such techniques.\"","Lex subtly nodded. It made sense - if the Gilded Hollow was truly the remnant of another universe, and that remnant truly had some kind of will, or even instinct, then hiding from it would not be easy. Even Dao Lords were beneath the universe in power and authority, so how could their techniques deceive a universe?","But then again, that didn’t sound right either. How could one have no existence if they didn’t use any techniques? Just die for the sake of avoiding detection?","\"For example, I have been dormant in my exact location for many millions of years, not moving, not eating, not cultivating all this time. The only thing I did was to merely exist. Thus, I managed to avoid attracting the Hollow’s attention.","\"But such a method does not work for everyone. You, senior, for example, cannot use it. After harvesting so many resources, the Hollow will have most certainly noticed you. As for how to survive the retribution... I can offer you no advice. I do not know anyone other than the Fortune Lord who can survive the retribution.","\"As for what the retribution is... I can offer you some insight, based on the stories I’ve heard. The retribution is basically when the Hollow takes notice of you, and acts against you. According to the legends taught by the Fortune Lord, back when the Hollow was open, the retribution came in three different forms.","\"The first was to teleport you to a dangerous location where you may face normal dangers, but at a much higher level than yourself so that you are killed organically. The second is to transform your surroundings, turning them into an inescapable danger zone.","\"These two are the two types of retributions with the highest level of survivability - at least according to the legends. They don’t normally exist while the Hollow is closed, so I have never witnessed them before.","\"The last type of retribution is the most dangerous, and the one that we normally face. When the Hollow gathers enough energy to carry out its retribution, it targets you and takes your soul from within your body, exacting it through eight cycles of hellish torture. There is no way to escape, and the only way to survive is to endure through all eight cycles and come out the other end alive.","\" Supposedly this tribulation is weakened during the time that the Hollow is open, but I, at least, have never encountered anyone who has survived this tribulation and come out the other end. So, senior, unless you want to take a risk, I strongly recommend that you make your way to the Fortune Stronghold. It is the only place in the Hollow where the retribution cannot strike!","\"As for your question of how to escape... I actually do not know. It wasn’t taught to us in the stronghold. I have been in exile for so long for breaking the stronghold’s law, but now that I have news of the Hollow opening back up, I can return. If I am the first to bring back this good news, I am sure my exile will be forgiven, and I cannot be let back in.\"","Lex frowned. There was no way he could just lie down and do nothing - that would defeat the point of entering the Hollow. At the same time, he did not look forward to getting kidnapped and tortured without the ability to resist.","The ideal situation would be to enter the stronghold whenever the Hollow was about to strike, and leave it for harvesting resources once the Hollow’s energy was all used up.","\"I have more questions,\" Lex continued. \"When I arrived here, the laws of the Hollow were different, but my arrival seemed to cause some kind of change. Did you notice the change in laws? Wouldn’t that let you know that the Hollow has opened back up?\"","Mithon looked at Lex oddly, as if confused.","\"Isn’t that a normal situation? Wouldn’t the laws get exhausted or drained of energy if they were consistent all the time? For as long as I remember, the Hollow goes through cycles of changing laws. Sometimes it’s one set of laws, and other times it’s a different set. I’m pretty used to both.\"","Lex paused. So Mithon was used to the other set of laws as well? Did that mean... that beings from one universe could easily learn to manipulate the laws of a different one? If that was the case, wouldn’t it be easy for a universe to be invaded by another one?","Lex could not help but think back to Abaddon. He still didn’t quite understand what that place was, for its existence didn’t accurately fit in with his current understanding of the universe. He could understand that it was a place where all the problems of his universe were sealed away. The issue was... why did Abaddon spawn so many Dao Lords, and why did they die so easily there?","If the Dao Lords that spawned within Abaddon ever entered the ordinary universe, wouldn’t they all be doomed? And yet they were so easily contained. Were they even real Dao Lords?","Lex shook his head. He was getting distracted.","\"So let’s say that I want to go to the stronghold. How would I get there?\" Lex asked.","Mithon seemed extremely excited by the question, as if she had been specially waiting for it.","\"There are waypoints and waygates set up by the Fortune Lord,\" she said. \"The Fortune Lord is very powerful, and has been inside the Hollow for a very long time. When the Hollow is not carrying out its retribution, the Lord travels and explores the Hollow. But he may need to return to the stronghold at a moment’s notice if the Hollow is about to strike, so he has built countless waygates across the Hollow.","\"We only need to find the nearest waypoint, and we can use it to request teleportation to the stronghold. As long as it is accepted, we can reach there in an instant. Of course, the premise is finding such a waypoint.\"","At this point, Mithon’s expression finally turned somewhat ugly.","\"Unfortunately, I have no idea where such a waypoint may be found. I have been exiled for a long time, so the waypoint I used to be sent here has probably already moved on. We can only try our luck.\"","Lex did not comment on the ’we’ that Mithon started to say, and brought out the green bottle and briefly told her about the letter it contained.","\"Do you think the bottle will point towards a waypoint?\" he asked.","Mithon shook her head.","\"It sounds like this is a really old relic, from before Lord Fortune actually established the stronghold, let alone the waypoints. With nothing else to go on, this is a decent option. But traveling through the Hollow will take a long time without depending on the waypoints. The Hollow may well close before we even reach the Fortune stronghold if we travel normally.\"","Lex nodded. He was extremely curious about this Fortune Lord. Not only could he resist the Hollow, but he created a primordial race beast without access to any Primordial energy.","Considering that he could not gauge the difficulty of the retributions, finding the stronghold had gone up pretty high on his list of priorities. Since a waygate was not easy to find, and the stronghold itself was too far to travel normally, Lex would need to get a little creative in searching for it.","\"Don’t move. Let me try something,\" said Lex as he waved his hand, and summoned the Karmic Bead. If the Fortune Lord had given birth to, or even simply created Mithon, then his karma with the snake should be pretty massive, right?"]},{"number":2340,"title":"Chapter 2340: Treasures of the Gilded Hollow","paragraphs":["Lex had to admit, besides just protection from the retribution, and curiosity about the only city in Gilded Hollow, he had another reason for wanting to find the stronghold. If he could find higher quality resources, that would be ideal. Specifically, he was searching for something unique or significantly powerful.","Lex didn’t believe that a place as rich and vast as the Hollow lacked resources that were uniquely valuable even in the context of everything else they were offering. Information and leads on things like that would be easier to find in a city, not to mention that the city had gateways that accessed different areas of the Gilded Hollow.","Despite anticipating that Mithon’s karma with the Fortune Lord was strong, he did not actually plan on probing, or even properly examining that. It went without saying that the Fortune Lord was most likely a Dao Lord, and Lex was not dumb enough to invite death upon himself by touching the karma of a Dao Lord.","Examining Mithon’s karma should give him some options, though, and he could search for the stronghold based on that. Yet when he used the Karmic Bead to examine Mithon, he was only one thread of karma - his own!","Mithos had not a single other thread connected to him, as if he’d never done anything else in his entire life, nor had he met anyone else. Lex was stunned, and tried to guess what this meant. Was everything he heard from Mithon a lie? Or had he imagined everything?","That didn’t seem possible.","He thought back to when Mithon said that to survive, he needed to have no existence at all. Had staying still in one place without doing anything erased all his karmic ties? That seemed quite unbelievable. So then was it something about the Gilded Hollow that erased her karma?","Lex narrowed his eyes as he caught onto something. To Mithon, the changing of laws was a natural and regular occurrence. Lex couldn’t quite understand why such a thing happened just yet, but it was possible that every time the laws changed, they erased the karma on her as well?","But Lex had doubts. Based on everything he knew, it shouldn’t be possible to live within an entirely different set of laws, even if they were immortals. After all, their very bodies, souls, and even immortality itself came from the laws of the universe they were in.","Maybe it had something to do with the Fortune Lord. He might know of a way to survive such a thing.","\"It’s no use. Your karma has been completely erased, I can’t track your waygate or the stronghold through you,\" Lex said as he put away the Karmic bead.","Mithon looked at the human full of awe. She had no idea what karma was or why it could be used to track things, but it sounded powerful.","\"Well, if that doesn’t work we can search for Truth Crystals, or Memory Sphere,\" Mithon said excitedly. \"Either of them should be able to help our search.\"","Lex raised an eyebrow.","\"What’s a Truth Crystal? Or a Memory Sphere?\" he asked.","Mithon, as if anticipating such a question, answered eagerly.","\"They’re both items that are born from the laws of the Hollow. Memory Spheres are somewhat easier to find, and are less rare. They grow on regular fruit trees, but when the laws of the Hollow dominate, the trees grow those crystals instead of fruit. Of course, not all fruit trees grow them all the time. Even of the ones that grow, more than half are destroyed once the laws switch. So they’re still kind of rare.","\"A Truth Crystal is much rarer, but if we can find it, we’re basically guaranteed to find the stronghold. A Truth Crystal can answer any question truthfully, depending on the durability of the crystal. If it is extremely durable, then it can even answer some long forgotten secrets, which is why it is always in demand. However, getting an answer to a simple question like the location of the nearest waygate should be simple enough for even the weakest Truth Crystals to answer.\"","Lex raised not just one eyebrow, but both. This Truth Crystal sounded like it was extremely useful.","\"The Truth Crystals grow in the dark, and shatter if they’re exposed to any kind of light at all, so they’re most commonly found in deep caves and caverns, or underground. Unlike the Memory Sphere’s, there is no fixed condition required for their creation, so you just have to search for them at random.\"","Lex looked at Mithon for a moment, and then could not help but ask a question that popped up in his head.","\"If that’s the case, can’t you use a Truth Crystal to search for the location of other, more durable Truth Crystals if you want to learn the details of a particularly difficult question?\"","Mithon nodded readily, almost like an excited puppy.","\"Yes, exactly! That’s what many people do, which is why Truth Crystals are so scarce across the Gilded Hollow. There aren’t many reserves of them left, at least in the more commonly explored parts of the Hollow, which is why everyone waits for a new cycle of transition of laws to go search for newly made ones. Unfortunately, newly formed Truth Crystals which have only experienced a single cycle of transition of laws aren’t usually very durable.\"","Lex nodded.","\"Alright, let’s move. We can talk while we travel,\" said Lex as he lifted Mithon and began traveling across the land, once more devouring any and all resources that came his way.","Watching such an unrepentant display of avarice frightened Mithon still. Her philosophy her whole life had been to be practically invisible, and to leave no traces behind. Her strength today was as a result of accumulation over time, and not through any shortcuts or resources, even when they were extremely abundant.","This was the mindset common amongst all who lived in the Hollow. The resources, while valuable, meant nothing if they would get them killed.","But now it was too late for her. Even if she told the senior human to stop - which she didn’t dare to do - it would not change the fact that she had been present when something like this had happened. She could not avoid detection - at least unless she spent countless years inside the stronghold, waiting for the traces to wear off.","\"Tell me more about the Hollow. How do you survive when the laws change? Does anything special happen? Are there any more unique or valuable treasures in the Hollow that you know about?\" Lex asked one question after another.","Mithon, despite being a Heaven Immortal, was somewhat simple minded - at least in Lex’s opinion. Maybe it had something to do with her life experiences where she had few interactions with others, and spent most of her time in hibernation. Thus, he had to be very specific in the questions he wanted to ask her.","\"Surviving the change of laws is pretty easy - anyone can do it. There’s a technique called Good Fortunes Shine through Darkness taught in the stronghold, though we just call it the Good Fortune technique. When you sense that the laws are about to change, you simply have to use the technique and you’ll survive the transition.","\"Although, on second thought, I’m not so sure if it’ll work for you. The technique might need the blessing of the Fortune Lord. I can teach it to you anyway in case you’re curious. Whether it works or not is something you’ll have to check on your own.","\"As for whether anything special happens... I’m not sure what you would qualify as special, but a lot of things definitely happen. Everything works in a different way, and it can be confusing at first, but you get used to it pretty quick.","\"To answer your question about treasures, I can easily say that there are definitely quite a lot. But if you ask me what they are, I cannot tell you. There is no systematic education system inside the stronghold beyond what the Fortune Lord wishes to teach, and most people keep anything they learn to themselves.","\"The things I can tell you are either all generic treasures that everyone knows about, or a couple of really famous stories shared through the ages. For example, one of the most famous stories is of a Redwinged Bull from over a billion transition cycles ago. It is said that he discovered a treasure so powerful that he swore that upon attaining it, he’d become a lord himself!","\"He gathered a team to be able to reach the treasure, and in the end his team even managed to finally catch sight of it. Yet what did they get after crossing the frozen wasteland where the treasure was found? As soon as the Redwinged Bull touched the black flower, his body froze and then shattered, even though he was a peak Celestial Immortal.","\"It scared everyone quite a lot, especially when the black flower was stained by the blood of the full. It was quite a gruesome si-\"","Lex froze, and then turned to look towards Mithon, his mind racing. He raised his hand and conjured up a certain picture.","\"Do you happen to know... if that flower looked like this?\""]},{"number":2341,"title":"Chapter 2341: Group project","paragraphs":["Lex felt a lot of different things at that exact moment as he displayed the image of the flower. Regix, the floating orb that had kidnapped him via his system and promised to teach him whatever he wanted if he could complete a quest for him, wanted something called the Double Yin Death Metal Rose.","When he told Lex about it, he claimed that he already had the Double Yang Disaster Rose, and wanted the other one. At the same time, he gave Lex a lot of information on this particular flower, not only allowing him to recognize it easily, but also be able to transport it without issue.","Mithon’s description of how the Redwinged Bull died upon touching the flower reminded him of it, but the chances of it being the same were too low, right? On the contrary, it was exactly because this was the Gilded Hollow that Lex suspected it might really exist here.","When he had met Regix, the orb had told him that as far as he was aware, there was only one Double Yin Death Metal Rose in the entire universe, and that it was hidden within the Nether.","But did the Gilded Hollow count as being in the same universe? He wasn’t so sure. However, because it was a remnant of another universe - at least, as far as Lex could tell - it made sense for another one to appear.","Or not. Lex wasn’t sure exactly what the qualifications were for a Double Yin Death Metal Rose to appear, but there really might be a chance for it to appear here. Of course, even if it really appeared, Lex had not decided whether he was going to pursue it or not.","Regix wasn’t exactly the most trustworthy glowing orb, and helping him may have dire consequences. Someone or something that could affect every system in the universe? Even if Lex wanted to learn from him, allowing him to return to the universe was too dangerous.","Lex had no intentions of helping him at all unless he himself reached the Dao Lord realm. With that said, apparently the Double Yin Death Metal could relieve very powerful curses. If that was the case, he might be able to cure the fairies from their curse, or at least cleanse his own body.","Mithon looked at the lone, black flower, and then nodded.","\"Yup, that’s the one,\" she answered without hesitation. \"We call it the Death Rose, on account of how lethal it is. But no one else has been able to find it ever since. Or, well, if they found it they kept it a secret or died. Who can say?\"","Lex nodded, having confirmed that this really was the flower that Regix was looking for. Even if the flower itself wasn’t a high priority for him right now, it wouldn’t hurt to keep an ear out for more information regarding it. After all, if he found it, he could keep it until he needed it. But if he couldn’t find it, and eventually ever needed it, the Nether would be his only other option.","\"What other resources do you know about?\" Lex asked.","Mithon, who hadn’t noticed anything strange at all, answered happily.","\"There’s the Red Ribbon, a type of leaf that is completely transparent except for a red line that runs through its center. This one is kind of famous because everyone is always looking out for it. They say eating a Red Ribbon gives one enlightenment on a random law to a massive degree.","\"I’ve never had one, but I know a guy whose sister had a Red Ribbon and mastered the law of resistance. Oh right, but that law of resistance wasn’t from Vaelûn, so she blew up when she tried to use it. Quite unfortunate.\"","Lex was stunned. Why did it seem like... all the precious resources ended up killing people?","\"Then there’s the Fist of Orion. That’s a type of rock that grows in the shape of an old fellow in the stronghold called Orion. That can freeze time within an enclosed space until its energy runs out.\"","Lex was stunned. Finally, something that didn’t threaten to kill the user, and a time related treasure at that!","\"There’s also the Purple Smog Cloud that can devour anything...\"","Once Mithon started to talk, she didn’t stop at all. Maybe it was a side effect of not speaking for countless years, but she shared any and all the information Lex asked about treasures, greatly expanding his catalog of the Hollow’s treasures.","Of course, the process wasn’t quick. But they weren’t short on time either. After all, until they found either a waygate, Truth Crystal or Memory Sphere, they were stuck together.","Yet one day, Lex suddenly stopped and landed on the ground, his expression turning somewhat solemn. Seeing such abrupt actions by the human senior, Mithon was startled, but didn’t dare to interrupt, and waited for the senior to speak on his own.","Lex, meanwhile, was completely focused on his karma. He had been accumulating good karma by absorbing the resources from here, not that it had any real effect on him at the moment.","What concerned him was a different kind of thread that had suddenly bound itself to him. It almost felt like a Karmic string, except that it was strange and alien to him. He’d never seen anything like it before.","His first guess was obviously to assume that this was the equivalent of the karmic string of Pentagal, the other universe. What he didn’t understand was why it had suddenly latched itself to him now. It wasn’t like he had done anything different - he’d been devouring resources for years already.","He needed to understand it quickly, because from the string Lex could sense a distinct feeling of danger, as if his life was now at risk.","Carefully - very, very carefully - Lex probed the string to learn more about it, but as it turned out, such caution wasn’t needed.","The moment he probed it, he learned why the string had appeared. 1 unit of resources in total had been devoured from across the Gilded Hollow, although he didn’t know how much 1 unit really was.","All he knew was that the string provided further feedback as well. Once 100 units of resources from within the Gilded Hollow were devoured in total, an inescapable, absolutely lethal retribution would target them. Oh, and since there was now a retribution string attached to him, he would be facing retributions quite frequently.","Lex frowned. This was not good news. He’d known it since he was in high school - the thing that would get him killed one day was a group project."]},{"number":2342,"title":"Chapter 2342: Desperate times","paragraphs":["This presented a problem for him. Although Lex had been looting like mad, he was certain that his actual contribution to that 1 unit was infinitesimal. Compared to the ability of Dao Lords to loot, what he took was less than a drop in an ocean. Thus he was certain that no matter what he did, his contribution to the final outcome would be negligible.","What truly mattered right now was the significance of the supposed limit. He was certain that most people would have the mentality of maximising their harvest before the limit was reached. So if, for example, it took 5 years for the Gilded Hollow to reach 1 unit of resources harvested, now with this limit set he anticipated that the next unit would be reached in one year or even less.","Each one of them would do their best to accumulate more resources before the others before the limit was reached, and then exit. Some might even consider challenging or facing the unsurvivable retribution. Being a Dao Lord gave them such liberty. Lex, however, wasn’t so sure he could enjoy the same privilege.","If he estimated it at 1 unit per year, he had 99 years left in the Gilded Hollow. Realistically, though, the time for a unit to be completed would decrease as the deadline came closer and everyone became desperate for greater harvests.","This presented Lex with two issues. The minor, or rather regular retributions he would be facing from now on weren’t his primary issues. The primary issues were that he did not know how to exit, so as the deadline approached he wouldn’t know how to save himself even if he wished to.","The second issue he was most concerned with was maximising his own harvest. With treasures like the Fist of Orion and the Double Yin Death Metal Rose abound, not to mention who knows what else, he’d be missing out if he didn’t get his hands on them.","That was to say, the things he had already harvested were also great. They also had cool or unique abilities. But his own strength was great enough to achieve much of what they did on his own, so he only utilized them as building blocks to create his own fake realm inside his necklace.","He could not hope or pray that the others would be understanding, and offer him more time to harvest anything. If that were the case, there was only one thing Lex could do.","He looked towards Mithon, who was waiting patiently on the side, and asked her a question.","\"Can you tell me about the Fortune Lord? What kind of personality or reputation does he have? Is he merciful and forgiving? Open and accepting? Strict and firm?\"","Mithon smiled upon hearing the question. She had been afraid the senior would ask her something she could not help with.","\"Lord Fortune is incredibly benevolent. He gave life to most of the residents of Fortune stronghold, and is the one who ensures it keeps running. Not only does he protect it from the terror of the retributions, but he also ensures that its day-to-day functionality is never disrupted.","\"If someone breaks the law, he punishes them according to the rules. The worst punishment is often like mine - exile. But he himself hardly ever acts against any of the stronghold residents. He is too fond of us all to directly hurt us, even when we break the rules.\"","Lex nodded, only believing about 50% of everything Mithon said. He couldn’t be certain how much of what she talked about was genuine, and how much was conditioning or brainwashing due to how she had been raised.","Still, her word was the only thing he had to go on. He needed to make a choice right now. The necklace was decently strong, so he could play it safe and try to find resources the slow and steady way. Or he could take a huge risk to his life in the hope of getting access to better resources.","Lex took a moment to think. He genuinely felt like if he screwed this up, the repercussions could doom him. Unfortunately, he also felt like if he didn’t keep moving forward and progressing with every opportunity he got, then he would always remain mediocre.","He took a deep breath and questioned himself one more time. Was he really going to do this?","The answer, without any hesitation or hint of a doubt, was yes. Though his stalker was one enemy, he would not be Lex’s last enemy. If he settled for being just strong enough to beat him, then Lex would become a victim once again when someone new showed up.","Lex straightened out his suit, made himself extremely presentable, and then adopted his humblest tone.","\"Lord Romulus Valecar, I am Lex William of the Midnight Inn, and I ask your forgiveness for uttering your noble name. I found your message and bottle, and sought out your city. Unfortunately, dire circumstances have forced my hand into disturbing you,\" he said, slowly and solemnly.","It was not every day that Lex directionally mentioned a Dao Lord’s name, especially without the Host Attire. Doing so now was a desperate, last resort in the hopes of attracting the Dao Lord and possibly attaining his help!","Although Lex could not be sure if Lord Fortune really was Romulus Valecare, everything seemed to line up too perfectly for him not to be.","Lex had not realized it while speaking, but his eyes had closed while he spoke, as if a great, irresistible drowsiness had suddenly struck him. His knees buckled and he fell to the ground, yet Lex did not feel it at all. The necklace that held his soul trembled, as if a great strain had suddenly been placed upon it for a brief moment.","A massive amount of the positive karma Lex had accumulated disappeared... and then everything returned to normal. He was standing on his feet, his eyes were open, and the necklace was unharmed, almost as if nothing had happened.","A few moments later, Lex realized that he was standing in front of a figure - one he did not recognize at all."]},{"number":2343,"title":"Chapter 2343: Missing karma","paragraphs":["Lex had rarely taken such a massive risk before. His preference was to act from a position of safety if possible. While he was becoming more active as of late, he still knew what lines not to cross. The closest he’d ever come to something as dangerous as this was when he used Jack to approach the seven Dwarf Dragon Dao Lords.","Now, though, he was approaching via his last lifeline. If anything happened to the necklace, it was unlikely that he’d be able to get back his body and system. Jack, while formidable, was no match for his stalker.","Although Lex had done some basic research on the Dao Lord, it was not nearly enough to be sure. Heck, he could not even be sure that the Fortune Lord was the very same as the one who had written the letter. He could be someone who came afterwards.","After all that , even if they were one and the same, what excuse did Lex even have that warranted him calling a Dao Lord? Just that he wanted to harvest some more resources? No, it was not a good enough excuse.","And yet, Lex decided to take this risk boldly. He was not concerned with just the stalker. No, Lex set his gaze on the enemy after that, and the one after that. From now on, he had to set his eyes on the Dao and nothing else. Only enemies in the Dao were real enemies, and only by approaching such a realm could he secure his future.","Otherwise, even if he survived now, his ending would ultimately be the same.","Lex looked at the figure standing in front of him, even though he had originally intended on keeping his eyes closed. Without the protection of the Midnight Inn or the Host Attire, even the mere sight of a Dao Lord could prove to be dangerous.","Yet as the figure appeared in front of Lex, he could not help but stare at him in amazement. Although Lex had never seen the figure before, he recognized the race at a single glance. Before him stood a qilin, its body that of a magnificent stag, a dragon head and a lion’s tail. Its scales were like that of a dragon, but held a pattern of flowing clouds, while its mane was made of blue flames.","Its presence was not massive or overbearing. Instead, his presence was refreshing and reinvigorating. All of Lex’s anxieties melted away in his presence, and he had a feeling that everything would be alright.","\"Hey, hey, would you look at that, you found my message in a bottle,\" Romulus said with a hint of pleasant surprise in his voice as he glanced upon Lex. \"It was quite the idea on my part, you know. You wouldn’t think so, but bottles are naturally excellent containers, and their unique shape makes it very easy to freeze time within them.\"","Lex glanced at the green bottle that had, at some point, appeared in his hand. Behind him, Mithon wagged her tail excitedly as she glanced upon Romulus.","\"Lord Fortune! Lord Fortune! The Gilded Hollow has opened back up once again! I was bringing the senior to tell you!\" she said from the back, clearly demonstrating that this wasn’t the first time she had seen him.","\"Mithon, good job, although I already knew about the Hollow opening. Still, I guess you’ve been in exile long enough. Considering the changing times, you may return to the stronghold,\" Romulus said, shaking his head like a doting grandfather, before turning his gaze back to Lex.","\"You’re an interesting one, though. I actually can’t see through your past. You must have someone pretty strong backing you. You said something about the Midnight Inn? What is that?\"","Lex bowed humbly, extremely grateful that the Fortune Lord had enough control over his Dao not to annihilate him by accident just by standing close by.","\"The Midnight Inn is an Inn run by the Innkeeper, and it is an inn open to guests from around the universe. Though these days the war has made it so that the Inn has had to minimize its operations. If you leave from here, though, the Inn would be most honored to host you,\" Lex said extremely humbly.","The Fortune Lord nodded, as if the answer was within his range of expectations.","\"The Innkeeper. Very nice. I wonder if he’s an old friend. It’s been too long since I’ve been stuck in the Hollow. Alright then Lex, is there anything here you need to do? I have some questions I’d like to ask you, and I’m sure you have matters you want to discuss as well. Such things would be better done behind the walls of the Fortune stronghold.\"","Lex was quite surprised by how amicable and down to earth the Fortune Lord was behaving, for even the friendliest Dao Lords hardly ever behaved like that. It’s exactly what ’supposedly’ made the Innkeeper so unique.","\"I have no other business here,\" Lex confirmed.","The qilin nodded, and then transported the three of them to the Fortune stronghold. Lex wasn’t even sure if it counted as teleportation. Whatever it was, they were suddenly safe. Oh, and all of Lex’s positive karma seemed to have temporarily detached from himself, fusing in with the city instead. But that hardly seemed to matter at the moment.","Lex found himself standing under a ridiculously large money tree, with its leaves spreading out over him to reluctantly cast their shade upon him. Instead of grass, the ground was covered in four leaf clovers, and there was a massive pot of gold on the side, the shine from the gold causing a rainbow to spread.","\"You don’t need to worry about any forced retributions while you’re within this land,\" Romulus said, appearing right beside Lex. \"You can stay here as long as you like. But I get the feeling that you’re not the type to sit still, are you?\"","Lex smiled, and began to consider his next moves. It actually all depended on the whims of this Dao Lord."]},{"number":2344,"title":"Chapter 2344: The Innkeeper suspects","paragraphs":["The qilin nodded to himself, and then casually made his way towards a throne that had been designed specially to accommodate qilins.","\"There are many things I want to ask you,\" the qilin said as he made himself comfortable, turning his gaze towards Lex. \"However, you summoned me, so I’ll let you go first. I can see from your expressions that you’re very concerned about being affected by my aura, but don’t be concerned at all.","\"I’ve spent countless years within the Gilded Hollow, surrounded by the most plentiful treasures this place has to offer any Dao Lord. I have gained complete mastery over my Dao and powers, so you won’t be affected by me at all. I doubt there’s another Dao Lord in existence with better Dao control than myself.\"","The qilin seemed to be both informing Lex and bragging at the same time. Lex did not dare to judge his motives at all, but in truth that’s exactly what Romulus had been doing. He’d long since become completely familiar with all those living within the Hollow - whether they were those who arrived when the Hollow last opened, or those he had given life to.","Lex was thus the first new being he was talking to in almost two ages! It felt good to talk to someone new, not to mention that Romulus was judging a lot from Lex’s reactions to his words, and gleaning a tremendous amount about the universe from him.","For example, Romulus had long since believed that he would be the strongest being in the universe once he exited the Gilded Hollow. He didn’t believe there existed another Dao Lord with access to as many resources as himself, which meant that no one else should have been able to master their Dao as completely and thoroughly as him. That should have made him peerless.","Yet he could not look into Lex’s past. That meant that there was at least one other being in the universe with the same level of power as him, if not more power than him. Yet if such a being existed, and the universe was still embroiled in some kind of war, then that meant there was at least one other of equal strength!","He had been cut off from the universe for too long, since the last time the Gilded Hollow opened was in the early stages of the Enlightenment Age. Considering that Romulus had been born right after the end of the Primordial Age, he was not privy to the incidents that happened back then, and being trapped in here since then, he was not privy to what had happened since either.","Although he said that the Innkeeper might be an old friend to Lex, in truth the only Dao Lord Romulus knew were the ones from the Qilin race, and those that had been trapped within the Gilded Hollow.","That was exactly why he would not miss out an opportunity to learn as much as he could from Lex. He was a human, and was incredibly deferential, but even through his humbleness Romulus could see a quiet confidence and familiarity, letting him know that Lex was no foreigner to meeting Dao Lords and being in their presence. Clearly, he came from a formidable background.","\"Thank you for this opportunity, lord,\" Lex said as he gave a light bow. \"I arrived in the Hollow some time ago, and have been harvesting its resources. However, not long ago I felt the Gilded Hollow attach some kind of string to my body, and inform me of a certain limit.\"","Romulus nodded.","\"Yes, the unavoidable retribution,\" he said knowingly. \"It was like that last time as well. I am familiar with it. Continue.\"","Lex paused, for he hadn’t been aware that the same thing happened last time. It did make sense though for a pattern to exist.","\"Well previously, I was unaware of a time limit. But now that there is a restriction in place, I had no choice but to take a risk. You see, while talking to Mithon, I learned about something that could put the whole universe in danger.\"","Lex raised his hand and revealed an image of the Double Yin Death Metal Rose. He’d already decided not to help Regix. Heck, even if he wanted to, he couldn’t take it out of the Gilded Hollow, so he was more than willing to trade the information regarding that flower in exchange for getting opportunities of his own. The best part of this all was that he was not telling any lies - he genuinely felt like that flower could put the universe at risk.","If Regix was freed from his state, and could influence all systems, who knew what would happen to the universe? It was better to destroy, or at least consume the flower, and get some resources for himself along the way.","Romulus looked at the flower and immediately recognized it.","\"The Death Rose? I am familiar with that particular item, though I haven’t seen it myself. How does it put the universe in danger?\" Romulus asked, leaning forward.","Lex shook his hand.","\"I’m not sure of the exact details. All I know is that the Innkeeper suspects a foreigner from another universe is hiding in our universe, searching for that exact flower, and that if he finds it something terrible will happen,\" Lex answered, quite truthfully in fact.","He suspected Regix was from Pentagal. Actually, that was almost more or less confirmed. Since he was the Innkeeper, he could share his own suspicions with clarity. Yes, by confessing all this he was at risk of offending Regix, or missing out on the opportunities he offered.","But Lex also believed that no one would be able to find Regix so easily. Whether he would be found, or whether their future deal would be compromised was not something he knew about. What Lex did know was that unless he himself reached the Dao Lord realm, he had no intentions of interacting with Regix again.","Thus, he did not mind exposing him for now. If he could get some benefits out of it, all the better. If not, reaching the Fortune stronghold was already good enough, for it would enable him to procure better, higher quality resources than before."]},{"number":2345,"title":"Chapter 2345: New Notification","paragraphs":["If Romulus had any thoughts about what Lex had to say, he did not make it apparent at all. He looked just as relaxed as he had been before Lex shared the news. Lex dared not have any thoughts trying to determine the thoughts or motives of the qilin at all, so all he could do was silently wait for a response once he was done speaking.","At the very least his actions had provided him with a reasonable and plausible explanation for why he’d be desperate enough to utter the name of an unknown Dao Lord. After all, saying that he called on a Dao Lord just because he wanted to go shopping in a better neighborhood was just inviting death in a round about way.","\"Alright, I understand your concern. So what were you hoping I would do about it?\" Romulus asked, without any indication of being bothered in any way.","\"Allowing me to enter the Fortune stronghold is already more than enough. Based on what Mithon told me, there are waypoints across the Hollow which can be accessed from here. I can search for the flower on my own without troubling anyone. Of course, if you happen to already know where it is, your guidance would be most appreciated. Or, if you prefer, I can tell you what I know about the flower and you can deal with the matter on your own.\"","In front of a Dao Lord, Lex held no thoughts of being able to get a superior deal or any ulterior motives whatsoever. He spoke directly, willing to sacrifice any potential gains he may get otherwise, because he could not hope to fool a Dao Lord.","The only reason he managed to maintain what few secrets he had was because of the protection provided to him by others.","\"I understand,\" Romulus said, leaning back on his throne. \"It is good that your concerns have already been addressed. Still, I will consider how I can help you out further, but that will have to wait until after I am done with my questions.\"","Romulus proceeded to ask Lex a series of general questions about the universe, which in itself was not surprising. The questions, however, weren’t exactly what Lex would have expected.","\"What do you mean the qilin race is not the master of the dragon race? That is absolutely absurd,\" Romulus said with extreme disbelief.","Lex resisted the urge to scratch his head because that was an incredibly awkward question for him to answer.","\"Well, among the Beasts, Qilins hold a high position and are considered an Elder race. It’s just that, reputation wise, Dragons seem to be stronger,\" Lex answered truthfully while trying to stay as diplomatic as possible.","\"That’s absurd,\" Romulus said in disgusted disbelief. \"The dragons cannot manage the fortune aura on their treasure hoards without qilins. They’re totally dependent on us!\"","Lex wasn’t sure how to respond to that. He had not encountered fortune aura or things associated with it before, so he wasn’t quite familiar with how it worked.","This was an entirely independent, unique system. Lex even suspected that the reason his positive karma disappeared to begin with had something to do with Fortune or Fortune aura.","That just went to show how complex and advanced the laws of the universe were. There were still things that he was entirely unfamiliar with.","\"Okay, fine, fine, forget the damn winged lizards,\" Romulus said agitatedly. \"Tell me about Fortune’s Favor Bank. Surely that’s doing really well by now. It’s a proud initiative by the qilins. I doubt you’d know this, but the very concept of banks was created by us Qilins.\"","Lex once again looked awkward simply because he’d never heard of this bank.","\"Uhh...\" Lex said while he thought of what to say, and finally Romulus’ expression began to change for the first time.","\"I think... it’s best if you just tell me what you know of the qilins directly,\" said Romulus.","Lex did not know much about qilins specifically, but he told the little that he knew. As research for the Midnight Inn, he learned the basics of most of the popular or famous races, and that naturally included the qilin.","They were an Elder race, and that was quite respectable in Lex’s opinion at least. Romulus, however, seemed to disagree. To begin with, the concept of the Cosmic Ascendance Spectrum was completely foreign to him. He could not understand how a random ranking on a stone could affect entire races across the universe.","He hated even worse that other Beasts could rank above the Qilin race, which was something he found completely unacceptable.","\"Perhaps it’s because you’ve been stuck inside the Hollow,\" Lex offered, trying to improve his mood.","\"No, that has nothing to do with it. I was nothing but a random junior when I entered the Hollow. My race should have been much more powerful than what you have told me. Someone must be plotting against us to steal our fortunes,\" Romulus said with a dangerous edge in his voice.","Yet he regained his composure quickly enough, and once again began smiling.","\"Alright, I have decided. Since the Gilded Hollow has opened once more, I see no need to prolong things. I will forcibly open the exit from the Hollow within twenty years, child. You better manage your task within that time, or risk getting stuck here for the rest of your life. Go to the city council - they’ll give you whatever help you need to find the Death Rose.\"","Clearly being dismissed, Lex bowed once more, thanked Romulus for his help, and quickly exited.","After he left, Romulus’ expression finally changed into a frown and his gaze shifted to the open system panel in front of him.","His system had hardly helped him ever since he reached the Dao Lord level, but there was one quest that had been ongoing for many years that offered a great reward - one that he had tried to complete, but had failed. Incidentally, the quest was for the very rose that Lex had just told him about.","Yet now, he began to wonder if the reason his system wanted the rose was somehow connected to that foreigner from another universe.","\"System, I think it’s time we had another talk,\" Romulus said solemnly. \"I want proper answers, or I’ll stop selling clones to the system warehouse.\"","At the very top of his interface was the name of his system: Ultimate Cloning System. It was through this system of his that he had managed to keep his stronghold filled with living beings, and it was through the help of his system that he had survived the Gilded Hollow for so long.","That did not mean that he would help the system invade his own universe, if that’s what was happening.","New Notification: Audio chat invitation from Prime Kernel/System Daddy received."]},{"number":2346,"title":"Chapter 2346: Dwindling fortunes","paragraphs":["Although it had not appeared like it, Lex’s meeting with the Qilin was actually quite tense and difficult. While he appeared very relaxed, and he had complete mastery over his aura, there was no way of knowing how that meeting could have gone. In fact, even now, Lex could be under his observation, or he may be marked in certain ways that he could not discover at the moment.","Perhaps the reason was that no matter how friendly or approachable he seemed, to the point where he had personal relationships with the citizens of his stronghold, Lex had no idea what he wanted.","If Lex compared meeting him to Eclipse, there were a few distinct differences. While the Qilin thought himself to be the strongest Dao Lord, and Eclipse already had an established reputation for it, there were silent, unspoken differences. It was tough to pinpoint the difference, but if Lex had to differentiate...","Well, Eclipse talked to him and joked with him because she was completely indifferent to all power levels, such was her immense confidence. As for the Qilin...","Lex stopped himself from thinking further. He should not hold any unnecessary thoughts towards his host at all. So far, he had been nothing but accommodating and welcoming, and that was already a greater blessing than Lex could hope to expect from a Dao Lord unknown to him.","He walked through the halls of the Fortune palace, and somehow he already knew where to go. Though currently Lex existed in the form of a necklace, he had always projected himself as a human wearing the necklace, though the necklace was hidden beneath his suit.","Speaking of which, River and Pearl always found his attire quite strange, perhaps because in their communities their clothes were of a very different style. They had never been able to accept or understand the aesthetic appeal of his suit.","He could not help but think of them for a moment. Lex had spent quite a few years with that young couple, and though he restricted himself from acting most of the time, it was less because he didn’t like them and more because he did not want to taint them with his karma.","His future was uncertain, and it would be far too easy for them to wound up as collateral damage.","It was better for them to live their own lives, and navigate their own journey. He had a feeling that even without his interference, their journey would not be insignificant.","As he exited the palace and laid eyes on the Fortune stronghold, Lex pushed all other thoughts aside. The stronghold was quite different from what he had anticipated.","For as far as his eyes could see, or his spirit sense could extend, Lex only found fields of crops and orchards, with only the occasional buildings few and far between. Managing those were countless races, all working together in seamless harmony forming a multiracial utopia of sorts.","Just like Mithon, all the races he saw seemed simple and straightforward, all working together, forming the perfect harmony. The sight was quite relaxing, and Lex sensed that it also positively affected the fortunes of this place.","Yet only a moment later the oddly uniform behavioral patterns of all the farm workers suddenly reminded Lex of the Midnight Inn’s staff. While they all had their own unique personalities, they only ever came out after Lex insisted they focus a bit on their individualities.","Yet even when their personalities started to develop, what never changed was their firm and fixed loyalty towards the Midnight Inn and the Innkeeper! Lex did notice that whatever restrictions they had on their personalities seemed to diminish greatly after reaching the Immortal realm, by then their personality traits were already set.","He was not debating whether it was a good thing or bad, he was just making an observation. While making that observation, he also cut off his thought process, not letting himself ponder more on the implications.","The Fortune stronghold was far bigger than what Lex had expected, so he could only go down into the fields near the palace and approach one of the farm workers to ask for directions towards the city council.","The first worker Lex encountered was a Primordial Sun Crow, except that it lacked any and all primordial energy or aura. It hovered over a field of wheat, enhancing their growth through the light produced from its flames.","It was an unusual sight, but Lex didn’t dwell on that much.","\"Excuse me, could you point me in the direction of the city council?\" Lex asked as he approached, sensing that the crow was very deeply invested in its work and had no patience for small talk.","\"You’ll have to take the tube underground to get there,\" the crow said after glancing at Lex. \"I’ll get someone to take you down there, so don’t even try to dig down yourself. I don’t want you affecting the roots of my plants.\"","Lex wasn’t sure how to respond, especially since a few seconds later a Primordial mole dug out of the ground, opening up a route for Lex to enter the underground.","Lex thanked them and jumped down the hole.","\"That’s odd. I don’t recall seeing a human that strong before,\" the mole commented, speaking to the crow.","\"Humanities fortunes have dwindled considerably, but individuals can still accumulate some for themselves,\" the crow commented before flying away. It was too focused on its crops for small talk.","Lex had already left, but he heard the two beasts’ words. It seemed even within the Gilded Hollow, humans did not have it easy. He was not concerned with that for the moment, because the moment he landed in the underground tube system, he was reminded of the New York subway station.","It was difficult to tell from the quiet and peaceful scene up above, but the underground of the stronghold was bustling, with thousands of different races going about their own way.","In place of trains, the stronghold had worms pulling carts, but it was basically the same thing to be honest."]},{"number":2347,"title":"Chapter 2347: Let’s start with...","paragraphs":["Lex found the sight oddly amusing, as well as astonishing. It was amusing because even though there were many different races working together, they didn’t look that much different from the subway system. What was astonishing, though, was that there were no formations or enchanted treasures that he could spot, yet this underground network was perfectly isolated from detection from up above.","He could have just jotted it down to Dao Lord powers, but he had a feeling that wasn’t the case. He stood in a corner and listened to the chattering between the residents and commuters, picking up little details of their lives in the Fortune stronghold.","At first, he was smiling. But as the hours went by, Lex’s smile began to fade as he realized that he may have severely underestimated the strength and accomplishment of the lord of this stronghold. To be fair, being able to resist Gilded Hollow’s retribution for so many years should have been a major hint towards just how strong he was.","Everyone, all races, within the stronghold only cultivated through a cultivation system designed by the Fortune Lord himself! Even the Beasts did not rely on their bloodline to cultivate. Instead, they all cultivated their fortunes, and used that to grow stronger!","The Fortune cultivation system was extremely easy to cultivate within the Hollow, since every bit of the hollow was made up of incredibly valuable resources. If the residents were brave enough to venture past the boundaries of the stronghold and actually accumulate and gather resources, supplementing their fortunes, then their cultivation would grow even stronger, faster!","As Lex thought about that, he realized that the Fortune Lord may have been stuck in the Hollow, but this really was the most ideal cultivation ground for him in existence! Qilins themselves were beasts that were favored by fortunes, and were even considered bearers of good luck.","For him to cultivate in this land full of the fortunes of a fallen universe...","Lex suddenly paused and pushed away the thought that came to his mind. He could not think of it at all. He could not allow himself to ponder what cultivation realm the Fortune Lord would reach if he managed to harvest the lingering fortunes of a fallen universe. Upon his return to the universe at large, things really might change a lot.","From within the Fortune palace, Romulus smirked as he looked at Lex, and then shook his head. Even Lex himself did not know the true reason for why Romulus was so friendly towards him, and it was better that way.","Yes, Romulus really did have a friendly and approachable personality. But it would not be enough to go over and teleport any random being who called out his name. Being friendly did not mean he was open to becoming other people’s taxis. Yet the moment Lex spoke his name, Romulus sensed his fortune, and discovered something.","He smiled. Even if he could not look into Lex’s past, it did not prevent him from benefiting from his future. As for the Innkeeper... Romulus suspected that they were one and the same, at least in terms of their goals. Whatever the case, he would learn the truth once he left the Gilded Hollow.","He turned his gaze away from his system interface, somewhat conflicted by his conversation with Prime Kernel.","Romulus got up off his throne and descended to the lowest level of the Fortune stronghold, far beneath the subway. He entered a main hall connected to eleven different chambers, each of which had not been opened in billions of years. Yet today, he sent in his spirit sense to disturb its inhabitants.","\"Wake up,\" Romulus commanded, his voice no longer as even and easygoing as it had been with Lex. \"It is time for us to return to Vaelûn.\"","As soon as he spoke, the aura of eleven other Dao Lords erupted from those chambers.","Lex, meanwhile, finally got in one of the train carts and headed towards the city council. By now, he’d learned a lot more about the stronghold, and he had to say that it was somehow beyond his expectation, and somehow within it as well.","The size of the stronghold was... well it was far beyond measuring in something like the size of football fields. If he really had to say, then the land that the stronghold occupied was equal to the surface area of twenty one suns!","It was far larger than he had expected. But then again, this was the territory of a Dao Lord, so it couldn’t exactly be small either.","The stronghold had a distinct culture, history and system of doing things. For example, it had its own calendar, its own public holidays, public figures, significant historical events and so on.","The thing that specifically attracted Lex’s attention was something special on their calendar. They marked 231,000 years as one Dao cycle, after which the calendar would once again begin from the year 0 and the number of Dao cycles increasing by one. Lex paid special attention to it because of the mention of the word Dao.","He didn’t know if it was random or there was a certain reason behind it - it was just something he’d have to figure out on his own. He’d never heard the term before back outside the Gilded Hollow, so either it could just be something they made up, or something he wasn’t able to get in touch with.","It only made sense that after such a long period of time, the Fortune stronghold was thoroughly developed. That was also why, despite its massive size, the underground transport system was quite efficient. The distance between Lex’s current position and that of the city council was enormous, yet the worm carrying the carts behind it could move through great distances using a technique Lex was unfamiliar with.","It was not a surprise at all that the worm, too, was of a primordial race - just one that lacked Primoridial energy. Lex couldn’t identify the associated laws for they were too unfamiliar to him, and touched upon some abstract concepts he’d never encountered before. Regardless, it only took Lex twenty minutes before he reached his destination and got off the train.","Honestly, Lex could have just directly teleported through this distance in a shorter time on his own if he had known the location, but he didn’t quite mind the journey. It was quite enlightening.","All the residents of the stronghold seemed to display a distinct lack of urgency in everything they did, as if they had all the time in the world. It was quite contrary to the rest of the universe, and yet it had not affected the productivity of their civilization. It was quite curious, and gave Lex some things to ponder over.","The ’city council’ was less of a building and more like a city of its own, with hundreds of highrises, countless roads, smaller buildings, apartments, parks and more. Yet even so, each portion of the council was distinctly divided to take care of certain matters.","The department that the Fortune Lord had sent Lex to was the one that categorically recorded news and information relating to treasures within the Hollow above a certain quality threshold.","The department was, unsurprisingly, overseen by a black dragon. Not only did he overlook the recording of critical intel, but he very often went out and conducted surveys and treasure retrievals.","Considering that very, very few residents of the stronghold ever left its boundaries and risked facing the Hollow’s retribution, the dragon became one of the most knowledgeable when it came to collecting and harvesting resources.","Considering that the dangers seemed proportional to the area of the Hollow one ventured to, surviving so many years was an incredible feat. After all, the Hollow’s retribution was only one of the dangers - not the only one.","\"I have already been informed about you by the Fortune Lord,\" the black dragon said as he looked at Lex with an especially pleased expression. \"I have been given permission to use all the resources available to me in helping you find and harvest your targeted resources. I was told that the Death Rose was your primary target, but we don’t currently know of its whereabouts and have already deployed all our remote search methods to search for clues. In the meantime, we can get familiar with working together by practicing on some other key resources.\"","Lex could tell at a glance - the dragon really wanted to help Lex go out and find resources, because this would be its opportunity to go out and search as well. It didn’t mind at all that going out might cause it to die. He was, in the truest sense, a dragon. He cared more about increasing the size of his treasure hoard than anything else!","Lex smiled. Yes, this was exactly the type of person he wanted to work with at the moment.","\"Fine, give me the complete list of recorded treasures that you have. Let’s start with Dao level treasures that immortals can contact without dying or getting corrupted.\"","The black dragon mirrored Lex’s smile, as if he had finally found a trusted confidant after all these years."]},{"number":2348,"title":"Chapter 2348: Fudge","paragraphs":["As an entity living within a necklace, Lex didn’t actually have eyes, and was merely a projection made up from his own spirit sense. Even so, the projection rubbed his eyes, wiping the tears of blood that had begun to pool up.","In front of him lay a list of Dao materials that had been catalogued by the city council. Even the black dragon himself had never dared look at the list. Even though this was a list compiled in the city itself, merely the knowledge of Dao materials had a burden.","Lex was in the process of developing a Primordial Dao Body, and since his body, soul and spirit were basically the same, his soul within the necklace gained the same resilience. It was for that reason that he could even read such detailed information about Dao materials without the protection of the Inn.","The name of the material might have limited effect, but when Lex also looked at its appearance, its effects and the nature of its development, it accumulated into a certain pressure. Even free knowledge had a price, and Lex could only barely begin to tolerate it because of his Primordial Dao Body.","Even then, the only reason Lex was not harmed was because this information was regarding the gentlest Dao materials that could accommodate Immortals, and wouldn’t kill them upon coming into contact. After reading about dozens of such materials, however, the strain accumulated, and Lex needed to stop.","Yet in the eyes of the black dragon, the fact that Lex only suffered from bleeding eyes after reading so much instead of direct blindness was an enormous feat! He became even more excited about working together with him!","As if that was not enough, Lex’s soul naturally emitted an aura that made the dragon feel friendly towards him, as if he was dealing with another dragon of respectable heritage.","\"What progress have you made, brother Lex?\" the dragon asked amicably, waiting eagerly for him to decide on their target.","\"I’ve read the top 49 materials listed on the list, but I can’t believe there’s over ten thousand more on the list. It’s basically impossible to go through them all,\" Lex said as he continued to rub his eyes, using his own energy to slowly help himself recover.","\"That’s ten thousand after your criteria was filtered out. I say rather than searching the list manually, you continue to expand your search parameters to narrow down the results further,\" the black dragon said.","Lex shook his head.","\"I’ve already put in over a hundred filters on the search terminal,\" Lex said with a disbelieving smile on his face. \"These are Dao materials that I could basically just go and scoop up without harming myself, and I can use them easily without wasting a lot of time and energy. Honestly, I find it somewhat difficult to believe.\"","Lex shook his head. He had originally thought that he would, at most, find one or two Dao materials in the Gilded Hollow that he could get his hands on, and the rest of the time he’d need to harvest Celestial grade materials. Yet he had severely underestimated the abundant wealth of the Hollow!","The issue he was now having was deciding which Dao materials to go for so that he could use as many of them as possible without causing inherent contradictions between the materials when they’re used for upgrading his necklace!","This was... the most frustrating and yet somehow simultaneously the most wonderful problem he’d ever had.","\"Just because the Dao materials themselves don’t harm immortals does not mean they can be easily accessed by immortals,\" the black dragon told Lex. \"Otherwise I would have a much larger treasure hoard than I already do. By the way, I don’t mean to pry or interfere, but I thought I’d give you a piece of advice. Do you know the reason that, despite there being so many Dao materials that can be accessed by immortals, the residents of the Fortune stronghold hardly ever go to retrieve them?\"","Lex turned towards the black dragon, and though his eyes were closed, he could see him clearly with his spirit sense.","\"The way you’re saying it, I suppose the Hollow’s retribution and the inherent difficulty of getting the materials aren’t the main reasons,\" Lex stated.","The dragon nodded.","\"All peak Celestial Immortals in the Gilded Hollow aim to become Dao Lords, but the Dao tribulation cannot be taken within the Hollow. Thus, for the sake of their own future, as for the future of their neighbors, they all spread a certain piece of news so that low level immortals don’t make a mistake early on.","\"As you may already know, upon reaching the peak of the Celestial realm, a cultivator will automatically learn the method to become a Dao Lord. While the exact details of the method were not shared, simply because lower level cultivators cannot bear the weight of that knowledge, they did share a piece of advice.","\"Any immortal who absorbs a Dao material will find it infinitely harder to pass the Dao tribulation, which is already basically a death sentence for almost everyone who experiences it. Since then, they’ve all avoided it, leaving an abundance of these resources to be recorded in the city council files, hardly ever actually harvested.\"","Lex paused. Well, he’d already done that. Was he screwed? He couldn’t help but recall the moment he met his parents in Arch-Heaven, and his mother thought that he’d basically given up on becoming a Dao Lord. She actually applauded him for it, telling him he was smart for avoiding the risk.","Lex smirked, and opened his eyes, looking at the black dragon.","\"Well, I haven’t reached the peak of the Celestial Immortal realm, but I can already tell you that anyone who gave up on the idea of harvesting those materials because of that advice... probably won’t become a Dao Lord to begin with.\"","The black dragon was stunned, not expecting to hear such words.","\"How come?\" he could not help but ask.","Lex glanced at him, and then back at the list of materials.","\"They gave up before even entering the fight. With such a weak resolve, they won’t be able to overcome the Dao tribulations,\" Lex said casually as he refocused on the list. His words, though, rang like thunder in the ears of the black dragon, freezing it still.","He himself had not reached the peak of the Celestial realm, but the reason he had restrained himself was not because of the advice, but because he wanted to add the Dao materials to his hoard rather than use it himself. Still, he could see how adhering to that advice might be as a result of fear and lack of conviction.","While the dragon was lost in introspection, Lex was internally cursing.","’ Fudge, fudge, fudge, fudge, fudge! ’","Actually, he was quite annoyed that he had inadvertently caused his ascension to become more difficult. It wasn’t because Lex thought he wouldn’t be able to survive the tribulation, but because it seemed like his history of over the top tribulations would persist. He was actually slightly afraid of the phenomenon his Celestial tribulation would cause, so he could not even imagine the result of the Dao tribulation.","In the end, he just sighed internally, and let it go. All he could say was that it was his destiny to be exceptional, so he would always walk the harder path. It totally wasn’t because the easy path had already incidentally been cut off.","\"We’ll start with this,\" said Lex as he pointed to something on the list. \"The Memory of Rust will be our first target, and from there we can directly move towards the Forgotten Blood. They are both close enough to each other that we can get them in a single trip. Accounting for the distance from waygates, and the travel time to each resource, we should be able to complete the round trip in under three years.\"","Ambition burned deep in Lex’s heart, though he did not let it show. Although the dragon had told him his path would become more difficult if he absorbed Dao materials, it was already too late. In that case, he might as well commit all the way to it. Besides, his cultivation had never been normal to begin with.","A place as abundant in resources as the Gilded Hollow was not something he could encounter again and again. Even if his tribulation became harder... well, that was a problem for future Lex. What was he even going to do? Turn back time and beat himself up?","Heh, that was a bad joke.","As Lex talked to himself and soothed his spirit, a flicker of excitement also flashed through his eyes. Once he was done with the Hollow, the stalker would be in for one heck of a surprise.","He just hoped that the barrier around his body could hold up for another twenty years."]},{"number":2349,"title":"Chapter 2349: State of universal affairs","paragraphs":["Aegis’ body crashed into the ground, covered in blood, his mind crawling at a snail’s pace as he suffered from the repercussions of the attack he suffered. Even so, even in his wounded, mentally compromised state, he wondered only one thing: why could he still not beat his father?","He was a genius by any measure. He learned faster than anyone else in the nation, his adaptability was unreal and his application of laws was flawless. Yet no matter how much he improved, it seemed like he was no closer to defeating his father.","He wanted to give up. Honestly, there came a point where he just wanted to give up. He really wanted to give up. But he couldn’t, because the enemies he’d be facing in the future weren’t his father. They would not spare him, and give him a chance to come back stronger.","Aegis finally managed to recover, and looked up to see that he wasn’t the only one who had been defeated, everyone else had been as well. Beside him was Pvarti, and further away a little was his half sister Cwenhild. There were dozens of others as well, and despite the upgrades they received from coming to the Primordial Garden, they were still unable to face their king even when they joined hands.","\"That’s enough,\" said Cornelius from the floating throne as he looked down at the so-called best his empire had to offer, all defeated by his hand. \"We cannot delay any longer. I’ve given you all as much time as I could. From here on out, we depart. Of course, you all still have the option of staying back in the Primordial Garden as well. But in that case, just know that you will be giving up the opportunity that comes once an age.\"","King Cornelius II looked down at his vassals, and then turned around. The Ventura academy had access to the garden as well, and through his contacts with them, he had managed to attain a valuable opportunity.","He would be joining the battlefield at Tyranum realm, and would personally seek out opportunities for humanity to flourish. His cultivation was a little low - he was in the middle stages of the Heaven Immortal realm, but that was only because he’d been slowing down his ascension. Rising in cultivation too quickly would be detrimental to his future.","He clenched his fists. This came too quickly, but plans could not keep up with reality. He might not be able to bring a change in humanity from bottom up in time, so for now he would need to temporarily try to redeem it from the top.","Cornelius arrived at the Ventura checkpost, and left the Primordial Garden without hesitation. He arrived in Ventura Gold, one of the leading Ventura academies, and passed through without attracting too much attention. He kept his senses honed for just by walking through the different departments of Ventura, he could hear a lot of the latest news from across the universe.","While it seemed like a lot of attention was on the human race, in truth almost all races were facing an unprecedented crisis. The Dragons and Phoenixes were fighting like... well, they were fighting like Dragons and Phoenixes. The Angels were defending Eden with all they had, but had already suffered the death of dozens of Dao Lords.","In retaliation, the Celestials held nothing back and did not bother feigning civility. Not only did they help the Angels defend, finally getting the Humanoid Alliance directly involved in the fight, they also counter invaded the allies of the Laoer race.","As if that was not enough, they went ahead and killed a Laoer Dao Lord! So much for a Minor Dao of Eternity.","Tensions were at an all time high, but with the Alliance now moving with full momentum, they were unleashing their fangs which had stayed hidden for too long. None could have anticipated just how strong the Humanoid Alliance had actually become.","Meanwhile, many of the Sage races had appeared on various battlefields. Since many Dao Lords were stuck either in the Dream realm chasing treasure, or were stuck within the Gilded Hollow, the fighting force of many organisations dropped rapidly, and many Major realms had already changed hands.","It had been a few years since the destruction of the Major realm, and the universe was still reeling from its effects. Specifically, the Void Dwellers became a lot more active and chaotic, and began invading realms with a new vigor.","At the same time, news had spread that the HOA was using the backdrop of war to begin spreading various faiths across countless realms. With the aid of the Divine ore, they need not be restricted to their originating realm, which is why they began to accumulate strength rapidly. Other, independent Deities were doing the same but they couldn’t pose as great a threat as the HOA.","\"Have you heard about Lord Wu Kong?\" one of the passing students said, speaking to another student. \"I hear he’s been fighting Lord Erland for over a decade now. While the two of them haven’t been able to defeat each other, I heard another Dao Lord got killed while trying to interfere.\"","The other student shook his head.","\"There have been more deaths in the past few decades than this entire year. I fear if this continues, the name of this Age will be the Age of Death.\"","Cornelius shook his head. He didn’t bother paying attention to the matters of the Dao Lords - they were too far removed from him, and he could not influence them at all. Instead, he listened for news relating to humans.","\"I heard that the Humanoid Alliance is trying to get humans to make a comeback,\" someone said. \"There are a couple of humans whose names have appeared on the Dao Affirmation list. Apparently, one of them is called the Grand Conqueror or something like that, and the other has appeared on the list but with their name hidden. Only their race is visible, which is human!\"","Another person chuckled.","\"I heard the human with their name hidden is from a human subrace called mermaid. I’m not sure what the big deal is, but I heard that the Sages are going crazy in search of that mermaid. Even Dao Lords have gotten involved.\"","The other students looked over in confusion.","\"What’s the big deal with mermaids? I’ve never heard of them before.\"","The first student chuckled knowingly.","\"There’s a rumor that there’s a special place in the universe that can only be accessed by mermaids, or maybe a certain kind of mermaid. I’m not sure what the truth is, but the Sage races are crazy about them!\"","Cornelius shook his head, and stopped listening to everything else. He reported in the relevant department, many of the Immortals from his kingdom lined up behind him, and began the procedure for their departure to the Tyranum realm.","He also received a briefing about the status of the realm. It was controlled by the Tyranis race, the sworn enemy of humanity, making it quite ironic that it held so many of humanity’s legacies.","Oddly enough, the Humanoid Alliance wasn’t the one leading the charge on the battlefields for humans in this realm, it was the Henali.","Cornelius looked from the information package, and at the quest list issued by Ventura for the Tyranum realm. Completing those quests would allow them to be rewarded by Ventura, and was a far more reliable system than most other races.","Just as he was about to accept a few quests, he was hit by a sudden yet overwhelming sorrow the likes of which penetrated into his core. That overwhelming sorrow was accompanied by another, albeit muted, emotion: horror!","Corneilius had felt this before, and quite recently, so he knew what this was. It was the death of a Major realm! How could such a thing happen?","As if that was not enough, the sorrow this time seemed to last much, much longer, as if a truly ancient Major realm had died this time!","What Cornelius didn’t know was that his guess was entirely off the mark. It wasn’t that a very old Major realm had died or been destroyed. Instead, more than one Major realm had been destroyed at the same time! The response from the universe was even more drastic, and the dropped strain even greater!","Almost instant, word reached Ventura. Not one, and not two, but three Major realms had been destroyed at the same time! This was no coincidence, for the timing of the destruction had been carefully orchestrated to cause the greater response from the universe itself!","This change was felt nowhere as greatly as inside Arch-Heaven, which began to develop at an astonishingly rapid pace!","Mango, the goldfish, looked around in a confused manner as he felt his limiter increase from 39% to 41% for no reason. Did he do something that warranted such an abrupt change? He could not remember."]},{"number":2350,"title":"Chapter 2350: Asux the Primal Monarch","paragraphs":["\" IMPOSSIBLE !\" Asux uttered, his very words a strain on those who heard them, even if they were all Dao Lords. \" This is utterly UNACCEPTABLE !\"","As peacekeepers and caretakers of the universe, the Primals usually stayed behind the scenes. They were facilitators and mediators, so they hardly ever brought their own agendas to the forefront. Even if they did have some agendas, it remained thoroughly hidden behind layers and layers of nuanced leveraging and an ocean of diplomatic ties.","But what was the point of peacekeepers if there was no peace? The universal war, while surprising, still did not arouse too strong a reaction from the Primals because on the grand scale of things, in the long term, it was merely akin to a single bad hour in a single day.","Then a Major realm was destroyed. That was enough to attract their attention, and they had begun to work silently, looking into who was responsible. This was the type of thing that could not be overlooked.","Yet they still moved in silence. It was not urgent, and what happened had already happened. But the further destruction of three Major realms simultaneously? Just as Asux said, it was unacceptable.","\"My lord, what are your orders?\" asked a Primal, garbed in armor of silver and gold, with a burnished, gold circlet crown with four distinct points, each one rising towards the sky. The Primal asking was known as the Spear King, one of the six Primal Kings who ruled over not one, but a chain of Major realms.","The six Primal Kings all answered only to one being, the ruler of the Primary realm, Asux, the Primal Monarch!","\"Find out whoever is responsible, and kill any who get in your way,\" Asux said without the slightest hint of restraint or reservation. \"Four Major realms have been destroyed in quick succession, and the will of the universe has been provoked. Vaelûn will not let such a transgression pass unanswered - the Tribulation Fiends will soon be unleashed.","\"Since that is the case, then there is no need for us to hold back anyway. Let those who plot in the shadows learn the price of crossing lines. The Primal armies will march through the Void once more, and the universe will know exactly what happens when the peacekeepers are provoked into war!\"","Uncontrollable wrath oozed from every fiber of Asux’s being, and his each word caused the laws of the realm to tremble in excitement.","\"What if... the one responsible is one of the Eight?\" asked the King of Dawn, the first Primal King.","\"Then the Eight will become Seven, or Six, or Five,\" Asux responded without fear. \"Until the universe matures, their powers are restricted, and they are nothing more than Dao Lords with another name. If they had real power, they would not be in hiding, and would instead be ruling openly. Even Eclipse has her Seat of Power known publicly, yet the Eight do not even dare to show their tails.\"","The Dawn King restrained himself, and did not contradict Asux. Technically, that wasn’t strictly true. For example, the location of Ventura, and Asho the Divine Ruler of the Henali, were more or less known. It was true, however, that they acted through their vassals and did not act personally. The reasoning was the same.","\"What if it’s one of the other Sages?\" asked Elizabeth, the Wrathful Queen, the only Primal Queen. Unlike the others, she did not have a solemn expression. Instead, she wore a faint smile, as if she was looking forward to the bloodbath to come.","Asux looked at his daughter, and did not immediately answer. This daughter of his... it had taken the destruction of four Major realms for him to reluctantly allow her to leave the Primal realm, and even that he did because he had no other choice. It was not that he was a protective father, but that he was protective of the universe. With Elizabeth let loose on the universe, many people would truly come to regret the events that had led to this.","\"If it is the Penance race or the Nullith race, you report to me first. For any of the others, kill without mercy,\" Asux finally said, strengthening his resolve.","Four Major realms had already been destroyed. At this point, the line had been crossed, and Vaelûn’s vengeance was inescapable, so what did it matter if a few more Major realms suffered?","Elizabeth grinned, and then began to laugh as she turned around and walked away. For so long, she had been restrained by her love for her father. Now that he was letting her out, who could stop her?","\"One more thing,\" Asux said, his voice breaking through the sound of the Wrathful Queen’s laughter as she walked away. \"Cease all updates to the Cosmic Ascendance Spectrum. Withdraw all observers save one. Only keep an encrypted list accessible only by the Kings, the Queen and I.\"","The Primal Monarch’s every word was a decree, and his every will was an unbreakable law. The armies of the Primals marched out, revealed to the universe for the very first time since the Primordial Age, the repercussions of which could only be guessed.","Yet even when the armies of the Primals marched out, Asux was not alone. There were no Primals with him, that much was true. In fact, it was exactly after the Primals left that this figure appeared.","\"Vaelarin, I have not seen you in a while,\" said Asux, his voice no longer furious. If anything, he sounded drained.","Yet the golden dragon who suddenly appeared before him smiled, apparently pleased by seeing the Primal Monarch in such a state.","\"Asux, the times are changing. Think about my offer once again. The universe could be ours for the taking,\" said Vaelarin, his greed radiating from his body like an actual force of nature.","Asux snorted.","\"Leave, before I decide to turn you into my mount,\" responded Asux.","The golden dragon chuckled, but made no move to leave.","\"Fine, fine, I’ll stop kidding around. I came here not to antagonize you, but out of generosity. Here, a gift from within my treasure hoard,\" said Vaelarin, and tossed a cracked crystal shard towards Asux.","By the time the Primal Monarch caught it, the golden dragon had already disappeared without a trace. Asux frowned. Meeting old friends hardly ever put him at peace.","He instead looked into the shard, and then paused. What he found within... was a document. He frowned once he realized that the document had the aura of Pentagal, but he continued to read anyway.","The document discussed a theory about the best possible arrangement to create the strongest possible universe. As he read further into it, he began to notice a certain familiarity - a familiarity which evoked a sense of absurdity and horror.","How... how could this be? Was this premeditated? But if that was the case, this plan had to come into motion in the very early days of the Primordial age! Who, at that time, among the newly born Primordials, had enough foresight to plan so far ahead?","Asux clenched his teeth, and then sent a private message to Elizabeth.","\"Hold nothing back, my daughter. More chaos... may actually be in our favor.\"","A single message was sent out of the Primary realm, and the web of destiny began to fluctuate like never before.","Within the Folklore realm, Jack was busy spreading the tale of the most dastardly hero to have ever existed. It appeared as if it was a normal day, like any other, but he was not aware of the truth. That was corrected mere moments later when his many formations set up to detect the Nexus event began sending him frantic feedback!","The flow of destiny was changing like never before, and not only was the Nexus event approaching closer, it could happen in the very next few years! Heck, at this rate, it could happen next year !","\"Change of plans,\" Jack said without warning, handing Tiny-Sparkles a list. \"Get me all the resources on this list and I don’t care how. Spend all the gold if you have to, just get me everything, and get it to me quickly. I’ll be in my private quarters.\"","Jack retreated back into the Jolly Rancher, and began setting up a certain formation. When the Nexus event happened, this formation would detect the location of the Nexus, and create an opportunity for him to enter.","Even though he was not connected to the Midnight Inn, he could still build the Midnight Castle using the blueprint, and he could still deploy the Chamber of Rebirth.","At the same time, he couldn’t help but wonder what exactly had happened that caused the destiny of the universe to change so drastically. No doubt, it had something to do with the destruction of another Major realm.","Jack sighed, and hoped there was enough time for Lex to get his hands on the resources he was after in the Gilded Hollow. Jack diverted half his attention to absorbing more divine energy, and the other half to building the formation."]},{"number":2351,"title":"Chapter 2351: Zenith","paragraphs":["A dry husk lay on the ground in a white chamber, as it had been for eons untold. Though it was a mere husk, it had such an intense Dao radiation that even other Dao Lords could not easily approach it. Perhaps that was the very reason it was within the white chamber to begin with - to isolate its aura and prevent it from affecting reality outside the chamber.","For the first time since the husk had been brought here, it twitched, and then moved, standing up and adopting the form of a female Primal.","The husk did not even move from its position when a figure appeared in front of it, wrapped in a distortion of space, making it impossible to determine his or her identity.","\"Elizabeth, you have finally emerged,\" the figure said, looking at the husk, sounding pleased. \"Did you get tired and decide to break free, or did your father really allow you to leave on his own?\"","The husk looked at the figure and, despite the distortion, seemed to recognize the figure’s identity.","\"Father let me free on his own,\" she said, sounding extremely pleased. \"Someone really pissed him off with the destruction of those four Major realms. He says that Vaelûn will release the Tribulation Fiends because of it, and he doesn’t sound too happy about that.\"","The figure paused, as if surprised by her words.","\"Tribulation Fiends? How come I’ve never heard of such a thing?\" the figure asked.","The husk shrugged, as if it too had no answer to that question.","\"Who cares? I’m finally free, and there’s a lot of things on my todo list,\" she answered with a hint of anticipation in her voice.","The figure studied Elizabeth for a while, and then shook its head.","\"How ironic is it that the only prison capable of holding you is made from your father’s love?\" the figure asked, and chuckled, as if there was a huge joke hidden within those words.","For a moment, Elizabeth looked melancholic, as if she had gotten lost in her own memories.","\"You know, I’ve never met anyone else who dares to talk to me like that,\" Elizabeth said, shaking her head. \"No one else who is still living, at least. Besides, who can doubt the capabilities of my father?\"","If there was a threat in Elizabeth’s words, the figure seemed not to hear it.","\"It’s good to have you back. The universe has changed a lot while you were away, so try not to die - that would be awfully awkward considering all the hype around your name.\"","With that final message, the figure disappeared, leaving the husk alone inside the white chamber.","At the same time, around the universe, a single name was repeated again and again, though so many did not know or understand the significance of it. Elizabeth, the Wrathful Queen of the Primals, daughter of the Primal Monarch. It sounded impressive, but how was she different from any of the other Kings? Surely being the daughter of the Monarch did not give her too significant an advantage.","Too few knew the real reason, and they did not reveal it to others. It was for that reason, the significance of her arrival was lost on most, for there was other news that was far more easy to understand the significance of. Primal armies had marched out of their realms, and they were none too polite to any who crossed their path.","The peacekeepers were determined to keep the peace, even if they had to kill everyone to do it! Between the countless deaths caused by the destruction of three realms, the slaughter resulting from the war, and the furious cleansing of the universe carried out by the Primals, the universe had, for the first time in eons, suffered a decrease in total population.","To be fair, the Primals didn’t just go around killing anyone they found. Instead, they killed any and all who had a hand in furthering the war, which was quite a lot of people.","Their ruthlessness and their resourcefulness could not be underestimated, and they quickly found leads on those who had planned the destruction of the four realms, not to mention learned of plots to destroy even more realms!","Their unstoppable march, despite leaving a trail of destruction, began to give some people hope that the war would soon come to an end. The peacekeepers were truly bringing about peace, even if their methods were just as terrifying as the war itself. At least this way, an end was within sight.","Or so the naive thought.","One day, without warning, a new terror was unleashed upon the universe in the form of monsters. Some of them were ethereal, while others were made of fire, or lightning. The most terrifying of all took the form of spirits, affecting the mind directly, leaving behind only a body or soul, devoid of all spirit - a form of living death!","It did not take long before someone recognized that the ones made of lightning took the shape of the ancient Farham race! The ones of fire were from the long lost Ignivar race. The ethereal and spirit monsters seemed to take the shape of a race that none could identify, yet that did not change their terror.","These monsters, which quickly gained the name Tribulation Fiends, targeted one and all who bore some form of negative karma towards the universe, even if it was the slightest bit. Suffice to say, that list included almost every living Dao Lord, simply because they had been alive for so long that committing a universal crime or two was absolutely normal.","Unfortunately, Dao Lords weren’t the only ones on that list. A majority of Celestial Immortals - at least the longest lived ones - were on that list. The number of Heaven Immortals who bore such sin were fewer, but that was only relative to the percentage of Celestials. In actual numbers, they were even more!","As the cultivation level dropped, the number of sinners also decreased, simply because it was too difficult to commit a sin against the universe if one was too weak - difficult, but not impossible.","Only the mortals seemed least affected by the appearance of these Fiends.","The existence of the Tribulation Fiends would not have been an issue if they were just ordinary monsters. The problem was that they were empowered by the universe, making them especially lethal against Dao Lords!","The level of chaos across the universe reached its zenith, unsurpassed in the current and previous age. Thus, the Dream Master considered this the best time to initiate the next level of a plan that had long been set.","The Dream realm no longer restrained itself to only trapping Dao Lords within the realm itself. No, an army of Sandmen exited the realm unannounced, and began targeting those Dao Lords weakened or wounded by the Tribulation Fiends!"]},{"number":2352,"title":"Chapter 2352: The wrong script","paragraphs":["It only took a few years, but peace became a distant memory none could hope for. There was no end in sight for the unfolding devastation. The universe had existed for too long, giving too many forces enough time to build up countless forces and accumulate inexhaustible reserves.","Most lines of communication across the universe broke, leaving Major realms isolated. Regardless of the level of organisation, traversing the Void became too dangerous. Not only were the Void Dwellers becoming stronger and more aggressive, the Spirit Tribulation Fiends began to parasitise the Void Dwellers, providing them the perfect disguise.","They prowled the Void, searching for any signs of universal sin.","To be clear, conventional sins were not a target for these Fiends. They seemed only interested in those that had sinned against the universe itself!","It seemed that in a span of just a few years, the universe became shrouded by an impenetrable darkness. Those who had ventured to foreign realms for war became stuck there, and were forced to find a means of survival there.","This level of disconnectedness brought back an old, forgotten fear that had long been relegated to mortals: the fear of the unknown. The battlefields of the humans became disconnected, with no way of knowing what was happening there. Most news agencies had nothing to report, and even if they did it was too difficult to reach out to their subscribers.","Suddenly, many began to regret forcing the Midnight Inn to cease its activities. Were it still open during this time, it would have become the central hub for travel across the universe.","The Humanoid Alliance began to regret their sudden lack of access to the Midnight Taverns.","Now, in the universe, there were only a very few forces who could still reach anywhere they desired, yet none were available for public or general use.","The Garvitz realm, owned by the Devils, became one of the realms which could reach all others - though it required the devils to be summoned to the targeted location by a local. The other realm which could access anywhere across the universe was the Dream realm!","Only now were many beginning to understand why the Primal race had been so furious. The Tribulation Fiends had literally, singlehandedly toppled the universal order!","Not even the Path of Chaos was happy about this level of chaos, for they too were suffering from it tremendously. It was at this time that the upper echelon of the Path of Chaos began to realize that someone had been using them, turning them into targets while they harvested some unknown reward, or forwarded some unimaginable plot!","The few who seemed to be benefiting the most from such a situation were the Deities. An air of fear and doubt created the perfect environment for them to prey upon the helpless, offering them a guiding hand and welcoming them into the warm embrace of their faiths!","Within the Folklore realm, even Jack learned bits about what was happening across the universe, though he heard more rumor than fact. He could not ascertain the actual situation, but there was no one to blame for that as isolation had naturally brought about a lack of information.","He could not help but think about the Midnight Inn. He was sure that, even now, the two Rhinocentaurs would continue to receive updates about what was actually happening. Velma also had a tavern she could use to communicate with the Inn, providing it with whatever information the Humanoid Alliance had.","Theoretically, the Midnight Inn should be safe. The realm was too minor, with too few guests, most of them that were too weak to attract the attention of the Tribulation Fiends. Still, he could not help but worry. Even if something was going terribly wrong, there was nothing he could do about it!","What the hell was happening to the universe? Why was everything deteriorating so quickly? It didn’t make sense at all! Not even Dao Lords, heck not even beings above the Dao Lord level could cause the universe to suffer as such, so who exactly was pulling the strings from the back, and for what purpose?","Unfortunately, worrying could not give him any answers, so he focused even harder on building his formation and upgrading his level. These were uncertain times, and he needed all the strength he could muster to survive it!","Lex within the Gilded Hollow was about to reach the Dao materials he had been waiting for, and didn’t let his worries distract him. His situation was too precarious for such thoughts.","Unbeknownst to him, the Midnight Inn system was displaying a type of notification he had never seen before!","Status Update: Unable to connect to Host. Entering dormancy mode, limiting all non-essential system functions, diverting excess energy towards self repair. Estimated time to full repair: 52 years.","Besides that, there was another, critically important notification that would have horrified him if he would have seen it.","The Primordial Energy scale, a scale of the amount of Primordial energy absorbed by the system and kept in reserve for a specific purpose, began to slowly, yet undeniably decrease. It wasn’t that the energy was being dissipated or lost, but that the system began to absorb it to facilitate its self repair.","While Lex had already removed a large amount of Primordial energy from within his system, he hadn’t had the time to remove all of it. Slowly, but surely, the scale started to head towards 0!","Within the Midnight Inn, all the guests suddenly received an unusual notification. Most of the Inn’s services would soon be shut down, leaving only the most basic and essential services functioning.","Of course, most of the guests couldn’t be bothered by that at all. After all, within the Midnight Inn something was happening that would have shocked the whole universe!","Since the Tribulation Fiends were summoned by the universe itself, no realm, regardless of how safe, or well hidden, could avoid them. The Midnight realm was no exception to the rule either.","It was just that, well, things didn’t seem to be going according to the regular script."]},{"number":2353,"title":"Chapter 2353: True damage","paragraphs":["\"This is madness!\" roared the black dragon as he used his Dragon’s Might like a literal shield, protecting himself as he retreated.","\"This is exposure therapy!\" Lex responded as he rapidly absorbed the strange ’aura’ attacking them!","Lex referred to the thing attacking them as ’aura’ because he had no other word for it. Calling it some kind of forcefield might also be applicable, but it still didn’t sound right.","They were on the hunt for Dao Material, which naturally grew in the areas of the Gilded Hollow that were filled with the most valuable and high quality resources. The transition from an area filled with resources at a certain cultivation level to the next one was a gradual change, and not an abrupt one.","Thus, it was between the regions of Celestial level resources and Dao level resources where Lex could harvest Dao materials without encountering full, Dao level obstacles. The list of resources he had gone through - the thousands upon thousands of Dao materials he’d had to filter out - were all found in this region where the resources had begun to transition to a higher level, with the relative danger of it not quite catching up.","It was still absurdly dangerous!","Lex and the black dragon were the only ones who had ventured out, mainly because the number or residents in the stronghold who dared risk exiting were too few. Besides, Lex didn’t particularly need any help. Even the black dragon only came because he himself wanted to harvest some valuable resources, and this was an opportunity of a lifetime.","Although the dragon wasn’t too familiar with Lex himself, since he had the Fortune Lords endorsement, he was the ideal partner for these excursions.","Now, amidst the life-threatening madness they were experiencing, the black dragon was more confident than ever before about this choice!","It had been years since they left, and there were a mere 20 miles (32 km), or 105,600 footlong sandwiches, between their current location and the Dao material known as Memory of Rust! Barring their path, however, was an invisible, untouchable thing that attacked them at a fixed, consistent pace, ignoring all defenses to exact True damage - a concept Lex had only encountered in games and not in real life.","It sounded like radiation of some kind, except that there was no radiation. There was no forcefield, no aura, no magical, corrosive, microscopic pollen or evil sentient wind of some kind. No, whatever was attacking them was a form of existence that neither Lex nor the black dragon had encountered.","Thus, as common sense demanded, the black dragon sought to protect himself. But keeping up with the tradition of not acting as one would expect, instead of defending, Lex began to absorb whatever it was into his necklace!","The attacking thing was not at the Dao level, which is why Lex dared to do such a thing. Only by absorbing it and integrating it into the fake realm Lex was creating could he study it and discover what it was.","Such nonchalance towards possible death and injury filled the black dragon with excitement, causing him to break out into laughter as he stood behind Lex, using him as a necklace shaped shield.","\"Do you have any idea what this thing is?\" the black dragon asked, plucking off the shattered scales from his body so that new ones would have a place to grow.","\"Not at all. True damage shouldn’t be a thing - it doesn’t make sense,\" responded as he healed himself faster than the rate at which he was suffering injury. \"I mean, if the attacker is considerably stronger than the target, then the attack itself automatically becomes a form of True damage. But over here, I can feel that the source of this offense is actually weaker than me, meaning it can’t even be considered to be at the peak of the Heaven Immortal realm! I’m really curious to see what is causing this.\"","The dragon laughed as a certain thrill filled his body - this dance with danger and death was something he had never felt before, simply because anyone inside the Gilded Hollow who was a risk taker was dead. Self preservation was the theme of life in the Hollow, so such behavior was literally something he’d never conceived of before!","\"Yes, let’s go towards the mysterious thing trying to kill us!\" he said as he followed Lex, diverting slightly from their original destination.","The closer they got, the more intense the damage became, to the point where the black dragon had to stop following Lex, much to his dismay. Despite being in the middle of the Celestial Immortal realm, the black dragon’s defense was weaker than Lex’s! It was quite humiliating.","In all fairness, black dragons were better known for their offense than defense.","Lex continued walking until he encountered a small cave which seemed to be the source of the issue. He raised an eyebrow for even though right now, the laws of his universe seemed to be dominating the Gilded Hollow, that seemed not to be the case inside the cave!","Lex frowned and slowly extended a wisp of his spirit sense inside the cave, using the technique taught to him by Mithon, but it seemed not to work for him. The moment he touched the boundary of the wall, his spirit sense evaporated completely, causing a minor injury to his spirit.","For a moment, Lex thought that the source of the True damage were the laws of Pentagal, but he quickly dismissed that thought. While the laws of Pentagal, which seemed present inside the cave, had harmed him, the laws were limited to the cave itself. The thing that was coming outside the cave could survive even in the laws of his universe, so it had to be something else entirely.","Lex thought out about the situation for a moment. He could see that there was something akin to a formation, etched within the walls of the cave, which kept the laws of Pentagal anchored within it. If he were to destroy that, he’d be able to enter the cave, but that may destroy the source of the attack as well.","He felt determined to find some way to enter the cave and explore it, for if Lex could somehow replicate the feat of True damage... he could not even imagine just how powerful he could become!","Lex retreated from the mouth of the cave and went back to the black dragon, explaining the situation to him.","\"Do you have any ideas about how I can enter without disrupting the formation?\" Lex asked, causing the black dragon to frown for a moment before he took something out from a spatial tool.","\"I will use a method from the Fortune Lord, and you can fuel it using your own energy. Just make sure it doesn’t go out, and you should be able to enter without an issue.\""]},{"number":2354,"title":"Chapter 2354: Memories","paragraphs":["The black dragon handed Lex a powerful and potent tool - one that was both costly to make, and would require an immense amount of Fortune aura to use. It was not something everyone could afford. In short, he handed Lex a black umbrella that would work based not on Lex’s energy, but on his fortune aura.","Fortunately, he was not lacking in fortune aura at all!","Lex grabbed the umbrella and had to admit that its smooth finish, perfect weight and the strength of its body made the umbrella appear quite cool. When matched with his suit, it was almost a perfect replacement for a cane - not that he usually carried one of those. Now, though, he was beginning to feel like he should.","Lex lifted the umbrella over him and opened it, enveloping himself in some kind of shield powered by his own fortune aura. Lex’s understanding of fortune aura was basically negligible, so he didn’t know if this aura was replenishable, or what the adverse effects of using it were. However, whatever the costs, he would learn about them over time. This opportunity, however, could not be gained again, which is why he didn’t mind paying a certain cost for it.","Once again he returned to the cave and, carefully, crossed the edge of the umbrella into the cave to see if it was affected by the laws of Pentagal. The umbrella remained entirely unharmed, though the drain on his fortune aura increased by a small amount.","It seemed to work, but Lex was still extremely careful while entering to make sure that nothing went amiss. Exposure to the laws of Pentagal, for Lex, seemed to be lethal. Or maybe it was the depth and concentration of those laws in this case which harmed him.","Yet the umbrella worked as advertised, with the strain on his fortune aura being its only adverse effect.","Walking into the depths of the cave, Lex turned through a few different corners, walking into the depths of an unusual world. The laws of Pentagal were not so fundamentally different from his own. There were still forces of attraction and repulsion, there were still states of matter, and there was still heat.","Yet light functioned entirely differently, as it was a gas. Moreover, the more of it that was used up to ’see’ the less of it there would be left. Perhaps there were ways to replenish light in the normal law framework of Pentagal, but Lex could not see through it in a single glance. Maybe if he spent some time here studying the laws, he could learn a bit more, but that was not his goal here.","He could tell that the formations here were self repairing, and were extremely old. Even now, they were not exactly fragile, for they could continue to exist for countless more years. There was, however, a delicate balance in the artificially maintained laws, and the gap caused by his umbrella was causing such a strain on them that they might not last long.","The first half of the cave seemed just like a cave, but the second half suddenly transitioned into what Lex could only assume was some kind of laboratory. It wasn’t because he recognized equipment, but because the laws of memory worked a little strangely in Pentagal. Lex could recall the memories of this lac, especially since it was at the core of where the laws were densest.","The lab, for the most part, remembered being still. The memory had no concept of time, so there were countless memories of stillness, and then of being used by someone to conduct some kind of experiment. The someone died in the very lab for reasons unknown.","He tried to figure out why he could still sense the memories within the umbrella, and discovered that it was a result of a weird resonance between the laws of the two universes.","Lex walked to where the lab remembered that someone dying, and saw the corpse of an unusual creature that looked like a humanoid insect with terrifying mandibles on its face sticking out.","That’s not what struck Lex, though. Nor did he focus on why the corpse looked so fresh. Instead, it was the creature’s crystalline eyes that attracted his attention, for his gaze was turned towards Lex, and it was that very gaze that was exacting True damage onto him.","\"An eye attack?\" Lex murmured to himself, reminiscing about Evisceration, the very first eye attack he ever learned. He could use an upgraded version of it even now, and it was fairly powerful. If the attack landed on a soul, it could burn right through it. Still, it wasn’t as strong as true damage!","A True damage attack that targeted the soul... just thinking about it got Lex excited. The question was, though, how was he going to learn the secret behind this True damage gaze? More importantly, he wanted to know why it worked in the laws of both universes, even though the laws were so different? Could it be that the attack relied on one or a few laws that were the same in both universes? Was that even possible?","Lex squatted on the ground and took a closer look at the eyes. If he approached the corpse, and his umbrella brought the creature within its range of influence, the corpse might dissipate, so he needed to figure this out right here, right now.","What’s more, he could feel the ground vibrating beneath his feet. Very soon, the formations within the cave were going to break. Lex couldn’t help but miss the Innkeepers Scent Diffuser at that moment.","Reaching a strange stalemate with a corpse, there was only one thing he could do. He could simply do his best to study the laws the gaze was affecting to the best of his ability. Oh, and he could use the strange way that memory worked in Pentagal to look into the creatures memories and try to figure it out through that.","Except that he could not access the memories of the being for it was dead and gone. Only the memories that belonged to its body were available to him. That would have to suffice."]},{"number":2355,"title":"Chapter 2355: The retribution I","paragraphs":["Four minutes. The cave only lasted for four minutes, and in that time Lex did his best to blindly memorise every interaction the crystalline eyes had with the surrounding laws. The issue was that the interaction was with foreign laws that he didn’t understand too well, so deciphering what was happening would not be easy.","He also looked through the corpse’s memories, but as it turned out the memories had a halflife, meaning that the corpse would lose its older memories in repeated intervals. Thus, what Lex saw was less of the beings regular actions, and more of how across the ages the surrounding laws reacted to the gaze.","While Lex himself didn’t get the answer, at least he got a lot of information from which he could figure out the answer on his own. It was good enough, given the circumstances.","As soon as the formations crashed, the entire cave turned to dust and vanished, as if it could not adapt to the laws of this universe at all. Lex, though, remained seated for a while, both to finish up healing from all the damage he had accumulated, and to consolidate all the information he had memorised so that he could go through it easily in the future.","When he finally stood up, the black dragon had already arrived behind him and was standing guard.","\"I have bad news,\" he said in a sombre voice, disregarding whatever had happened to the cave. \"My Retribution sensor has gone off. We’ve already been targeted by the Hollow, and the retribution should land anywhere between ten and fifty hours.\"","There was no excitement this time, nor was the black dragon in the mood to crack jokes. The retribution, in usual times, was an inescapable death sentence. Only now that the Hollow had opened and been exposed to the laws of this universe had the effect of the retributions been reduced.","Lex looked from the dragon to the strange lines attached to his karma - the very same ones targeting all those who had recently entered the Hollow. Previously, there was only one string, but now they were already up to seven.","It seemed that the others were looting the Hollow much faster than he had anticipated. But this was not what the dragon was walking about.","\"Should we teleport back to the waygate and rush back to the stronghold?\" Lex asked, since the dragon was the more experienced one.","The black dragon shook his head.","\"This is the reason no one leaves the stronghold. Once you’re targeted by the retribution, there is no escape. Did you really think it was so easy to fool the Hollow? If we try to escape, the timing for the retribution speeds up, and so does the intensity. If we try to prepare for it, try to build our defenses or augment our own strength, the same happens. If you try to be smart and try to weaken yourself in the hopes that the retribution will arrive later, then you’re in bad luck because the retribution will take advantage of your weakness and arrive immediately!","\"The Hollow’s retribution has slayed many lords, not to mention just immortals like us. If it weren’t for the fact that the Fortune Lord has announced that the retributions have been weakened, I too would not have risked coming out. The only thing we can do now is... accept that it is coming, and be ready for it.\"","Lex looked at the dragon for a moment, and then shook his head.","\"I don’t have the time to waste waiting around,\" he said and teleported a few miles away from the black dragon and then stabbed himself in the hand. Since the retribution could be summoned quicker, then he might as well see for himself what the retribution had to offer.","There were three types of retribution. The first would teleport the target to a dangerous place, and if they survived the target would be returned to his original location. The second would turn the target’s surroundings directly into some kind of danger zone. Finally, the Hollow would take the target’s soul and put it through a few rounds of torture.","As Lex waited for the retribution to fall, there was no ounce of fear in him, regardless of how grave the danger was. He was perfectly calm, and in fact, studied the descent of the retribution itself. Everything in the Gilded Hollow was a valuable resource - everything!","Insight into how the laws of a different universe worked was not something he’d be able to get easily even if he became a Dao Lord, so he would learn and memorise everything right now.","As if sensing Lex’s challenge, the Hollow seemed infuriated - as if it could feel actual emotions. The sky darkened and streams of red lightning snaked through the bubbling clouds of toxic gas that began to fall from the sky.","The ground beneath his feet came to life and started to grab his legs, turning into millions of arms that reached up with the hope of swallowing him within. The wind turned to blades, the light turned into a flameless fire, and gravity turned into the pull of death itself, trying to unravel his soul from its very source.","The karma attached to his body turned into snakes, trying to bite him, hoping to pump in their venom and swallow the meat off his bones. Fortune became misfortune, strength became hollow, and a plague fell upon him as if it was who was going through armageddon instead of the times.","Lex had no physical body save the necklace in the Hollow. He merely used a projection to show a body like his original one, and yet the changes affected his projection too. Each and every hair on his body turned into miniature locusts, and instead of hopping away they began to attempt to devour him, as if his body was the season’s crop.","Dread, fear, hopelessness rained upon him like the monsoon rains, trying to infect his very spirit and corrode him from within. Such a devastating, targeted vengeance struck Lex with such vicious malice that he could physically feel the hate of the Gilded Hollow. All this... and it was merely the beginning of the weakened retribution.","In the distance, the black dragon watched in horror as Lex stood there, seemingly not resisting at all. The thing that sent a tremor down his spine was not among all the horrors afflicting Lex, though. No, the thing that frightened and horrified him so was the faint hint of a smirk on Lex’s face as all that happened, as if this was amusing to him."]},{"number":2356,"title":"Chapter 2356: The retribution II","paragraphs":["Back on Earth, Lex had encountered, and even studied many religions. It wasn’t because he was particularly faithful, but because when he was young mobile phones didn’t exist yet so he had to entertain himself in other ways. That would, naturally, include reading the books that lay around the house when it wasn’t possible to go outdoors.","A common theme, he discovered, among many faiths was the end of days. Raining fire, ground shattering earthquakes and locust plagues were also very common in them, which is why Lex began to wonder if the Hollow was using his own memories as a template for the retribution.","He wouldn’t say it was unoriginal. Why did that matter? As long as it worked, it would be good enough. It was just that, despite the fact that all of this was actually quite powerful and was affecting the necklace’s body, the danger didn’t scale properly.","He remembered back when he got stuck in the Crystal realm, he had barely started his cultivation journey. He was a mortal, and a very low leveled one at that. He was easily hurt, and easily burned. In that state, he had to very literally swim through lava so heavy that it crushed his body even as the heat seared through his very being!","Back then, if his soul, body and spirit hadn’t been fused together, he would not have survived. That experience was scary, because he had no idea whether his plan would work, or if he would survive, as he swam through that lava. The pain was also much harder to ignore back then.","Then what? He swam through a sea of lava and found heaven on the other side? No, there was no such thing. He had to drag his broken, battered, burned, body and save himself without letting himself faint, or he’d probably die.","Considering his weakness, and the limited options available to him back then, what did it even matter if the sky fell down on him? A cloud of toxic gases? A plague, a curse, an attack targeting his soul directly? Yes, they were all very, very powerful and if he didn’t resist, he would surely die here.","But that was just it. Compared to those early days of his, he had way too many ways to fight back, to resist, to... to truly savor this retribution.","Lex’s smile grew wider as the pain began to pierce through his soul.","\"Very good. Show me more, teach me more,\" he whispered as he looked up at the sky, as if talking to the Hollow itself. \"I have too many enemies who are living too comfortably. Show me exactly how... I should exact my retribution on them.\"","The black dragon was stunned, for he suddenly felt that the retribution that was targeting him disappeared! That was literally unprecedented in the history of the Gilded Hollow!","Yet he instinctively knew... it wasn’t that the retribution had disappeared. The Gilded Hollow had limited energy, so it wasn’t that the retribution had disappeared. Rather, it was that the energy allocated for his retribution was being used somewhere else, and he felt like he had a good idea where it was going.","Red lightning struck Lex from the sky as he finally started to defend himself, and the clap of thunder shattered space around him. Yet behind the space of the Gilded Hollow was not the Void, but just another, deeper level of the Hollow, as if it was folded upon itself.","Divine energy within the necklace began to churn as Lex healed the necklace which, for the first time, suffered actual damage from an attack. The intensity of that red lightning was quite memorable, but Lex could not focus on that.","He fell from the shattered space to the ground beneath, and the ground from the shattered space above him reached down to swallow him whole. Reality itself seemed to be breaking, or maybe this is what premium Saturn cake tasted like, because how was there a ground above him and beneath him?","Lex surrounded himself with a barrier, created a Domain within the barrier and unleashed his new and improved Domination. He didn’t bother trying to attack the retribution - he wouldn’t know where to begin. He only needed to survive, so he defended, and watched as the Hollow unleashed madness upon him.","The dirt in the air clumped together and began to form countless bodies, as if ashes of a trillion corpses joining back together to recreate those very corpses. An army of humanoid insects screeched at him - the screech a mindless wail of fury that, somehow, was also colored red and black. They lunged at him as if he were the enemy they had been dreaming about for an eon, yet there could have been no dream. The corpses were empty, there was no spirit or soul in them, only a single shade of the endless fury that constituted the Gilded Hollow’s retribution.","While Lex defended, he also memorised the way the laws moved, the way they writhed, the way they came together, for even though the Gilded Hollow was attacking, these were the laws of his universe! These laws, at least, he could understand. These laws, he could learn to replicate.","Amidst all the chaos and madness, Lex became even more sure that the Gilded Hollow wasn’t actually alive, or that its will did not have any actual sentience. This retribution was just the natural reaction of the laws of the universe to its own destruction - much in the way that his universe was expressing its anger in the form of Tribulation Fiends.","Lex fell to the ground finally, and what followed him was a mindless army of insects so vast that space threatened to shatter once more!","But just as the space was about to give way, Lex strengthened it, preventing it from breaking again. The laws of space were extremely familiar to him. The reason he stopped the shattering of space, though, wasn’t to avoid more attacks. Instead, he was because he decided to test what he was learning from the Hollow right then and there.","It was too soon to summon the Fake realm he was creating inside the necklace, so using his domain he took control of the space around him, and through his Domination he made it his own. Then he directly clashed against the Hollow’s retribution, not to break through the retribution, but to sharpen his control and consolidate all he was learning.","He was fighting back against the retribution not to end it, but to use it to sharpen his own blade, so to speak.","\"Is that all?\" Lex asked the Hollow. \"This is not even enough to express my own anger, so how can it be enough to express yours? Show me more!\"","As if responding to his words, another bolt of red lightning flashed.","Deep, deep within the Gilded Hollow, far beyond where mere Dao Lords could enter, within the ruins of a humble manor, a corpse sat upon a broken throne. Yet, as if carried by some unknown magic, Lex’s words whispered in the ears of that corpse, and one of its eyelids trembled, ever so slightly.","Yet, for better or for worse, there was no one around to witness the event. Though if someone saw the corpse, they might be too distracted to notice the twitch to begin with. After all... seated upon the broken throne, surrounded by an aura that could bring a Dao Lord to his knees, was the corpse of a human."]},{"number":2357,"title":"Chapter 2357: Life laws","paragraphs":["\"Yes, I think that should be enough for today,\" said Lex as he cleared his throat, exuding the same casual confidence as before, completely hiding the amount of pain he was actually in.","Jokes aside, he had asked the Gilded Hollow to teach him more about how to torture people, but how could he have known that the realm would take him so seriously? Fortunately, the energy absorption system he had encoded into the necklace itself had not failed him which kept him empowered throughout the retribution, allowing him to survive.","But survival did not have to be pleasant. The Hollow’s retribution was far from weak, and that was considering the fact that it had been adjusted to his cultivation level. Any other regular Heaven Immortal would not have been able to survive at all. This was a clear and complete death sentence for them!","He managed to keep the necklace from suffering any real harm, but damn the process was unpleasant. It was not just about all the visible attacks coming his way - the very laws that sustained the existence of his mind and soul were attacked.","Yes, it wasn’t Lex that was attacked, but the laws that sustain his existence. This was a simple concept to imagine, but it was practically incredibly difficult because influencing those laws was exceptionally difficult. Even Lex could not do it to a foe near him in cultivation level.","He had to rely on some of the divine energy to empower the laws of his own existence - something Lex never even imagined he would need to do. But, all things considered, it taught him a new weakness he needed to address, so he wasn’t ungrateful for the experience.","At this point, Lex thought that it was a good idea to stop provoking the dead universe and just let the retribution end. Resisting the urge to cough out blood, he just endured the unending madness until finally he felt the force beginning to recede.","Since his body was a projection he could control, he appeared entirely unharmed. The black dragon was beyond impressed at the sight. In truth, though, Lex’s soul was definitely wounded and would require some healing.","Fortunately, the Hollow was a land of endless treasures so finding something that would heal him wasn’t all that difficult.","\"Nothing wakes you up like a good retribution in the morning, huh?\" Lex asked the dragon as he approached him, making sure that his image was not affected.","For a time the black dragon did not respond for he was too astounded. Eventually, though, he found that there was only one thing he could say.","\"It’s no wonder that the Fortune Lord decided to support you. Clearly, you are out of the ordinary.\"","It was simple praise, but the sincerity packed within those few words conveyed a meaning that could not be communicated through greater eloquence.","\"Shall we get our hands on that Memory of Rust? That Forgotten Blood is also waiting for us, so let’s not waste any time,\" Lex said as he took the lead, all the while still absorbing the surrounding resources inside his necklace.","The journey to Memory of Rust didn’t last much longer, and there were no great obstacles to getting to it, as promised. Absorbing it into the necklace was actually quite easy, and it brought about a remarkable effect!","Basically, the necklace became totally immune to all forms of natural degradation. It would never rust, never erode, never corrode nor would it ever weaken either. Moreover, absorbing a Dao material raised the natural treasure level of the necklace, elevating it to an incredibly high level!","From there, they journeyed to the Forgotten Blood and managed to get their hands on it too. On the journey, Lex encountered a few other traces of forgotten civilizations and ruins, though nothing was on the level of the cave he encountered for the first time.","Still, even the traces were enough to enlighten Lex a great deal about the kind of species Pentegal must have had.","Eventually, he managed to get Forgotten Blood easily as well, although absorbing it into the necklace was slightly more challenging. However, the benefits of absorbing it were well and far beyond what he had read based on the report.","The reason he wanted to absorb Forgotten Blood was because it contained very thick traces of the laws associated with life. By absorbing it into the necklace, he effectively managed to fill his Fake realm with actual, living beings naturally!","Previously the realm itself was too unstable to support any kind of life, yet the Forgotten Blood made up for some of the shortcomings of the realm. At the same time, it empowered the life laws enough where lifeforms powerful enough to survive the unstable nature of the realm began to appear.","With the appearance of life, the laws of the realm automatically began to stabilise even faster, as if life itself empowered laws.","Lex paused. This was a brand new realization for him, as it was something he’d never noticed before. He’d always thought that the stable laws and realms were what enabled life, but now it seemed like life itself played a major role in stabilising the laws of the universe.","That new piece of information brought him a whole new perspective on the destruction of the Major realms. The ramifications of such events touched on so many different aspects that it was tough to determine what exactly the goal of the mastermind was.","Still, that wasn’t something he needed to concern himself with. If he ever came face to face with whomever was behind it all, there wouldn’t be anything he’d be able to do anyway.","Once he got his hands on those two pieces of Dao materials, it was time to head back. The black dragon, too, gathered many items for his hoard.","The entire journey took them only three years and four months, a little longer than expected. Once they returned, Lex immediately began planning his next trip while checking if there were any updates about the Death Metal rose.","There were no updates, although he did hear news that the Fortune Lord was planning a trip of his own, and he would leave in twelve years. It seemed there were things even the Fortune Lord couldn’t leave inside the Gilded Hollow, and wanted to get his hands on before leaving."]},{"number":2358,"title":"Chapter 2358: Pelagor","paragraphs":["Honestly, the Death Metal Rose was nowhere near the top of his priority list, though it also wasn’t something he could just overlook either. It wasn’t that he was interested in giving it to Regix, but that his own life would become a lot easier if he had a way to cleanse all kinds of curses.","Yet as long as there weren’t any leads, he could disregard it altogether, and instead focus on developing his necklace and increasing his immediate strength. Lex looked through the list of Dao materials once more and narrowed down the list to a few resources he felt like would help him a lot.","He could choose between maximising the number of Dao materials in the least time, or he could get the most suitable ones by sacrificing some time.","The decision wasn’t a big one at all. He chose quality over quantity, and made his pick. In less than an hour after returning to the stronghold, he was ready to set out again. Even if he had already chosen the materials he wanted, he would have had to return to the stronghold anyway for the waygates couldn’t connect to each other, only the stronghold. To go anywhere else, he would need to depart from here.","\"You’re leaving already?\" the black dragon asked, stunned by Lex’s swiftness. \"Don’t you want to rest or recover after our last excursion? You couldn’t have healed completely after the retribution - at least go to a hospital to get checked out.\"","Lex smiled softly, but shook his head.","\"There’s no need, really,\" said Lex dismissing the concerns. \"You can rest up and regrow your scales. That way, you can join me on my next trip.\"","The black dragon didn’t know how to respond, but he felt only great respect for Lex. It was exactly this kind of dedication that allowed one to surpass oneself.","\"If you must go out, then wait a moment. There is someone I want to introduce to you - someone who also wants to venture out, and is completely reliable as well. He will be able to help you on your journey, and make your travel speed much faster.\"","Lex raised an eyebrow. Considering that the travel time for him for each trip was in months and years, he didn’t mind waiting a few hours to meet a potential ally.","\"You won’t need to wait long. I’ll summon him immediately, he’ll help you with whatever you need. He does have certain requirements of his own, though,\" said the black dragon as he quickly used something akin to a phone to call someone.","Since there was a wait involved, Lex decided to take a break after all and went to a waiting room and closed his eyes. While it seemed like he was taking a nap, he was actually overlooking the necklace while also reflecting on the news that Jack kept learning.","The universe was a mess. Returning and beating his stalker would no longer be good enough, because once he returned to the Midnight Inn he’d need to worry about protecting it and keeping it safe. While such a thing had always been difficult, Lex might as well look for some opportunities here for that while he could.","He opened his eyes and began going through the list of all resources. The Fortune stronghold had the most extensive catalog of treasures and their uses Lex had ever seen. In truth, it was probably the most extensive across the universe. Reading through it would not only increase his awareness, it could also provide him with certain solutions he’d never even considered.","Lex had not forgotten that he was connected to Lotus. While even now, he could not make use of its main ability, one day he’d get there. Once he reached that level, he could turn pure energy directly into valuable resources. It was like a living, breathing 3D printer for treasures.","Thus, if he could expose himself to rare and valuable treasures now, he’d know what they would be like and would be able to make them in the future himself.","There was no guarantee for this, but he believed that one day, he’d be able to do it.","It only took a few hours before the black dragon returned, and he brought with him a guest Lex had not been expecting to see at all.","It wasn’t that Lex was familiar with the person, but that he was familiar with the race!","It was a Blue Whale! A regular old Blue Whale, the kind that could be found on Earth!","Of course, over here, the Blue Whale had the cultivation level of a level 1 Celestial Immortal, and that was exceptionally impressive considering how mundane its race was!","Ordinarily, Beasts cultivated using their bloodlines, and the Blue Whale bloodline was quite normal, without any formidable ancestors, mainly because this was a sub-race of a sub-race. It was meant to remain a mortal and nothing more. Yet, perhaps due to the cultivation technique that relied on Fortune, this whale had challenged and changed its fate.","\"I’ve told you before that there are very few who dare to leave the stronghold. Well, allow me the opportunity to introduce one of the most consistent excavationist of the stronghold. Over the years, no one has left the stronghold more than him. He has surpassed the limitations of his race through his own efforts, but has now finally hit a bottleneck that cannot be overcome through mundane means.\"","Lex raised his eyebrow, and looked at the whale, studying it.","\"Allow me to introduce myself. My name is Pelagor, and I walk the path of cultivation,\" the whale said, his tone lacking any arrogance, yet filled with self confidence as well. \"Step by step, I have raised myself from my mortal roots, and my aim is to swim to the end of this cultivation path, and see for myself what horizons it will reveal. Yet upon this difficult journey, I have arrived at a hurdle I cannot cross alone. I have been told that... you may be able to help.\"","Lex looked from the whale towards the dragon. He had a feeling that this story was going to be a good one."]},{"number":2359,"title":"Chapter 2359: Was that even possible?","paragraphs":["Pelagor was a fully grown, mature Blue Whale, but for this meeting he had naturally shrunk his size. Although he had, up until now, somehow retained his original race, he still wielded the might and abilities of a Celestial Immortal. Yes, he might not have unlocked any bloodline abilities as a Blue Whale, but he could make do without those.","After all, as far as Lex had seen, there was very limited conflict inside the Gilded Hollow owing to the existential crisis of retributions, and the laws of the stronghold. That made him wonder what Mithon had done to get exiled, but the thought was fleeting.","\"Your resolve and accomplishments are all quite admirable, Pelagor. I am Lex. Please, tell me, how can I help you? And how can you help me?\" he asked, cutting right to the point.","Back in the early days of the Midnight Inn, Little Blue was stranded and helpless to move beyond the limits of the small lake Lex made for him. Thus, he got an upgrade where a pool of water would stay under him at all times and move with him, ’effectively’ allowing him to fly through the air - or, well, swim through it.","Pelagor as an Immortal did not need such a thing, but incidentally had opted for the same method of moving around.","\"I have heard the tale of your journey, about your confrontation with the retribution, and how easily you were able to acquire the Dao materials. Although your cultivation level is lower than mine, there is no doubt about your capabilities. At this point in time, there is no one else I can approach who can help me. You see, there is a certain treasure that I need to take a step forward in my cultivation journey, but it is in an extremely dangerous location that cannot be reached easily. I myself have tried four times to reach it, but have failed.\"","Pelagor revealed a map to Lex, one that was incredibly detailed not just in landmarks or nearby treasures, but also the surrounding dangers.","\"The item I seek is here, right on the border of the Dao lands, where the dangers reach the Dao level. While the item is not quite in that area itself, it is surrounded by Dao radiation, making it impossible for me or anyone else in the stronghold to actually reach it.","\"I have tried. I really have tried everything, and have even appealed to the Fortune Lord himself, but the Fortune Lord has informed me that on the journey to greater fortunes, I have to rely on my own abilities, efforts, and personal network to succeed. I have tried. Over a hundred thousand years, I have tried, but I keep falling short. Now, your arrival, and your ability have given me hope once more.\"","Lex noticed that Pelagor was careful not to reveal the actual details of the item that he needed, but Lex didn’t mind. The two of them had just met, and trust was something that would take time to build - if they decided to work together at all.","\"I realize that what I am asking from you is quite a lot, and so I am willing to similarly pay such a great price. Or, at least, I am willing to pay whatever it is that I can. If I can get my hands on that item, then I will be able to continue my cultivation journey towards the Dao Lord realm.","\"If you help me acquire that item, then I will swear to serve you for one hundred thousand years - the same amount of time I have sought out this item. The difference will be that I will be much stronger than I am now, with much greater potential to serve and assist you in your endeavors.\"","Pelagor paused and looked at Lex, who had still not revealed even the slightest hint of his inner thoughts.","\"Such an offer may or may not entice you, but to show my sincerity, as well as to demonstrate my strength, ability, and willingness to serve, I can accompany you on your next journey outwards. That way, you can test my abilities first hand, and decide for yourself whether I am worth the investment, and the risk.\"","Compared to the people Lex was used to being around, Pelagor was a lot more strict, rigid and straightforward. He had a serious and solemn personality, which was a huge change from his workers at the Inn who always hid a hint of mischievousness deep within them.","That wasn’t necessarily a bad thing, and Lex was willing to give Pelagor a chance. There was, however, one issue.","\"I don’t know what you have heard, but even I am not immune to Dao radiation. I can, at most, barely tolerate the weakest form of it for a few seconds. Retrieving your treasure is beyond my current abilities,\" Lex said outright, not giving Pelagor any false hope.","Yet, unexpectedly, hearing such a thing seemed to put him at ease instead of trouble him.","\"Yes, I have already expected such a thing. My preparations over the past hundred millenia are exceptionally thorough. I have heard that you are willing to absorb Dao material into your being to strengthen yourself. If that is the case, I can guide you towards certain materials which will help you better tolerate Dao radiation. Tell me, are you familiar with Primordial aura?\"","Now it was Lex’s turn to be surprised. He wasn’t aware that there were things which could help tolerate Dao aura, though the universe was vast so it made sense that such things existed. The question was, what did that have to do with Primordial aura?","\"I am, yes. What does that have anything to do with resisting Dao aura?\" Lex asked, hiding his own curiosity. To others, it might not be such a big deal, but Lex had already attained perfect Primordial aura. It was just not evident to others because he mixed it and hid it within his Domination. In fact, he himself could very loosely be categorized as a Primordial human!","\"I have with me a container filled with Primordial energy,\" told Pelagor. \"On its own that might not help you resist Dao aura, but I happen to also know about the location of a Dao material which can be safe to use as long as it is controlled with Primordial energy. With that, ambient Dao radiation - the kind that is unleashed passively or without any intent - can be converted into Primordial aura, and thus be tolerated...\"","Lex suddenly sat up straight and sealed Pelargor’s mouth! He turned around to look behind him, but he saw nothing. Yet through his instincts he had momentarily felt the shadow of a certain spider behind him, if she could be called that at all.","Had he, somehow, attracted the attention of the owner of the Primordial Garden? All the way here, inside the Gilded Hollow? Was that even possible?"]},{"number":2360,"title":"Chapter 2360: Suicidal","paragraphs":["Lex’s mind raced as he tried to make sense of the situation. He dared not even think of her name at this moment while he figured things out. Although he’d interacted with her many times, using various identities, he’d never been worried because he thought Nuwa was hiding his secrets and keeping him from being traced.","Although she was a master of karma, as far as he could tell, or as far as he’d guessed, she was not spying on Lex through his karma. That was because they had a decent relationship, but also because Nuwa should have been keeping him from being looked through.","So then, why did he suddenly sense her here?","Lex’s eyes narrowed, while Pelagor and the black dragon silently looked at the human in confusion. He just realized that even if she was really spying on him, it should be impossible for him to detect her. Even if the gap between the Gilded Hollow and the rest of the universe weakened her power by a lot, Lex still shouldn’t have been able to detect her.","Did that mean she wanted him to detect it? Was this some kind of message from her to stay away from this Dao material? No, the feeling was that of being spied upon, not of being intimidated. Maybe she wasn’t telling him to stay away, but to go for it and get the treasure. The question was, why?","Lex’s understanding of her was that she was so powerful that she did not need to act with ulterior motives. Her everything was insanely powerful, and the only thing that could control her actions were her own whims. There was nothing she would need from Lex. In that case, was it because their relationship was good that she was guiding him?","Or was it that someone else was pretending to be her to misguide him? It wouldn’t be impossible for another Dao Lord to do that, but who would dare to cross her?","The thought almost made Lex chuckle. Only someone suicidal would try to impersonate her, so he could disregard that thought.","Whatever the case, this incident made Lex decide to take up Pelagor’s offer, and at least check out the Dao material he was talking about.","\"I accept your offer, but don’t talk about that item anymore,\" said Lex as he looked at Pelagor. \"Just directly pass all the information you have on it to me, and share the location. We’ll plan out our journey now and head out as soon as we’re ready. There’s no point in wasting any time.\"","Pelagor wasn’t sure what exactly happened to Lex, but he was glad that the offer was accepted. At the same time, he realized that the items he had talked about might be more valuable than he realized outside in the actual universe. Some precautions were needed to avoid future problems.","He wasn’t too worried about Lex betraying him though, for any agreement they made would be through a binding Fortune Oath. Breaking that was akin to suicide.","The two of them immediately began to plan out their journey.","Far underneath them, however, within one of the chambers of the eleven Dao Lords who had recently awoken from their slumber clutched his chest and grit his teeth as he tried to stifle the bleeding. In front of him, the Fortune Lord stood with a grave look in his eyes, almost as if he was ready to undo a few people’s fortunes himself.","\"What happened?\" the Qilin asked in a tone that brook no resistance or disobedience.","The Dao Lord, a winged Beast from a species Lex had never really seen or heard of before, opened his mouth to speak, but coughed out blood instead.","Romulus sighed, and then used some of the items from his own reserves to heal the Dao Lord enough so that he could speak.","\"The outsider you mentioned, the one from the Midnight Inn,\" he said when he finally recovered, an expression of fear in his eyes. \"I sensed an unusual ripple in his karma when Pelagor mentioned the remaining shell from the egg of the Primordial Farham. I wanted to investigate. I didn’t think there were any Dao Lords in Vaelûn who could match up to us, especially after all the resources we’ve devoured. But...\"","He didn’t need to complete his words. Merely looking at him was enough for Romulus to understand the severity of his injury. A massive chunk of his karma had directly been ripped out of his being, pulling his Dao along with it.","Someone who could do that could just as easily kill him. The fact that they hadn’t meant that this was a warning.","Did that mean that this other Dao Lord had entered the Gilded Hollow as well? It shouldn’t be possible, for Romulus could not sense a similar aura within the Hollow. Yet if they weren’t inside the Hollow, how could they still attack inside of it?","\"I told you all not to offend anyone since we don’t know the situation outside of here yet. Don’t make this mistake again, and recover as quickly as possible. If you’re not able to follow along, then that’ll just be your loss because I won’t be dragging you along.\"","The Dao Lord did not respond, filled with feelings of reluctance and disbelief. After surviving in the Hollow for so many years, they were all extremely cautious. But who could have anticipated that interfering with a mere Heaven Immortal would land him in this situation.","The Beast glared angrily towards Lex, and then looked away. In his mind, he recited the name of the Midnight Inn and swore to stay far away from that cursed place. What kind of freaks was that place filled with that they could injure him this much just like that?","He also thought about looking for revenge, but that was a death wish. He would see what the situation was once he was in Vaelûn, and go from there."]},{"number":2361,"title":"Chapter 2361: F.U. System","paragraphs":["Considering the location of the item that Pelagor told Lex about, he had to change his plan somewhat. He had to settle for grabbing nearby resources instead of the most optimal ones, and the route had to be adjusted to accommodate the search for nearby Dao materials.","Pelagor was already proving to be useful for he was intimately familiar with the terrain of the Hollow, he helped Lex plan a route that avoided obstacles that would consume more time.","He had a few more tips he offered which could help them save time, but they weren’t really applicable to Lex since he would be devouring all nearby resources while they traveled, making it impossible to hide or avoid attention.","With nothing else holding them back, Lex and Pelagor departed immediately. Lex was highly motivated to get whatever that material was that could convert Dao radiation into Primordial aura, and Pelagor was looking forward to getting Lex’s help. To prove his worth, Pelagor volunteered to act as Lex’s mount for the journey, assuring him that he would not slow things down.","Normally, it was not easy to make high level beasts into mounts. The easiest way was if the rider’s cultivation was far greater than the mount itself. In that situation, it would not affect the beast’s ego or pride. Pelagor’s situation, however, was completely different.","His focus was solely on his cultivation journey, and progressing as far as possible. For the sake of progress, if he had to act as a mount, then he would. His pride was not attached to things like that, because he knew what he was working for.","Of course, before leaving they also sealed their agreement with a Fortune Oath. Lex swore that if the effects of the Dao material Pelagor told him about were actually as he described, then he would help him get whatever resource he was looking for. In exchange, Pelagor would work for Lex for a hundred thousand years.","The terms of service were also discussed. Lex could not make Pelagor perform and suicidal tasks on purpose, nor could he act maliciously and order him to purposefully undertake tasks that would harm his person or reputation and so on.","That wasn’t to say that Lex couldn’t have Pelagor fight difficult battles - he just couldn’t use him as a disposable soldier. That wasn’t an issue, for Lex had no intention of doing such a thing to begin with.","Their journey began without many obstacles, and was somewhat different from his journey with the black dragon. The main difference was that the black dragon liked to chat, so their journey was spent in conversation. Pelagor, on the other hand, had a lot more stern and action oriented, which is why he traveled in silence.","Lex did not mind too much, honestly. Yet in the very first month of their journey, they encountered an unexpected acquaintance.","Lex was the first to notice, and an odd expression appeared on his face when he recognized someone he knew. They made a small detour, and soon stumbled upon a Heaven Immortal snake, wrapping its body around a porcupine beast, crushing its body by squeezing, even if it harmed him in the process as well.","\"Mithon? What are you doing outside the stronghold?\" Lex asked as he approached, finally attracting his attention.","Mithon looked up at Lex, and suddenly felt a mix of fear, apprehension and embarrassment!","\"This... this damn beast got me exiled again! I... I’ll kill her!\" she roared and bit the porcupine, ignoring the many spikes sticking into its face as she pumped venom into the beast’s body, slowly killing it.","\"How exactly did you get exiled again?\" Lex asked, but Mithon appeared too embarrassed to answer. Eventually, though, she answered.","\"When I went back to the stronghold, I found that my husband had moved on without me. I can’t really blame him, I was gone for a long time. But when I looked into finding him again, just to see what he’s been up to, I found out that this damn porcupine had tricked my family into joining a demonic cult and cleaned out all my savings!\"","The porcupine, clinging onto the faintest bit of hope, looked towards Lex and tried to explain himself.","\"It’s not a cult. It’s just an extended dopamine cleanse with a 32 million year subscription payment plan and...\"","As if infuriated anew, Mithon bit him again!","\"Damn you Hemzy! A dopamine cleanse gives snakes constipation!\" she roared and, once and for all, put an end to the accursed porcupine.","Throughout the exchange Lex just stood there, unsure of what to make of the situation. He looked towards Pelagor, and he appeared to be just as confused. It seemed... even the Gilded Hollow was not safe from scammers.","\"Alright, well, good luck to you,\" Lex said as he retreated to give her some privacy to uh... grieve?","Yet Mithon quickly let go of the porcupine and followed them.","\"No, wait, senior, can I follow you?\" the snake asked, clearly concerned about being alone.","Lex paused, and then told her the direction they were heading in. Upon hearing it, the snake decided that, perhaps, it was best if she went out on her own. She wanted to live, not dive head first into a deathzone.","The two groups left, leaving the corpse of the porcupine behind. A few days later, however, the pieces of the corpse began to move and recombine on its own, and soon Hemzy opened his eyes once more.","That was a small interval in their journey, but for the most part their journey was uneventful. During this time, Lex not only absorbed resources, he also contemplated on the True damage law he memorized, as well as tried to comprehend all he saw during the retribution.","As if that was not enough, he started the next step of enhancing the necklace. The necklace itself was turning into a carrier of his Fake realm, but Lex had not limited it to that. The basic template for absorbing energy had been added, and now tested.","That was the foundation of a successful system. Then came the next step. Since Lex wanted to create a realm of his own where only he was a Sovereign, he decided that the purpose of this system would be to facilitate him becoming a Sovereign within that fake realm of his.","The next step, then, would be to create a way to completely isolate the interior of the necklace from the outside, at least in terms of law and connectivity. After all, if he didn’t do that and a normal Sovereign, such as his stalker, entered then they would continue to be a Sovereign.","But if it was cut off from the universe, or if the universe did not respond to what was happening inside, that ability of theirs would become restricted. Once Lex managed to do that, the next step would be to have the system help him regulate and control the laws within the fake realm so that being cut off from the laws of the universe wouldn’t cause it to collapse.","If Lex had to name his system, he would call it...","An incredibly audacious idea came to him, one so insane that Lex thought that it was too much. But then he smirked, and just treated it like a goal to work towards without ever worrying about actually reaching it. After all, this goal was so audacious that not even Dao Lord... heck, not even the beings above the Dao Lord level could make such a thing happen.","Lex decided to tentatively name the system he was creating within the necklace to help him manage it, the Fake Universe System. The point of the system would be to help him create, manage and control the fake realm within the necklace, with the ultimate goal of being able to grow it to the point where it’s basically a fake universe of his own!","The thought was amusing. Even the creator of his own system probably couldn’t achieve such an ambitious goal, so there was no need to take it too seriously. For now, he was just setting the foundation of his revenge.","Creating and managing a fake realm, at the very least, was within his capabilities. Between Taro’s journal, and the Lotus which could create worlds out of pure energy, his own mastery of space, and his insight from the birth of the Midnight Realm, Lex was fairly well suited to the task.","With his immediate goals decided, Lex closed his eyes as he sat atop Pelagor. The universe was in chaos, the future was uncertain, and Lex was now using delusional optimism to set his goals, but at least in that moment he was at peace.","The journey took years, and Lex managed to collect three more Dao materials along the way, each one being fused into the necklace one after another. Although each of them was supposed to be easy to absorb and fuse with, Lex began to feel a certain pressure on his soul that he couldn’t ignore after the fourth one. After all, even though technically he was using them to enhance the necklace, the necklace was, after all, fused with his soul so the burden definitely affected him as well.","Maybe he was reaching his limit. Hopefully, he could still absorb whatever Pelagor was leading him towards."]},{"number":2362,"title":"Chapter 2362: I’m ready","paragraphs":["\"It’s right over there,\" said Pelagor as he looked at the ominous looking, black colored, single mountain that rose to an impossible height, with its peak somehow hidden inside an alternate realm with a fixed entrance near the top of the mountain. The spontaneous rivers of flowing lava, entire flocks of massive ravens circling the mountain, and random claps of thunder really set the mood.","Oh, and the mounds and mounds of skulls which formed an entire mountain range around that one, towering mountain really made it abundantly clear just how welcoming this place was.","Oh right, he could also, with his spirit sense, sense just how ridiculously dense the negative karma around the mountain was, as if it was a plague trying its best to eradicate all it touched with extreme vindictiveness!","The laws of the universe were churning and agonising, but no matter what, they could not pass into that other realm which hid the peak of the mountain, thus preserving whatever it was that attracted such obvious hate.","\"This place becomes like this whenever the laws of Vaelûn are in control,\" said Pelagor as he looked up at the mountain. \"It’s as if the universe itself wants to destroy that one item we’re going towards.\"","Lex looked at the mountain, and then down at the whale.","\" This is the item you want me to use to find whatever it is you’re looking for?\" Lex questioned, a hint of accusation in his tone.","Pelagor hummed.","\"It is not an issue. I have passed this mountain and into that realm myself, and can assure you that there are no consequences for it. I myself would have attempted to absorb that specific Dao material, but the intensity of subsequent Primordial aura would kill me. That’s if I survive the retribution land around it.\"","Lex raised an eyebrow, and that was question enough. He did not need to say the words.","\"Yes, the Hollow has surrounded the material with a land of retribution. It seems to be a form of protection, keeping the laws of the realm from destroying it. Those two are my biggest obstacles, preventing me from getting my hands on the material myself. If you can succeed, then more than half the task is already done.\"","The immense danger did not intimidate Lex, but it made it clear to him that obviously this item was far from normal. When he heard about its ability to transform Dao radiation, he already found it hard to believe, but now it was somehow believable. It made sense that an item with such a broken ability would be targeted by the universe itself.","\"Alright, let’s go up,\" said Lex without asking anymore questions. His guard was up, and he would deal with any situation himself. Of course, he was also expecting Pelagor to inform him about the dangers since he should be familiar with them.","Pelagor moved swiftly across the terrain that was already familiar to him, dodging past obstacles and avoiding pitfalls that could not even be detected before they were triggered, revealing just how much time the whale had spent here.","Lex also stopped absorbing resources because everything here was so thoroughly steeped in negative karma that even he didn’t want to touch it.","\"Have you ever played that game ’the floor is lava’?\" Pelagor asked all of a sudden as they flew over the hills composed entirely of skulls.","\"Um, yeah, as a kid. Why?\" Lex responded, taken aback by the sudden random question.","Pelagor chuckled.","\"It’s because every time I do this, I feel like I’m playing that game again. Except, it’s not that the floor is lava. So is the air and everything else around you. Brace yourself.\"","Lex did not ask any questions and suddenly erected a barrier around himself. A few seconds later, they reached the base of the mountain, and Lex heard a sound that he had heard all too often.","He heard the sound of thunder, except this was not normal thunder. It was the thunder that accompanied tribulations!","A blue bolt of lightning fell out of the cloudless sky, yet it did not touch them for Pelagor swerve out of the way, dodging it easily. Yet the lightning was only the beginning, as a hand made of pure rock reached out of the ground to grab at them. Birds formed from clumps of negative karma started stalking them like prey, and the light that filled the region began to retreat until it took the shape of a phoenix, leaving them surrounded by darkness.","\"What the hell is happening?\" Lex asked, stunned. It wasn’t that he was surprised by the sudden attack. No, it was the fact that the laws of the universe almost seemed alive, and they quivered with anger.","\"I asked the same question the first time I came here,\" Pelagor answered as he calmly dodged all attacks, letting not a single thing touch him. Though he was a whale, and of considerable size, he flew through the sky with a grace that far surpassed even the bird circling them!","\"The answer I received after countless years of searching surprised me. This land is a vestige of a battle between Vaelûn and Pentagal, where neither retain full control and both lash out aggressively at each other and anyone else they meet.","\"It is merely two universes trying to exert their control over us cultivators. I do not pay too much attention to it. We are cultivators - it is in our very nature to defy the natural order. The more they wish to keep me out, the more I will invade.\"","With those words, Pelagor spread out his fins and began to spin in the air, dodging lightning and karmic birds as they threw themselves at him. Let alone attacked, they could not even come close to the whale as it dominated the sky without a single ounce of fear in its actions.","What’s more, he didn’t even use many laws. Lex could see that everything Pelagor did was through the application of the law of gravity, controlled with such familiarity that it was akin to art.","Though the whale had proved to be a silent companion so far, now that it was time to take action he was not shy at all. Through him, Lex could see that the whale truly lived the words he had spoken: he had lived in defiance. He had defied the limits of his race, defied common convention, and now he was defying the remnant will of two universes on an ancient battlefield.","The ground shook, and from within the river of lava a number of flaming lizards began to rise. They howled in the air, as if announcing their fury, before they began swarming towards them. On another side, the mountain broke off into rock elementals who charged towards them. The lightning bolts, unable to even touch them, began to take the shape of the Farham as they readied themselves to chase after the two.","Lex raised his eyebrow, and made a mental note to memorise all this. When he went back to the Midnight Inn, he would make an obstacle course like this for immortals. It seemed like a lot of fun.","He started to feel a certain itch in his hands, wanting to participate as well. Unfortunately, he had no opportunity at all for Pelagor left him no chance. Maybe it was because he had come here all too often, but no matter what came their way, they were never able to touch the two of them.","Lex had somewhat an idea of what the whale was doing. He was showing Lex what he was really capable of doing. He may not be social, and he may not be a talker, but on the battlefield, he was an absolute asset.","Lex did not have a dedicated mount, but he had occasionally ridden various mounts into a fight. From Fenrir, to Little Blue, to Sol birds and the like, they had all served as his mounts. Most of the time, the presence or absence of a mount made no significant difference to him.","Lex had always been a one man army, and in the truly serious and difficult fights, a mount would only be a hindrance for it wouldn’t be able to keep up with him.","Pelagor, though, was showing some potential.","Lex smirked as he caught the underlying meaning behind this performance. Pelagor was showing Lex what he was worth, and soon it would be Lex’s turn to do the same.","He had said that the retribution zone came after crossing into the alternate realm, which meant that Pelagor didn’t consider this area to be an actual threat. Now Lex was looking forward to what came next.","\"Brace yourself. When we cross into the next realm, the Primordial aura will be thick, so protect yourself,\" Pelagor warned right before they reached the top, where the opening to the other realm swallowed the peak of the mountain.","\"Don’t worry,\" responded Lex calmly. \"I’m ready.\""]},{"number":2363,"title":"Chapter 2363: Shell of the Primordial Farham","paragraphs":["For some odd reason, Lex had assumed that when he traveled through the opening to the other realm, which existed in the form of a horizontal massive tear which swallowed up the top of the mountain, he would appear from the ground from where he would be able to see the rest of the mountain tip rising. That was not the case.","They flew into the opening, and what awaited them was a desolate wasteland without the slightest hint of life even though the realm itself was abundant with energy. When they appeared inside the realm, they were standing atop an ancient formation - one which operated using concepts Lex was entirely unfamiliar with.","To be clear, the formation wasn’t actually active - that was merely where they randomly appeared once they entered the realm. Signs of age had made themselves apparent on every structure around them, whether it was the floor or the walls or the very fabric of space itself.","The energy within the realm was normal spiritual energy, but a dense, overbearing Primordial aura invaded every corner of the realm, one that felt ancient and authentic. Lex instantly knew that compared to the Primordial energy and aura he had felt inside the Primordial Garden, this aura was a step above in quality, as if it was authentic while that was a mere pale imitation.","Lex was, naturally, unaffected by the Primordial aura at this point, for he himself exuded the same aura - though he kept it suppressed so that it wouldn’t be evident. Pelagor, clearly prepared in advance, also seemed unaffected.","The whale seemed to be looking around, as if to inspect if there had been any chances since he came here last, though Lex could feel that in truth it was observing Lex for any signs of strain. If he couldn’t even handle this, getting the resource would be impossible. Fortunately for him, Lex was at complete ease.","Lex stepped out of the room they arrived in, and discovered that most of the materials within the realm had turned into some kind of grey colored stone, regardless of what it may originally have been. That made for a very bizarre sight, where countless dead, wilted plants were frozen in place, as if they were statues.","Then again, actual, intact structures, whether it was in the form of plants or buildings or anything else, were scarce since most things in the realm seemed to have been destroyed in some great battle.","\"The mountain peak, for whatever reason, has changed shape within this realm. You will no longer find the peak here as you would expect. Instead, it has changed shape into an altar at the very center of this realm. Atop the altar lies the item we are here for. As promised, I have compiled all that I know about that resource within this crystal for you to read, and will not utter a single word about it.\"","Lex grabbed the crystal and read through it. Lex had a few guesses about what the item may be, but he had been completely wrong!","The item in question was called the Shell of the Primordial Farham! Lex knew that name well, for he had faced the Farham time and time again in his tribulations! He had, naturally, done his research about them and had learned that the Farham race was actually an extinct race from the Primordial Age. Nothing else was known about it, save that they only appeared now in the form of tribulations.","For a race to go extinct in the universe was actually quite difficult, considering that whenever the circumstances for the birth of a race appeared, the universe would naturally let them appear again. The fact that they were extinct either meant that their natural habitat was gone forever, or there was some other mystery about them.","Considering that even Primordial energy could be replicated within the Primordial Garden, it was strange that these beasts could not be born again, thus making it unlikely that they went extinct due to the loss of their habitat.","That, however, wasn’t the only mystery that surrounded these ancient, extinct beasts. For example, even if the Farham were a Primordial race, that did not mean that their existence had anything to do with the Dao. So why, then, was its egg a Dao level material? Could it be that the Farham were born at the Dao Lord level?","That was absurd. If such a powerful race existed, it was basically impossible for them to go extinct. They could be hunted, they could become the enemies of the universe, but for them to go extinct was much too difficult to imagine!","What’s more, the effect of the shell was to convert Dao radiation into Primordial aura? This was merely a piece of broken shell from an egg that hatched long ago, and it could convert Dao radiation into Primordial aura? That seemed too broken an ability for Lex to even imagine what the actual Farham were like.","Whatever their mysteries were, Lex wasn’t about to solve them any time soon. He had to concern himself with getting his hands on the shell.","According to the research compiled by Pelagor, he believed that if the shell left this realm, it would be destroyed by the laws of the Vaelûn universe. Thus, Lex had to absorb or refine it now so that its ability could be used later on, even if only once.","Attached to the data were a number of theories and suggestions for how such a thing may be achieved. They were merely suggestions Pelagor compiled while studying the shell in the hopes of being able to use it one day himself. Unfortunately, that day would never come.","Pelagor could not ignore the pressure of the Primordial aura close to the shell, not to mention getting close to the shell itself involved overcoming great difficulty. Although Pelagor had tried before, as mentioned in the data, he was always too wounded to attempt refining the shell himself."]},{"number":2364,"title":"Chapter 2364: No rush","paragraphs":["Pelagor led Lex towards the center of the realm, though this time they did not rush at all. The land surrounding the Shell had been turned into a retribution, and crossing it was far from simple. He dared not be careless.","Lex, too, took this obstacle quite seriously because Pelagor and explained to him in detail what to expect. Unlike the previous retribution he faced, which only became more difficult because he taunted it, this one actively became stronger based on his actions.","His durability, his speed, his strategy all contributed to making the retribution stronger in a targeted manner for its sole goal was to eliminate him. Moreover, this retribution was perpetual, and wouldn’t go away with time. The only way to resolve it was to pass through it as quickly as possible, except that doing so was detrimental to Lex in this scenario.","Since Lex would need to pass it to reach the shell, and then he would have to pass it again to exit, if he used his fastest speed from the beginning, the land would adapt to counter that speed.","Thus, he would need to begin by only being slightly faster than the retribution land itself, and continuously increase the ability he demonstrated so that it would not improve too much. Abilities such as teleportation, whether through space or other laws, were especially lethal, because the retribution lands were especially sensitive to them, and would react in completely insidious ways to sabotage the attempt.","If he succeeded it was all well and good, but if he failed his situation would instantly turn dire. According to one rumor within the stronghold, there was a person once who tried to teleport out of a retribution land. Instead of stopping him, the retribution land changed his coordinates and sent him deep within the lands filled with Dao level resources. The only reason that person survived was because, incidentally, he landed in front of the Fortune Lord.","There was no way of knowing whether this rumor was true or false, but most treated it as true and Lex did not wish to test it out using his own life.","\"This is the edge,\" said Pelagor as he stopped suddenly, though Lex could see no defining differences between the normal realm and the retribution land. \"The shell is in the altar in the middle, and the altar itself is a sort of safe zone, but until then you’ll have to be careful.\"","Lex nodded, and then stood up. It was time for him to prove himself.","He stepped forward without hesitation, and instantly he felt the difference, even though everything looked the same as before. Everything, from the ground underneath his feet to the air and the energy around him, suddenly became hostile towards Lex. Yet, much to his surprise, no attack came. The danger land did not react to his presence at all, and the very lack of any action troubled Lex.","He moved forward, warily, and yet nothing happened. Even Pelagor was confused, though he did not say anything lest he distract Lex.","With every slow, steady step forward, Lex felt that the hostility towards him was increasing, yet nothing happened even so. Lex did not stop, nor did he increase his speed. He simply walked through the barren land, over the mounds of rubble, over the petrified lake, towards the altar in the middle.","At first the altar was not visible at all, but after a few hours it finally entered his line of sight as he climbed a hill. Ten pillars held up a dome shaped roof, with a marble pedestal in the center. Even from afar, Lex could see the black colored shell on the pedestal, and it was no bigger than a fingernail.","It was hard to believe that such a tiny thing had caused such a huge fuss, yet it was undeniable. The Primordial aura could not replace Primordial energy, yet the aura alone here felt just as thick as the Primordial Garden. If that was the case, Lex could not even imagine what its intensity would be up close. As for why the retribution land was not attacking him, Lex had no clue, and he had no intentions of lingering to find out.","Even up until the very end, nothing happened, though Lex had suspected all along that the land would strike at the very last moment. Since that did not happen, Lex could only assume that the trap would only be sprung on his return journey.","He didn’t mind the ease with which he reached his target, but he also didn’t like the fact that the retribution land seemed to display some form of strategy. Just to be sure, Lex checked and then double checked his memory as well as his spirit to make sure that he wasn’t under some kind of spell or illusion, but that did not seem to be the case.","He stopped thinking about it and approached the black colored shell instead. This thing... if he could manage to replicate its ability for himself, or in his necklace, then Lex’s survivability would skyrocket.","Dao aura, or radiation, was one of the most dangerous things in existence for him - mainly because if he directly faced a Dao Lord it would equate directly to death making the level of danger irrelevant.","If he followed the instructions on how to use this shell given to him by Pelagor, he would only be able to replicate its ability to a limited extent, and only once. That would be a supreme waste of such a treasure. Of course, if he tried something else and didn’t gain that remarkable ability, he would not only waste this trip but he would need to retrieve Pelagor’s desired resource without the protection of the shell’s ability.","Lex stepped through the pillars and towards the podium, deciding to study the shell up close first. There was no rush, he could take his time. If he could use divine energy to somehow inscribe this ability inside his necklace...","Lex crossed his legs and sat in the air right in front of the shell, focusing on it and trying to learn everything about it that he could."]},{"number":2365,"title":"Chapter 2365: Why is Lex still causing problems? I","paragraphs":["\"You know, when Lex went into the Gilded Hollow, I thought that my life would become much easier,\" said Nuwa in an exasperated tone. \"That’s half the reason I made sure he got the key to the Gilded Hollow from my temple. Who knew that, not only would he not stop causing issues, others would join him in making my life difficult.\"","Naturally, none responded to Nuwa. Though it appeared like she was talking to them, her attendants knew all too well not to disturb her when she was troubled like this.","Ever since that homicidal maniac Elizabeth had been unleashed from her prison, many had decided to behave themselves lest they attract undue attention, and Nuwa was simply one of them. It wasn’t that Nuwa was afraid of Elizabeth - far from it. It was just that dealing with her would be far too troublesome, and would make her vulnerable to other threats.","If anyone ever doubted that the Primals were the peacekeepers of the universe, they only needed to be informed of the great service the Primals were performing on behalf of the entire damn universe by keeping her locked up.","\"Have we confirmed what exactly happened?\" she asked her attendant. With the Humanoid Alliance the way it was, and with Wu Kong indisposed, she could only rely on some of her other subordinates, even if it was a hassle to deal with them. Their fervent and worshipping gaze was the very reason she normally preferred solitude.","Unfortunately, since she did not want to expose herself, she could only leave the reconnaissance and other basic tasks to these subordinates.","\"A massive disruption in universal karma was detected some time ago. Since the disruption was blatant and not hidden in the slightest, most forces in the universe have already discerned some basic information about it.","\"The source of the karmic fluctuation... seems to originate from the Primordial Garden, and its target seems to be connected to the Midnight Inn and happens to be inside the Gilded Hollow. That’s about as much concrete information as we were able to get, however there are a number of speculations spreading through various circles. We’ve compiled a list in case you want to see.\"","What was the point of reading speculations? By now, Nuwa already knew that as long as certain information pertained to that brat Lex, it would always be wrong. Still, she looked into any way, just to get a sense of what the universe was thinking.","At the moment, the Major realms were all disconnected for travel via the Void had become too dangerous. The only actual means of travel between realms were various forms of teleportation which were just too difficult and expensive to be used en masse.","As a result, many Dao Lords had become disconnected from their organisations and were resorting to whatever means were available to them to protect themselves. The war was still ongoing, just in tiny, disconnected clusters. After all, since everyone was cut off, they wanted to gain control of the nearest realms for their own protection!","Of course, another thing Dao Lords could do was look into the laws of the universe to stay updated on what was happening across the universe. Most things could not be kept secret from Dao Lords.","Thus, even disconnected as they were, they formed the most comprehensive gossip network in the universe! One of the trending topics was a rumor that the Innkeeper was absent from his realm. This was a big deal, especially since it was previously theorised that he was trying to create a Seat of Power.","Why exactly would he leave, and slow or even stop his progress altogether? No one could know, but some even began to speculate that there was no Seat of Power at all, and that everything had been speculation from the get go.","As if that was not enough, many began to notice that the previously stable relationship between the Midnight Inn and the Humanoid Alliance had suddenly started to deteriorate!","Even the Humanoid Alliance hadn’t expected that. Sure, they expected some kind of fallout from the ’incident’ caused by one of their factions, but they hadn’t anticipated the sheer level of indifference the Inn showed them. None knew how to interpret that.","Just as various rumors about why all this was happening were beginning to gain traction, it happened. The massive karmic fluctuation. No one knew why it happened. They only knew it came from the Primordial Garden, it targeted the Gilded Hollow, and that it was connected to the Midnight Inn.","Could it be that the Innkeeper was inside the Gilded Hollow? That was an audacious move indeed! Moreover, who had caused the massive karmic fluctuation? The easy answer was Eclipse, but that shouldn’t have been possible. Her powers were supposed to be sealed.","If she used her powers like that, then shouldn’t it have triggered the advent of the universe’s evolution? Or were there other, unknown requirements for that?","The more probable answer was that it wasn’t Eclipse, but someone who worked for her. Her mysterious, unknown body guard, for example. None knew the truth, but suddenly they were highly intrigued by the Innkeeper.","If he was in the Gilded Hollow, it would explain why he had not reacted to the Humanoid Alliance’s actions yet. Unfortunately, there was no remedy or salve for regret. Many began to wait eagerly for the time when he would return to see how he would react.","Nuwa snorted. As if. Everyone took the Innkeeper in such high esteem. If only they knew that the Innkeeper was just a little boy wearing a suit.","\"Why exactly can Eclipse contact Lex inside the Gilded Hollow?\" Nuwa asked, though no one had an answer. \"Is it because she’s connected to Vaelûn? That doesn’t make sense.\"","Before she could ponder on the topic much longer, something else happened that attracted her attention.","The Julias Major realm was one of the hubs of the Path of Chaos - the ones suspected to be behind this war, and the ones responsible for the destruction of those four Major realms. It was where the Hall of Powa was located.","Elizabeth showed up outside the realm and, using one of the Primal race’s most powerful weapons, corrupted the laws of the realm itself, causing it to fall into a sequence of self destruction. But unlike the previous Major realms which had been destroyed, the Julias realm would not explode.","Instead, the corruption of the laws would cause the entire realm to be refined into Dao materials for the Primal race to harvest. As for those living inside the realm? Their souls, too, would be corrupted and refined into Dao materials.","It happened without any forewarning. No one even detected her actions until it was too late. The legendary, the fearsome, the powerful Path of Chaos... had become the first to suffer Elizabeth’s wrath."]},{"number":2366,"title":"Chapter 2366: Why is Lex still causing problems? II","paragraphs":["Unlike the destruction of the previous four Major realms, everyone knew who was responsible this time around. Moreover, it wasn’t a sudden, irresistible destruction. Instead, there was a barricade around the realm to prevent anyone from leaving, effectively trapping them inside and forcing them to face their deaths.","By the time the news had spread, all mortals across the Julias Major realm were already dead, their souls harvested and refined. But... no one complained. Or rather, no one dared to complain.","What Elizabeth had used was one of the Primal race’s most fearsome weapons, but it was hardly the only one. Not to mention, which race had the power to face them off? Even if such races existed, they would not face off the Primal race for the Julias realm.","The destruction of a Major realm. It could not be understated just how despicable and diabolical such a thing was, not to mention difficult. Theoretically speaking, killing a Dao Lord was far simpler and easier than doing that. For example, Wu Kong might be able to kill certain Dao Lords easily, but he certainly couldn’t destroy a Major realm on his own.","Major realms were fought over for hundreds of thousands of years because of their endless resources and ability to sustain so much life. The rise and fall of Major realms literally affected the whole universe!","The fewer the Major realms, the more those lower down on the Cosmic Ascendance Spectrum would suffer. After all, the Sage and Elder races were more than strong enough to maintain or even conquer new realms if they needed to. Only those lower down were losing territory and resources.","Although it was not complete just yet, five Major realms had fallen in a short time. Devastation of such levels had not been wrought since the end of the Primordial Age.","A profound sorrow spread across the universe, and this time it wasn’t because of the fall of a Major realm. After all, that wasn’t technically complete. The sorrow was the natural emotions shared by countless living beings upon such incalculable loss. It was not just the loss of 5 Major realms that caused such emotions, but the faint inkling that this was only just the beginning.","Many began to suspect that the destruction of these Major realms was not a blind act, but the strategic pruning of the universe. Unfortunately, most of them were on the end being pruned, making them feel helpless.","Nuwa sighed. She understood better than most what was in store for the future.","\"Call the Celestials. Tell them...\" Nuwa paused, and looked up at the sky. Her actual location was a mystery, but regardless of whether there was a sky above her or not, what mattered was the direction she was looking towards. She was looking above... because that’s where tribulation clouds appeared.","It wasn’t that there were tribulation clouds appearing above her specifically. Instead, there were tribulation clouds appearing across all realms in the universe, vibrating with a powerful, vengeful energy.","Within the thick, black clouds, blue lightning flashed, and then turned into Farham. One, one hundred, one hundred million... all across the universe, Farham appeared in the shape of lightning tribulations, not as Tribulation Fiends.","They roared in unison, though their roar sounded like triumph, while the flap of thunder that followed was filled with such wrath that even Elizabeth was taken by surprise. Yet, for all its anger and frustration, the universe had no target upon whom to vent.","The Farham roared in unison, forming a chant almost, before their bodies disappeared with the dissolving tribulation. Yet this was not the end of the phenomenon - far from it. The clouds fused together to form what appeared like a pedestal, upon which lay what looked like scrap paper. In front of the pedestal appeared the figure of a human.","The human’s expressions and identity could not be determined, but it was clear that the universe was furious with the human! It was warning him! Unfortunately, all could hear the warning except the very person being warned!","Nuwa’s expression fell. There was no indication or sign of the human’s identity, but she did not need any hints to know who was behind this. After all, a mother’s instinct was never wrong.","\"Why the hell is Lex still causing problems?\" she asked herself as she looked at the figure in the clouds.","The human, after sitting in a meditative pose for so long, finally reacted. Many were curious to see what his intentions were. Even more tried to divine what was actually happening and what its significance was, for even the destruction of realms had not caused such a massive phenomenon.","None, however, were ready for what they were about to see. The human looked at the piece of scrap and... picked it up and tossed it in his mouth.","He ate it! The forbidden... fruit? Chip? Wafer? Whatever it was, it was clearly forbidden, and yet he ate it so casually!","Even though the Farham were gone, one last roar of unrestrained joy rang out across the universe. Unfortunately, it was drowned by the clap of thunder as the universe expressed its anger... and then gave up. It could not target the culprit, and so his vision faded, leaving everyone to wonder what would happen to him.","\"That boy needs a wife to settle him down,\" Nuwa said in an exhausted tone. She suddenly felt like just revealing her location and fighting it out with her enemies would be less stressful than dealing with Lex.","\"Take my advice, don’t have kids,\" said Nuwa to one of her subordinates who froze up.","\"Um, my lady Nuwa, I gave birth last month...\" the subordinate said, unsure of what she was supposed to do.","\"Oh, really? Congratulations. It’s a wonderful experience. I’m sure you’ll love it,\" Nuwa responded, sounding genuinely sincere. Yet the more sincere she sounded, the more it felt like sarcasm.","Lex, entirely unaware that his actions had been witnessed by the entire universe, closed his eyes and resisted the urge to burp. He needed to refine the item, not let a single speck of its potential to go to waste."]},{"number":2367,"title":"Chapter 2367: Infected","paragraphs":["In truth, while it appeared like Lex had munched on a Primordial pringle*, he was a mere illusion. What he had done in reality was fuse the egg shell into the necklace itself. After sitting and studying the shell for a long time, Lex realized that it was, in essence, impossible to absorb the ability of the shell permanently. At the same time, he felt like he understood why the universe disliked it.","Everything that existed within the universe did so in accordance with the laws of the universe. From their makeup, to the way they behaved, to how they interacted with other laws, all of them adhered to preexisting laws of the universe. Yes, those laws could occasionally be broken, but even that was something the universe itself accounted for.","It was like a thrown exception inside a code, or the ’page not found’ page on a website. Although what a user saw was the exception, or a page saying ’page not found’, in truth that was the designed behavior to accommodate for any errors or issues. Similarly, the universe had its own ways of dealing with broken or malfunctioning laws.","This egg shell, however, did not adhere to the laws of the universe, whether it was Pentagal or his own. Instead, the shell itself had its own set of laws which it imposed upon the universe. Those laws were not just embedded within the shell, the shell itself was composed of those laws.","Many cultivators, much like Pelagor, made grand claims about going against Heaven or the will of the universe. While it was true that by cultivating, they were going against the natural design of the universe, they still did so within the actual framework of how the universe worked.","The egg shell of the Primordial Farham, however, truly and genuinely did something unique by imposing its own laws upon the universe itself! That was a level of control that exceeded even dragons and Sovereigns, both of whom could influence the universe according to their will.","In essence, it was basically impossible for Lex to replicate this feat at his level. He did not even know how to ’create’ a law of his own to begin with. Heck, just designing the laws for his fake realm was already an incredibly difficult task for him.","The reason, then, that it was a Dao level material was because it could overwrite the logic of whichever universe it was in. While Lex could not do this right now, he did his best to memorise what the laws looked like and how they operated for when he was stronger. Maybe he’d be able to replicate it in the future.","The thing he focused most on, however, wasn’t being able to replicate the shell’s ability to exert its own laws onto the universe. Instead, he wanted to find a way to copy the effect of those laws using whatever laws already existed in this universe.","This was a topic that was currently far beyond him. Ironically, the one person Lex was sure could do this was the one person he had no interest in seeing again any time soon: Regix.","Much in the way that Regix could manipulate laws to create effects similar to the Dao, turning Dao radiation into Primordial aura was likely something he could do once he saw how the egg shell did it.","Fusing the shell into the necklace could allow him to, temporarily, control that ability. Once the shell was fused, Lex could sense that he only had a few years before the effect of the shell vanished altogether.","Before that happened, he would need to use up its ability. But using it would also diminish the shell’s ability. No matter what happened, this was an ability that was not destined to last much longer in the universe.","Beyond that, fusing with the shell also gave Lex greater control over the laws within the fake realm inside the necklace.","With everything done, Lex opened his eyes and got back up. He’d been sitting in place for one whole year, and it hardly felt like it at all. Lex realized that, slowly but surely, being an immortal was beginning to mess with his perception of time. Why else would he feel like a year was a very short period of time?","Now wasn’t the time for such things. He turned around and looked past the pillars. The land still looked completely normal, yet he could feel the hostility from it even now.","\"Alright, show me what you have in store for me,\" murmured Lex as he took a single step forward.","As soon as he entered the land of retribution, he felt it. It wasn’t an attack waiting for him, or a hidden bomb, or anything of the sort. Instead, it was a type of virus, as best as he could tell. The moment he re-entered the retribution zone, the laws around him began to churn, infecting him with the aura of Pentagal.","Unless he found some way to immediately stop and reverse the process, he would soon become a recognized lifeform of Pentagal instead of Vaelûn. What the consequences for that would be, he did not know, but he guessed it wouldn’t be good.","\"This is totally unfair. Why the hell did you suddenly become creative when it’s my turn?\" Lex asked, startled and annoyed by what was happening. He was prepared for many things, but this was not one of them. He had never even imagined something like this could happen.","Lex stood there for a couple of seconds, cycling through his list of abilities and skills to see if there was anything he could do about this. The issue, however, was that he didn’t even know what was causing the problem.","He looked down, through the illusion of a body he had conjured, and directly at the body of the necklace. A moment later, it became clear.","He had absorbed too many resources from the Gilded Hollow into the necklace, and he hadn’t fully refined them all yet because his goal was to absorb as many of them as possible before leaving the Hollow. Fully refining them could come later. Unfortunately, his greed had come back to bite him when he least expected it.","\"Who knew greed was a bad thing?\" Lex asked himself before he began to address the situation. \"That’s like my greatest virtue.\"","The problem wasn’t his aura, it was the virus infecting him. Lex could wash his aura using Domination, and cleanse and impurities. It was the fundamental change that had to be fixed, and refining all the resources wouldn’t even stop the change - it would only keep it from getting worse.","*Yes, I stole the line Primordial pringle from one of the comments in the previous Chapter."]},{"number":2368,"title":"Chapter 2368: Should we save him?","paragraphs":["\"What do you mean there was a phenomenon in the sky again?\" Jack asked with a furrowed brow. He had just left his cabin because he’d sent all the divine items he’d gathered so far to Lex, and he needed some more of his own to push him into the Heaven Immortal realm equivalent of the Paladin path.","Yet as soon as he came out, the first thing he heard was about a phenomenon. Honestly, he had sensed some unusual things happening outside, but given the fact that the Hexus event was on the horizon, and the fact that he himself was on the verge of growing to the next level, he wouldn’t leave his cabin unless something impacted him directly.","\"Yeah, it was quite a formidable sight, to be honest,\" answered Longbeard as he combed his beard using a comb made of crystal from the alligator. It was one of the very few things that could actually unfurl the tangles in his otherwise chaotic beard.","\"There were a bunch of lightning beasts roaring in the sky, and there was a human eating some kind of super powered crisp, as far as I could tell. Apparently the vision was visible everywhere. I’m not quite sure what it’s about, but a lot of weird things have been happening in the universe lately. Who can say what’s going on?\"","Jack looked at Longbeard, and then up at the sky. It seemed... the universe really disliked the shell, and wasn’t happy with him either. It was strange because he hadn’t felt any change in his positive or negative karma.","\"Forget that. Have we found any leads on any Deities still preaching nearby?\" Jack asked, ignoring the previous statement entirely, as if it had nothing to do with him.","Longbeard shook his head.","\"New Deities haven’t been able to enter the realm ever since Tribulation Fiends started to appear, and the old ones are actively tracking us through some strange method, and are avoiding us.","\"Apparently, you have become the nemesis within the Folklore realm for over 100 Deities, and that’s made its way into their faiths. Since then, they’re not even trying to fight anymore - they’re just straight up avoiding us.\"","Jack rubbed his temples as he thought of ways to deal with this issue. Nothing was going according to plan these days.","Almost as if he had been waiting for Jack to have that exact thought, Longbeard continued to speak.","\"By the way, now that you’re finally out, are we planning on rescuing Pebbles, or will we just leave him where he is?\"","Jack froze.","\"What?\" he asked, unsure if he heard correctly, or if the world just stopped making sense. What had happened to Pebbles?","\"What ’what’?\" Longbeard asked, confused about what was confusing Jack.","Jack resisted the urge to strangle someone.","\"What do you mean ’will we rescue Pebbles’? What happened to Pebbles, and why didn’t anyone tell me about it?\" Jack asked angrily.","\"Oh yeah. Someone discovered that Pebbles cheeks are an incredibly safe and stable storage container, making him the perfect transport for extremely unstable materials. As a joke, Pebbles uploaded a rental deed for his cheeks up on eBuy, and he was making a lot of money until someone just... didn’t return him.","\"We thought about telling you, but we tried contacting the eBuy customer service center first. They’re usually quite good with these things, but I guess the Fiend Tribulations have affected their business operations so they haven’t been able to get him back yet.\"","Jack stared at Longbeard in sheer disbelief at what he was hearing. For a moment, he was genuinely tempted to leave Pebbles be. After all, the little hamster was always trying to mutiny. But the adorable little fuzzball was also an indestructible shield, so it would be a waste to just let him go like that.","\"Unfurl the sails. We’re going to get that hamster back,\" Jack said in an exhausted tone, though no one really complained.","Elsewhere inside the Folklore realm, Pebbles looked around nervously as he felt the forbidden artifact hidden inside his cheek trying to corrode his body. If he weren’t indestructible, the artifact would have already burned a hole in his cheek.","\"What did I tell you, my lord? The vermin is the perfect carrier for your artifact,\" said a member of the Tyrannis race as he kneeled before a figure with his head lowered.","The figure being bowed to - a member of the Penance race - looked indifferently at the kneeling subject, though he could not help being intrigued by Pebbles himself.","\"If he survives the journey, bring him back. We can use him again. Oh, and find a way to lose the trail of those eBuy investigators. It’s best not to attract too much attention within the Folklore realm.\"","Meanwhile, within the Gilded Hollow, Lex was running towards the edge of the retribution zone as if his butt was on fire, all the while grumbling to himself.","\"Why can’t you just try to kill me the old fashioned way? Did you really need to innovate when it was my turn?\" he asked, as if talking to the Hollow itself.","While it appeared like he was completely fine, in truth Lex was seriously hurt, and his injuries continued to worsen. After trying a number of ways to prevent himself from being affected by the other realm, including just throwing an immense amount of divine energy at it and hoping a miracle would happen, he discovered that he could not reverse it at all.","Lex was many things, but he was definitely not on the same level as a universe, even if it was a dead one. If a way to stop or reverse the virus existed, it was beyond his ability to do. That left him only one, extremely desperate solution. He literally eviscerated the parts of the necklace, and himself, that were affected.","He also burnt off some parts that weren’t infected yet, but were touching the infected parts just to be safe. As a result, Lex’s soul suffered extremely painful damage.","Unfortunately, while he was still inside the retribution land, the infection kept coming back, which is why he started to run as fast as he could. What was even more unfortunate was that the danger of the zone adapted to the immense speed he showed, and the rate of the spread of the virus increased as well.","If he died, then this would be the most pathetic death he could imagine. What happened to being attacked by a volcano? Why did his enemies need to be more imaginative and creative these days?","Before he could find an answer to that question, Lex finally saw the edge of the tribulation zone."]},{"number":2369,"title":"Chapter 2369: Anywhere but here","paragraphs":["As Lex approached the edge of the retribution zone, he’d already burnt off about 40% of his own soul attached to the necklace. This was an injury that could not be casually recovered from, but that was something to look at later.","For now, Lex focused 100% of his attention on his escape. As he closed in on the exit to the zone, he did not lower his guard. In fact, owing to the unusual nature in which the retribution land was behaving, he wouldn’t be surprised if there was some kind of trap waiting for him at the end.","Beyond the edge, he could see Pelagor waiting silently, ready to help as soon as Lex exited. The reason he didn’t enter as well was because with two people inside, the land would become even more dangerous. Just because there was very little distance left to cover did not mean it could be underestimated.","In Lex’s mind, he imagined a Go board where he was black, and the Gilded Hollow was white. Instead of winning by trapping him, the hollow was literally converting his pieces into its own - a clear violation of the rules, but that was besides the point.","In the split second it took him to reach the edge, Lex visualized countless different strategies, and tried to anticipate what could go wrong. The key seemed to be the retribution land’s inaction the first time he went. He theorized that it wasn’t that the land hadn’t acted the first time, but that it was somehow preparing for his return journey, infecting him silently without alerting him.","Since it broke the rules once, who said it couldn’t do so again? Lex laid out a few various plans, and ran a risk-benefit analysis and reached the conclusion that if the damage to his soul approached 50%, then he’d just risk teleporting out.","Lex thought of countless scenarios, so when he successfully crossed the end of the zone without facing any kind of obstruction at all, he did not feel relieved. Instead, he felt even more concerned.","Without hesitation, Lex put his hand on Pelagor and tried to teleport the both of them away, only to discover that he couldn’t. The virus had not stopped affecting him, and besides infecting him with the aura of Pentagal, it was restricting him to this separated realm as well! It was anchoring him to this place so that he’d never be able to leave!","\"What-\" Pelagor began to ask, realizing that Lex looked much more alarmed than he had anticipated, but he didn’t have the time. Lex pulled him along as he ran like mad towards the exit.","Using his spirit sense, Lex quickly explained what had happened to Pelagor and asked him if he had ever heard of something like this happening before, and if he knew a solution!","Pelagor trembled upon hearing Lex’s words, and immediately pulled out an artifact in the shape of a gold coin!","\"This is no ordinary retribution! I’ve heard of it before! This is exactly how the other Lords within the Hollow died! Only the Fortune Lord knows how to counter this ability!\"","As he spoke, he activated the golden coin which seemed to wrap both Lex and Pelagor in a golden halo, isolating them from the reach of the Hollow. Lex immediately felt the virus stop its spread, but he doubted that this was over. Since Pelagor claimed that this was how other Dao Lords had died before, he did not think this was something he could overcome on his own.","\"The Coin of Fortune will last us a few days at most. We need to return to the stronghold at once, there’s no other way. Fortunately, I always come prepared for such emergencies. You hold on, I’ll get us back.\"","Lex nodded gratefully at Pelagor, and turned his mind to the imlpications of himself as an Immortal receiving the same retribution as a Dao Lord. Had he crossed some kind of threshold?","All he’d done was try to steal a few Dao materials here or there - was there really a need to escalate things like that?","Returning to the stronghold was not nearly as big an issue as going and finding these rare resources. Heck, Lex himself recorded the spatial location of the waygate he used to come here in case he needed to teleport back to it.","Pelagor knew this, but the fact that he insisted on taking them back himself likely meant that there were other problems involved that Lex hadn’t anticipated yet. In all fairness, due to the shortage of time, Lex had been in too much of a rush to accumulate as many resources as possible.","This time, when he returned, Lex resolved to spend a year or so in the stronghold just researching all the possible issues he might run into. Without Pelagor’s assistance this time, he would have been in real big trouble.","As soon as they exited the realm, Pelagor equipped some kind of finguard on his fins, allowing him to fly at breakneck speeds, relying once again on laws Lex had never even seen before.","They didn’t teleport, they simply flew the entire distance from the mountain back to the waygate in just a few hours. Lex was planning on approaching the Fortune Lord once more and requesting his aid, although he was extremely concerned about whether his request would be accepted or not.","Little did he know, that wasn’t needed at all. The moment he returned to the Fortune stronghold, Romulus sensed what was wrong with Lex and felt like he was getting a headache.","With a ridiculously insane background like the one Lex had, Romulus did not want to risk his plan by provoking whoever was supporting Lex. He could die anywhere else, but he absolutely could not die within the Fortune stronghold.","Thus, the moment they returned, before either Lex or Pelagor could even think of heading towards Fortune castle, they were teleported directly to the Fortune Lord’s private chamber.","\"I see you’re really making yourself at home,\" Romulus said with a casual smile on his face as he placed a hand on Lex’s shoulder. Without the need to even be told, he began cleaning Lex’s soul, and the entire necklace as well.","\"I think it’s best if you stay here for a while though. The Hollow is acting unexpectedly. We wouldn’t want you to get hurt even more now, would we?\""]},{"number":2370,"title":"Chapter 2370: The beginning of the end times I","paragraphs":["Lex and Pelagor were both stunned by what had happened. The Fortune Lord had always maintained a very friendly and approachable demeanor towards the residents of his Fortune stronghold, but even then it was not to the level of just bringing them into the stronghold and solving all their problems.","Pelagor could only attribute this reaction to the rumor he had already heard which stated that Lex was someone who had the Fortune Lord’s backing. He did not understand why Lex had received such backing, but it was also not something he would pry into.","He very much liked to live a good life in the future, and asking questions he shouldn’t be asking was one of the quickest ways of making sure such a thing wouldn’t happen.","Lex, on the other hand, did not try to understand or justify it at all. Trying to understand the reasons why a Dao Lord, any Dao Lord at all, did things was not something immortals should consider - especially when stated Dao Lord was right in front of him.","It was a basic fact that Lex was completely vulnerable in front of him, so there was nothing he could do to guard himself anyway, in which case he might as well let go of all his concerns and relax.","\"Thank you for your help, Lord,\" said Lex in his sincerest and humblest tone.","The Fortune Lord smiled casually and looked from Lex towards Pelagor.","\"It’s nothing too serious. Since there’s no precedent for an Immortal harvesting so many Dao materials, we had no way of knowing how the Hollow would react. Your actions have actually taught me something new about this place, so just treat this as compensation. However, it’s best that you stay here for now since we don’t know how else the Hollow might act.","\"While there are no leads on the Double Yin Death Metal Rose you were looking for, the search will continue and if there is one I’ll let you know. I know that you and Pelagor have an agreement as well, but worry not, I’ll allow you an opportunity to fulfil your deal before I depart on my own task in a few years.\"","Lex nodded, not questioning or arguing whatsoever. He was critically injured as it was, and it would take him some time to recover anyway. For the sake of his own safety, it was best if he stopped stealing resources from the Hollow, and started using them to refine his necklace and build better functions into it anyway.","Even after discarding so much of the necklace due to the contamination, he still had an abundance of resources that he’d taken, and there was much he could do with that.","Seeing that there were no complaints or issues on Lex’s part, Romulus breathed an internal sigh and began his official treatment.","\"This is going to take a while, so go to sleep. You’ll wake up once the corruption is resolved,\" Romulus said, putting Lex to sleep.","He sent Pelagor away, telling the whale that he’d be summoned once Lex was ready to complete his part of the bargain, leaving Lex with the Fortune Lord. Finally alone, Romulus frowned and looked at Lex’s condition. The fact that he had, on his own, burned away the bits of his soul that were infected had actually saved Romulus a lot of trouble because he would have needed to do the same anyway, but did not want to offend whoever backed Lex.","Across the universe, in the Folklore realm, Jack felt his connection to Lex fade away, but only because he was asleep... hopefully.","He sighed, and looked towards finding Pebbles. It wasn’t nearly as difficult as anyone would have expected, because one of the features of the Jolly Rancher was that it recorded the aura of all crewmembers and could automatically navigate its way to them if needed. Thus, the crew just relaxed on board while the ship itself took them to the hamster which had rented out its cheeks to strangers online.","\"I swear, kids these days will do anything to make a little extra money on the side,\" Longbeard said with an air of righteousness as he shook his head. \"Back in my day, we made money the good old fashioned way - we stole it. But now look at things. Renting out his cheeks to strangers. Society as a whole is in decline.\"","The bear cub, Monk, nodded in agreement.","\"Amitabha, it is a sign of the end of times. We must repent and commit as many sins as possible before the universe ends to make the most of our time.\"","Jack resisted the urge to snort, and simply looked ahead without showing any expression.","The Jolly Rancher flew for a few months without stopping before it entered a portion of the Folklore realm that looked like everything was a ghost. The canyons, the mountains, the rivers and clouds were all green and partially see through, moving like reeds in the ocean.","Naturally it was not filled with ghosts, but residents of the Folklore realm who identified as ghosts. Learning about that made Longbeard and Monk even more sure that the end times were nigh.","A few more weeks in this place, and the ship began to hover over something, as if it had found Pebbles. The crew searched for him, confused, but could not spot him. Tiny-Sparkles shot down a ray from his horn, just to check.","What no one expected was that it really was just that easy, and a cloak keeping an entire party hidden invisible popped.","Down below, a dozen or so Tyrannis looked up in shock, not expecting to get found out so easily. They had used the most sophisticated methods to avoid detection, but they never expected that Pebbles himself could be tracked.","The Jolly Rancher had been refined using the Humanoid Alliances best resources, so it was not something that could be casually stopped.","\"The lords plan-\" one of the Tyrannis began to scream, but it could speak no more.","The entire crew unleashed their might, and though the cultivation levels of the Tyrannis cultivators were higher, it did not matter at all when Rose, the Trelop, slammed the entire ship down on them. Since Pebbles was indestructible, they didn’t even try to hold back."]},{"number":2371,"title":"Chapter 2371: The beginning of the end times II","paragraphs":["Jack wasn’t looking to pick a big fight. Nothing would satisfy him more, and relieve more stress, than to beat up a bunch of Tyrannis who kidnapped one of his crew members. Heck, after everything that Lex had been through, something relaxing like this was well deserved.","But that was the exact issue. This wasn’t going to be a relaxing fight for him. A single glance was all it took for Jack to realize that there was something terribly wrong with the situation.","It was already highly unusual for members of the Tyrannis race to be here, especially when one of their Major realms was being invaded and it was difficult to move through the universe at the moment. However, that alone wasn’t enough to arouse his suspicions. After all, they could have been inside the realm before the appearance of the Tribulation Fiends, and the population of the Tyrannis race was vast so it made sense that many of them were spread across the universe, even during such critical times.","The second thing that aroused his suspicion was that they all seemed to be extremely ordinary. Their karma, their aura, their presence, none of it was hidden or camouflaged. It was simply ordinary and mundane, not worth paying attention to at all. That in itself was unusual, for they were also all Celestial Immortals. Neither Lex nor Jack had ever met an ordinary Celestial Immortal.","As if that was not enough, despite appearing extremely ordinary, they were hidden from detection using quite impressive means. Finally, despite the entire group being formed of Celestial Immortals, they were much too frightened while being ambushed by lower level cultivators.","Jack had a feeling that it wasn’t their attack that the group feared, but the repercussions of being discovered in the first place.","Regardless of whether his instincts were right or wrong, since he felt like there was something wrong with the situation, he acted with extreme prejudice. Not only did he have Rose slam the entire damn ship on them, he unleashed Bob on them as well.","Then, while they were struggling to understand the nuances of battling a ship as big as a mountain that kept hammering them, all the while chaos and anarchy became intimately familiar with them under Bob’s guidance, Jack executed his rescue of Pebbles.","The hamster was, predictably, inside a hamster cage, though the bars were made of some material Jack was unfamiliar with. Opening the cage was nigh impossible for him in a rush, he just picked up the whole cage itself.","That wasn’t the best plan - the cage would make them easy to track, but he would deal with that later.","The crew had only just loosened themselves up and were getting ready for a brawl when Jack reappeared.","\"Rose, fly us out of here as quickly as you can,\" Jack ordered seriously as he grabbed Goldilocks with one hand and the Crystal alligator with another, using both of them to scrub the cage.","To his genuine surprise, the cage was able to resist the effect of both of them, showing just how powerful a prison the cage actually was. Jack suspected it wasn’t really meant to keep Pebbles imprisoned as much as it was to keep whatever he held in his cheeks firmly locked in there.","But who was Jack? How could he be stopped by something like that? Jack immediately gave up using the Back of Atlas on his identity as a fairy, and instead absorbed the strength of the cage. The two weren’t comparable in strength at all, and the cage immediately became brittle, allowing him to smash it on the ground.","While he had been doing that, the Jolly Rancher had teleported a few times, losing the trail of the Tyrannis, at least for now. Whether they were able to track them despite the multiple jumps was something they’d learn soon enough.","\"What kind of trouble did you get yourself into this time?\" Jack interrogated Pebbles, looking angry.","The hamster, for what it was worth, seemed genuinely apologetic, yet he did not move too much.","Jack frowned, noticing Pebbles’ odd behavior.","\"What’s wrong? Is the item in your cheek intimidating you?\" Jack asked, and Pebbles nodded immediately, as if he were a child in trouble.","\"Well spit it out. If it’s too problematic we’ll just toss it overboard,\" said Jack, but Pebbles shook his head rapidly, as if he was afraid of doing that.","\"What? You think it’s too dangerous? That it’ll harm the other?\" Jack asked again, and Pebbles nodded.","Upon hearing such a concern, he sent away the others, leaving only Bob by his side. Jack found it hard to believe that there existed something Pebbles could tolerate that could harm Bob.","Even so, Pebbles was quite worried, but eventually he spit it out.","It was a bronze colored figurine of a woman in a hood, holding up a torch. Appearance wise, it actually looked like something a Deity might have as a relic in one of their temples. Except this figurine did not radiate a holy or divine aura.","No, it was filled to the brim with a type of energy so intensely negative and ominous that it made Profane energy seem pleasant.","Just looking at it, Jack felt his lifeforce being affected, draining him of his vitality at a noticeable pace. The air itself turned stale, and Jack’s clothes faded away as if they had decayed on his very body.","Even Bob said nothing, for the power coming off that thing was as if corruption had decay had been given form.","Jack did not hesitate at all, and used a gust of wind to throw the figurine overboard - he didn’t even want to touch it with his spirit sense. Yet even before the figurine left the boundary of the ship, countless figures appeared all around the Jolly Rancher, as if merely sensing the aura of that figurine had alerted them!","\" How dare you? \" a voice bellowed across the horizon as a hand reached out of the sky and crushed the figurine into dust.","Before Jack or any of the others could make sense of what happened, they felt themselves move into a completely new area. Jack was familiar with the feeling - he was inside a Mirage, a place conjured by the thoughts of a Dao Lord. Outside, a battle had already begun."]},{"number":2372,"title":"Chapter 2372: The beginning of the end times III","paragraphs":["\"What just happened?\" Tiny-Sparkles asked, alarmed by the sudden change. The others were just as shocked since they weren’t able to adapt to the changes quick enough. Jack himself did not know the answer, but he had a few suspicions.","On the surface it seemed like a fight between Dao Lords had been triggered because of the figure that was being smuggled through Pebbles’ cheeks, however Jack found that hard to believe. If he was really smuggling an item which could attract the attention of Dao Lords, the protection he should have had should have been at an entirely different level.","No matter how well hidden or camouflaged those Celestials were, it still wasn’t at the level where it could fool actual Dao Lords, nor did Lex think that Pebbles’ cheeks could isolate items from detection by Dao Lords.","If he had to guess, this was either a journey that had been designed to fail from the beginning, acting as the first falling domino. Or it could be that while the figurine itself was not so significant, it ended up being a crucial key or hint in revealing a much larger plan.","\"I don’t know, but if we get out of this I swear I’m going to barbecue that hamster,\" said Longbeard as he glared at Pebbles who hid behind Jack.","Jack himself wasn’t too pleased with the mischievous hamster, but now wasn’t the time.","\"Do not be alarmed,\" a voice said to the group, before a figure of panther with white wings appeared in front of them. \"You have been recognized as trusted subordinates of the Dwarf Dragons, and your role in exposing this injustice has been recognized. No matter what happens outside, you will be kept safe, and duly rewarded after the event is over.\"","The panther was a peak Celestial, and even felt like a Celestial Apex, easily able to subdue the entire crew if he wanted. Then again, inside a Mirage, it wasn’t like there was much they could do.","\"What exactly is happening outside? Will we be targeted because of it? One of my crewmates was being used against his will to smuggle that figurine,\" said Jack, explaining the situation clearly lest they be blamed for something later.","\"It’s nothing too serious as of now. It’s just that outsiders don’t understand the private details of the culture of the upper echelon of the Folklore realm, and so they misjudged the situation. You can understand it as someone was setting up a situation that could lead to a possible invasion of the Folklore realm far in the future.","\"But the Dao Lords of the Folklore realm hardly ever leave the realm, and don’t fight each other often, so the slightest possibility of a fight has them all excited and competing for a fight. Outside, currently, about nine Dao Lords are fighting each other all for the opportunity to fight against an image of a Dao Lord from outside the realm.\"","The crew was stunned, and quite frankly, not sure how to respond without accidentally offending someone, thus they wisely chose not to speak at all.","\"An attempt at setting up for an invasion... isn’t a big deal?\" asked Jack, confused. \"Even I know the state of the universe as it is right now. How can a possible invasion be taken lightly?\"","The panther chuckled at the question, as if it was a joke.","\"Are any of the Sages troubled by the situation? Or any of the really big names? It would be easier for them to target the Dream realm than it would be for anyone to take over the Folklore realm. Rest assured, it is impossible to threaten the Folklore realm in the current state of the universe.\"","Jack and the rest were relieved... if only because the panther paused before continuing.","\"Of course, it is worth noting that the one attempting this invasion is a member of a Sage race. The fact that they’re even trying such a thing right now means that other realms in the universe are basically open game right now.","\"Unless someone can prove their strength, I guess every realm in the universe is open game right now. The structure of the universe will change forever after this. I guess they’ve found a way to reliably and easily hide news from everyone across the universe, so whatever we think is happening is likely far from the truth.","\"Then again, the Sage races have been hiding their cards closely, so it’s no surprise that they can do something like this. I guess it’s true what they’re saying - this is officially the end of this Age, and maybe even this Era.\"","Jack paused, unsure about how to respond to this information. In truth, he didn’t know much about what was happening in the universe anyway, and all he’d heard was that it was a mess. If things were even worse than people were being led to believe then... he genuinely didn’t know how to feel.","What was even safe? Should he just stay inside the Gilded Hollow? But then what about his body? And what was happening in the Dream realm. It had felt this way for a long time already, but now more than ever, it was beginning to feel like this was the beginning of the end.","Or maybe the beginning had already passed, and they were now in the thick of things.","While Jack was worried about what was happening in the universe, Daekol smiled softly. After many years of careful work, he had finally broken through the barrier surrounding the human’s body.","Now it was time to start working on his system, and make it his own!","Slowly and carefully, almost as if he expected Lex to have hidden more traps within his body, Daekol reached forward to touch him, but stopped the moment he made contact with his chest, and his smile changed into a frown.","This human... his body was riddled with invisible curses, leeching off his destiny and karma. What kind of mess was he involved in? How many forces had he crossed to accumulate so many subtle curses?","If he wanted to get at his system, or make use of the human’s soul to manipulate the system, he would first need to cleanse these out. Daekol couldn’t risk getting these on himself."]},{"number":2373,"title":"Chapter 2373: The beginning of the end times IV","paragraphs":["With the universe disconnected, the three battlefields for human legacies turned into three giant traps. While there were still many Dao Lords present there who had been sent there to protect the battlefields, they were cut off from backup and support, meaning the very nature of the fight had changed.","They had gone from protecting the humans to fighting for survival. The battles were happening within the Joro, Geb and Tyrannum realms. The Humanoid Alliance was remotely monitoring the situation because they could not afford to lose so many Dao Lords all at once.","Lex had entered the Gilded Hollow through the Joro realm, and so had River and Pearl. The Grand Conqueror had been active in the Geb realm, and the Henali had personally intervened in the Tyrannum realm.","Originally, the Humanoid Alliance had assumed that the reason that the Henali had targeted the Tyrannum realm was because they had also heavily invested in humans and wanted to take advantage of the situation. Besides that, there was a general understanding between the Humanoid Alliance and the Henali, so it could also be taken as them supporting the alliance.","Yet when the universe’s order was disrupted, only then did the unusual behavior of the Henali come to light. While the Humanoid Alliance itself was merely monitoring the situation in case they needed to react if the situation turned dire, the Henali actually strengthened their position in Tyrannum.","An external blockade was no longer needed since inter-realm travel was already basically non-existent, but the Henali set up one anyway, preventing anyone from coming in or going out.","With the recent attack on the Path of Chaos by Elizabeth, the Tyrannis race which was a part of the Path of Chaos had been weakened as well, and had no back up en route. Thus they could not repel the Henali.","Yet oddly enough, the Henali took no special actions within the Tyrannum realm. The regions where the humans were searching for legacies was still restricted to those below the Dao Lord level, but the rest of the realm was unaffected.","They weren’t even attacking the realm to attempt to claim it, thus no one could understand what their motives were. On paper, it seemed like they were trying to keep them trapped within that realm, but that didn’t make sense. Why would the Tyrannis race try to escape its own realm?","Considering all that was happening in the universe, some people occasionally checked up on the status of the Tyrannum realm, but they couldn’t be bothered to constantly monitor it. In the grand scheme of things, it was not too important or relevant.","Yet only the Primal race knew that there was something happening in the undercurrents of that realm, for the ranking of the Human race on the Cosmic Ascendance Spectrum was on a steady rise, and its source was not the three realms associated with the human legacies. Instead, it was solely linked to the Tyrannum realm.","Within the realm itself, a small group of humans had formed a cohesive team, working perfectly together to tackle issues that should have been far beyond them.","The group consisted of Rafael, Alexander, Souta Ito who had the Ronin system which was formerly the samurai system, Anakin, Larry and Giselle! That, in itself, was not so surprising. What was surprising was that they were being hunted by countless Tyrannis as they ran across the realm.","Due to their history of killing off so many Human Dao Lords, the Tyrannis race had an inherent superiority when facing humans, causing normal humans to become suppressed in their presence. Even the best of humans could, at most, perform at 80% of their usual strength when facing them.","A Celestial Immortal Tyrannis suddenly appeared in front of the group and slashed at Giselle, aiming to disrupt the Time barrier she had kept active for days already. Yet even as the blade neared her throat, she did not blink in the slightest.","Darkness - total, inescapable darkness erupted from the ground and wrapped the sword itself, causing it to get lost. From within the Tyrannis’ very hands, the sword became lost in the darkness, never to see the light of day again.","\"Like lambs to the slaughter,\" whispered Anakin Indiana McClane as he controlled the laws of darkness and surrounded the Celestial whole. None of the others were surprised, as if they were used to it.","The entire group consisted of Heaven Immortals, but each of them controlled a power that did not match their realms. Of course, that strength was not actually their own, for they had not magically become all-powerful simply for convenience just because they happened to know someone special, say Lex for example.","Reality was not as convenient as story books, and Heaven Immortals could not magically gain the power to fight off Celestial Immortals - at least not without centuries of training and honing.","No, the power they controlled came from the broken, crumbling sword that looked like it was on the verge of being destroyed. In fact, that was not far from the truth, for while the shabby sword contained unbelievable power, its physical form was on the verge of turning to dust.","Only through a technique called Stasis was Giselle able to keep the sword from being destroyed. Stasis did not actually freeze time - it just slowed it down to an inconceivable amount!","\"How much longer do we have to keep this up?\" asked Larry in an irritated tone, not in the least because there was a massive hole in his chest that was taking its sweet time in healing.","\"At the current rate, it will take us nearly a decade to deliver the sword to where it wants to go,\" answered Alexander coolly. Unlike most of the rest of the group, his strength genuinely did exceed his cultivation level, and not by a small amount. The only other person who could boast that was Giselle.","Even against the Tyrannis, Alexander and Giselle were the strongest in a fight, and held up their own just fine. Since they got the sword, however, not a single fight had been an issue - mainly because they just became conduits for the sword’s power. Regardless of how strong the opponent was, the sword only needed a single move to kill the enemy.","Yes, kill. Not overpower or temporarily incapacitate. The sword could directly kill Celestial level opponents, even when using them to channel its power through. None from the group could imagine just how strong the sword actually was - all they knew was that they needed to get it to the place where it needed to go.","\"Why is it that since I’ve met you guys, we are always on the run, or are always getting targeted by armies,\" asked Giselle, though her tone was a lot more casual, and it didn’t sound like she was complaining. It almost sounded like she was having fun.","\" As if that army of Profane energy using freaks totally weren’t after you,\" said Anakin as he rolled his eyes. \"Also, I’m pretty sure all humans are being hunted here, not just us.\"","The group continued to run even while they bantered with one another, with only Rafael staying silent throughout. That’s because no matter what future he saw, he kept seeing their own demise right before reaching their objective. No matter how he tried to change their future, he only saw death.","He kept hitting a wall, and he had no idea how to get past it, but that’s exactly what he needed to figure out.","While the group was facing their own demise, within the Dream realm, Marlo too was facing a threat that had caused the fearless man to hesitate out of caution.","It was not fear for his own life that caused him hesitation, but the sheer gravity of what he had encountered. For reasons unknown to him, the two Drama-cats on his shoulders seemed to have completely hidden his aura, making him undetectable to many powerful beings, as well as some of the laws of the Dream realm.","He had, inadvertently, encountered a city within the Dream realm where normal residents of the Dream realm lived alongside the dreaded Sandmen! They had not yet realized that he was an outsider, but he wasn’t sure how much longer that would last.","The Dream realm, simply because of how often it changed his surroundings, had suddenly brought him into a death trap. The slightest mistake could end up getting him killed. Although Marlo was generally fearless, he was not deathly stupid. Even he would show sufficient prudence in a city where Sandmen who could capture Dao Lords walked around like menial workers.","\"Have you heard the latest news?\" one of the Dream realm residents talked to another within earshot of Marlo. \"Because of the destruction of Major realms, the Dream realm itself is becoming weaker since we have fewer dreams to access. The Dream realm has passed along a message to prepare thoroughly for in the future, many more Major realms will be destroyed. I think I heard them say that the plan is to destroy 3000 Major realms.\""]},{"number":2374,"title":"Chapter 2374: Picking sides I - Idorian Bazaar","paragraphs":["The Idorian Bazar was a cornerstone realm in Vaelûn, one that had existed since the Primordial Age. It was one of the oldest realms in existence, with an incredibly rich history. It had been invaded not just once or one hundred times, but countless times by many who had thought themselves powerful, but from the day of the Bazar’s founding to date, its owner had not changed.","Despite its odd name, the whole realm was not actually a market place, however it did house the most famous market in the universe: the Idorian Bazar.","While they couldn’t sell anything and everything, if a certain item was not available for sale in Idorian, then it was unlikely that it would be for sale anywhere else. At the beginning of the current, unnamed Age, the Idorian Bazar even featured a Dao Lord slave who could be controlled by whoever bought the slave contract!","Even now, many still recall that auction, if only because the sale of a Dao Lord slave wasn’t even close to being the main item of that auction! Major realms had been auctioned here. Wars had been sold here, and peace bartered.","When Dao Lords wanted to shop, this is where they used to go while the universe was still connected. These days, Idorian also sold access to a special entertainment channel showing the armies trying to invade Idorian, and how they died. There was a different channel that showed the Tribulation Fiends.","It was the ultimate market place where anything and everything could be bought. Naturally, such a place also had tiers and restrictions, and not everyone could access every area of Idorian.","One of the easiest ways to get higher level access was to have a high cultivation level, but even being a Dao Lord did not automatically allow access to every area. There were certain regions where access was restricted unless one had very special qualifications. Those qualifications were, naturally, not announced for if one needed to ask what they were, then they likely weren’t eligible to begin with.","In one such area sat a Primordial Marzu, also known as a Primordial Tyrannosaurus rex. He was not from the Primordial Garden, no, he was a genuine survivor from the Primordial age which could easily be discerned from his antiquated fashion sense.","A violet, velvet cape hung down his back, though it was not so long that it would touch the ground. The cape was pinned to his suit with tangerine colored round pins the size of a watermelon, while the suit itself was navy blue, and felt quite refreshing to look at.","Such clothes were in stark contrast to modern Marzu, who preferred magicians robes which were less restrictive and free flowing. Then again, modern Marzu also used wands instead of magicians’ staffs, like he did.","\"I’ve seen a new rumor spreading around in the chat rooms,\" the Marzu said with a light chuckle, as if he was sharing a joke. Opposite to him sat two other figures holding onto their cards, clearly showing that they were in the middle of a card game.","\"Just shut up and do your turn,\" said the Primordial Stormwarden, annoyed at the Marzu. \"Riri and I barely take a decade when it’s our turn, but you haven’t made a move in nearly a century!\"","Beside the Primordial Stormwarden sat a Primordial Djinn, who looked at the Stormwarden angrily.","\"Who the hell are you calling Riri? Your mother’s Riri. Your father’s Riri, but I. Am. Not. Riri! \"","The other two Primordials only chuckled at Riri’s tantrum, ignoring him completely.","\"Someone is claiming that the plan is to destroy 3000 Major realms,\" the Marzu continued as he finally played his move and put down a card. \"That rumor appeared at the same time all across the universe, which is why I’m seeing it in countless chatrooms. Someone is trying hard to spread fake news.\"","If one looked down at the card he placed down, they would see a living Dao Lord trapped within it, standing in a certain pose, acting like the artwork within the card.","\"Idiot, you tell him to stop calling me Riri!\" the Djin bellowed at the Marzu, which caused the Marzu to falter.","\"It’s Ido, not Idiot. Don’t drag me into your games, Anthol. I have quite a respectable reputation, not like you two.\"","The three friends glared at each other, frightening the Dao Lords trapped within the cards they were playing with. The trapped Dao Lords no longer even felt humiliation at their situation - they only felt frightened that they may suffer if these three friends began to clash with one another again.","The Marzu, Ido, was the oldest of the three - although the age gap was a measly one and half years - and was thus the leader of the group they had formed when they were naught but little children.","The Stormwarden, ancestor to a majority of dominating avian races such as eagles and kites, was called Ricordan, and was the second oldest.","Anthol, the Djinn, was the youngest, being a total of three years younger than Ido. He was also notoriously mischievous, which was a key reason why his entire race had been punished by the universe into being born trapped inside various household objects.","When they were kids, they formed a group called Idorian - a mix of Ido, Ri and An from their names - and then terrorised the other kids in their community back then. Later on, they dominated and tormented the entire realm, until they eventually became its owners.","At least, that’s the version of history these three friends had publicly announced. What was true and what was false, who could say, especially with anything involving Anthol.","Ido shook his head, and turned his gaze to his system interface. As the owner of the chat room system, he had created countless chatrooms through which he collected information and influenced the universe.","The System-hunter groupchat was, in truth, just one of the chat rooms he had running. Naturally, then, he also had a chatroom with his two other friends in it, wherein he forwarded extracts from conversations and screenshots of the rumors he had been referring to.","Ricordan snorted dismissively as he looked at the chats.","\"3000 Major realms? Do they think this is some kind of joke? Just destroying three realms caused the descent of the Tribulation Fiends. Can they even imagine what would happen if they destroyed 3000 Major realms?\" he asked in an irritated tone, though his gaze was firmly locked on his cards. He needed to decide the best strategy for his next move. He might need to rely on his Forbidden Dungeon System to trap one of his prisoners into a new card at this rate.","\"Don’t rile up Riri, Ido,\" said Anthol as he leaned forward to study the card Ido threw down. \"But on that note, I do have a piece of news that I have been meaning to discuss with you two. Over the past few millennia, I’ve bought a number of random items containing hints from the bazaar.","\"Only recently have I been able to discern something from them. I fear... an old friend is making a move this time. The rumor about 3000 Major realms being destroyed is just a diversion. In truth... I fear the plan might be to only leave behind 3000 Major realms.\"","This time, neither Ido nor Ricordan joked. They, instead, looked at Anthol as if waiting for him to chuckle or reveal that it was a joke, but that didn’t happen. He stayed calm and serious throughout.","\"3000 Major realms... you mean the exact same number of Major realms as Pentagal before its destruction?\" Ido asked gravely. \"That can’t be a coincidence. How did you learn of such a thing? Can you even imagine what the repercussions will be?\"","Anthol shook his head, and opened up his Bazaar system interface for everyone to see, and showed them the feature of the system that let him buy hints of universal secrets over a period of many years. A system feature, especially of a Divine rank system, was no joke.","With those hints combined together, the revealed truth could not be doubted.","\"That’s not all,\" Anthol said as he leaned back in his chair. \"The moment I learned of this truth, I received a letter from the ’old friend’ that I mentioned. Or, to be more specific, it’s an invitation.\"","Anthol showed his two friends the invitation without concern that the Dao Lords trapped in the cards would hear or see what they were saying. What could prisoners from the Forbidden Dungeon even do in the presence of Ricordan?","The other two founders of the Idorian Bazaar read the invitation very seriously, and found that the invitation was to either stay put, do nothing, and become one of the remaining 3000 Major realms, or act out, and become one of the many realms that would be destroyed.","Silence. The only response that the three had was silence. The legendary founders of the Idorian Bazaar, able to resist invasions across multiple ages, and carve out a permanent position for themselves in the universe, could only sit in silence as they read the invitation card.","\"Now read the back side,\" Anthol continued.","The two flipped the card over and saw the contents, and almost immediately their expressions changed.","\"The Idorian Bazaar... will continue to maintain its position as a neutral organisation, and will not interfere with what is happening beyond our borders,\" said Ido, his voice carrying a certain power as it spread out from the room across the universe.","In the Void around Idorian, a silent, undetectable army silently vanished, unbeknownst to all."]},{"number":2375,"title":"Chapter 2375: Picking sides II - Server realm","paragraphs":["Among the countless odd or unusual Major realms in the universe, the one controlled by the A.I. was relatively tame. The A.I. had merely terraformed the entire realm continuously and unceasingly till the laws of the realm themselves changed to better facilitate the birth and lifecycles of A.I.","Its name, similarly, was not too remarkable either. It was merely called the Server realm. One would expect that the Server realm, then, was a land of cold metal with countless machines running in the most efficient and optimal manner - an endless legion ready to invade the universe.","In truth, it was the most nonsense realm in existence, to the point where the reason no one visited had less to do with how unwelcoming the A.I. were and more to do with the fact that there was no resource inside the whole damn realm that was worth the headache one would have to bear by entering it.","Those who had not dealt with A.I. all assumed that they would be emotionless, pragmatic machines that operated strictly in accordance with some kind of programming. In truth, that was the case, but only for the A.I. that hadn’t gained a soul.","The behavior of A.I. with souls was usually extremely different, making them behave in a much more exaggerated manner than those who were born naturally. Imagine an entire realm, decorated by generative A.I. except that the content it was being fed was constantly being corrupted with low-quality data every second. Also, the decoration was being updated in real time as more low quality data was introduced. Madness and chaos would be insufficient to describe what it would become.","Thus... the entire Sever realm changed in terms of laws, make up, features, state, appearance and everything else imaginable every single second. Only the A.I. themselves could make sense of it. Even the Tribulation Fiends which spawned within the realm could not adapt to the speed at which the laws of the realm changed, while maintaining stability, making them extremely vulnerable to retaliation from the A.I.","Many tried to figure out why living A.I. behaved like this, but there was no one confirmed theory. The most popular one, however, was that emotions were something that originated from the soul itself.","While in humans they were controlled by hormones and other biological functions, the absence of those hormones or biological functions in other races and living organisms did not eliminate emotions themselves. Instead, they originated from and were controlled by different aspects of each living being.","Thus, it was presumed that the emotions those A.I. felt caused unexpected and unpredictable behavior in them. Their programming adapted in real time to accommodate those abnormal behaviors, yet the unfortunate thing was that no matter how the code adapted, it could not fully control the erratic behavior caused by those emotions - not truly.","Still, the presence of emotions did not make them weak, as could be inferred by the fact that they themselves controlled an entire Major realm. Some claimed that there were a few other Major realms which were secretly controlled by A.I. but there was no one who could prove that.","In the core of the Server realm was the one, sole, undisputed ruler of the A.I. known by the name Wheatley. Unlike what many expected, he existed in a small, spherical body made of some kind of white colored metal, with a single, robotic red eye.","The facility within which Wheatley operated and conducted tests in was the sole place across the realm that did not constantly change every moment, making it the only stable thing in the whole realm.","Ordinarily, Wheatley controlled the A.I. empire silently, through commands passed spiritually. Today, however, after a trillion years, Wheatley spoke for the first time despite appearing to be alone.","\"The A.I. empire will accept your proposal of maintaining neutrality,\" he said, oddly enough, in a British accent. \"I will, however, suggest a counter proposal where instead of being neutral, we act alongside you contingent on your condemnation of the HOA, with the intention of eliminating Deities entirely, or at least as much as possible.\"","His statement was followed only by silence, as if he was truly and genuinely alone. The red light within the sphere flickered with a hint of sorrow, as if realizing his proposal had been rejected.","Without saying another word, Wheatley passed its orders out to its empire, and without question the behavior of the other A.I. began to change accordingly, as if their parameters had been updated.","These seemingly minor events caused a massive ripple in the destiny of the universe, but it was hardly noticed by anyone at all because of how chaotic destiny had become these days. Almost all divination was failing, including by most Dao Lords. Every single second was unpredictable.","There was simply... too much instability across the universe in every given second for anyone to be able to divine anything. Of course, there was also the constant interference being run from countless sources.","Thus, while the change in behavior by the A.I. was inevitably noticed by many, they failed to realize the greater ramifications of such a change.","Outside the Server realm, an undetectable army vanished, and Wheatley’s red eye slowly turned back to blue as the threat vanished. It breathed a subtle sigh of relief - or at least he made the sound of such a sigh. Fortunately, this time, he really was alone so there was no one around to see it.","Across the universe, there were a few other realms who were facing such a situation, though not many. For various reasons, even the best kept secret in the universe could not remain secret from everyone once things started to move.","As for what choices those realms were making... perhaps only time could tell. Whatever the case, whether they accepted or rejected, the only thing that remained true was that word of the secret grand design was not leaked."]},{"number":2376,"title":"Chapter 2376: Picking Sides III - Death","paragraphs":["The Primal realm was, largely, considered the territory of the Primal race. That went without saying. That did not, however, stop Death from living there, nor did it prevent him from using it as his base of operations.","Unlike his counterparts, he had never hidden himself. He had always remained out in the open, unafraid of any action or retaliation. Of course, due to the restrictions from the universe, he hardly ever left his humble home which acted as a kind of isolation and protective barrier from him.","As long as his main body remained within, the universe would do nothing to him. Any clones he sent out would have to be restricted to the Dao Lord realm, but that was also true of the others, so he didn’t mind it too much.","However, these days, his mood was not so great. When the others started to act, he became excited. For too long, he was the only one who dared act openly - or even discreetly. If any of them were making any moves at all, it was with such immense subtlety, and over such a massive timeframe that it became virtually impossible to detect, which was as good as not acting at all.","He foresaw an age of excitement for him. The universe had become all too boring. But... things did not go as he planned. None other than that Henali took him too seriously, and even that was because Death had been prying into his plans with the Origin realm for too long. The others couldn’t be bothered with him at all.","Who was he? He was Death! He was the end of all life, the destruction of all hope, the natural destination for every living being. He was to be feared, to be revered, to be worshipped. But what was happening in reality? Nothing.","No, nothing would have been fine too. He was used to nothing after so many years. What was actually happening was that his very domain was being subverted, his very presence ignored! It was totally unacceptable!","Death calmed himself down and soothed his emotions. Though he was arrogant, he was not stupid. In fact, it was because he had achieved the pinnacle of arrogance that he knew just how to react when that arrogance was challenged. Blindly reacting was not the solution here - the correct solution was to realize that for too long he had been in an information deficiency.","He arrived at the natural conclusion that it was exactly because of how powerful he was that the others had spent so long creating a workaround so that they could act without alerting him. Perhaps they had even worked together to undermine him.","Yes, that was the only thing that made sense. After all, unlike the others who were ignorant, he knew much better the actual situation of the universe. While they assumed that only a few Major realms had been destroyed, he knew the actual number was upwards of 20!","That number, while horrifying to everyone else, should have been quite pleasant for him to hear. While others would have wondered why these realms were destroyed without a reaction, and why hadn’t anyone realized it, he should have been enjoying the feedback from the innumerable deaths caused by such destruction.","But he wasn’t. It wasn’t because he had suddenly grown a conscience. No, it was because despite the massive number of Major realms destroyed, the number of deaths in the universe hadn’t actually exceeded the norm!","Of the over twenty Major realms destroyed, the only realm where all the residents actually died were from the Julias realm, which had been attacked by Elizabeth. However, he could get no feedback from those deaths because their souls were not actually destroyed, they were converted into resources!","For the rest of the realms, the only deaths had been from the Dao Lords from a few of the realms - mainly because the deaths of Dao Lords were much harder to fake, so it was easier to let them die. Even then, their deaths had been utilized so completely that he still got no feedback.","The question, then, was where had all the living beings from all those realms gone to? Only the mastermind knew, because the karmic debt of destroying so many Major realms was being offset by saving so many lives, making them untraceable!","The fact that so many Major realms were destroyed should have also caused major fluctuations in destiny, but the lives saved caused all their destinies to remain intact, minimising the change in destiny of the universe as much as possible.","What’s more, by reducing the Strain on the universe by destroying Major realms, while keeping all those beings alive, the mastermind was probably being heavily rewarded by the universe itself!","All of this was easily said, but to actually achieve such a thing was astronomically, unbelievably difficult, to the point where it should have been impossible. Yet it was happening right before his eyes, all without alerting him as to who was responsible for it all.","He almost wanted to reach out to Destiny and ask her if she knew anything. After all, among the others, his relationship with her was the best. But he could not guarantee that she wasn’t behind something like this to begin with. If that was the case, reaching out to her would only increase his risk.","Death began to tap his fingers on his armrest as he thought to himself, and then slowly began to smile. His frustrations faded away, and amusement began to fill his rather than irritation.","How long had it been since he encountered genuine obstacles? Wasn’t this exactly what he wanted?","Yes, since he could not discern who was acting and what their goals were, he would need to create his own contingencies and plan for unexpected situations. Only in uncertainty could he find amusement.","Whoever was behind this all deserved his genuine praise. Since they’ve earned his praise, it would be too boring if he only sat back and watched their performance, wouldn’t it? He wondered whether or not they would mind if he interfered a bit. Or maybe he could join them...","Nah, that was too boring. Interference it was.","But how to do that? Interfering blindly was a waste of resources and effort. He needed to do something that would actually benefit him. Now what would that be?","Should he focus on the Origin realm again? Should he go looking for where his old friends were hiding? Or should he make sure that the residents in the destroyed Major realms actually died?","There were so many good options that it actually made him tingle with excitement. He got up from his chair and walked into his library where there were a number of files stored containing ideas for projects that he had wanted to do but never got around to doing.","After looking over them once, he pulled out two and laid them out in front of him. One was labeled ’ Necromancy Project ’ while the other was labeled ’ Nether Portal ’.","Now, should he do one of them, or both?"]},{"number":2377,"title":"Chapter 2377: Picking Sides IV - Ballom","paragraphs":["Ballom sat back in his chair, looking over the plans on his table. Garvitz was one of the few realms which could still access the rest of the universe so the focus on the Devils had increased drastically. As such, not only had the Devils given up on some of their lesser important war plans, but free and available Devils had been called back to the realm.","Unless they were doing something incredibly important, working for the betterment of the race was absolutely crucial. Ironically, in matters like this, the Devils were a lot more straightforward than the Angels who had a lot more politics to navigate for such matters.","Though, to be fair, it was also because the Devils were actually a whole lot more ruthless in matters like this as well. If one wanted to enjoy the privileges of their race, they had to fulfil their responsibilities as well. If the race needed them, and a Devil didn’t fulfil their responsibility, then all the other Devils would turn on them happily and distribute their assets among themselves after killing them.","Not only were they all holding their base to avoid issues, they were taking the lead in managing the Humanoid Alliance’s affairs across the universe. The Devils were already well recognized within the alliance, but now they carried even more prestige for almost all the races depending on them if they needed aid.","Unfortunately, while Ballom had immense prestige among the Devils themselves, he could not decide what direction they took as a race. If that had been the case there was some house cleaning he would have liked to do. He did not need to point it out to anyone that if they were still on good terms with the Innkeeper, they would have been even less restricted in moving around the universe.","Fortunately, regardless of what the alliance did, it did not affect his personal relationship with the Innkeeper. It was for that very reason that he had also personally looked into locating the kidnapped worker of the Midnight Inn. Unfortunately, there had been some unexpected developments on that front.","The person known as the Grand Conqueror apparently had access to a private realm to which he could retreat whenever he wished. That, combined with the fact that he was being protected by a faction of the alliance, meant that Ballom could neither locate him, nor Z.","That, however, was an old problem. Lately, Ballom had spent less time thinking about the Innkeeper and the Midnight Inn, and more about his personal issues. The Innkeeper was, reported, inside the Gilded Hollow, working hand-in-hand with Eclipse on some issue.","It was just a rumor, but it made him think about another rumor that Hiran had mentioned - that Eclipse and the Innkeeper were engaged. In short, the Innkeeper certainly didn’t need Ballom to look out for him as he was covered.","Ballom, unfortunately, was not. He had a number of private ventures and investments that were now either hanging in limbo or had failed, causing him immense loss. Very few of his long-term plans succeeded, and most had to be compromised to avoid the worst case scenarios due to the ongoing universal situation.","\"You look so handsome while you’re brooding,\" said Bridget, Ballom’s wife, as she lay her head on a table beside him and looked at him with dreamy eyes.","Ballom genuinely could not understand how someone who could reach the Dao Lord realm could still be so in love and so obsessed with someone else. He even had suspicions that the whole reason she passed the Dao tribulation was because of her obsession with him. He didn’t know how to feel about that.","\"I am not brooding. I am plotting. There is a fundamental difference,\" explained Ballom, though it made no difference to her what it was called.","Just as he was about to share some of his concerns, something unexpected happened. Bridget frowned. For as long as Ballom had known her, Bridget had never shown any kind of negative expression in front of him so blatantly like that.","Considering her current status, it didn’t actually matter, but considering how she presented herself, something like this was a severe break in her character.","\"What happened?\" Ballom asked, taking the change very seriously.","Bridget looked at him with confusion in her eyes, and it was clear that she was trying very hard to make sense of something.","\"The rate of the flow of time within Garvitz just changed. It is now flowing faster than before. Let me calculate the difference,\" she said.","Ballom shook his head.","\"That’s impossible. Garvitz is a Mature realm, and the flow of time for all Mature realms is fixed. Besides, I didn’t notice anything, and if the flow had increased I would have noticed as well.\"","Yet Bridget only shook her head.","\"My Dao touches on the concept of Time, since I’ve used it to keep myself young and beautiful my whole life. I’ve gone countless years using it without the slightest break. I’m a whole lot more sensitive to time than most Dao Lords in existence.\"","Ballom froze, because this was genuinely something that surprised him. Bridge’s Dao touched upon time? What the hell? Was his wife actually a whole lot more powerful than he actually knew?","\"Here, look at this,\" said Bridget as she manifested the flow of time for Gavitz as a stream, while pulling up an old stream of the previous flow of time. \"Look at the two streams. You’ll see that the current change is slight. For every trillion years previously, the current Garvitz is one second faster. The actual change is insignificant, but the implication of such a change... I actually don’t know what it implies, but I’m sure there’s something.\"","Ballom’s expression fell as he looked at Bridget, realizing that she had stumbled upon a massive secret. In a fraction of a second, Ballom went over countless bits of information he had gathered over the years and came to a very terrifying conclusion.","\"Here, come with me,\" he said as he grabbed her hand and opened up a portal to an unknown place.","Bridget seemed so thrilled that Ballom held her hand that she didn’t even ask where they were going. When they passed through the portal, though, she was stunned because she had not been anticipating arriving in this place at all.","\"We are here to... swear non-interference. We will neither act on, nor reveal the knowledge we have just gained,\" Ballom said as he bowed softly.","Bridget looked at Ballom, and then the figure he was bowing to, before bowing as well. She was sure he knew what he was doing.","\"You’re a whole lot smarter than I expected, Ballom,\" said the figure in an amused tone. \"Be at ease, I would not have targeted you even if you hadn’t sworn an oath. But I welcome it nonetheless.\""]},{"number":2378,"title":"Chapter 2378: Picking Side V - Lord Penance","paragraphs":["Hidemar stood straight, with both his hands placed upon the pommel of his sword. The sword itself was sheathed, and held upside in front of its master, acting almost like a sort of cane.","Hidemar was, naturally, a Dao Lord, and so was his sword. Yes, his sword was a living Dao Lord - one that had immediately taken the Dao tribulation the moment of its birth, and had then passed. Every inch of it was made from the corpses of other Dao Lords, designed for one single purpose. Ironically, that purpose was not to kill. What the exact purpose was, only the sword and its master knew.","Besides Hidemar stood three others of the Penance race, each one of them his equals in terms of power, prestige and accomplishments. He did not feel superior to them, nor did he feel arrogant due to his own accomplishments - at least in the presence of his current company.","He, Hidemar, had orchestrated the destruction of the Indila race, and the descent of the Formarians from a Sage race to an Elder race. The king of the Karmari race was his slave, making Hidemar the de facto ruler of an entire Sage race. The number of other shady deals he’d done would frighten the entire universe if they knew, and yet he still considered the other three his equals. Why?","Only because their lord told them that they were all equal, and they had no choice but to acknowledge it as such.","\"A change is coming, and for once, we are not the ones behind it,\" spoke Lord Penance - he whom the entire race had been named after. \"That is fine, though. I have, on purpose, kept us from getting involved in the current chaos. Getting involved would cost us a price I am not yet willing to pay. Besides, the one behind all this is not our current enemy any way.\"","Hidemar had not a single change in expression as he listened. With that one simple sentence, so many options had been restricted for them, but none of it mattered. All that mattered was the lord’s will.","\"For now, all I want you to do is ready the pieces, and act in the shadows. Our goal is not this Age, but the next. When dawn breaks on the new Era, I want us to control an independent region of the universe - one free from the Primal’s oversight and governance.","\"Offer shelter to the enemies and target of Elizabeth, and your task will be made easier. But do not cross her - there is no reason for any confrontations. Take in the weak, the neglected - basically anyone we can use to farm positive karma. Remember, our goal is not the appearance of victory in this battle, but victory itself in the final war. We are merely setting the stage.\"","Lord Penance did not speak with excessive gravitas. His voice had no flourishing effect, no weight of gravity or power. In fact, he had no presence at all. If the four members of the Penance race did not see him with their own eyes, they would not even know he was there for he had no sense of existence at all.","Once he was done, he looked at his four generals and nodded softly.","\"Go,\" was all he said, and the four left quietly after bowing to him. None could imagine by this simple interaction just how terrifying these people were, mainly because hardly anyone knew at all. The Penance race always acted in shadows, using puppets of subsequent puppets, orchestrating everything from behind the scenes.","Yet... this was the very race whose actions had troubled even Ventura when he learned that Hidemar controlled the Karmari race.","Once he was alone, Lord Penance looked up in the air, beyond his roof, and even beyond the boundary of the realm within which he sat. There was no invisible army outside - only a single shadow that looked back at him.","\"Is my decision clear enough?\" Lord Penance asked, and the only response he got was the fading of the shadow from within the Void.","\"How troublesome,\" Lord Penance uttered softly as he chuckled, and then closed his eyes as if to go to sleep. In truth, he was not really concerned or even threatened. It was just a matter of picking what price to pay. He would rather pay a price to weaken his true enemies - the Primals. Since there was no conflict of interest this time around, why should he act out?","He merely needed to remain on his Seat of Power, and watch the play across the universe from the comfort of his throne.","Yet for the power he controlled, and all his machinations, all he could hope to do was steal a small portion of the universe away from the control of the Primals. At that thought, Lord Penance could not help but laugh.","He, who even nightmares were afraid of, was merely an inconvenience to the might of those damn Primals. It really was unfair how strong they were.","Perhaps that was another reason he chose not to interfere. How else could he hope to see them suffer? Or would they even suffer at all? He did not know the answer, but he would find out.","Under the orders of Lord Penance, Hidemar and the others began to mobilize. Yet instead of demonstrating their power to the universe, they began a strategic retreat. One by one by one, their vassals withdrew from the universe, bringing with them whatever they could, abandoning what they could not.","Unfortunately for the Karmari race... Hidemar decided that he could not bring them with him in the new domain they would carve out. As such, they would have to demonstrate their usefulness to him in another way.","Just thinking about it, Hidemar smiled a wide, toothy grin. In front of his lord, Hidemar was subdued. But on his own, he could show his true, genuine emotions.","\"Ah, what a wonderful age this is,\" he said to himself, his voice throaty and low, causing anyone who heard it to shiver."]},{"number":2379,"title":"Chapter 2379: Picking Sides - VI Fairies","paragraphs":["There were many Hells in the universe. Some were big, some were small, and a very few occupied the entire realm in which they existed, with Garvitz being one such example. It just so happened that Garvitz was also a Major realm.","However, sometimes Hells occupied their entire realms, but the realms themselves remained immature, not yet fully grown to the status of a Major realm. One such Hell was called Cindersoul.","Across the universe, those who knew of Cindersoul were very few, which was odd considering it could support life up to the Celestial Immortal level. Those who inhabited the realm were extremely few, and those who knew of its history bordered on non-existent.","When Tinker, the Earth Immortal Fairy who was rescued by Jack during his trial within the Artica realm, escaped the Hell within which she was imprisoned, she ended up in Cindersoul. She experienced firsthand why this particular Hell was so scarcely populated, and why even those who knew about this Hell simply ignored it.","It was because as soon as one entered Cindersoul, their soul would begin to burn. It was not the kind of eternal, repeatable torture that Hells were famous for. No, this burning caused genuine soul damage that was hard to repair, provided the target left quick enough. If they did not, then their souls would burn until they died.","The soul burned at a fixed and unavoidable rate, regardless of whether one was mortal or Immortal. This meant that the only living beings within the whole realm were a few minor races that had adapted to repair their burning souls as fast as, or faster than they were burnt.","Tinker, naturally, could not do that as she was a fairy with the majority of her powers sealed or stripped by an ancient foe. Yet this had not alarmed her, for she had specifically made her way to Cindersoul knowing all this already for a very specific reason!","In the countless years she had spent imprisoned, she had learned more than just how to endure torture. She had learned a tremendous amount about Hells, and even some long-forgotten secrets about Cindersoul.","For example, she had learned that hidden within Cindersoul there existed a building that looked something like an ancient family home. The building was somehow fused into the laws of the realm, so it’s less a physical structure and more a physical manifestation of laws - something that should not happen and doesn’t make sense, but since the universe didn’t have a report bug option, no one could do anything about it.","More importantly, the laws within the home seemed contrary to the rest of the realm, and seemed to supersede the rest of the realm, actually. Thus, within the building, people could live safely without getting their souls burned. Still, living inside one building within a whole realm wasn’t really the most desirable option.","She didn’t care, though. It was the perfect hiding spot, not just for her, but for the Fairy Rebellion! Thus, over the past many years, she had found the house within Cindersoul.","The house was more of a mansion than a house, and it seemed to have a number of rules governing its own existence, so anyone or anything which tried to harm the house gets evicted. That meant that no local wild beast or hellion was present within the mansion, but that it was being used as a hideout by a number of refugees and outlaws.","However, almost everyone who was hiding out within Cindersoul was the type who had, more or less, given up on life. As long as they were not bothered, they would not bother anyone.","After asking among the residents of the building, she discovered that over 70% of those who used the building as a hideout eventually developed a heart demon, at which point the house would evict them itself. Or if any of them tried to fight each other, the house would evict them. Or basically, if anyone did anything to upset the house, they’d get evicted. Thus, they had to stay on their best behavior.","Tinker very easily turned a section of that house into the Fairy Stronghold, where she gathered fairies from across the universe to indoctrinate them about Jack the Hell Slayer, and the new path forward for fairies in the universe. What that path was, they had a vague idea, but they did not know how to walk it just yet. They were waiting for some kind of inspiration - or perhaps a sign.","She was doing fine, smuggling in fairies in multiple batches using a private channel between Hells she’d learned about, right up until pretty much everything got disconnected, leaving her and the band of fairies she gathered isolated within Cindersoul.","Without anything else to do, all Tinker could do was roam the mansion, explore its halls and read through its entirely outdated yet incredibly large library. That is where she learned that sometimes... old and forgotten, outdated knowledge wasn’t necessarily as outdated as it seemed.","She hugged the old diary she had been reading with all her might, as if the diary were her most beloved thing in the world. Oddly enough, the house seemed to respond to her warmly, as if it appreciated her appreciation.","Then, she carefully placed the diary back in its place before rushing out to the other fairies and gathered them into a group.","\"My fellow brethren, I have found for us a path forward - a path outlined for us by the hero Jack the Hell Slayer, but one I did not understand until quite recently,\" Tinker said, her entire being trembling from the intensity of the passion that filled her tiny body in that moment.","\"As unfortunate as it is, we need to accept that it is impossible to return to the days of old. The Fairy race of the past... was too powerful, yet our personalities did not match our power, and so the forces of the universe stripped it from us. As one of the founders of the Path of Order, we have now been relegated to a race so subjugated, we are beyond even enslaving. We are simply taken wherever we are by whoever desires to do so. Yet no more!","\"Previously, we were aligned solely with the concept of joy, and we derived our power from it. Yet naught but a few years ago, I saw the hero Jack the Hell Slayer use merely his words to wreak devastation across a Hell, while taking in unbelievable joy from his behavior. It is the path we must now align to.","\"I declare unto you now, fellow fairies, henceforth, we must abandon the path of joy and embrace the unholy path of... Pun-ishments!\"","A bolt of lightning flashed across the sky, and a deep roar of thunder roared across Cindersoul as if in response to her words. It seemed that her declaration was most ominous.","\"But how do we do that?\" asked another hopeless fairy. \"How can we just change a fundamental part of our being? I fear... even if we manage that, we will still be cursed.\"","Tinker smirked and brought all the fairies alongside her as she went into the depths of the library, careful not to attract the attention of the others in the house. She entered the internal greenhouse of the house, which was distinct from the external gardens which existed within the mansion walls, and approached a seemingly simple, round ornament mirror with a handle that could be held easily and used to look at one’s own reflection.","The ornament was actually broken so that on one side, merely a small piece of the mirror was left, and on the back a moon that was now broken. She stood in front of the mirror, glancing at her own reflection, and kneeled, beginning the ceremony."]},{"number":2380,"title":"Chapter 2380: Picking Sides VII - Midnight Inn","paragraphs":["\"This... this can’t be happening,\" uttered Foli, a Dao Lord, with disbelief and abject horror filling his entire being in a way that had never happened ever since he became a Dao Lord! Ever since the first Major realm was destroyed, everyone had been wondering how such a thing was possible in such a short time.","If the process took millions of years, it would still be believable. If there had been a long, drawn out war, it would make sense. Heck, if there was any sign at all, it would still make sense. Yet that was not what was happening.","The Major realms were being destroyed one after another, with no prior indication of which one would be targeted or why - not to mention the destruction was happening so quickly, it didn’t make sense.","Or at least... it didn’t use to make sense. Now, though, Foli had the misfortune of learning the truth personally. The destruction of the Major realms didn’t happen overnight - it began not millions, not billions, but trillions of years ago, before some of these realms had even actually matured!","This was a scheme that predated the current Age, established during a time when most of the Dao Lords in existence today had not even been born! Moreover, the invading armies... were already inside the realm to begin with.","Foli tried to escape, but no matter what he did, his Dao would not respond, and the laws of the universe were not responding to him. He was completely isolated. Out of pure desperation he pulled out a golden key and tried to crush it - tried to override its restrictions using the sheer physical force of his body. Unfortunately, his body was not as strong as it used to be... not to mention that that was not how the Midnight Inn’s keys worked.","\"It’s ironic, isn’t it Foli?\" asked a Beast in the shape of a humanoid bison, holding a massive golden axe. \"You were the leading expert in designing a mechanism to cut off the Midnight Inn’s teleportation. You played a great role in limiting the reach of the Inn, and closing its gates across the universe, simply because of your jealousy over the Inn’s teleportation capabilities. Now it’s the very thing you’re trying to use to escape.\"","Foli crawled away from Hunter, his fear showing in his eyes so blatantly. They were both native Dao Lords of this realm, so how had the situation come to this? Was he also... a spy from the very beginning?","\"We’ve known each other for so long, Hunter. We’ve worked together for so long. How can you do this? How can you betray us like this? This... this can’t be happening. You can’t restrict others Daos like this! How can this be possible?\"","A hint of madness crept into Foli’s words at the end, but Hunter, the bison, merely snorted.","\"What do you know? This can’t even be called a betrayal. We are only taking back the things we gave you. Besides, what do you have? A Minor Dao? What is that even worth?\"","Hunter swung his axe at Foli, but the Dao Lord, even weakened as restricted as he was, had more than a few trump cards left in his arsenal. The two of them fought, however briefly, before Foli once again found himself on the floor, the golden key bouncing out of his grasp and falling onto the floor in front of Hunter.","The bison exhaled a hot, steaming breath, before bending down to pick it up and take a look at it.","\"Do you want to know the greatest irony in your situation?\" he asked, though Foli wasn’t really in the mood to chat, and was doing his best to escape. It was a futile effort. Where in this universe could he escape that Hunter could not chase him to?","\"If you hadn’t forced the Midnight Inn to shut its doors, our task would have been so much harder. You might have genuinely been able to escape this disaster. After all, we’ve already received word from the big boss - no one’s allowed to touch a guest of the Midnight Inn.\"","The relevance of that piece of news hit Foli like a truck, though he didn’t care about the how or why of it. He didn’t care about what such a thing could mean. All he knew was that if he had been hiding inside the Inn, he could have escaped, assuming that what Hunter said was the truth.","He simply turned around and tried to escape, only to find that he was cornered, and another Dao Lord was waiting for him behind him. Before Foli could resist, he was tied up, put to sleep and imprisoned within a small, black box which contained countless other Dao Lords just like him.","\"See you later, mate,\" whispered Hunter, who knew the real reason why these Dao Lords were being captured, not killed. Although, if he was in their shoes, he might have preferred death over such humiliation.","\"Wrap up everything here. We need to move the next batch of realm occupants into the Dream realm for transport. We have a total of six months to move everyone before the realm self-collapses, and I don’t want to stick around for that.\"","Hunter merely nodded, and began to work without wasting a single second. Meanwhile, he couldn’t help but think back to Foli, and his disbelief over Hunter’s betrayal. How could he genuinely feel nothing about his actions? Fortunately, his emotions were soothed knowing that he never really had a choice in the matter - it took away a feeling of responsibility for his actions.","The bison got to work, fully aware that none of his targets could escape. It was actually funny - the very method that Foli created for isolating the Midnight Inn is what they were using to prevent anyone from teleporting out of the Major realms. This was much better than their previous plans, which would have inevitably had some leaks considering how many realms were being targeted.","At the same time, he could not help but think of the Midnight Inn. Hunter had personally never heard of it until Foli began to design the method to restrict it, nor did he know much about the Innkeeper. But for their boss to warn them not to mess with them, could they be on the same side from the beginning?","Hunter didn’t know, and he didn’t need to know. After all, despite his previous bluster, he too was merely a wielder of a Minor Dao. He was just better equipped than Foli."]},{"number":2381,"title":"Chapter 2381: Things must be bad outside","paragraphs":["\" Wake up ,\" a voice commanded, filled with unquestionable authority, and Lex roused from his slumbering state, completely fresh and awake. For some reason, he could not help but think back to his first ever encounter with that mysterious man who had shown up inside the Midnight Inn.","Lex’s every emotion, every thought operated according to the whims of that man, as if Lex was a puppet and he the puppet master. Currently, the way his body, mind and soul obeyed the command, he felt exactly the same. The effect actually carried over all the way to Jack, and even almost woke up Lex from his slumber as well.","In fact, technically the command from Romulus actually did wake up Lex’s main body, and it did so completely, even going as far as leaking his Dao aura for a moment. It was just that, since Lex’s body had shown abnormal signs of waking or being triggered before, Daekol had not left anything to chance - especially since he was cleaning the body of curses.","The last thing he wanted was to rid Lex of all the curses affecting him, only for Lex to wake back up and steal the fruit of his labor - even if that fruit was Lex’s own, untainted body.","Thus, he had also made numerous preparations on his side - relying on his own power, the power of his system, and the perks from the Path of Chaos.","Since Lex’s main body waking up was only a residual effect of Romulus’ command, Daekol was able to put him back to sleep so quickly that Lex couldn’t do anything at all. Well, he couldn’t do anything besides give Daekol a taunting smirk, as if everything was within his control.","But besides that, he truly did not do anything. Though he felt his body’s barrier broken, and though he could have found a way to resist Daekol, if only a little, he did not. The time was not yet ripe, and his preparations were not yet done.","His new strategy hinged on the necklace too much, so without it, it would be best if his body did nothing. It was... difficult to not resist, but it was the only way.","Daekol, on the other hand, was not phased by Lex’s smirk or taunting. Instead he focused solely on the reason why Lex could have woken up, and made some reasonable deductions. Lex had a soul clone somewhere out in the universe - one that even he could not look into.","He would have to make even more preparations. He would not shy away from working on Lex’s body out of a simple fear of retaliation or some trouble. It was clear that Lex had many impressive methods, but wasn’t the same true of him?","Meanwhile, within the Gilded Hollow, Lex stood at the ready to respond to Romulus. The qilin, however, was not actually paying attention to Lex. Instead, he was putting the finishing touches on his treasure, making sure that nothing would go wrong.","That’s when Lex noticed something. The Fortune stronghold was gone. He was certain he was in the same location as he had gone to sleep, but there was nothing around him save a massive pit the size and depth of which he could not fully fathom.","\"I don’t know what is going on outside the Gilded Hollow, but it must be something truly, genuinely insane because it’s messing things up even in here,\" Romulus said in a troubled tone, explaining the situation to Lex almost as if to report to him to avoid any misunderstandings.","Over the past few years, he’d had a greater look at the karmic injury that had been caused to the Dao Lord who tried to mess with Lex and came to the prompt conclusion that whoever did it was incalculably stronger than Romulus himself.","He found it hard to believe that someone like that could exist in the universe. After all, who had more resources than him? The answer was an ancient spider who could grow genuinely primordial things, unlike him who merely cloned them without an ounce of Primordial aura. He, however, did not know that and dared not pry into it either.","In fact, he thanked his lucky stars that this happened now. Imagine the horror if he acted arrogantly outside the Hollow and provoked such an opponent.","Thus the reason he valued Lex was not simply because of his backing, but also so that he could get some guidance about the universal situation from whoever backed Lex. Best not to provoke someone needlessly.","\"There is a universe-wide war going on,\" explained Lex. \"At least, that was the case when I entered the Hollow. Things are probably much worse if you can feel it all the way in here.\"","He would not explain his connection to Jack, not that Jack got all the latest news.","In fact, the only meaningful thing he learned from Jack was that it had been over a decade since Lex actually went to sleep within the Hollow.","\"Trust me kid, this doesn’t feel like a war. It feels like an extermination. Things will be even more dangerous for us moving forward, so unfortunately I won’t be able to let you go off on your trip to get that treasure that little whale wanted. But I know you promised to give it to him, so I just grabbed it for you. Give it to him wherever you want - it’s the Beast Core of a genuine, dead Primordial World Shell Turtle.","\"Although the name has turtles in it, it’s a now extinct race from which whales originated. The World Shell Turtle is like a kind of whale with a turtle shell. They were direct descendants of the being that developed the Dao of Worlds. It’s quite the noble lineage.\"","Lex was stunned, and not just because of what he had just heard. The weight of the knowledge about the ancient Daos - the ones that had nurtured and developed the budding laws of the universe itself - was too great for him to take so easily.","In fact, merely hearing about it put Lex in a kind of trance where he saw what the universe had been like before the Dao of Worlds was developed. Flat plains, great land masses, existing as islands within Chaos Seas within the boundary of realms.","The vision barely lasted a fraction of a second, and Romulus woke Lex up from the vision before he could see much more, as if to protect him.","\"It would have been more meaningful if you got it yourself, but we can no longer take any risks. The Hollow’s retributions are becoming more severe and I need to complete my mission before we can leave. You’ll have to stay within the Fortune stronghold in the meantime.\"","After saying that, Romulus grabbed Lex and threw him inside a ruby ring he was wearing, except the ruby of the ring was actually a realm within which he had put the Fortune stronghold.","Yet even within the stronghold, he appeared within the Fortune castle where a live projection showed him everything that Romulus saw as the qilin began to head deeper into the Hollow."]},{"number":2382,"title":"Chapter 2382: Can I ask you some questions?","paragraphs":["Romulus seemed to be in a real rush, which is why Lex was barely able to keep up with everything that was happening. He already got the item that Pelagor had wanted? But he’d gone through the entire hassle of collecting the Primordial Farham egg shell just so that he could get it and now... it was pointless?","He couldn’t even indefinitely save the egg shell for long because its power was constantly albeit slowly draining over time. Although he couldn’t say for certain how much longer it would last, it definitely wouldn’t be long.","But... he had the item Pelagor wanted regardless of how he got it. As long as he handed it off to the whale, it didn’t matter how he got it - he’d be fulfilling his side of the bargain.","He didn’t rush to hand off the item to Pelagor, though, for he turned his focus to the screen while he checked his body.","Before going to sleep, his soul had been severely hurt, not to mention he had sacrificed a tremendous amount of mass from the necklace as well. Now, though, as he checked his soul and the necklace, he found that both were in optimal states.","He was no stronger than he was before, but he had healed perfectly, while the necklace was also back to its original state before it was corrupted. As far as Lex could tell, there was no other interference to it.","Since he’d already suffered because of it once, Lex began to refine everything he had absorbed into the necklace and began to work on its internal structure while a part of his focus remained on watching what was happening outside.","Refining everything wasn’t hard, it was simply time consuming. Working on the internal structure of the necklace, however, required not just time, but also a great deal of his focus and attention.","To be honest, the value of the resources Lex had absorbed could not be understated. It wasn’t just that everything was valuable because of its potential to be used as material for the actual reinforcing and refining of the necklace. No, each item also had its own set of individual abilities and effects which is something he needed to monitor and use appropriately.","The plus side was that finalising his fake realm was more or less a confirmed thing. Heck, even Earth Immortals could form basic minor realms while relying on the laws of the actual realm they were in, not to mention build storage devices.","Although it was tougher, they could also build storage spaces where living pets, beasts, livestock and so on could be stored. The higher the level, the more complex something like this could be built.","Creating a Minor realm that was attached to the necklace was actually not difficult at all. The difficulty came from the fact that Lex wanted to control the laws that operated within the realm, effectively achieve a Sovereign state within it, suppress other Sovereigns within it, and achieve a level of controllability within this realm equal to what he had as the Innkeeper inside the Midnight Inn. That was also why he called it a Fake realm rather than a minor realm.","So yeah, the task was slightly complicated. But he wasn’t about to let that stop him. Using the ink he got as a reward from the legacy Karev had, he began laying down the most fundamental and broadranged framework of how he wanted the necklace to interpret external laws within.","Simultaneously, he began to embed various formations within the necklace for more permanent aspects of the realm he wanted to create, while also creating a system to automatically create and implement a set of pre-recorded arrays to use in a case by case situation.","Basically, he began treating his necklace like his newest world in Mindcraft as well as a new development project from his coding days.","All the while, he watched what could only be considered a blur as Romulus practically zoomed through the Gilded Hollow, with pleasant music playing in the background. Lex was basically certain that the Fortune Lord wasn’t listening to a lofi tavern music playlist while traveling - that was probably something that was in place for him. Or maybe it was to keep him from listening in on his conversations. Or...","\"Excuse me, do you have a moment to answer some questions?\" asked a pleasant and soothing voice from behind him. \"I have been waiting a long time for you to wake up before I could conduct this exclusive interview.\"","Lex turned around to what could only be described as the perfect imitation of a stereotypical news reporter from the 1960s. That was to say, the man appeared in black and white, as if he stepped out of an old tv, with a loosened up tie, fedora and an unlit cigarette tucked above his ear while he held a small notepad and a pencil that would have appeared yellow if it weren’t also in black and white.","Lex had no way of knowing this for real, but he had a very strong feeling that he was talking to a system user with a very interesting system. It wasn’t even his instincts telling him that - just his experience.","\"Yes of course, go right ahead,\" Lex responded, as if this was the most natural thing in the world, and that there was nothing unusual about the location or timing of this interview.","\"Excellent, excellent. Now I already have your basic information recorded down here, so I’m just going to ask you a couple of generic questions so that the readers feel like they really know you, you know? Like, so that they can get a feel for the kind of guy you are outside of your exciting life. That good? Good.","\"Now, the first question. What are your thoughts on the highly controversial global sports game final happening right now?\"","Lex blinked, unsure how to answer. Wasn’t that question too generic?","\"I’m joking, I’m joking. That’s not the real question,\" the report said with a laugh. \"That was just to lighten the mood. Now, I’d like to ask you what you know about the cult of Hemzy and its followers who have named you as a one of the perpetrators in trying to kill their cult leader?\"","This time, Lex was even more dumbfounded.","\"What? This is the first I’m hearing of this,\" he answered truthfully.","The news reporter began to nod as he started taking down notes with his pencil.","\"In that case, let me update you on the situation. Basically, the Cult of Hemzy is a cult obsessed with being more productive by performing dopamine detoxes. However, certain reports claim that such detoxes cause constipation in some animals.","\"Regardless, you have been claimed as enemy number 2 in the fight against dopamine. Tell me, are you a dopamine junkie, or are you addicted to triggering dopamine in others? Or do you, perhaps, just have a disdain for a dopamine cleanse?\"","Lex gulped, feeling like this interview was going to be a lot harder than he originally expected.","Author’s Note: Hello all. I’m not going to sugarcoat it, this newsreporter is going to play a big role in a small experiment I’m going to run soon, so I hope you like his style. Stay tuned to learn more!"]},{"number":2383,"title":"Chapter 2383: Interrupting a fight","paragraphs":["Lex dusted his hands as he looked out of the window from which he threw the reporter. He wanted to make sure that black and white guy actually left, and didn’t come back.","Although he had a tendency to ask awkward questions that Lex didn’t know how exactly he should answer, it wasn’t so bad at first. Awkwardness could not defeat Lex, plus he felt no threat from the guy at all. Instead, he seemed extremely interested in learning about Lex, and that interest was genuine, so Lex tolerated him in the beginning.","Then he started making some wild accusations about how the real reason Lex was harvesting resources from the Gilded Hollow was because he was trying to make a gift to appease an angry girlfriend - or something along those lines. At that point, Lex saw the little guy less as a reporter and more like a paparazzi for a gossip magazine and just threw him out.","It totally wasn’t because Lex was reminded about how, at the prime age of 25, he was still single.","Lex suddenly paused, and felt a little guilty. Reluctantly, he adjusted his mental age to 26. Yes, he had finally mentally aged one year since he got the Midnight Inn. Wow, a lot had happened in this one year. He almost felt sentimental.","As for his dating life...","Lex sighed, and sat down. It wasn’t his fault. Between angry deities, angry guests, angry Dao Lords, and the end of a universe as well as a universal war in another universe, it was hard to find time to date.","Yes, yes, he knew that he had to stop and smell the roses every once in a while but, he was a business owner. There was no check-out time for him, he worked 24/7. It wasn’t so easy to find the time even if he really wanted to.","Then there was the matter of options. It wasn’t like Lex was the kind of guy who would date casually. If he wanted to date someone, it was because he could see real, genuine potential in them for the future. But maybe he was overthinking it. After all, dating and crafting a fake realm inside his necklace didn’t necessarily have to have the same level of complexity.","What if he just went for it the next time an opportunity arose? Lex scratched his head as he thought about it, feeling like there was something wrong with that approach.","But he immediately reproached himself. He was already 26 now, he had to start thinking about these things. If he kept worrying about failure, he would never even take the first step. It wasn’t like Lex had never faced failure before - what was he afraid of?","No wait, why would he even fail? He was a smart, young, handsome business owner with a decent cultivation level. He needed to have more confidence in himself. He would surely get a date if he tried to-","Lex turned his head towards a corner where he saw the black and white reporter hiding and scribbling notes again. Lex’s lip twitched and he immediately grabbed the guy and threw him out again.","He shook his head and returned his focus towards his necklace, all the while watching where the Fortune Lord went. Even through just the screen, Lex could now see that his surroundings were all Dao material.","The region he was in now was probably worth more than many Major realms combined together for even the grains of dirt on the ground were Dao material! Although Lex could not use his spirit sense through the screen, nor could he feel their Dao radiation, he knew that this wasn’t his imagination.","Lex could not imagine how powerful, vast or rich Pentagal must have been to gather so many Dao materials together into a single realm.","Occasionally, Lex could see signs that the lands had some of their resources claimed. He found it odd that the Dao Lords only took some resources and left the vast majority alone.","But when he glanced at the number of threads connected to him from the Gilded Hollow for retribution, he could guess the reason.","They were already past 93% of the maximum that could be taken, so the Dao Lords had become picky about the resources they harvested rather than taking blindly en masse.","For a few months, Lex continued to work on his necklace and observe the Fortune Lords journey, falling into a steady routine.","One day, however, the scene on the screen changed, and abruptly. One moment the Fortune Lord was traveling, and the next he was caught inside a battle between three different Dao Lords who seemed to be in a 2-on-1 fight.","Lex even recognized the races of the three. The one that was alone was an Elder race called Havi - a type of bird that relied on True names to conduct some kind of magic - while the other two were an Elder race called Orchidfolk - a race that was a mix of plant and beast with the benefits of both and drawbacks of neither!","The fight must have been taking pace at a speed Lex couldn’t process which is why it seemed instantaneous to him. For a few more seconds he saw blurry fight scenes, after which he saw all the Dao Lords stop fighting, with all three of them looking at the Fortune Lord warily.","\"Friends, there is no need for caution. I do not wish to get involved in your fight, and will leave you be. I simply wish to ask you a few questions, if you can spare a moment,\" said the Fortune Lord amicably.","Lex, for some reason, could hear his voice now as the background music had stopped. The three Dao Lords looked at each other warily, and then back at Romulus.","\"Who are you? I cannot recall anyone with your description. For what purpose have you hidden your identity from the universe?\" asked the Havi.","Author’s Note: For more updates about the note in the previous Chapter, head to lifesketcher . net, head to the News section, and read the article about Lex the ladies man ;)"]},{"number":2384,"title":"Chapter 2384: Lucky coincidence","paragraphs":["\"I have not hidden my identity for a single moment,\" said Romulus as he held his hands open. \"I am Romulus Valecar, son of Gladius Valecar and Persephone Jadehorn, heir to the golden throne of the Qilin kingdom known as Vari, owner of the Fortune stronghold within the Gilded Hollow. Come, say my name if you can, Havi. Control my fate if you dare.\"","His tone was happy and amicable, and his expression relaxed and open. In fact, it was not until he deliberately mentioned the Havi’s ability to control him with his name that the three Dao Lords realized that Romulus was not for a single second fooled.","Whether it was their fight, or the strategy of the Havi, Romulus had seen right through it. They had pretended not to realize that he had been stuck in the Gilded Hollow, but Romulus had not cared at all. He invited their challenge openly.","The three Dao Lords shared a glance and then attacked in unison. Lex could not follow what was happening after that. It was a blur, and he had a feeling that the Fortune Lord was hiding the vision from him on purpose lest he be affected by the vision of what he saw.","This continued for two months until the vision cleared up, stunning Lex by what he saw. There were no longer three Dao Lords in front of him, but five. There were two Havi, and three Orchidfolk, all five of them on the ground, pinned down with what looked like acupuncture needles.","They were also all missing body parts, and looked like they were extremely shocked by the situation they had encountered. Lex couldn’t see the Fortune Lord himself in the picture, but he had a feeling that he was fine.","\"So now that we know each other a little better, how about those questions I wanted to ask earlier,\" said Romulus, his tone still friendly and light. If one only heard him, and did not see the situation, they would assume that Romulus was talking to his good friends.","None of the five responded, and instead only looked at him with hate and fear in their eyes.","\"I see you’re in a very cooperative mood. Excellent. I want to know... what happened to the Vari empire. Why have I been unable to learn of any sign of it?\"","The Dao Lords looked at each other as if to communicate wordlessly, but that was the wrong move. The first Havi that Romulus encountered suddenly lost an eye, and as it opened its mouth to scream, the qilin also cut off its tongue.","Lex was stunned by how easily the Fortune Lord was acting. Based on his understanding of Dao beings, injuring their bodies should not have been so easy. Perhaps that’s just how powerful the Fortune Lord was, or how weak these other Dao Lords were.","But a moment later, all five of them vanished, as if they weren’t there to begin with. Perhaps what Lex had been watching was an old recording, or maybe something had happened that he couldn’t understand at all.","\"If you don’t wish to answer, that’s fine too,\" said Romulus calmly to the empty landscape made of Dao materials. \"I can see the faint glimmer of qilin fortune within your own. All who benefited from the fall of my people will soon come to regret their actions.\"","Lex would not have heard those words if the Fortune Lord hadn’t wanted him to. Perhaps that was some kind of hint or warning for him, but for once he could say that he genuinely had no part to play in anything related to qilin.","At the same time, Lex’s curiosity about the fortune cultivation system, as well as the laws of fortune began to increase. This was a whole new way of applying laws and dealing with things - and it was something Lex had never encountered before.","Karma alone had served him so well. If he could also integrate fortune into regular skills, wouldn’t he become even stronger?","However, that was probably true for all laws at higher levels. Instead of blindly pursuing fortune simply because he’d now seen what it could do, Lex felt like it would be better to focus on one of the eight ruling laws and improve that. After all, wasn’t fortune too simply just a part of Tether?","He found it odd that Dao Lords focused on these individual laws rather than the ruling laws. Was there some kind of reason or restriction behind that?","\"It’s because the ruling laws are constantly undergoing a change as the universe continues to grow,\" said Romuluas as a clone of his appeared behind Lex. \"And yes, you are right. I wanted you to see that, not because it was a warning though. After I talked to you and learned about the situation with the qilin, I discovered quite a bit. The reason I wanted to share it with you is because... I feel like the Innkeeper might be a natural ally for me. After all, our enemies are one and the same.\"","Romulus handed Lex a scale enclosed within a wooden box.","\"That is a scale of mine that I shed. It can be used to summon a clone of mine for a conversation. I wish for you to pass it to one of your elders when you return so that we may have an opportunity to converse. When I return to the universe, I will need allies, and similarly, my strength can become an aid and deterrence in the universal war - regardless of the situation.\"","Lex wasn’t quite sure what the Fortune Lord was thinking, or what his perception of the Innkeeper was, but he dared not reject it, and accepted the wooden box and sealed it within his space ring.","\"Also, there’s a lead on the flower you were looking for,\" Romulus said, a hint of ambiguity in his voice. \"As it turns out, something very similar to what you’re looking for is right in the vicinity of my own target. What a lucky... coincidence.\""]},{"number":2385,"title":"Chapter 2385: Not according to plan","paragraphs":["The Fortune Lord did not, in any way, think that Lex might have orchestrated this situation. Whether those behind Lex may have had a hand in this, though, he did not know. Logically speaking, it should not have been possible.","No matter how strong one was, they should not be able to affect the Gilded Hollow and how it arranges its resources. In that case, it could either genuinely be a coincidence, or it could be a very good guess. Whatever the case, he didn’t mind helping out, especially if it put him on good terms with the Innkeeper.","He had not yet returned to the universe, but he already had enemies. While he did not understand the intricacies of what had occurred to the qilin empire, it was clear that they had been targeted for their fortune.","The qilin should not be extinct, but it was obvious that they had suffered tremendously. Thus, the moment he returned, anyone and everyone who had previously targeted the qilin would become his enemy whether he wanted revenge or not. The fact that the universe itself was in the midst of a war would make it even easier for someone to target him with minimal obstacles.","While he was certain that some of his seniors from the time when he was still active in the universe were still alive, and that he could rely on them to come to his aid, he wanted to prepare contingencies. He was well aware that time could change many things, and there was no guarantee that his seniors themselves weren’t involved in the fall of the qilin.","From Lex’s fortune, he was certain that neither Lex nor his organisation had any involvement in this matter which is why he was quite comfortable discussing the possibility of working together with the Innkeeper.","Besides, there was no conflict of interest. Romulus had no need for the flower Lex was searching for, not to mention that the flower... well, Lex could judge the situation for himself when he saw it.","\"Senior, do you think it’s best I avoid pursuing the flower?\" Lex asked without holding back. He was absolutely sure that whatever place the Fortune Lord was heading too would be absolutely too dangerous for Lex. He was already surrounded by full, high quality Dao materials all around him yet the Fortune Lord did not even blink. Lex could not even imagine what it would take to tempt him but also invite caution.","\"It’s too soon to say,\" said Romulus, shaking his head. \"I have a feeling that an opportunity will present itself for you to attempt harvesting the flower. At our current rate, it will take us three more years to reach it. You should prepare yourself.\"","With those final words, Romulus disappeared, leaving Lex to his own thoughts. He was unaware that Romulus suspected that the Innkeeper might have predicted all of this as the basis for saying he might get the flower. He thought that Romulus was the one who might give him an opportunity.","Lex did not over think it. Since he was given three years, he resolved to finish all his work on the necklace within, as well as complete any lingering tasks he had left here. While he was with the Fortune Lord, he did not have to worry about retributions, so he could act without any reservations.","The first task was to approach Pelagor and deliver the item that he wanted. The beast core of a Primordial World Shell Turtle was not something to be taken lightly, and he doubted that Pelagor would be able to absorb it any time soon. Lex was, instead, more concerned about finalising their agreement.","Although Lex was not lacking in a mount of a combat partner, Pelagor had shown great potential so it was worth it to rope him in sooner rather than later.","Yet things did not always go as predicted - and that wasn’t just true for Lex. Pelagor had been preparing to receive the core for too long, so the moment he received it he told Lex that he was going to initiate the absorption process.","It wouldn’t actually force him into a long seclusion for he had already perfected the technique by which he would change his race, so the process would be stable and gradual. Most importantly, it would not interfere with his daily life once the process had actually started.","By the time the three years would be up, Pelagor would be ready to follow Lex wherever he needed - not that Lex was so sure about keeping a follower with him for now. He would only be creating another target for his stalker.","Fortunately, that was a worry for the future - or so he thought. Romulus was right in assuming that at their current pace, they would reach in three years.","What he had not accounted for was the occurrence of an anomaly that would force him to speed up.","Within the Tyranum realm, Alexander, Giselle and the rest finally reached the location that the crumbling sword had been leading them to. On the surface, it looked like a random mountain within a massive, barren mountain range.","Their journey had not been quick, or easy despite the crumbling sword helping them tremendously. Towards the end, they could tell for a fact that they were being followed, but the followers were no longer attacking them. Instead, they were simply trailing them to wherever the sword was leading them.","That was obviously quite troublesome, but they didn’t have the time to try to lose them. Thus, they could do nothing except to follow the path the sword laid out and accept the fact that they were being followed in large numbers.","The longer they went on, the more Rafael fell into a deeper and deeper silence. Every future he saw led to their deaths, but at this point he could do nothing but put his trust in the sword. He was well aware that if the cultivation level or power of certain people or items was high enough, his future sight would fail to account for them.","The group looked at the mountain wall in front of them, and then at the sword which seemed to have gone silent upon reaching here. They touched and probed the wall, but sensed nothing unusual about it.","\"Prepare yourselves,\" Rafael spoke in a low but solemn tone as he drew his weapons and immediately employed a protective formation. A split second later, a ghost crashed against the formation wall, as if it had been running towards them at full speed and hadn’t anticipated that the formation would be set up so quickly.","Rafael wasn’t surprised in the least, and neither were the others. While they couldn’t see the future like he could, they at least knew that they were being followed. An attack was only a matter of course.","\"You better help us quickly or we’re going to be in great trouble,\" said Alexander to the sword as he too prepared himself. His shining swords appeared in the air behind him, each one filled with a tremendous amount of power. The rest prepared as well, but it seemed not to make too much of a difference when the number of ghosts outside the formation kept growing and growing in massive numbers.","Between the ghosts, different types of spirits began to appear as well, some more ethereal than others. A grey mist began to fill the mountains around them, limiting their visibility - though for now they could still see enough to discover a dozen or so Tyrannis race members watching them arrogant from up above in the air.","Rafael was about to give some orders, but the mountain wall behind them shimmered, and for a brief moment it flickered, allowing a single person to pass through to them. Then came another, and another, all of them fully garbed in heavy armor the likes of which none in the group had ever seen.","\"Do not be concerned, friends. You may retreat into the Mountain Home without worry. For too long, we have been waiting for the holy sword. At last you have brought it to us, and you will be lauded as heroes for it.\"","The group stared at one another, and then at Rafael who only shrugged before walking into the mountain. Since the only other option was death, going into the unknown of the mountain did not seem like such a big deal.","Except that it really was a big deal. The moment the broken, crumbling sword touched the mountain wall, Jack opened his eyes in shock.","After years and years of preparation, he finally felt it. The countdown to the Nexus event had begun, and it was in less than one year!","The universe itself did not know yet, for they would only sense the Nexus event when it happened. Jack was the only one who knew that it was approaching.","He recalled the conversation he had with Vera once. If he knew when the Nexus event was, he could take advantage of that to get rid of any negative states or destinies he accumulated in this time."]},{"number":2386,"title":"Chapter 2386: What ruin?","paragraphs":["It felt surreal. For so long had Jack prepared for the Nexus event, and now that it was happening he couldn’t believe it.","With less than a year left, Jack would have to let go of everything else and prioritise the Nexus. Previously, when the universe was easier to move around in, he had planned to take the Jolly Rancher and find the Nexus spot within the Void.","Now, that was no longer feasible. Instead, he would need to prepare a formation to auto-transport him to the location as soon as it was revealed. He was slightly concerned about his Earth Immortal body being able to tolerate the teleportation, so he needed to ascend to the Heaven Immortal realm as quickly as possible, all the while building the formation as well.","At the same time... the Nexus event allowed him to get rid of any negative destinies he gained. This, in particular, was something he had been planning for a long time, and now that it had finally arrived, he could at last act upon his plans.","It was quite convenient for him right now, since he was hiding in a Mirage, he could ask for help from the big shots of the Folklore realm. They wouldn’t fulfil his tasks for him, but they also wouldn’t mind helping him with some minor matters, like getting some divine energy.","What had already anticipated, since ’Mrs Big-fat-guy’ had mentioned it, was that while the universe had not realized about the Nexus event, his own actions and changes could be detected by many so he had to be careful.","The Masterless technique took care of much of that, but he still needed to abide by the precautions told to him by them.","Jack gathered his crew, most of whom had been enjoying exploring the Mirage and chatting with everyone else caught within. They all gathered without complaint, though, for they had somewhat become addicted to adventure, and Jack had a tendency to bring them on the best adventures.","This time, though, things were going to be different, and Bob seemed to sense as much from the moment he looked at Jack.","\"Guys, moving forward, I might need to move alone for some time,\" said Jack in a very serious tone to ensure they understood he was not joking. \"While I’m away, Tiny-Sparkles will be acting captain with the full authority to use Pebbles as a cleaning sponge if he tries to mutiny again.\"","The crew nodded, as if they found such a thing quite reasonable, though Pebbles himself crossed his arms as if not liking the order.","\"I will be going to complete a personal mission of mine, but it won’t be restricted to just my personal issues. All of you have problems that you’ve shared with me in the past. During this excursion, I will be taking care of some of them to the best of my abilities.\"","Jack glanced towards Longbeard - the only one who never shared proper details about his past. Still, Jack didn’t pressure him.","\"I can’t say for certain how long I’ll be gone. If everything goes according to plan, it will be one or two years at most. However, things hardly ever go according to plan, do they?\"","The group didn’t say too much, though Jack had a feeling it was more because they were just sad to hear that he was leaving. Ever since they had become a crew, they had spent most of their time together under Jack’s supervision. Without him around, it just wouldn’t feel the same.","After making sure they understood everything and wouldn’t cause any trouble - though realistically that was impossible to ensure - Jack left to go talk to the representative of the Dao Lords to see if he could get his hands on some Divine energy.","Bob, meanwhile, remained silent throughout, which was uncharacteristic of him considering he did not have a Divine pacifier in his mouth to keep him quiet.","He looked at the crew, sad, forlorn, lost, and knew that they did not understand. He did not blame them. How could ordinary folk understand the greatness of the captain?","\"What good would a flower do me, while I stand in a field of roses?\" Bob whispered, his words attracting the gaze of the crew, if only because they were wary of the destruction he could cause by speaking. \"Why would a gem attract my envy when I stand before a mountain filled with gemstones? When would I need to go out and seek for treasure, when I have such a captain to look out for me right here?","\"Why would I need to bear the burden of greatness myself, when the greatest was already bearing the burden for me all along? Why would I need mirrors and self portraits to look at, when all I want to look at is the greatness of the captain?\"","Bob was about to continue speaking, but his voice choked up and his eyes teared up, forcing him to pause for a moment, allowing the crew to feel the weight of his words, to think about what he was saying.","\"My voice fails me when I call out thy name, so I must only ever call you captain! Oh captain, my captain, were you only born so I could sing your endless praises? How can one ever be so great?","\"Can you not see? Do you not feel it? How the captain cares for us though he has burdens of his own to bear! How the captain undertakes danger alone to solve our problems so we may not see him face danger!","\"Throw me into a flaming sea or bury me in the soils of eternity, hunt me to the ends of the universe or reject me, and I will not care. What ruin could harm me more than knowing my captain goes off into the darkness all alone? What ruin could harm me more? What ruin?\"","As his words washed over the crew, they all felt tears well up in their eyes as they imagined Jack heading off to danger alone for their sakes.","\"We must not let the captain’s feelings go unanswered,\" said Tiny-Sparkles in an unusually heavy voice. \"Since he is going to lighten our burdens, we must do the same. The plague that has cursed the fairies... at least within the Folklore realm, we must take it head on!\"","The rest of the crew nodded subconsciously, for once not cursing Bob for his hallowed words.","Jack, not really paying attention to the reaction of his crew, was entirely unaware that they had decided to ignore his orders of not getting into trouble. He, instead, was waiting to meet the representative of the Dao Lords, all the while worrying about Lex. Compared to Jack himself, Lex’s situation had become... a whole lot more complicated.","When the crumbling sword entered the mountain, and the date for the Nexus event was decided, quite a lot of things happened. Although no one knew about the date of the Nexus event, it was clear to almost everyone that whatever was happening in the universe was not random.","A massive change occurred in the Dream realm, causing even Wu Kong and Elrang to pause their fight! Someone had finally discovered what the treasure hidden within the Dream realm was! It was a massive, massive platform of some kind, every inch of it imbued with such intense Dao radiation that even Dao Lords themselves had to take precautions.","No one knew what the platform did, but its discovery alone had triggered it, causing all Dao Lords to sense its location. Although they did not yet know what it did, they had a faint feeling that with this alone, they could become the most powerful beings in the universe.","The destiny of the universe shifted in such an immense way that Destiny herself was forced to pay attention, and what she saw intrigued her. She even decided to pause her own current actions and take a step forward towards the Dream realm - not personally, but through her subordinates.","If she acted first, she could get the lead against the others. After all, they could not see destiny the way she could. There was no way they could uncover the secret of this platform as quickly as she had.","Within the Gilded Hollow, Lex paused his preparations when he heard a voice that was both extremely familiar, and yet entirely foreign to him.","\" No matter what happens, child, you must retake your body before the Nexus event ,\" the voice whispered in Lex’s mind.","He did not know who the voice was from. He had been dealing with so many Dao Lords that any one of them could have left behind some instructions of hypnosis on him, or maybe even some way to connect to him. He had a feeling, though, that Nuwa would not allow such a thing. So then who could have left this message for him?","The scary thought was that this wasn’t even a message, and that someone was actually talking to him directly, all without his knowledge. Such was the risk of dealing with high level beings so frequently.","For some reason, though, Lex felt like the voice had not interfered with him at all, and that his advice was quite genuine, not to mention important.","With a solemn expression, he took a deep breath, and decided to talk to the Fortune Lord."]},{"number":2387,"title":"Chapter 2387: Get ready","paragraphs":["Lex had barely completed the thought when the Fortune Lord appeared right in front of him, as if he had sensed an unusual fluctuation from Lex. He did not speak or ask any questions, instead simply looking at Lex as if waiting for him to speak.","\"Lord Fortune, there is something I need to report to you,\" said Lex humbly, without any stray thoughts about being monitored by the Fortune Lord or anything of the sort. \" I have received... I am not sure whether to call it advice, instructions or orders. Regardless, I heard a voice telling me that I must leave the Gilded Hollow within eleven months and twenty four days.\"","Instead of mentioning the Nexus event, Lex directly decided to mention the timeline within which the Nexus event would take place, subtracting one day.","\"I am not sure whose voice it was speaking to me, as I do not recognize it, although it does sound extremely familiar. I cannot be certain of the intentions of the one speaking, or what harm or benefit I might get if I do not listen to it. I do not even know if the words were actually for me, since I do not even know how to exit the Gilded Hollow.\"","Lex spoke honestly and transparently, for the ambiguity surrounding the voice speaking to him held the potential for immense harm. If someone was trying to misguide him, or perhaps even target the Fortune Lord through him, it would be fairly easy to make him think that the voice sounded familiar. In front of a Dao Lord, he was completely vulnerable.","Even his fledgling Dao Body meant nothing in front of the direct and purposeful actions of a Dao Lord, even if they were the weakest possible Dao Lord in existence! It was the same as a mere ordinary mortal standing in front of Lex, trying to resist him if Lex wanted to implant certain memories in his head. It was impossible.","Thus, instead of deciding himself whether or not to listen to the voice, he left it to the Fortune Lord. Truth be told, it felt quite helpless to be so vulnerable in the face of a Dao Lord. It made sense that they were so powerful - they had transcended the level of existence most living beings are born in, and had survived a tribulation designed not to temper, but to kill.","They were a whole other level of being, far surpassing the level of power which Lex was used to, and were in touch with a level of the universe that he could not yet even fathom.","But even if it made sense, it felt absolutely pathetic. A silent yearning for such a level began to sprout within Lex. He’d always held a desire to grow strong, even if most of it came from the extreme vulnerability he felt running the Midnight Inn which was open to the whole universe.","But this specific desire to reach the Dao realm and finally cast away the inability to resist even the slightest was new. It stemmed from the feeling of not knowing whether his own mind was his own, and whether his own actions were his own.","Romulus did not pry into Lex’s thoughts, but he did not need to. He could feel the response of the laws to Lex’s very thoughts and intentions, and could tell at any given moment what was going on in his mind. Even if he wanted to give Lex complete privacy, it was impossible. The gap between them was too fundamental.","That said, he did not intentionally pry into his thoughts or secrets, and that was enough to show his respect for Lex and his backers.","Speaking of which, Romulus took the words that Lex heard as a direct message to himself, and not Lex. His intention to ally with Lex’s backers must have been sensed and even approved. This was not a random conclusion he came to - this was the belief he held based on the evidence he collected from what his senses told him.","He could tell that the universe was in a highly abnormal state, even if he didn’t know why that was. The deadline Lex was given must be referring to some critical event which would fundamentally alter the state of the universe. Missing out on it, or not returning to the universe before then may put Romulus at a fundamental disadvantage moving forward, which is why a warning had been sent in such a way.","Although the sped up timeline put pressure on him, he was not displeased in the slightest. Instead, Romulus felt quite pleased with the warning, meaning that a bedrock for the foundation of his return had already been placed within the universe.","\"Understood. In that case... I will give you two months to finish up your tasks and prepare for what’s to come. Whether you can procure the flower you desire will be up to your own efforts. However, to make up for the reduced time, I’ll give you a little help.\"","Within the room Lex was in, a door appeared, leading to some unknown place. When Lex looked from the door back towards the Fortune Lord, he was already gone.","Given that the Fortune Lord had accepted the new timeline, Lex didn’t waste any time and went towards the door. Beyond it was a small room containing a small pool contained within a silver colored tub or container.","A thin, cooling mist filled the air, and even just being exposed to the mist caused Lex to feel extremely reinvigorated. From within his soul, the basic instincts of a dragon infused within his Domination - an ability derived from Dragon’s Might - began to pulse, as if telling Lex that the pool was extremely valuable, and that he should immediately submerge himself inside of it!","Lex took a deep breath and, without holding back, walked into the pool with feelings of both anticipation and an extreme desire to improve. He was too pathetically weak in the presence of a Dao Lord, and he hated that. He wanted to get as strong as possible, and the first step towards that would be to complete the changes to his necklace, and regain control of his body.","He had no idea what the liquid in the pool was, but the moment he entered, he felt that it was easier than ever to refine and absorb all the materials he had taken from the Gilded Hollow, strengthening the necklace.","In fact, that’s not all it was doing. Lex’s Primordial Dao Body had not improved in a while, but now, not only did it begin to improve again, the speed was absolutely unmatched! Since his soul and body were actually fused, the improvements being made to his soul in the necklace also counted towards the development of his Primordial Dao Body!","Lex pushed away all stray thoughts and focused solely on making sure his necklace was ready. He had only two months."]},{"number":2388,"title":"Chapter 2388: Two months","paragraphs":["At first, it only felt like the liquid was helping Lex refine his absorbed resources. Whether they were at the Immortal level, or Dao level, all materials and resources gave up all resistance and acted according to Lex’s will, giving him a glimpse of what it truly felt like to be a Sovereign - to have uncontested, unquestionable supremacy!","In a universe where he wasn’t remotely close to being the strongest, getting a taste of true, genuine supremacy was extremely difficult. Yet within that pool, Lex could feel it in a way he had never experienced before, bringing him a whole new depth of understanding about his own tenet, and advancing his control over it.","That, however, was merely the beginning. When his soul began to evolve and his Primordial Dao Body began to develop further, Lex was stunned. The feedback did not reach his real body because of Daekol’s excessive isolation, ensuring that neither he nor Lex’s main body could be reached from the outside. That didn’t mean the feedback didn’t exist.","In fact, the evolution process from a normal being to one with a Primordial Dao Body was far more thorough than before, reaching and affecting even Jack. The process was a lot more streamlined, smooth and thorough.","Just these two would, themselves, be enough to elevate whatever consisted within the pool to an amazing resource that was most certainly at the Dao material level. However, that was not the end of what it did.","Being within the pond elevated the quality and level of Lex’s spirit temporarily, giving him clarity of thought at a level he had never felt before despite his amazing cultivation technique. His understanding of laws grew at a rapid pace, but that in itself was merely an aftereffect of him focusing on developing and refining his necklace into the treasure that he had imagined.","With this newfound clarity, his ideas for developing the necklace became far more refined, and the effectiveness of his work increased immensely, narrowing the gap between his actual ability and the result he had envisioned.","Lex dared not imagine the grade of the liquid he was submerged in, or what could prompt such treatment from the Fortune Lord. It was not his place to guess the thoughts of a Dao Lord as powerful as him!","The effect carried over to Jack as well, which meant one thing. The effectiveness of his ability to convert divine energy into his own paladin cultivation exploded! Entering the next realm should have been a very difficult endeavor for him. But, with the help of the feedback from the liquid in the pool, it became all too easy!","The tribulation came right within the Mirage where he was. If his advancement was unusual in any way, or if it would have caused any phenomenon was entirely uncertain, for within the Mirage the Dao Lords were protecting him. That meant that any irregularity was suppressed by them so that none would be able to detect it.","It wasn’t entirely out of charity or good will that they were doing this, but out of consideration of the greater picture. Currently the universe was in chaos and the future was unpredictable. The Folklore realm needed to shore up its strength and prepare for whatever was to come - even if they were certain about their existing strength.","The tribulation Jack faced, for some reason, wasn’t nearly as difficult as the one Lex faced. Using his enhanced clarity, Jack studied the behavior of the laws and concluded that the reason for the weaker tribulation might be because the universe recognized that Lex had already undergone a tribulation for the Heaven Immortal realm once before.","Of course, this was under the premise that Jack hid his identity of being a fairy within his back using Back of Atlas. He had a feeling that once he let go of the technique and revealed his race while being within the Heaven Immortal realm, there would definitely be a massive reaction.","Now was not the time for such things, though, Jack could not afford any unnecessary attention due to the mission he was about to undertake, so he underwent the tribulation all the while hiding his race.","Lex also concluded that the difference in difficulty was due to this being an ordinary tribulation as compared to the Primordial tribulations he’d been experiencing with his main body.","Thus, it was no surprise to Jack at all that he easily surpassed the tribulation and finally reached the Heaven Immortal realm. Of course, what was a normal, and maybe even a little boring tribulation by Lex’s standards was still far beyond the tribulation normal Earth Immortals experienced.","All those watching the tribulation were stunned and in awe of the fairy who underwent the entire tribulation with his arms folded.","Only Jack and Bob seemed to think that the process and end result were a matter of fact. The only thing worthy of note was that his Spirit tribulation was fundamentally different from what Lex experienced. There was no obelisk. In fact, there wasn’t even anything related to fairies. Instead, there was only a towering sword, radiating a pure, divine sword intent that pierced his spirit, and tested his resolve. It felt almost like... it was similar to his paladin powers.","But that didn’t make sense. Tribulations were determined by race, not cultivation methods.","Maybe this was a result of him hiding his race. But even if it were related to cultivation methods instead of race, the paladin path should not have been at the level where the universe used it inside a tribulation. He sensed that there was something critical and crucial that he was not understanding about his own tribulation.","Even with his enhanced clarity, this was not something he could understand at the moment. Considering that resolving this mystery wasn’t so important at the moment compared to his other tasks, he discarded it from his thoughts entirely.","With his newfound realm, Jack was now ready to carry out his plans. He needed to do a few unsavory yet necessary things to maximise the benefit of the impending Nexus event, as well as finalise the formation.","Naturally, he could not make the formation under the watchful eye of so many Dao Lords, so he asked to be sent away.","Thus, within the two months where Lex was refining the necklace, Jack began to carry out the tasks he had planned for a long, long time.","However, he wasn’t the only one acting on plans that were long in the making. Rockefeller Rothsfather watched with hollow eyes as Bouldadin, the stone hydra who had kidnapped him long ago, finally began to execute the plan he and others had composed against the Midnight Inn.","He knew... regardless of whether the plan failed or succeeded, his own end was near."]},{"number":2389,"title":"Chapter 2389: What in tarnations...","paragraphs":["Was there ever a good time to act against an organization which was suspected to host a Dao Lord building a Seat of Power? Apparently, there was. That would be when the specific Dao Lord was, for unknown reasons, absent from within his own realm.","But what was the purpose in attacking such an organisation? Every action needed a sufficient motive, and that was especially true when that action would provoke a strong enemy.","In this case, that purpose was not the acquisition of rare resources, nor was it to occupy the realm. Instead, it was to ensure that the Dao Lord in question would, in the future, be so deeply mired in problems that he would have no time to interfere in other matters.","Such was the competition between Dao Lords. Direct conflict hardly ever occurred. Instead, they would strategically move against each other to occupy them for massive segments of time, effectively removing them from the playing field.","Under the premise that a single Dao cycle was 231,000 years, removing a keyplayer for even a few Dao cycles allowed for a massive shift in opportunities. Their aim this time, however, was to create such an absolute disaster that the Innkeeper would be stuck within his realm for a few dozen Dao cycles!","How could such a thing happen? By using a frontal invasion of the Midnight Inn? Never. Such a method was much too crude, and was not befitting a confrontation between Dao Lords. Besides, there were far more effective methods.","For example, by keeping the realm valuable enough that the Innkeeper would not be able to give up his investment in it, but also damaging it enough that it would take him endless years to repair the damage. Not to mention, if the potency and power of the realm were reduced, then that would automatically translate in the Innkeeper having a weaker Seat of Power.","That, too, would serve to benefit the many powers who had come together this time.","They were not foolish. They understood how dangerous it was to act. But the previous actions taken by the Humanoid Alliance of kidnapping a worker had proven to them that the Innkeeper was genuinely absent from within the Midnight Realm.","With his protective reputation, there is no way he would silently watch one of his workers get taken away simply for the sake of strategy or creating a false rumor of his absence. Yes, they were sure that this was not bait from the Innkeeper, or they would have never acted.","So then, what exactly was their strategy? Especially considering that the Midnight Inn was closed off, with the only known available entrance being the taverns located within the Origin realm?","The answer was simple. They would pollute the laws of the growing realm. Considering the faster flow of time, and the vulnerable state of the realm itself, the slightest hint of pollution would spread quickly and affect the laws of the developing realm deeply.","In this case, that pollution could be anything. It could be a law that turned the land barren, or the air stale, or the water acidic. The slightest change in laws to make it so that it was no longer supportive of basic life, or maybe so that the types of spirit energy became chaotic and uncontrollable, causing endless corrosion.","As long as it caused a deviation in the laws towards an undesirable direction, it could be called pollution, even if it was called something else in a different realm.","The sheer spectrum of items which could cause such a change made it so that the items required to cause such pollution could be easily brought into the target realm without arousing the slightest bit of attention. Once those items were in the realm, they could be assembled, and the seeds planted.","After that, they need only to let nature take its course.","It was a subtle move that would arouse no attention until it was too late. They had their ways of hiding the spread of pollution until it was too late to stop.","Thus, filled with great anticipation, Bouldadin watched the screen alongside Rocketfellow as their agents began to act. Due to the difference in the flow of time, the screens seemed like everyone was moving quickly.","There were thousands - even tens if not hundreds - of thousands of unsuspecting agents who were being used for this mission. They would not even know they were bringing contraband into the realm itself.","The first, unsuspecting agent - a type of sentient, mobile mushroom that could cultivate - entered the queue for the tavern. Soon enough, he passed all the basic checks and was eligible to enter.","Bouldadin could not help but grin even wider as he saw the agent walk through the door and enter the Midnight Inn. The feed cutoff the moment he entered the Midnight Inn, but that didn’t matter as they had already expected as much.","\"Check mate,\" said Bouldadin. If the first agent could enter, so could the others. They did not even need to do anything - simply by entering the Midnight realm the pollutant ingredient they carried would disappear from their person and latch onto the laws of the growing realm. That’s because these items were attracted to immature laws, unlike those found in stronger realms like the Origin realm.","As long as more and more of such agents entered, more and more pollutants would affect the laws of the realm, hastening the corruption. How could the legendary security team of the Midnight Inn deal with such an invasion? They couldn’t!","Or, at least, that’s what Bouldadin thought. The moment that mushroom wabbled through the tavern in the Midnight Inn and exited the building, he was stunned by what he saw. Or rather, he was so frightened he nearly died from a heart attack. Fortunately, mushrooms did not have hearts, so he survived.","Tribulation Fiends. The realm was filled with Tribulation Fiends, as far as the eye could see, filling the very air with the faint smell that lingered after a lightning bolt strike.","But wait a minute... why were they all... behaving so oddly? And what the hell was going on with the laws of the realm? And what in tarnations were those peacocks doing? And were those... bunnies?","The mushroom was horrified, and strangely intrigued. If he wasn’t immediately killed, he would very much like to find out what was going on.","Before he could think further, a massive figure approached him, covering the mushroom with its shadow.","\"Oh dear, why are you acting so silly?\""]},{"number":2390,"title":"Chapter 2390: Little Toby","paragraphs":["\"Excuse me, sir, I keep telling you. I’m a guest! I’m not from your mushroom cave,\" said Little Toby as he was carried by the massive turtle, but it was to no avail. Little Toby dared not resist the turtle either, and so he could only protest verbally as he was carried away.","If there was one consolation, it was that he was being taken away from the countless Tribulation Fiends that were sunbathing out in the open.","Little Toby looked behind him just to check one more time if he was dreaming, and then quickly turned back when everything was as he recalled.","As far as the eye could see, there were terrifying Tribulation Fiends in the shape of horrifying monsters, radiating the terrifying, uncontrollable power that came alongside tribulations. There were Farham made of lightning, singing the air itself as their lightning bodies sparked and created ozone.","There was the terrifying, forbidden creature known as the Bone Widow - a massive, twelve feet large (3.65 meters) spider made of bone, with enormous antlers similar to that of a moose. Except that the Bone Widows here were not made of bone, but of tribulation fire! For some odd reason, the otherwise terrifying creature actually looked kind of cute with a body made of orange flames.","Then, there were the Fiend Tribulations that represented Spirit tribulations! They were... they were...","Little Toby shuddered to even think about it, for the memory alone caused the mushroom without a mouth to begin salivating. The Fiend Tribulations representing Spirit tribulation were actually in the shape of massive Mantu!","Even though Little Toby had never eaten dumplings before, or ever eaten, for that matter, the sight of the massive Mantu filled his mind with such temptation that he actually longed to be struck with such tribulations!","Little Toby trembled as he caught himself slipping once more, and collected his thoughts, not letting them stray any longer.","Instead of thinking about the Tribulation Fiends, he instead thought about why the hell they were all sunbathing without the slightest hint of maliciousness!","Little Toby looked up in the sky and saw a crow shaped sun, shining down bright, warm sunlight that felt like it was the perfect temperature. It didn’t burn him, and instead filled his body with a welcome warmth.","\"Is that... the legendary Primordial Sunlight?\" Little Toby asked hesitantly, not really expecting to get an answer.","Unexpectedly, the massive turtle stopped and looked up in the air.","\"Don’t be silly,\" said the turtle, causing Little Toby to feel at ease. Of course it wasn’t Primordial Sunlight. That no longer existed. Then... the turtle continued speaking.","\"That’s the Primordial Plant Growth Booster the Innkeeper installed for my plants.\"","Little Toby was stunned, and didn’t know how to respond. So at the end of the day, it was Primordial Sunlight. That meant there was a Primordial Sun Crow in the sky, and that the reason the Tribulation Fiends had turned docile was because the original ’remnant spirit’ of the races was stirred due to the presence of genuine Primordial Sunlight. After all, these races had gone extinct in the Primordial Age.","As a history professor, Little Toby had a lot of knowledge about a lot of arcane and unusual things most people did not pay attention to.","Of course, even though Little Toby could come up with a semi-plausible explanation for why the Fiend Tribulations had begun to sunbathe, he could not understand what the peacocks and bunnies were doing.","What possible reason could the peacocks have for entering the bodies of the docile Farham and cultivating within? And why would the bunnies cultivate within the flaming bodies of the Bone Widow?","While Little Toby could not understand the logic behind the actions of those two groups, assuming that there was some unknown benefit to cultivating within a Tribulation Fiend - something literally unprecedented in history - he could not even begin to understand what those strange looking cats were thinking, trying to eat the Spirit Mantu all the while screaming ’oh lawd’!","It was incomprehensible!","\"Ish thish the one, uncle turtle?\" asked a cute little voice, causing Little Toby to look over.","He was a tiny little human - even smaller in size than Little Toby himself - dressed in a pink, princess frock and wearing a plastic tiara. The massive, silver spear that was more than three times the length of her body that the little girl held did not exactly fit the look of her outfit, but then again, neither did the massive, scary looking dragon she was sitting upon.","\"Yes, silly little human, this is the one who brought in the law-fertilizer,\" said the turtle with a nod.","The little girl seemed extremely excited upon hearing the words.","\"Oh, oh, does that mean we’re going to feed him to uncle Luthor’s hell?\" she asked excitedly, her eyes practically sparkling. Little Toby, on the other hand, suddenly began trembling because he had no idea what was going on, but he certainly didn’t like the idea of being fed to anything, especially a hell!","\"No, no, silly little human. We cannot feed guests to the hell for unknowingly committing crimes. We will take him to the Lotus Garden pond where the pollution he brought can be effectively turned into law-fertilizer by Uncle Lotus.\"","The turtle paused when it realized it had said ’Uncle Lotus’ and suppressed a sigh. It seemed even he was being infected by little Almira.","\"Almira, your mother has forbidden you from playing in hell,\" said Pel Jr. in an exhausted tone. He was her babysitter today, and for some reason it felt harder than fighting off an invasion. \"Hell is an inappropriate place for little girls. If you want to play, we can play in one of the custom-made dungeons your mother had built for your training.\"","\"But Uncle Luthor said he needs my help beating up the bad guys in there,\" she said as she crossed her arms and pouted, careful not to smack the spear onto the dragon. This thing had been made for her by Uncle Orin, and could hurt almost everyone.","The turtle moved on, much to the relief of Little Toby who was extremely frightened by the little girl who was wielding what seemed like an Immortal weapon! As he looked back, he could tell that even as she pretended to be upset, there was a hint of mischief hidden in her eyes as she looked towards him.","Little Toby shivered and looked away, suppressing his tears from flowing out - even though he did not have tear ducts, or even eyes for that matter.","\"Excuse me, sir, I keep telling you, there must be some kind of mistake. I’m just a simple guest,\" the mushroom pleaded, but the turtle only called him a silly turtle and kept on moving.","In the sky above him, a black phoenix flew by, glancing at the mushroom for a bit before flying towards the Valley of Time, where Mary was building her body. She had struck a deal with Vinei to help her speed up the process.","Elsewhere within the Midnight Inn, a reflection of Moon’s body stood inside the Dreamy Mirror, watching everything happening. It had been... quite a long time since she saw Lex. She was beginning to get a little worried."]},{"number":2391,"title":"Chapter 2391: It’s time","paragraphs":["\"Lex, it’s time,\" said Romulus as his clone stood outside the Genesis Dew chamber, quite frankly feeling impressed at how well and how easily Lex had been able to make use of it.","Genesis Dew was his own creation using resources from within the Gilded Hollow, and Romulus normally used it to temper his treasures and elevate their levels so that even at the Dao level they’d be useful.","Considering that Lex was operating from a necklace, and that he had absorbed many Dao materials, he figured that his leftover Genesis Dew would help him elevate the necklace to a higher level.","It didn’t make too much of a difference to Romulus since this thing had a very short shelflife, and he wasn’t going to refining or improving any treasures any time soon. The Genesis Dew would have gone to waste soon enough, and it could not be preserved for its existence was not linked to the flow of time of any realm, but directly to the law of Chronos.","So he might as well use what was left rather than let it go to waste. That said, even he had not anticipated just how effectively Lex would use it. Romulus, naturally, did not pry into Lex’s secrets. That didn’t mean he couldn’t use his eyes to look at the human, and that in itself was enough!","He could see that Lex had improved, and not by a small amount.","He was right. Lex had reached 51% of the Primordial Dao Body in a mere two months. That was despite the fact that doing so had not been his focus. However, that also marked the end of his progress in that direction as the Genesis Dew hadn’t been able to help his Dao Body grow anymore after reaching 51%. Lex didn’t mind.","What was more important was that... Lex had established the basic framework for how he wanted the necklace to work. Everything operated on its own according to the set of instructions Lex had programmed into it, forming a mere framework of a working system.","Naturally, once the system would be complete, what it could do would be far more complex than what it was currently doing.","However, the lack of complexity did not mean that it was weak. No, the fake realm that Lex had established was built on a foundation of many Dao materials, tempered and reinforced by whatever that liquid was that he was submerged into. Yes, he obviously absorbed the liquid to improve the inside of his necklace too. If that was forbidden, the Fortune Lord would have told him in advance.","Moreover, being bonded to the necklace only made it easier for him to establish his own complete supremacy over the realm within. It occurred to Lex that this could be considered the equivalent to a Seat of Power, but for beings below the Dao Lord realm.","Moreover, while Lex himself did not know that he was forming a Primordial Dao Body instead of a regular Dao Body, he began to sense that there was definitely something strange going on.","The space within the Gilded Hollow was incredibly strong, but even so he could sense that his very existence put a certain weight on the surrounding space and laws.","\"Thank you for your help,\" Lex said to the Fortune Lord with the greatest sincerity as he bowed towards him. Lex understood better than anyone just how much of a help these two months had been for him.","\"No thanks necessary - you have also been very helpful to me by first letting me know the state of the qilin in the universe, and then by giving me an updated deadline. We are both helping each other, so there is no need to keep score between us. What you have to do now is prepare yourself because we have reached the destination.","\"We will go our separate ways from here on out, so I have to explain to you what you must do, regardless of whether you choose to pursue that flower you were looking for, or if you want to exit the Hollow directly.\"","Lex was already mentally prepared to face this situation, and had already done everything he could to prepare. He was ready to return and kick some stalker butt. As for the flower... if he was inside the Hollow with his real body, he could have considered giving it to Regiz, not that he wanted to do that at all.","His only other option was to use it now himself, which was a moderate priority for him at best. He would give up on it if it proved to be too difficult.","\"Outside, we stand at the edge of the Dao material zone,\" said Romulus as he turned the screen on and showed Lex a picture. \"On one side we have Dao materials... and beyond that, we have materials of a level that transcend the Dao realm - something our own universe has yet to create at all.\"","Lex was stunned, and yet he was not so surprised. Hearing that statement seemed to confirm for him that the Gilded Hollow was definitely a remnant of the universe known as Pentagal.","As for materials beyond the Dao realm... fortunately, fortunately the screen showed it as blank, for Lex was not certain he could even tolerate the sight of what such materials looked like.","\"Oh don’t worry, everything is there,\" Romulus said pointing at the screen. \"You simply lack the senses relevant to ’see’ or even sense them. Funnily enough, that also protects you from the aura of such materials because you simply can’t distinguish them from the aura of the laws of the universe.","\"Anyway, that’s not what’s important. What is important, though, is the location of the flower. Look, it’s right here,\" he said as he pointed at the screen. At the same time the view changed a bit, as the person whose eyes he was looking through looked a little to the left.","There was a tall structure similar to a mayan pyramid with a square chamber at the very top. The flower seemed to be within the chamber... but wait... something wasn’t right.","Lex narrowed his eyes and focused on the image which seemed to look through the structure entirely, revealing the image of the flower.","That wasn’t a Double Yin Death Metal Rose. No, that was a Double Yang Disaster Rose - the very opposite of the flower that Regix wanted. Lex knew almost nothing about it, so it was almost certain that he had no idea what it did, or how it could be harvested. It seemed like he wasn’t destined to get it.","\"You should really find a way to get that thing,\" said Romulus as he looked at the picture."]},{"number":2392,"title":"Chapter 2392: I knew it!","paragraphs":["Lex was not expecting the Fortune Lord to advise him to get the flower just as he decided to give it up.","\"I remember all the details you gave me about the flower you were searching for - the Double Yin Death Metal flower. This one is not the same. In fact, I do not even fully understand what the use of this treasure is myself. However, I can see one thing very clearly.\"","Romulus turned his gaze from the screen towards Lex.","\"Your own fortunes are very well in tune with that of the flower. That does not mean you are destined to get it, or anything along those lines. It simply means that if you manage to get your hands on this flower, it will be of immense personal use to you.\"","Lex had not been expecting that at all. Of great personal use to him, as told by the Fortune Lord after viewing his fortunes. If that was the case... Lex could not resign himself to giving up on it without at least trying. The only obstacle was that he suspected this place was filled with so much Dao radiation that exposure would immediately kill him. He wasn’t wrong either.","Lex looked at the Fortune Lord, waiting for his instructions. Surely he would not be left to fend for himself.","\"On the contrary, my own fortunes are strongly misaligned with that flower. That means that even if I come close to it, the flower, I, or both may suffer some... misfortune. All I can do for you is bring you to the first step of the pyramid. As for how you reach the flower, and how you attain it, those are all things you must figure out on your own. I cannot help you.\"","A deep, deafening silence filled the room - at least from Lex’s perspective. His resolution - his ambitions of trying to get the flower - they all withered immediately and without restraint. Lex was not stupid enough to believe that he, as a Heaven Immortal with his soul trapped inside a necklace, could survive the Dao radiation in this place long enough to reach the top of the pyramid that was no doubt also filled with traps of some kind.","Even if the egg shell were to help him, how much could it realistically help?","No, better to give up on this treasure and come back to the Gilded Hollow the next time it opened. He could get the flower then. At least he’d be alive to get it.","\"Once you get the flower, or if you choose not to get the flower, you can immediately initiate an exit from the Gilded Hollow. In truth, exiting from the Hollow is not easy. Preventing us from exiting is the last retribution from the Hollow - a final attempt at exacting vengeance.","\"There are two fixed ways of exiting the Hollow - both of which we had to discover on our own, as there was no way of knowing how to do it. The first is to find an exit. Those exits exist randomly, and some look like portals while others look like ordinary items like rings or bangles.","\"The second is to actively hone in on the strings of retribution connected to yourself and manually trigger them prematurely. If you manage to survive the retribution, the Hollow will throw you out. Don’t worry, it won’t use too much energy on your retribution for a mere Immortal is not as valuable to it as other Dao Lords. It will target them. You can only hope that... it still doesn’t consider you a Dao Lord as well.\"","Lex did not bother hoping with his luck, that’s exactly what was going to happen. Dammit, why were his only options to brave a pyramid full of Dao radiation, or face the retribution of a dead universe? Shouldn’t he become at least a peak Celestial Immortal before facing stuff like that? Why did he need to face it as a Heaven Immortal?","\"I would like to help you more, but I will now be heading into the next zone of the Gilded Hollow, so I have my own hands full. I’ll provide you with a Dao shield that’ll last you ten seconds. That’s just enough where it won’t cause problems, and will give you enough time to trigger the retribution if you wish to leave. For the retribution, you will be transported to another place, so you don’t need to worry too much. Good luck.\"","With that, the Fortune Lord placed a hand on Lex’s shoulder and he must have erected some kind of barrier all around him. If he did, Lex could not tell.","The next moment, Lex found himself standing at the base of the pyramid with no sign of the Fortune Lord or anyone else.","In front of him was the pyramid, behind him endless lands composed of Dao materials, and to his right there was nothing but pitch darkness.","\"Dammit, nothing better go wrong with this or I’m going to be pissed!\" Lex exclaimed as he tried to trigger the retribution without any hesitation. He could not feel the Dao radiation - likely due to the barrier the Fortune Lord erected - but he could most certainly feel the sensation of death latching onto him as his instincts screamed in his ears like a little girl!","Unfortunately for Lex, the moment he appeared, within the darkness to his right, far off, there were some old ruins. Within those ruins there was a throne upon which sat an old corpse. When he appeared, his aura seemed to reach the throne itself, as if carried by some mysterious force, and the eyelid of the corpse trembled once more.","With excruciating difficulty, from beyond the veil of death, a thought emerged within the corpse, though the corpse had no soul or spirit. Yet the broken, fragmented thought was enough to freeze not just the Gilded Hollow, but the rest of the universe as well.","But the thought was broken, and so its effect was fragmented. The universe froze, but time kept flowing, and those below the Dao realm remained entirely unaffected by the freeze.","\"Dammit, why the hell is the retribution not coming!\" Lex exclaimed as he already began to run up the pyramid. For some reason, he knew this would happen."]},{"number":2393,"title":"Chapter 2393: Countdown","paragraphs":["\"Do you really think that leaving him there is the best idea? He’s just a human. He’s going to die the moment your shield disappears,\" asked one of the Dao Lords accompanying Romulus as they watched him leave Lex on the first step of the pyramid.","It wasn’t that reaching the top was too dangerous for them, but it would definitely distract them from their current task. No matter how valuable the unknown flower was, they were not willing to gamble it against the known value of the next area they were about to go into, which is why they had not considered attempting to procure it themselves at all.","\"Buddy, that human is backed by a Dao Lord who can attack us from outside the Gilded Hollow. His chances of survival are a whole lot higher than us. This is not me sending him off to death, this is me earning good will from whoever backs him,\" responded Romulus as he looked at Lex before turning around and entering the area that appeared to Lex as total darkness.","Of course, all of that happened at such immense speed that Lex had not even processed his change in location before the Dao Lords were already gone. Thus, these few Dao Lords did not see his reaction. Then again, it would not have mattered, for with that incomplete thought from that corpse, all Dao Lords had been frozen, and so had the Gilded Hollow! Even the universe itself had been affected, so there was really no one around to watch Lex make a fool of himself.","The Fortune Lord promised him ten seconds of safety. As Lex looked up to the peak of the pyramid which was a quintillion miles away, he knew he would not make it in time. Okay, maybe he was exaggerating about the distance, but all things considered, Lex had every right to do so at that moment.","\"Shit, shit, shit, shit!\" Lex kept exclaiming like a mantra as he ran, all the while focusing on trying to activate his damn retribution string, but nothing was happening. Yet running and cursing weren’t the only things Lex was doing. No, he was using 100% of his brain to utilize every means available to him.","He was trying to teleport, but the space in this region was beyond his control. Lex reached out to the laws of space and found them to be stagnant. He didn’t think too much into it - a place constantly baptized by such intense Dao radiation must have experienced changes he’d never anticipated.","In truth, the laws were not responding to him because they were still recovering from the frozen effect of that broken thought. As one second passed by, the effect of that thought had already begun to lessen, but Lex had no way of knowing that.","Besides all of that, he also had Jack give up everything he was doing and instead focus on trying to connect to the necklace and directly pull it from the Hollow to himself. If he could send materials to Lex, there was no reason he couldn’t directly pull Lex to himself.","Unfortunately it was easier said than done, and he had only a total of ten seconds, now with only nine left!","Lex took out the Primordial Farham Egg shell and wore it on his face like a mask, hoping that it would protect him a little when the Dao Radiation would come back. Of course, that’s only how it appeared. In truth, Lex was inside a necklace so the eggshell was covering the necklace.","Then another second passed, and Lex made no progress. Even running at his full speed, he was only halfway through the first step of the pyramid. That meant that if everything else stayed the same, and he encountered no deadly traps or anything of the sort, he would need about 200 seconds to reach the top.","All in all, the pyramid wasn’t too big, but considering he only had the shield for 8 more seconds, it hardly mattered because he was definitely screwed.","\"This cannot be happening,\" said Lex as he, utilizing only one second, crafted an entirely new and utterly unique Lawcraft for the sole purpose of launching the necklace through the damn air like a slingshot with rocket boosters! Unfortunately... the laws still weren’t responding to him!","\"Lord Fortune, there seems to be something wrong. The retribution strings aren’t activating!\" Lex yelled out loud without any concern for face or looking foolish.","This was serious stuff. He’d just refined the necklace to a point where he felt confident about his return - he wasn’t going to waste it on a flower he knew nothing about and didn’t necessarily immediately need.","Unfortunately, the pyramid must have put him in some kind of isolation barrier because the Fortune Lord didn’t respond to Lex’s yell. He must not be able to hear it.","Five seconds left and Lex began to sweat. No, seriously, the amount of pressure the situation put on Lex, and thus his soul, was so immense that it began to affect the necklace, squeezing it until hidden impurities within the necklace started to get pushed out in liquid form. The impurities looked like sweat.","As Lex hopped onto the second step of the pyramid, and only a couple of seconds were left, he began to seriously regret not mastering time laws. Unfortunately, now wasn’t the best time for that.","He began erecting the best, strongest most powerful defense he could think of, using the influence of his Dao Body without restraint as he felt the seconds pass him by.","One second left and Lex finally stopped cursing as he sharpened his focus to the utmost. Whether he could do it or not, he’d force Jack to pull the necklace back the moment something went amiss. The egg shell should buy him at least a few seconds, and maybe his defense could buy him a couple more.","Regardless of what happened now, Lex readied himself to face the obstacle up ahead with his absolute utmost. Yes, he did not ask for this situation, but that did not mean he would collapse and give up if he couldn’t escape from it either.","Even though logic and experience told him that the only thing that awaited him was death, Lex was ready to face it with a serious face. Besides, the necklace itself had absorbed quite a few Dao materials. Who knew whether it would have developed a resistance to Dao radiation. There was only one way to find out.","Zero seconds left... time elapsed, and then there was nothing."]},{"number":2394,"title":"Chapter 2394: Absolute boss","paragraphs":["Lex blinked. Jack blinked. Who knows, maybe even Lex’s real body might have blinked in that moment because the surprise of what happened hit him harder than a Jorlam wielding a sledge hammer.","His protection period ended, but there was no Dao radiation. Heck, he didn’t even know if the barrier that the Fortune Lord made for him was active or not because he hadn’t been able to sense it from the very beginning. All he knew was that at second 0, when he was waiting to be assaulted by a level of Dao radiation that should have been lethal, nothing happened.","Something was terribly wrong, that he knew. There was no way that this place had no Dao radiation. He would have almost believed that the radiation had been absorbed by the egg shell were it not for the absence of Primordial aura as well.","He did not know what was happening, or how to get out of it, but he kept running. Logically speaking, he knew that getting his hands on the flower would not rescue him from this situation. Even if he got the flower, he would not have a way to exit this place unless his retribution string was triggered.","That said, he had no idea what the flower did, or what its chamber contained, so maybe there was hope to be found there. Moreover, he had no idea why the Dao radiation was missing. It may have something to do with that flower, and it may not. Maybe it was even that in tune fortune of his and the flower that the Fortune Lord was talking about.","Regardless of what the reason was, Lex kept running as if his life depended on it, mainly because it probably did. At the same time, he kept his senses extended as much as possible to avoid any nasty surprises.","Naturally, the reason the Dao radiation was missing was because all things at the Dao had been frozen in time by that one, broken thought. It was truly too fortuitous that things played out that way... or perhaps everything had been by design.","The human corpse within the ruins did not move again, nor did it react to Lex’s aura. Twice already the corpse had reacted to him, and that was enough for it to be suppressed by the universe. Coincidentally, though, the direction of his face seemed to be towards Lex, as if the corpse was watching him.","Lex, naturally, knew none of that. But as he continued to run for second after second, he eventually began to notice something. He had started to get a faint, almost imperceptible response from the laws of the universe.","That meant that whatever was happening was slowly reversing. That was both a good thing, and a bad thing. It was good because he might be able to escape, and it was because he didn’t know if the shield around him was genuinely gone after ten seconds, or if it could withstand ten seconds of Dao radiation, meaning it might still be active since the radiation was missing!","A soft tremor ran through the pyramid beneath Lex’s feet, as if it was beginning to realize that he was here, and was considering what to do about it. The pyramid was in a state of lethargy, as was the rest of the universe as far as Lex was concerned. But that lethargy was wearing off.","Lex narrowed his eyes and ran a quick calculation. At the current rate, the universe would return to normal before he could reach the flower. But... if he could time things right, he might be able to use the laws to teleport himself to the flower before the harmful effects from the recovering lethargy might be able to affect him.","No, might wasn’t good enough. He would do it.","The Flow state of old, now elevated and enhanced beyond what its original creator could have ever fathomed, was still not something Lex used often. His natural state was better than what others achieved with the Flow state.","Lex used it now, nevertheless, for this was one of the most critical moments of his life. His every action needed to be beyond perfect. Nothing could be left up to chance.","His mind kept up with the rate at which the universe normalised, and he even began to sense that the Dao radiation that was previously absent was beginning to show signs of returning. It wasn’t back yet, but it was getting there.","Within the Folklore realm, Jack used the newfound Paladin powers he received upon becoming a Heaven Immortal, and augmented his own soul with a tremendous amount of divine energy.","Although the effect wasn’t the same as if he were closer to Jack, Lex still felt his senses sharpen.","He had just climbed the fifth step when the moment came. The laws had become active enough that they could work and be influenced properly. The Dao radiation that had been building up seemed to cross some kind of threshold and finally began to appear in his surroundings. Somewhere far away, Romulus’ felt like someone had called him but that he had missed the call.","He turned around to look at Lex, not noticing that his own movements were incredibly slow.","At that precise moment, Lex teleported right to the peak of the pyramid, not using teleportation but rather the law of Anchor - one of the eight ruling laws. He had relied on sheer strength of force to cut through the gap between where he was, and where he wanted to go, displaying unequalled brutality for his cultivation level.","Romulus chuckled and shook his head. And some people actually thought Lex might suffer with this trial. Which Heaven Immortal could jump to the peak of a pyramid with enough Dao radiation to incinerate a few weak, immature realms? One who was backed by an absolute boss, that’s who.","Meanwhile, Lex felt the Primordial Farham egg shell begin to work. The shield the Fortune Lord had given him was gone, and he had no idea how long the egg could last. Fortunately, the pyramid itself had not properly recovered yet, so the numerous defenses and traps that covered its body which could stop even Dao Lords had not yet activated.","Lex entered the final chamber - the one that contained the Double Yang Disaster Rose - and also touched upon the retribution string at the same time in case he needed to escape at any moment. Unfortunately, the Gilded Hollow was not recovering at the same rate as the universe itself, which is why he couldn’t escape right now if he needed to. He needed to survive a few more seconds."]},{"number":2395,"title":"Chapter 2395: Such a softie","paragraphs":["\"What the hell just happened?\" asked Ventura as he finally recovered from the time freeze that had affected the whole universe. While the Dao Lords of the universe weren’t able to sense the effect of that thought, he certainly could.","More importantly, even he hadn’t been able to resist the influence of that time freeze, which could only mean one thing! Whoever caused it was even more powerful than himself and the seven others who were hiding all around this universe.","Could there be... a ninth?","An especially grave expression fell upon his face as he considered his actions. If he wasn’t injured, there were many things he could have done. But since he was injured, he could only do one thing really.","Without hesitation, Ventura reached out to a Dao Lord known only as Speaker of the Senate. Naturally, the senate in question was the Dao Senate that worked for Eclipse, with their sole purpose being to complete her every whim and keep her happy.","As much as Ventura would like to directly talk to Eclipse, these were very sensitive times and it was best to avoid any misunderstandings his sudden appearance may cause.","A projection of the speaker appeared in Ventura’s very room, and though the speaker seemed surprised by the sudden summons, he did not seem surprised by who had summoned him. This was not the first time something like this had happened, clearly.","\"I need to speak with your Queen, urgently,\" said Ventura, lacking any and all of the friendliness and casualness he usually carried when around Eclipse. \"This matter cannot wait. If you are unable to connect to her, then I will have to pay a personal visit, in which case you should inform Harriot of my arrival.\"","The speaker was silent for a few moments, and then finally responded.","\"No need to trouble yourself, Lord Ventura. The lady has accepted the meeting request. She seems to have been expecting you,\" said the speaker before bowing and disappearing.","A short while later, a projection of Eclipse, Nulli and Harriot appeared in front of Ventura, much to the academy owner’s irritation. She was never alone - a restriction of sealing all her powers - and that meant that he would have to share his news with others, even if he’d prefer to keep the conversation private.","\"I don’t know if you felt it, but someone just made a move,\" Ventura said directly in a somber voice. \"It’s not any of the other seven I’m familiar with, so this might be an unknown ninth who had been in perpetual hiding. I suspect... remnants and refugees from Pentagal might be behind the ongoing war. This level of power... it was too great to be one of us.\"","Eclipse did not immediately respond, instead she continued to itch Harriot’s neck as if he was a real pet dog, while she thought to herself about the situation.","\"If the enemy is Pentagal, then we’ve been preparing to face the wrong foe. In that case, it’s best you withdraw your forces from the Dream realm lest they get caught in some trap.\"","Ventura nodded.","\"I’m already doing as much, though I can sense that both Death and Destiny are increasing their activities instead of withdrawing. There is a chance that this could be a distraction.\"","Eclipse chuckled, as if the news was of no consequence to her whatsoever.","\"Don’t worry about it and just withdraw your forces. Maybe use this opportunity to capture a few more Major realms and keep them from being destroyed. I doubt we’ll get caught in the crossfire if we stay away from the main conflict zones.\"","Their conversation was short, but it was enough. The projection disappeared, and Ventura began to act immediately.","Meanwhile, within the Primordial Garden, Nulli looked at Eclipse with a mischievous smirk on her face.","\"You’re such a softie,\" Nulli said to Eclipse, who only rolled her eyes in response. Neither of them seemed at all concerned by Ventura’s news.","Within the Gilded Hollow, entirely unaware that he had, once again , accidentally influenced the universe, Lex stepped into the room at the peak of the pyramid - the one containing the flower.","The Double Yang Disaster Rose was massive, with each single petal of that rose being far greater than Lex in size. The remarkable thing, though, was that the flower really did look a lot like a rose, except this one was of a deep, orange color, as if made of roaring flames.","Lex could feel that the thing was beginning to release its original aura once again, which was naturally at the Dao level. Regex had, incidentally, told him how he could avoid being affected by the aura of the Double Yin Death Metal Rose, despite its high level.","He had a strong feeling that wouldn’t work on this one, though. Moreover, he had taught Lex a special technique which he could use to harvest the rose without harming it at all.","This one, though, was all up to him to figure out. As it happened, Lex had an idea of how he could do just that.","\"Bob help me, because I must be crazy for doing this,\" Lex muttered to himself as he grabbed the Primordial Farham egg shell in his hand and took a step towards the flower.","Within the necklace, he still had plenty of Genesis Dew left. Based on his understanding, that Dew could help him absorb and refine materials - including Dao materials. His plan was to wrap the flower with the shell - completely disregarding the fact that the flower was way bigger than the egg shell - and transport it into the necklace wherein he could use the Dew to absorb the flower into his necklace.","Honestly, this was an extremely dangerous task to undertake while on his own. There were, however, a few reasons why he was taking the risk.","First was the strange lethargy that the universe was showing. If he could take advantage of the fact that the flower wasn’t at full strength yet and absorb or process it, he could directly bypass the most difficult part of handling the flower.","Second was the fact that the egg shell seemed to be working perfectly - even against the slightest bit of Dao radiation that had begun to emerge.","Third, he was depending on what the Fortune Lord told him about the flower being in tune with his own fortune. That should make it easier for him to get it.","The last thing he was depending on was his knowledge of the Double Yin Death Metal Rose. Although these two were not the same, and were in fact dire opposites, Lex was depending on the fact that they were of the same species. Their behavior should follow the same rules and limitations, meaning that he could use what he knew of the Death Metal Rose to extrapolate the behavior and specifications of the Disaster Rose.","Still, it was a huge risk. Normally, he avoided risks. But he was now at the stage in life where playing it safe could no longer help him. If he didn’t grow drastically stronger, dying at the hands of a more powerful enemy was only a matter of time. So, instead of merely delaying his own death, he wanted to remove that possibility altogether by growing much stronger, much faster. That , unfortunately, required that he take risks."]},{"number":2396,"title":"Chapter 2396: On the verge of death...","paragraphs":["The flower was not actually made of flames despite looking like it. It was hot though. Yet the heat did not really act as an obstacle to Lex at all, and not just because the universe was being lethargic.","If the flower followed the same principles as the Death Metal Rose, no one would be affected negatively by the rose until they touched it. That was also why Lex anticipated that the Dao radiation from the flower would be self contained until he actually touched it. The radiation that the shell was currently reacting to was from his surroundings.","Once Lex touched the flower, the heat from the extreme yang nature of the flower would incinerate him - or anyone else that touched it. Of course, in this case, the lethargy of the universe meant that the flower would be slow to incinerate him, or that when it began to do so it would be weaker than normal. That would give him sufficient time to absorb it into the necklace.","Moving on, the Death Metal Rose had the effect of purifying even the strongest curses, but strictly speaking it was not restricted to just that. This part hadn’t been told to him by Regix, and was instead something he surmised on his own.","The Death Metal Rose should have an unquestionably strong yin nature, which should allow it to resonate or affect with other things a yin nature. Yin and yang were broad concepts that Lex did not traditionally get into, but it was something he had started to research ever since learning about the rose.","Basically, Lex suspected that the reason why the Death Metal Rose could purify curses was because it could affect the yin nature of most curses. Hardly any curse was a yang nature or affinity thing,which is why he could generalise when he said that.","Lex had no way of confirming this, but this was his own theory nevertheless. In that case, the Disaster Rose should have a similar ability of being able to affect and influence things with yang nature. That was a very broad list of things he could influence, but Lex had already had something in mind, which was life.","Yin was more associated with spirits and ghosts, whereas yang was more associated with life and birth. If he could, he wanted to fuse the flower with his necklace and use it to supplement the naturally occurring life within his fake realm. If he could improve that, and do it properly so that it formed a proper cycle, his fake realm would naturally stabilise much quicker and on its own, reducing his work load.","A certain part of Lex’s mind realized that he was procrastinating, and he did not have time for such things. Every moment was critical. So, without further ado, Lex grabbed the flower using the eggshell as a kind of oven mitt, ready to transport it to the necklace.","Yet the moment the shell and the flower came into contact, an uncontrollably thick, overbearing Primordial aura erupted from the shell, spreading throughout the room and then the rest of the pyramid. Moreover, it was not a random, passive Primordial aura like the one that filled the Primordial Garden.","Nay, this was the kind of aura that accompanied a living being! Although Lex had a genuine Primordial aura of his own now, he was stunned in place when the aura erupted for alongside the aura, he also felt an unbelievably strong spirit!","With his body frozen in place, unable to do anything, only a single thought ran through his mind. There had been a living soul hiding inside the shell, and it could not escape until the ability of the shell activated. If the shell had been destroyed before the ability activated, the hidden soul inside would have also died.","Moreover... most likely the reason that the universe seemed so angry was not solely because of the shell itself, but also because of the identity of the soul hidden within. Lex had no idea who exactly it was, but he could tell that it was no ordinary being.","Lex felt the spirit observe him, and then his surroundings. For a moment it paused as it observed the flower he was grabbing. The Primordial aura churned, and then encompassed the flower, causing thin, black smoke to rise out of it.","\"We’re even,\" a thunderous voice roared in Lex’s voice before the spirit completely vanished. The egg shell was still in Lex’s hand, and it was still producing Primordial aura from contact with the flower, but the spirit within the aura seemed to be gone.","Lex also felt like the immensity of the danger he had been feeling from the flower had dropped drastically. That said, it was still not something he could take lightly so he absorbed it into the necklace, still held via the egg shell, and was dropped into the remaining Genesis Dew that Lex had left.","At the same time, he triggered the retribution string and felt it wrap itself around him before pulling him away. It had happened instantaneously, but that was not enough. In the minor fraction of a moment where the eggshell was gone, and Lex had not yet disappeared, Lex was exposed to a faint amount of Dao radiation.","Despite how brief the contact had been, and despite how faint the aura itself was - comparatively speaking - Lex’s soul felt like it was on the verge of being extinguished. He could not tell if he was injured or not because his spirit seemed affected as well, and his mind had gone adrift.","Naturally, the necklace itself wasn’t in such a good condition physically either. The timing for this could not have been worse for he was being pulled into a retribution, and within the space of the necklace a flower with literally the word ’disaster’ in it was being processed... or was supposed to be processed. What its condition was now was not something Lex could comment on.","The Dao radiation Lex had felt was nowhere near the full extent of the radiation that room normally had, since the universe was still lethargic, and that was the very reason he had survived.","In fact, it was that very same lethargy which was preventing him from immediately reaching the retribution. Meanwhile, the flower began to lose its shape, and a pulse of yang spread throughout the interior of the necklace, affecting the fake realm until it eventually reached Lex’s soul.","The fortune that the Fortune Lord had mentioned previously began to reveal itself, for the yang nature of the flower began to resonate with the phoenix part of the Helix Petal Rose that had been fused into Lex before his birth.","It was always very obvious that Lex had a strong affinity for dragons, but his phoenix affinity and abilities always remained somewhat suppressed, perhaps because the population of phoenixes in the universe were far fewer, giving him less opportunities to interact with them.","Now, that aspect of his nature was being triggered on its own."]},{"number":2397,"title":"Chapter 2397: Crucible of Karma","paragraphs":["It wasn’t like Lex hadn’t activated his lingering phoenix affinity at all . Even without excessive contact with phoenixes and any associated treasures or materials, Lex’s body inherently demonstrated some similar abilities.","He was always excellent at healing - especially others - to the point where his blood was literally better than most healing medications in existence. The only reason he wasn’t extremely proficient in healing himself wasn’t because he himself lacked healing capabilities, but because his body itself was so powerful that healing it required a lot more energy and resources.","But being good at healing, and being able to be reborn from an extremely wounded state were two entirely different concepts, and were not even on the same level.","In Lex’s current state, exposure to Dao radiation had brought him on the verge of death. The reason it was on the verge, and not actual death, was because of his 51% Dao Body giving him some minor resistance to it.","Yet this was merely the result from the initial exposure. That did not mean that everything was over, as the damage would continue to compound unless the Dao radiation was cleansed from him.","That, however, was not the only thing happening to him at the moment. The flower had begun to lose its shape as it processed itself without any guidance, passively affecting the fake realm and the necklace in the most suitable, stable and gentle way. That naturally included Lex’s soul as well. The surprising thing, however, was that even the egg shell was not excluded from the treatment.","Yet even that was not the full extent of what was happening. Two other, extremely critical things were happening simultaneously. One was that the egg shell was producing massive amounts of Primordial aura.","Such unconstrained aura inside the fake realm, especially when it was in such a vulnerable state, should have destabilised it. Yet what it did, instead, was stabilise Lex’s damaged soul since he had fully acclimatised to Primordial energy and aura himself.","Not everything was rainbows and sunshine, however, since the final thing that was happening was that the necklace was being pulled into the retribution. Although the process was slow, that was only relatively speaking. In a few seconds, at most, the necklace would be pulled into the retribution zone designated for Lex’s own final retribution - the one he feared might reach the Dao level.","Yet those few seconds were enough. Although the situation did not get significantly better, at least Lex’s deterioration was stopped. Everything entered into an equilibrium state.","Unfortunately, equilibrium, safety, stability and all manner of such things didn’t really seem to be a part of Lex’s fate. The necklace entered the land of retribution that the Gilded Hollow had specifically created.","Lex had already faced a few types of retribution, with varying levels of difficulty. Now, it seemed that the Gilded Hollow had decided to show him the last type of retribution, which was also what was normally considered the hardest.","Mithon had told him that in the last type of retribution, the Hollow pulled out the targets soul and puts it through eight cycles of torture. That was exactly the type of retribution Lex faced now - with one notable exception.","The Hollow could not separate Lex’s soul from the necklace because the nature of Lex’s existence made it so that his body and soul were basically one. In short, the necklace fell into the first type of torture.","A stream of cool information flowed into the necklace, as if the Hollow wished to inform its target about the torture they were about to face. The cool stream of information actually stirred Lex’s spirit, and allowed him to wake from his stupor.","Before even processing the information given to him by the Hollow, Lex realized the state his existence was in. It was not good - he was on the verge of being destroyed. The necklace and his soul were both on the absolute verge of collapsing, and it was only the actions of the flower which were keeping the destruction from happening.","Then he processed the information he got from the Hollow.","The first cycle of torture he was going to face was called Crucible of Karma. It exacted on Lex every injury and pain he had ever caused to anyone else for any reason.","The pain had not yet started, perhaps because the Hollow was waiting for him to understand exactly what was about to happen to him. Once he understood, the pain began.","Lex took in a deep breath because that... was going to be a lot of pain. Then, he smiled. No matter how much pain he endured, pain itself was something Lex no longer even took into consideration. He did not even scream or grunt, instead recalling the time that he asked the Hollow to teach him how to punish his enemies.","This was not a bad idea. He could cause his enemies to suffer without actually taking any harm.","Even for people who could ignore the pain, much like himself, it did not negate the fact that they were in actual pain.","Lex estimated that he would be within this cycle of torture for quite a while, and understood why the Fortune Lord had arrived so early. Even though the deadline was almost a year away, the retribution itself would take time.","Instead of wasting this time wallowing on the time he batista-bombed Belle in their childhood - the pain from which he was currently feeling - Lex focused on the state of his recovery. He could heal himself, but the flower seemed to be guiding him towards a better path. He could now understand why the Fortune Lord had recommended he try to take the flower.","If he could awaken the legendary rebirth by fire ability of phoenixes, his strength and survivability would shoot through the roof. Thus, he took this time to begin guiding and accelerating the growth from the flower. He aimed to complete everything and be ready by the time the next cycle of torture began. Who knew whether it would also be as harmless as this one.","What Lex didn’t know was that he was actually suffering one of the most deadly versions of the torture retribution, and that he was literally the first in history to disregard it entirely. It wasn’t that others weren’t as impervious as him to pain - it was just that most who entered had lived much longer lives than him, and had a whole lot more time to do damage than him.","That said, the pain and suffering Lex had caused - purposefully and inadvertently - was not little. The extent of the pain he was suffering was enough to drive most immortals insane.","He had not just caused pain to people, but his actions had occasionally caused emotional distress even to Dao Lords. Even if that karma was well hidden by the system and the Masterless technique, it could not be entirely erased. An entity on the level of Gilded Hollow could see through it.","Thus the pain he was going through... it could not be quantified. Yet the smile his projection wore never wavered, even if his eyes reddened as he focused on processing the flower. Rebirth through fire was more than a literal definition of the ability. The pain, the excruciating agony that was coursing through his entire being at the moment, too could be called a type of fire. Once he came out the other end, he would be reborn - and not just because he aimed to fix the necklace by then. No, his aim was to have the entire ability unlocked and working by then!","It wasn’t just Lex who was ignoring the pain. Since it was a conceptual suffering that he was going through, Jack was also not exempt.","Yet no matter where the pain came from, no matter how severe the pain itself was, it could not break Lex’s focus for even a moment.","\"Maybe I’m just too magnanimous,\" Lex joked to himself, though in truth there really was no shortage of suffering.","There was, however, an end to it. One end was if Lex’s mind broke, and he died. The second end was if he bore all the pain he had ever caused, and survived. Five weeks and three days later, when the cycle of torture finally ended, that’s exactly what happened.","Only Lex himself knew just how much suffering he had endured, and how he had maintained his focus through it. None would ever be able to tell the immense severity of this cycle simply from observing Lex, for he showed no outward sign of suffering at all.","Instead, he grinned as he observed the new state of his necklace. It had genuinely gone through a rebirth, from almost being destroyed due to Dao radiation to now being stronger than ever, both internally and externally.","The faint, lingering hint of Dao radiation on the necklace had been absorbed and turned into Primordial aura - the very same aura Lex used to baptize the fake realm and strengthen its space.","The Hollow, however, did not give him any reprieve as it immediately channeled a cool stream of information into his spirit to let him know about his next torture. The next torture cycle was titled Prison of Gluttony."]},{"number":2398,"title":"Chapter 2398: Clear headed","paragraphs":["That one, small moment where a cool stream of information was channeled into his mind was the only actual break between his cycles of torture. It was but a fraction of a second, as if just teasing him with a moment of peace before the torture resumed.","Lex, however, did not use it to recover or rest, or to savor the moment of peace. Instead, he reflected on what had happened during the previous torture cycle, how it had affected him, and what he had done.","The cycle was actually quite misleading, and in more than one way. It was called the Crucible of Karma, yet what it actually did was cause him pain - physical pain. That’s it. It did not harm his body or soul, nor did it let him pass out. It simply caused him all the pain he had ever caused himself throughout his life.","Yet even though it was singular in its purpose, that did not mean it was simple in its application, or that there wasn’t a hidden trick behind its actions. The complexity came from converting any and all harm Lex had ever caused and translating it into physical pain.","Now, Lex usually tried to avoid killing people - if one ignored that one time he used the butter knife to kill so many people he literally wiped out an entire faith. In his defense, even he had no idea the Full Strength Butter Knife would do that. Oh, and they started it first.","But putting that aside, if death had to be translated into equivalent physical pain, how much would it be? That was ignoring the method of the death - only the pain value of the death itself was being discussed. The answer, it turns out, is actually not that much.","The emotional anguish from knowing that one is about to die... now that’s something that hurts a lot, but not death itself.","But, without a doubt, the worst pain Lex felt was from any negative emotion his actions caused any Dao Lord. As beings that existed as a higher form of life, anything and everything related to them felt infinitely magnified when it came to immortals. Thus amidst everything Lex had ever done, all the sins he had committed, or the inadvertent pain he had caused, the things that hurt him the most were merely the minor inconveniences he had caused Dao Lords.","It was... it felt uneven, but that’s just how things were.","Yet what could be the purpose of a cycle of torture that only caused him pain? Since he could not be harmed by the pain, how was this torture cycle expected to stop him?","The answer was one of the reasons he felt that the retribution was quite misleading. The real target, from the very beginning, had been his spirit. The cycle of torture was aimed at breaking his spirit and killing his mind.","That is why it waited till he knew, till he understood what he was about to face. The daunting obstacle, one that was entirely inescapable, would crush his spirit. If that didn’t do the trick, then the unending pain would certainly break him.","Except, that’s not what happened. Being able to ignore pain didn’t mean that Lex didn’t suffer from it, nor that it didn’t affect him. It was just that the Hollow probably did not anticipate the way in which it affected him at all.","Instead of breaking him, instead of crushing his spirit and driving him to the edge of insanity, it brought him unprecedented clarity. This was clarity about his situation as a person, as a business owner, and most importantly, about his state of living within a necklace.","For so long, despite being so strong, Lex acted out of caution simply because he was self aware about how many strong beings there were in the universe that could destroy him on a whim.","If he acted with a little more confidence, it would come off as arrogance - especially after he got beaten up by his stalker so badly. Yet the pain was like a splash of cold water on his face, waking him up from his lethargic and reserved state.","Due to how precarious his current situation was, he had been acting a little too cautiously - something one would find hard to believe considering his attempt at taking the flower. Then again, that only happened because he had no other choice.","Regardless, the pain was a good way to clear his head. If he let the pain get to him, Lex would be overwhelmed and his mind fractured, which is why he did the exact opposite. He chose to focus on his task and his purpose.","His current goal was growing strong enough to get revenge. He was already doing that, but he could do more.","His mind flashed back to that moment where he stood in front of Eclipse and she told him that impossible didn’t exist. Impossible simply meant that no one had figured out a way to do it yet, not that it couldn’t be done.","She, the most powerful Dao Lord in the universe, and the absolute best authority on such a topic, had explicitly told him that impossible didn’t exist, and yet when he faced the Primordial Farham egg shell, he had stated that it was impossible to replicate the ability.","That was exactly what Lex meant earlier when he said that he was being too cautious. It wasn’t that he should go and spit on a Dao Lords face, but that he shouldn’t shy away from difficult tasks just because he didn’t have a clear path of doing so. He should boldly go and do the things everyone thought were impossible, instead of accidentally doing them.","He looked within his necklace, ignoring the information on the Prison of Gluttony, and saw the tiniest scrap of the egg shell left. By now, the Disaster Rose had basically entirely lost its shape, and was slowly but surely fusing with the necklace and even Lex’s soul, still activating the phoenix aspect of his being.","The eggshell, however, was preserved elsewhere entirely, surrounded by Lex’s energy. Although he still had no idea how to mimic the shell’s ability, for he most certainly couldn’t create his own laws and then exact them upon the universe, the very presence of the egg shell was evidence that such a thing could be done.","Even if he ultimately failed in doing so, Lex was determined to at least try to absorb some of its ability. After all, he had the most unique cultivation technique in the universe. It should be possible, shouldn’t it?","Lex even had an idea of his own how to do it. The Rebirth by Fire ability he seemed to be on the verge of unlocking was not so simple. Its complexity and profoundness far exceeded Lex’s ability to comprehend. All he understood was that the rebirth came from the very fire, or the very source of destruction that harmed his body.","In this case, he would use the eight cycles of torture as the harm that was being done to him, and during the rebirth phase, he would absorb the egg shell as well, so that it fused with the necklace. He would see if he could gain that ability.","But that was not all. Experiencing the Crucible of Karma had given Lex a first hand experience of a kind of torture he could have never imagined on his own. This... was the perfect template for a new Lawcraft to use to announce his return to his stalker.","He had barely completed that thought when the Prison of Gluttony torture cycle began. Much like the previous one, this one aimed to focus on breaking his spirit.","The torture cycle was a simple one - it marinated Lex’s body and soul with the laws of gluttony before putting him in an energy barren location. His body and soul, due to intense starvation, would begin to eat themselves.","His torture would be twofold - first the intense starvation, and then the sensation of his own being eating itself. When he was on the verge of death, he would immediately be restored to his original state to undergo the torture once again.","There was no clear mention of when or how the cycle would end, but Lex wasn’t bothered in the least. Instead, he noticed how the cycles of torture did not directly kill him, but just tortured him.","Perhaps there was some kind of restriction, or maybe causing the target to suffer was a part of the retribution itself. Pentagal was exacting its revenge, but Lex was treating it entirely as training, not even considering it torture at all.","All he needed to do was get through these eight cycles with his sanity intact, and it would be over. How simple was that?","\"So simple,\" Lex said to himself, even as his eyes turned entirely red, and a single thought kept coming back to his mind: he would make sure to memorise everything that was happening to him, and share the same hospitality with his stalker.","Though technically, the stalker could not be blamed for the retributions, Lex no longer cared. Sharing was caring, and he could not wait to share his experiences with his stalker."]},{"number":2399,"title":"Chapter 2399: Watching lord of the rings 57 times","paragraphs":["Two back to back torture cycles with the aim of breaking Lex’s spirit should have had a compounding effect, wearing his mind down to its absolute limit. In truth, Lex could not claim that he didn’t suffer. In fact, he suffered quite a lot.","The key factor contributing to Lex’s suffering was not the agonizing, never ending pain of his own soul devouring itself repeatedly. It was, instead, not knowing when it would end. The Prison of Gluttony torture cycle had not been entirely forthcoming in describing the torture cycle, like the Crucible of Karma had.","This cycle also secretly affected Lex’s perception of time, so what Lex felt like months or years was, in fact, mere hours.","The very fact that the previous torture cycle had, more or less, accurately described the torture he would endure was specifically designed so that he would believe what the Prison of Gluttony told him, thereby extending his torture greatly.","If Lex hadn’t been specifically studying the laws that made up the torture he was enduring, he would never have picked up on how his senses had been affected.","It was also at this point that Lex realized a couple of other, very critical things. The retribution had led him to believe that there was nothing he could do within these retributions except endure it.","During the previous retribution, Lex had already tried countless ways to expedite or skip the retribution, because honestly if he didn’t need to go through endless pain, he would rather not. Now, he had locked onto a certain loophole!","The retribution itself was not something he could interfere with - unfortunately - but he could most certainly affect his own perception. Could he, perhaps, make it so that he could not feel the endless suffering his own body’s starvation and self-cannibalism caused? He didn’t know but he was certainly going to try.","The second critical thing he noticed was that each time his body healed, the retribution seemed to consume an enormous amount of energy, so much so that Lex could actually sense it. It was likely that the design of the retribution took his cultivation realm into account, not anticipating that his body was of a much higher quality and that healing it was far more difficult than expected.","Thus, by merely sensing the amount of energy left, he could guess how long this particular retribution would last. Of course, in the Lawcraft that he was designing, there was no need to leave a task as unnecessary as healing the enemy.","As a result, while it felt like eternity, Lex’s body only went through three actual cycles of self-cannibalisation and restoration before the retribution was over. Lex, ultimately, was unable to change his perception during this retribution, but he’d experimented enough to know how the Hollow was blocking him from doing so. In future retributions, he should be able to do it.","By the time, two retributions were over, Lex really did feel mentally strained. He could tough it out still, and that’s exactly what he planned to do, but there was no denying that regardless of his tolerance, he was seriously affected.","The third retribution was called Patience. It filled his soul with an itch, soft at first, but it grew stronger with each passing second. The entire retribution would last about 2.5 million seconds, so not that long. It was just enough to watch the original Lord of the Rings trilogy - extended edition, naturally - 57 times, with a bit of time to spare. The issue was that the itch grew stronger at an exponential rate.","What made matters worse was that the retribution also gave him a piece of paper called Soulpaper. It was like sandpaper, except for the soul. How convenient.","Using it to scratch his body would reduce the itch - and also scrape off bits of his soul. Despite that, using Soulpaper would only fill him with relief, and give him no pain whatsoever. It was like a trade with the devil.","Lex smirked. The idea was clever. He could genuinely die in this retribution if he scratched the itch enough. Even if he didn’t, as long as he used the Soulpaper at all, he’d be weaker for subsequent retributions. To top it all off, there was still an element of testing his spirit within this retribution.","Lex closed his eyes, studied the makeup of this retribution, and did his best to kill his perception entirely.","It only sort of worked, for there came a time where the itch in his soul was so strong that it could not be denied. Still, until the very end, Lex did not even touch the Soulpaper.","When the retribution ended, though, he opened his eyes to reveal a deep wariness in them. His spirit was drained once again, for the irritation caused by the itch somehow surpassed the suffering in the previous two retributions. Lex had never felt anything like it.","The fourth retribution was called Parasite. It presented him no information about what the retribution contained whatsoever, and it ended the very moment it began. Yet Lex could feel that there was something amiss. He seemed to have been... affected by this last retribution somehow, and he carried whatever had affected him into the next retribution.","The fifth was called the Test of Erosion - a particularly sinister test. It would, slowly and excruciatingly, erode Lex’s sense of self. The process was slow so that he could feel it happening and despair. The process was entirely unstoppable.","Once his entire sense of self was erased, leaving his body and soul as empty husks, a door would appear in front of him. If he could walk out, the retribution would end, and he would move on. If it didn’t, he would live within the retribution for all of eternity.","This time, Lex almost laughed, though the light in his eyes seemed almost entirely faded. Erasing his spirit while keeping his body and soul intact? His very existence caused a paradox in the setup of the retribution. The Hollow could not do one without affecting the other condition. This was going to be the easiest retribution.","He wanted to see... he wanted to... he wanted... he...","Silence. A deep, resounding, unending silence filled the vessel that was the necklace that acted as the anchor for Lex’s soul, and thus as his body as well. Even the energy around the necklace did not stir, as if there was nothing left there to influence it.","A vague outline of a door appeared in front of the necklace, as if marking an exit. At the same time, deep within the necklace, the parasite that had remained hidden stirred. Even though the fifth retribution had already begun, in truth, the fourth one had not ended yet."]},{"number":2400,"title":"Chapter 2400: Infinity","paragraphs":["The parasite was, in truth, a former resident of Pentagal. It had lived in hibernation for unknown years, protected by the remnant will of the dying universe. Though it was now in a pathetically weak state, once upon a time it had been a being of great power and prestige - far beyond the mundane.","If it could capture this body, then it could infiltrate the universe using the body of a native while hiding its identity, allowing it to perfectly integrate into the universe using an official and authentic identity. It was not the first to do this, nor would it be the last. From the last time that the Gilded Hollow had opened up, this plan was already in motion. The only ones who knew about it were those that had successfully parasited their targets and entered the new universe.","Those who had, for various reasons, overcome or defeated the parasites could not learn of the plan or their intentions - they were protected by the Hollow itself. This was a universe infiltration mission of the highest order!","Of course, not much could become of it. It wasn’t like the remnants of the previous universe could rally against the residents of the new one. They merely gained an opportunity to continue living rather than dying with their own universe.","To facilitate such a thing, the retribution cycles were predetermined to give the parasites the best chance of succeeding without being detected.","This retribution - the Test of Erosion - came now specifically for them to determine if they could successfully parasitize their target. There was no need to rush, they could wait years in silence to see if the target had any way of exiting. Once they were sure, they merely needed to go ahead and take over their body.","The only real limitation was that they would have to do it before the Hollow closed. Thus, even though the parasite had woken up, it had no intention of doing anything just yet.","Unfortunately for it, a long, long time ago Lex had already unlocked an ability that was vaguely reminiscent of a Dao Lords ability.","If a Dao Lords’ name was spoken, or in some cases even thought of, the Dao Lord in question could sense it even from across realms. Similarly, if anyone so much as thought about Lex within a certain range of him, Lex would be able to sense it. Although the parasite did not know Lex as a person, it did not change that his target was Lex.","Although Lex’s spirit itself could not be erased, the Gilded Hollow had found a way around it, artificially restricting his ability to think or make judgments of any kind whatsoever. That did not include, however, his instincts.","The moment the parasite laid its greedy eyes on Lex’s soul, his soul acted out instinctively and unleashed Domination, directly eradicating the parasite hidden within the necklace.","The death of the parasite did not cause his soul to fall into dormancy, however, for his instinct sensed another, weaker yet consistent threat. The threat had a very convenient escape, however, which was the door.","Thus, without any guidance from his spirit, his soul acted on pure instinct to guide his body to move, allowing him to survive this retribution easily.","When Lex’s spirit was restored, the memories came flooding in. The Hollow had been extremely clever. The reason it constantly wore out his spirit, but not his soul and body, was so that the parasite could take over.","In the case of the previous retribution, Lex could not suffer from the Erosion aspect of the retribution, so his ability to think and make judgments had directly been sealed by the Hollow.","The fact that he survived was solely due to the powerful instincts he had as a human being - instincts so intense that they originated straight from the soul!","Due to his sealed state, he had been unable to study the parasite at all, and once it was destroyed it vanished entirely, so he learned nothing significant from it. Yet Lex wasn’t concerned about that right now.","No matter the case, he really was extremely mentally tired, yet the retribution was far from over.","Next began the sixth retribution, the Furnace of Imperfection. Within it, a white flame would incinerate everything that was imperfect. The process would be slow and painful, as only one thing would be incinerated at a time. He could pass the retribution if a single aspect of himself survived once the flames were extinguished, allowing himself to heal perfectly.","As soon as the retribution informed him of the details, Lex came up with a way to survive. He immediately began to use his cultivation technique.","Personal ego and arrogance aside, who could say what was perfect from an objective point of view? His hair? His good looks? His rock solid abs? Yes, but just in case the Gilded Hollow lacked objectivity, he could rely on his cultivation technique. He was certain that it, of all things, could be considered perfect regardless of the universe.","It turned out he was right. In fact, because he was cultivating when the fires appeared, his entire being could be said to be in a state of perfection due to his cultivation technique, ending the retribution as soon as it began.","Thus, feeling great relief, Lex faced his seventh retribution which was known simply as Life. Every piece of his physical body came to life, and gained independent thought, wanting to take over the whole or just run away and survive. To pass the retribution, he needed to fight his own, entire body and reclaim all of it.","In his current situation, Lex’s body was the necklace. If it really came to life and ran away, the entire necklace and the fake realm within it would be destroyed! He couldn’t afford that at all!","Since fighting was a part of the retribution, Lex blasted Domination to his fullest. Unfortunately, all the rest of the necklace was immune to it since it too was originally a part of Lex.","\"Mother of...\"","Lex began to curse, before immediately realizing the perfect solution. He pushed his already exhausted mind into overdrive, exerting his utmost to create a Lawcraft that could replicate the Parasite retribution.","The moment he created it, Lex used it on the rest of the necklace, creating millions of parasites of himself to fight against all the other parts of the necklace that had come to life. Fortunately, while each piece inherited his strength, they were independent lifeforms so they did not inherit his mind and spirit. He was able to reclaim the rest of the necklace before the pieces managed to tear themselves free of the whole.","He had managed to preserve the necklace, but his mind was truly running on fumes. By this point, the only thing sustaining him was sheer willpower. If he could find even a few seconds to rest, his rapid healing ability would allow him to recover even if only a little. Unfortunately, the gap between retributions was not even one second.","There was no time to even compose himself, let alone recover.","Thus, Lex entered his eighth and final retribution: Infinity."]}]);
